tors":["Doctor","Cook","Teacher"],"card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"00c65d29-a9f4-498e-8372-a8b32ef42f34","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4006-0001-b20000000000","type":"sentence_transformation","hint_text":"Verb-final in the wenn-clause; würde + infinitive at the end of the main clause."},"after":{"hint_text":"Put hätte last in the wenn-clause. In the main clause, place würde before ich, optionally with dann before würde; fahren goes last."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"026a5fbf-6538-407d-96be-a5fa0ee621ba","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4006-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":["я бы хотел заказать кофе","я хотела бы заказать кофе","я бы хотела заказать кофе"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["я бы хотел заказать кофе","я хотела бы заказать кофе","я бы хотела заказать кофе","Хотел бы заказать кофе.","Хотела бы заказать кофе.","Мне хотелось бы заказать кофе."]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"027497a1-9d0e-4e94-a7ae-f6c50c95ff51","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[],"explanation":"Reported speech after ha detto backshifts the present to the imperfect: era, parallel to voleva in the second clause. The direct words were: sono stanco e voglio dormire."},"after":{"accepted_answers":["si sentiva"],"explanation":"Era gives the backshifted state was tired, parallel to voleva. Si sentiva is also possible: he said that he felt tired. The blank does not specify essere or provide exact direct words."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"02aa9375-72d9-4fd8-98c8-6c8502d6ac75","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4006-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":["Si llueve mañana nos quedaremos en casa","Si mañana llueve, nos quedaremos en casa","Si mañana llueve nos quedaremos en casa","Si llueve mañana, nos quedamos en casa","Si llueve mañana nos quedamos en casa","Si mañana llueve, nos quedamos en casa","Si mañana llueve nos quedamos en casa"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Si llueve mañana nos quedaremos en casa","Si mañana llueve, nos quedaremos en casa","Si mañana llueve nos quedaremos en casa","Si llueve mañana, nos quedamos en casa","Si llueve mañana nos quedamos en casa","Si mañana llueve, nos quedamos en casa","Si mañana llueve nos quedamos en casa","Nos quedaremos en casa si llueve mañana","Nos quedaremos en casa si mañana llueve","Si llueve mañana, vamos a quedarnos en casa"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"033595f8-ddd6-49bc-bc46-80efc9ee9d2b","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1004-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Hora","correct_answer":"Hora","hint_text":"Time","card_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1004-c009-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Vestido","correct_answer":"Vestido","hint_text":"Dress","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"0466ef88-155c-441d-b408-eaedfc6a43c9","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4006-0002-b20000000000","type":"error_correction","metadata":{},"hint_text":"Movement out of a room takes вы-, not при-.","explanation":"«Пришли из класса» is contradictory: при- means arrival, but «из класса» describes movement out of the room. Exiting an enclosed space requires вы-: «вышли из класса»."},"after":{"metadata":{"correction_instruction":"Describe the students leaving the classroom, not arriving somewhere from it. Keep the first clause, the subject студенты and из класса; replace пришли with a verb of departure."},"hint_text":"For the selected exit, use вышли; ушли can also describe departure.","explanation":"«Пришли из класса» can mean that the students arrived from the classroom, so it is not contradictory. The requested focus on leaving the room is expressed by «вышли из класса»; «ушли из класса» is also accepted."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"059217eb-1de6-41e5-bd64-05f1dbf448c7","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4006-0002-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":["зашел","зашла","заехал","заехала","забежал","забежала"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["зашел","зашла","заехал","заехала","забежал","забежала","заходил","заходила"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"05d8a6d3-1122-4fe5-bb43-961269077166","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":["Se lo avessi saputo, te lo avrei detto","Se l'avessi saputo te l'avrei detto","Se l'avessi saputo, te lo avrei detto","Se lo avessi saputo, te l'avrei detto"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Se lo avessi saputo, te lo avrei detto","Se l'avessi saputo te l'avrei detto","Se l'avessi saputo, te lo avrei detto","Se lo avessi saputo, te l'avrei detto","Se l’avessi saputo, ve l’avrei detto","Se l’avessi saputo, gliel’avrei detto","Se lo avessi saputo, ve lo avrei detto"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"0760f64a-3ab1-48a5-a621-d27d955c5608","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","hint_text":"V + 着 (zhe) = an ongoing state.","explanation":"着 marks a continuing state, not an action: 开着 = is (in the state of being) open. It is not a command and not an event happening right now."},"after":{"hint_text":"Here 开着 describes the continuing state of being open.","explanation":"开着 describes the door as open, followed by an invitation to enter. Here 着 marks a state; with other predicates it can also mark a continuing or background action."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"07bd314c-6a00-4639-8182-da427f1993e2","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":["母に日記を読まれた","私は母に日記を読まれた。","私は母に日記を読まれた","日記を母に読まれた。","日記を母に読まれた","ははににっきをよまれた。","ははににっきをよまれた"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["母に日記を読まれた","私は母に日記を読まれた。","私は母に日記を読まれた","日記を母に読まれた。","日記を母に読まれた","ははににっきをよまれた。","ははににっきをよまれた","母に日記を読まれました","私は母に日記を読まれました","ははににっきをよまれました"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"082d2cbd-784d-4893-b57b-e06fb3d2b318","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","explanation":"着 expresses the ongoing state of having something on: 穿着一件红大衣. 正在穿 would mean she is in the act of putting it on, 要去买 is a future purchase (nothing worn yet), and the object cannot move before the verb."},"after":{"explanation":"穿着一件红大衣 gives the state of wearing the coat. 正在穿 describes putting it on, while 要去买 describes a planned purchase. The displayed pre-verbal object order is not the neutral way to express the requested wearing state; this is not a general ban on topicalized objects."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"08388381-e078-4e5a-8a93-cf07e0e8036c","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0001-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Caldo","correct_answer":"Caldo","hint_text":"Hot","card_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-c007-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Cuoco","correct_answer":"Cuoco","hint_text":"Cook","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"09d719c6-8c31-4a87-ad00-3a440016280a","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"여름","correct_answer":"여름","hint_text":"Summer","card_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-c009-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"기타","correct_answer":"기타","hint_text":"Guitar","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"0a8d0b59-fb78-4389-9ab8-8df6eabc3e8b","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4006-0001-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","explanation":"Credo che expresses belief, so the verb takes the subjunctive: siano, the present subjunctive of essere. The indicative sono would be wrong after credere che.","prompt":"Credo che loro ___ stranieri. (essere)"},"after":{"explanation":"This exercise asks for the third-person plural present subjunctive of essere: siano. It practises formal credo che usage; indicative sono occurs in colloquial reporting of beliefs.","prompt":"Complete in formal Italian with the present subjunctive of essere: Credo che loro ___ stranieri."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"0ae0af81-dec8-472b-9bbd-ddcab9c88384","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"雕塑","correct_answer":"Sculpture","options":["Plot twist","Poem","Sculpture","Novel"],"distractors":["Poem","Novel","Plot twist"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-c004-b20000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"音乐的速度加快了。","correct_answer":"The music gets faster.","options":["The music gets quieter.","The music gets slower.","The music gets faster.","The music starts again."],"distractors":["The music gets quieter.","The music gets slower.","The music starts again."],"card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"0b62a1d8-27a9-431d-a704-82a115fd9158","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0003-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["うけみ"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"0b88959f-fa44-48aa-8fa9-6c3a2f8e53bb","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0003-b20000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["Bias","Claim","Argument","Fallacy"],"distractors":["Bias","Argument","Fallacy"]},"after":{"options":["Bias","Claim","Conclusion","Fallacy"],"distractors":["Bias","Conclusion","Fallacy"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"0c6dec86-5c6e-489b-bb89-cc28eabe49e3","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4006-0002-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","explanation":"Stepping out briefly («на минуту… из комнаты») takes вы-: «вышел». «Пришёл» means arrived, «зашёл» means dropped in, and «дошёл» means reached a point and requires «до» — none of them fits a brief exit «из комнаты»."},"after":{"explanation":"Stepping out briefly («на минуту… из комнаты») takes вы-: «вышел». «Пришёл» means arrived, «зашёл» means dropped in, and «дошёл» means reached a point — none of them fits a brief exit «из комнаты»."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"0e17409d-c838-4f61-b3cd-454f1b5bb5ce","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-3001-0003-b10000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["Therefore","To argue","Debate","Politics"],"distractors":["Politics","Therefore","Debate"]},"after":{"options":["Therefore","To argue","To whisper","Politics"],"distractors":["Politics","Therefore","To whisper"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"0ec36cce-f2b2-4eac-865c-8e9e69b0f351","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4006-0005-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","hint_text":"After чтобы the verb is always PAST tense; «наконец» also cues the perfective.","explanation":"«Чтобы» historically contains бы, so the verb after it must be past tense regardless of real time: «чтобы ты сказал» = that you tell. Future or present forms after «чтобы» are ungrammatical."},"after":{"hint_text":"This wish has a separate subject ты: use a past-form verb after чтобы. «Наконец» selects the completed telling.","explanation":"With the separate subject «ты» in this wish clause, use «чтобы ты сказал» (female: «сказала»), even though the desired telling is not past in real time. This does not apply to every чтобы construction: «чтобы учиться» uses an infinitive."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"0f56ebfc-a69f-4bee-a2bb-294dffc6ed3c","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"error_correction","metadata":{},"hint_text":"The one speaking is 할머니 — her verb needs honorific 말씀하시다.","explanation":"The subject 할머니께서 requires an honorific verb of speaking: 말하다 → 말씀하시다, giving 말씀하셨어요. The quoted command 오라고 stays plain because it targets the speaker (저).","accepted_answers":["할머니께서 저에게 빨리 오라고 말씀하셨습니다"]},"after":{"metadata":{"error_sentence":"할머니께서 저에게 빨리 오라고 말했어요.","correction_instruction":"Keep the message and use polite speech, but honor your grandmother’s speaking action with a subject-honorific verb."},"hint_text":"Use a subject-honorific speaking form: 말씀하셨어요 or 말하셨어요.","explanation":"말씀하셨어요 is a respectful lexical choice, and 말하셨어요 also marks the grandmother’s action with honorific 시. The quoted command 오라고 continues to describe what she told the speaker to do.","accepted_answers":["할머니께서 저에게 빨리 오라고 말씀하셨습니다","할머니께서 저에게 빨리 오라고 말하셨어요","할머니께서 저에게 빨리 오라고 말하셨습니다"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"0f630a16-c2fb-46a4-aa79-228e23486963","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_transformation","accepted_answers":["закончив университет он уехал в москву"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["закончив университет он уехал в москву","Окончив университет, он уехал в Москву."]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"0fdf7689-9abb-473a-a28f-05e6703caab8","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4006-0002-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","hint_text":"The agent (the doer) in a passive sentence takes this preposition + dative.","explanation":"The person who performs the action appears with von + dative in passive sentences: von einer jungen Autorin. Durch is reserved for means or intermediaries, not the true agent."},"after":{"hint_text":"Use the usual agent preposition that takes dative with einer jungen Autorin.","explanation":"Von + dative introduces the writer here: von einer jungen Autorin. Durch takes accusative, so it cannot precede einer in this sentence. Durch can express an agent in other passive sentences; it is not restricted exclusively to means or intermediaries."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"10cec285-d36b-4a10-b182-485393fea09f","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4004-0003-b20000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"그림","correct_answer":"Painting","options":["Novel","Masterpiece","Poem","Painting"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4004-c003-b20000000000","distractors":["Masterpiece","Poem","Novel"]},"after":{"prompt":"관객","correct_answer":"Audience","options":["Novel","Audience","Poem","Masterpiece"],"card_id":null,"distractors":["Novel","Poem","Masterpiece"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"116805d5-dd15-428d-b7f2-15a2dc8f8b68","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2008-0002-a20000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["To celebrate","Birthday","Dance","Party"],"distractors":["Dance","Birthday","Party"]},"after":{"options":["To celebrate","Birthday","Dance","To sleep"],"distractors":["Dance","Birthday","To sleep"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"11aec572-8782-4a55-bdd3-17b8bda5c252","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4006-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":["я хочу, чтобы он пришел","я хочу чтобы он пришёл","я хочу чтобы он пришел","я хочу, чтобы он приехал","я хочу чтобы он приехал"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["я хочу, чтобы он пришел","я хочу чтобы он пришёл","я хочу чтобы он пришел","я хочу, чтобы он приехал","я хочу чтобы он приехал","Хочу, чтобы он пришёл.","Хочу, чтобы он пришел.","Хочу, чтобы он приехал."]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"11c977b8-cb6d-4a60-9f16-fafa6725922f","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[],"explanation":"Plural subject «muchas casas» → plural verb: se vendieron. Review: in the pasiva refleja the noun after the verb is the grammatical subject and controls the agreement."},"after":{"accepted_answers":["vendían"],"explanation":"The plural subject muchas casas requires a plural verb. Se vendieron presents completed sales; se vendían describes ongoing or repeated sales during the crisis. Both past-tense readings fit the prompt, which does not require the preterite."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"12c78ebf-2c46-4e59-9769-fb50118178a0","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4006-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","explanation":"Doubt triggers the subjunctive: dudo que tenga (not tiene). The subject pronoun «él» is optional because the verb ending already marks the person.","accepted_answers":["Dudo que él tenga el dinero","Dudo de que tenga el dinero","Dudo de que él tenga el dinero","Yo dudo que tenga el dinero","Yo dudo que él tenga el dinero"]},"after":{"explanation":"Doubt takes the subjunctive here: dudo que tenga (not tiene). The pronoun «él» can be omitted when context identifies him. The form «tenga» itself can be first- or third-person singular, so the ending alone does not identify the subject.","accepted_answers":["Dudo que él tenga el dinero","Dudo de que tenga el dinero","Dudo de que él tenga el dinero","Yo dudo que tenga el dinero","Yo dudo que él tenga el dinero","Yo dudo de que él tenga el dinero","Yo dudo de que tenga el dinero"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"13bddacc-7f3d-43f0-a6b9-80cc9a6aa37e","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["Nevertheless","However","Claim","Evidence"],"distractors":["Evidence","Nevertheless","Claim"]},"after":{"options":["Therefore","However","Claim","Evidence"],"distractors":["Evidence","Therefore","Claim"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"13c1888a-b5ab-440d-85c2-bcbb844c0273","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4006-0001-b20000000000","type":"sentence_transformation","prompt":"Rewrite using « Il faut que » : Vous devez être patients.","accepted_answers":["Il faut que vous soyez patient","Il faut que vous soyez patiente","Il faut que vous soyez patientes"]},"after":{"prompt":"Rewrite using « Il faut que », keeping vous and the agreement patients: Vous devez être patients.","accepted_answers":[]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"14d29f87-4d22-44b9-9907-0cfb4414d904","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4006-0003-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":"听 + result: 清楚 (qīngchu) = clearly."},"after":{"accepted_answers":["清"],"hint_text":"Use a result complement meaning clearly after 听."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"178ac03a-b4de-45fd-b332-ea286bad598b","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"新聞によると、来年この町で国際会議が開かれる___です。— Choose the correct form.","explanation":"〜によると announces a source, so the sentence must end in hearsay そうです after the plain form 開かれる — itself a passive: \"will be held.\" はず, つもり, and べき state deduction, intention, or opinion — none of them report a source."},"after":{"prompt":"新聞によると、来年この町で国際会議が開かれる___です。— Report the newspaper’s information using the hearsay form.","explanation":"For the requested hearsay report, use the plain passive 開かれる followed by そうです. によると identifies the newspaper as the source. はず instead presents expectation or deduction; the source phrase alone does not prohibit that different meaning."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"19ba077b-1a62-49b0-be6a-5d282b4614e4","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1005-0001-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"热","correct_answer":"热","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":"Hot","card_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1005-c007-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"厨师","correct_answer":"厨师","accepted_answers":["廚師"],"hint_text":"Cook","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"1a5160ff-1bff-4be0-b888-8d8024ed5215","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"error_correction","metadata":{"error_sentence":"先生はさっき、職員室で昼ご飯をいただきました。"},"hint_text":"いただく is humble — wrong for the teacher's own action.","explanation":"いただく lowers the eater, so it can only describe your own eating. For the teacher use respectful 召し上がりました (or the honorific passive 食べられました).","accepted_answers":["先生はさっき、職員室で昼ご飯を召し上がりました","せんせいはさっき、しょくいんしつでひるごはんをめしあがりました。","先生はさっき、職員室で昼ご飯を食べられました。","先生はさっき、職員室で昼ご飯を食べられました"]},"after":{"metadata":{"error_sentence":"先生はさっき、職員室で昼ご飯をいただきました。","correction_instruction":"You are respectfully describing your teacher’s eating to another person. Honor the teacher’s action; do not present the teacher as your own in-group representative."},"hint_text":"For the honored teacher’s eating, use 召し上がる or respectful 食べられる.","explanation":"For the teacher being honored here, use 召し上がりました or respectful 食べられました. Humble いただく is not restricted to the speaker alone; it can describe an in-group person’s action in an appropriate relationship.","accepted_answers":["先生はさっき、職員室で昼ご飯を召し上がりました","せんせいはさっき、しょくいんしつでひるごはんをめしあがりました。","先生はさっき、職員室で昼ご飯を食べられました。","先生はさっき、職員室で昼ご飯を食べられました","先生はさっき職員室で昼ご飯を召し上がりました","先生はさっき職員室で昼ご飯を食べられました"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"1a9f2345-20fa-4a61-8694-ee1e2b05b354","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4004-0003-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"그림","correct_answer":"그림","hint_text":"Painting","card_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4004-c003-b20000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"관객","correct_answer":"관객","hint_text":"Audience","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"1e7a0858-ed12-4a4a-8f58-5a44856bc8bb","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1005-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Verano","correct_answer":"Verano","hint_text":"Summer","card_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1005-c009-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Guitarra","correct_answer":"Guitarra","hint_text":"Guitar","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"1e8bd52e-147e-4809-9f00-ea1c59c10e7e","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4006-0002-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","hint_text":"듣다 → 들리다 (to be heard); the ㄷ changes to ㄹ.","explanation":"듣다 becomes the passive 들리다 — the ㄷ-irregular stem changes to ㄹ before the suffix -리-. Present polite: 들려요. \"This song is heard often\" means you often hear it."},"after":{"hint_text":"Learn the passive counterpart 듣다 → 들리다 (to be heard). Its present polite form is 들려요.","explanation":"The passive counterpart of 듣다 is 들리다, meaning “to be heard.” Its present polite form is 들려요. Learn this lexical pair; it is not the usual ㄷ-irregular change before a consonant-initial -리- suffix."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"20488551-e3f4-4e14-a801-6f51f813bfef","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1004-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"시간","correct_answer":"시간","hint_text":"Time","card_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1004-c009-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"원피스","correct_answer":"원피스","hint_text":"Dress","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"2075c023-7ae7-433b-8174-22d9c813d32b","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"Ufficio","correct_answer":"Office","options":["Doctor","Winter","Office","Summer"],"distractors":["Winter","Summer","Doctor"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-c003-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Mi piace disegnare.","correct_answer":"I like drawing.","options":["I like reading.","I like cooking.","I like drawing.","I like swimming."],"distractors":["I like reading.","I like cooking.","I like swimming."],"card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"20f656d2-8633-42b6-8884-b4b0c4087c59","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1005-0004-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"Leer","correct_answer":"To read","options":["To read","Doctor","Winter","Summer"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1005-c004-000000000000","distractors":["Doctor","Summer","Winter"]},"after":{"prompt":"Lluvia","correct_answer":"Rain","options":["Wind","Rain","Snow","Cloud"],"card_id":null,"distractors":["Wind","Snow","Cloud"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"222c116a-da84-4a52-b647-178b43d5219d","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-1005-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"夏","correct_answer":"Summer","options":["Friend","Cold","Summer","To cook"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-6666-1005-c009-000000000000","distractors":["To cook","Cold","Friend"]},"after":{"prompt":"ギター","correct_answer":"Guitar","options":["To cook","Guitar","Soccer","To read"],"card_id":null,"distractors":["To cook","Soccer","To read"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"2265816f-c507-47a3-9e76-90ec6a5f7947","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4006-0001-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","hint_text":"Penso che triggers the subjunctive mood.","explanation":"After opinion verbs like penso che, Italian requires the subjunctive: abbia, the present subjunctive of avere. The indicative forms ha, aveva and ha avuto are the classic English-speaker error here.","prompt":"Choose the correct form: Penso che Luca ___ ragione."},"after":{"hint_text":"Choose the present subjunctive used after penso che in formal Italian.","explanation":"Formal Italian uses abbia, the present subjunctive of avere, in this opinion clause. Indicative forms occur in colloquial usage, but do not satisfy this formal subjunctive exercise.","prompt":"Choose the present subjunctive for formal Italian: Penso che Luca ___ ragione."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"22f3d30a-62c9-4c6d-a206-99d11116b5be","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1005-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Oficina","correct_answer":"Oficina","hint_text":"Office","card_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1005-c003-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Nadar","correct_answer":"Nadar","hint_text":"To swim","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"2526146e-8938-447b-8f6b-f11e629df932","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-3007-0002-b10000000000","type":"listening_choice","correct_answer":"Would","options":["Would","Regret","Suppose","Otherwise"]},"after":{"correct_answer":"Would do / would make","options":["Would do / would make","Regret","Suppose","Otherwise"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"254a4cf3-f667-47c8-8437-d65b6545bf4d","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0002-b10000000000","type":"listening_type","hint_text":"Would"},"after":{"hint_text":"Would do / would make"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"26182675-f0d5-430d-bf80-eae98332a583","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"Каждое лето мы ___ к бабушке в деревню. (Every summer we go to visit grandma in the village.)","explanation":"Habitual round trips take the multidirectional verb: «ездим» (by vehicle). Unidirectional «идём» describes one walking trip in progress, «поедем» is a one-time future trip, and «ушли» means departed on foot for good."},"after":{"prompt":"Каждое лето мы ___ к бабушке в деревню. (Every summer we go to visit grandma in the village.) Choose the present-tense multidirectional verb for repeated trips by vehicle with a return journey.","explanation":"The requested repeated round trips by vehicle use «ездим». «Идём» presents walking in one direction and does not match that selected vehicle-trip perspective; it need not always refer to right now. «Поедем» is future, and «ушли» is past departure, not necessarily departure for good."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"2680f28a-fc7f-4e9a-b60d-bac4fb7c54a3","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1005-0001-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Caliente","correct_answer":"Caliente","hint_text":"Hot","card_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1005-c007-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Ingeniero","correct_answer":"Ingeniero","hint_text":"Engineer","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"26e99315-6998-4b4b-9e8e-9725769378d7","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-1005-0001-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Горячий","correct_answer":"Горячий","hint_text":"Hot","card_id":"aabbccdd-9999-1005-c007-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Водитель","correct_answer":"Водитель","hint_text":"Driver","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"2743eacf-36e1-47de-92fb-2e407478304a","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-1004-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"Hora","correct_answer":"Time","options":["Blue","Shirt","Time","Red"],"distractors":["Shirt","Blue","Red"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-5555-1004-c009-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Saia","correct_answer":"Skirt","options":["Shoes","Shirt","Dress","Skirt"],"distractors":["Shoes","Shirt","Dress"],"card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"27ebed61-193e-4471-a5da-8fe50f356c0a","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4006-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":["Ella dijo que estaba cansada"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Ella dijo que estaba cansada","Dijo que ella estaba cansada","Ella dijo que se encontraba cansada"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"28dee065-caa9-477d-8fc1-788c5a7dd745","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4006-0003-b20000000000","type":"error_correction","metadata":{},"hint_text":"작년에 + -았을 거예요 is an unreal PAST — the condition must be counterfactual too.","explanation":"The result clause 샀을 거예요 refers to an unreal past (작년), so the condition cannot be the plain 많으면; it must carry past counterfactual marking: 많았더라면 (or 많았다면).","accepted_answers":["돈이 많았더라면 작년에 그 집을 샀을 텐데요"]},"after":{"metadata":{"error_sentence":"돈이 많으면 작년에 그 집을 샀을 거예요.","correction_instruction":"Express an unreal past: you did not have enough money, so you did not buy that house last year. Rewrite the condition to mean “if I had had plenty of money.”"},"hint_text":"For this explicitly unreal past, use 많았더라면 or 많았다면.","explanation":"The requested unreal-past meaning uses 많았더라면 or 많았다면 with 샀을 거예요 or 샀을 텐데요. The original can instead express an open condition and a guess about a past purchase. A past-time result alone does not make every condition counterfactual.","accepted_answers":["돈이 많았더라면 작년에 그 집을 샀을 텐데요","돈이 많았다면 작년에 그 집을 샀을 거예요","돈이 많았다면 작년에 그 집을 샀을 텐데요"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"29174f9b-388b-45b6-b077-790a7266cba6","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-1005-0001-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"暑い","correct_answer":"Hot","options":["Friend","Hot","To read","Soccer"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-6666-1005-c007-000000000000","distractors":["Friend","To read","Soccer"]},"after":{"prompt":"エンジニア","correct_answer":"Engineer","options":["Teacher","Engineer","Doctor","Nurse"],"card_id":null,"distractors":["Teacher","Doctor","Nurse"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"2a819ef4-0867-4b4c-a000-68e53c1313a5","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["Yes","Thank you","Excuse me","Sorry"],"distractors":["Sorry","Thank you","Yes"]},"after":{"options":["Yes","Thank you","Excuse me","Good morning"],"distractors":["Good morning","Thank you","Yes"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"2a85845a-4814-4054-8f09-a8be88cd6374","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0002-b20000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["Agenda","Strategy","Proposal","To implement"],"distractors":["Strategy","Proposal","To implement"]},"after":{"options":["Agenda","Strategy","Deadline","To implement"],"distractors":["Strategy","Deadline","To implement"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"2ac1d691-efda-4ed2-bb3a-3e401e68f133","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4006-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","hint_text":"Präteritum passive: wurde + Partizip II. German says 1950 or im Jahr 1950 — never \"in 1950\".","explanation":"A completed past event in the passive: wurde gebaut (or Perfekt: ist gebaut worden). Note that German uses the bare year or im Jahr 1950; \"in 1950\" is an anglicism.","prompt":"Translate to German: The house was built in 1950."},"after":{"hint_text":"For this standard written-language exercise, use the bare year 1950 or im Jahr 1950. Passive: wurde + Partizip II.","explanation":"The Präteritum passive is wurde gebaut; the accepted Perfekt is ist gebaut worden. This exercise practises the standard year expressions 1950 and im Jahr 1950. In + year also occurs in usage, but is not the form being taught here.","prompt":"Translate to standard written German using the bare year or im Jahr: The house was built in 1950."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"2b04ce29-ecd2-4779-bb48-4c90ab504852","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"Sculpture","correct_answer":"Sculpture","options":["Painting","Symbolism","Sculpture","Plot twist"],"distractors":["Plot twist","Painting","Symbolism"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-c004-b20000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Le tempo s’accélère.","correct_answer":"The music gets faster.","options":["The music gets quieter.","The music gets slower.","The music gets faster.","The music starts again."],"distractors":["The music gets quieter.","The music gets slower.","The music starts again."],"card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"2bdf4d1d-9604-4d91-8cd3-1c682e517e00","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-2007-0006-a20000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["Cheaper","More expensive","Taller","Better"],"distractors":["Taller","Better","Cheaper"]},"after":{"options":["Cheaper","More expensive","Slower","Better"],"distractors":["Slower","Better","Cheaper"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"2be0982d-84cf-4f81-92f1-56d8332f36d0","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0001-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","hint_text":"To pull someones leg"},"after":{"hint_text":"To pull someone's leg"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"2e185a94-e2e6-460c-aa4c-c4faea4039e3","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0003-b20000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["Argument","However","Evidence","Claim"],"distractors":["However","Evidence","Argument"]},"after":{"options":["Conclusion","However","Evidence","Claim"],"distractors":["However","Evidence","Conclusion"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"2f773fd0-e7e0-43cb-8d51-74ed30602ec1","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-1004-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"Heure","correct_answer":"Time","card_id":"aabbccdd-2222-1004-c009-000000000000","options":["Breakfast","Blue","Cheap","Time"],"distractors":["Cheap","Breakfast","Blue"]},"after":{"prompt":"Robe","correct_answer":"Dress","card_id":null,"options":["Shirt","Blue","Dress","Shoes"],"distractors":["Shirt","Blue","Shoes"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"2f9d0a82-dad8-4d12-b22d-3ca35c07d884","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","accepted_answers":["Se habla español aquí"],"explanation":"English passives usually become the pasiva refleja in Spanish: se habla español. Neither the progressive («está hablando») nor a literal passive works for general statements like signs."},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Se habla español aquí","Se habla aquí español","Español se habla aquí"],"explanation":"Here, se habla español is the idiomatic way to state that Spanish is spoken at this location. Está hablando describes an ongoing speaking event, not this general notice. Spanish also has ser + participle passives; their suitability depends on context, so they are not categorically excluded from general statements."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"2ff4d7ba-3fe6-470c-8541-15f9b140643f","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0001-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","hint_text":"To pull someones leg"},"after":{"hint_text":"To pull someone's leg"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"305103a9-048a-4102-939d-e5b4157253d8","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-1005-0004-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"読む","correct_answer":"読む","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":"To read","card_id":"aabbccdd-6666-1005-c004-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"雨","correct_answer":"雨","accepted_answers":["あめ"],"hint_text":"Rain","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"317b109b-a80f-4725-9b82-70c53789155e","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-1005-0004-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Lire","correct_answer":"Lire","hint_text":"To read","card_id":"aabbccdd-2222-1005-c004-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Il pleut","correct_answer":"Il pleut","hint_text":"It is raining","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"320d95cc-26a2-46ad-aa1d-a4e0f272ddc0","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-4006-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["A ponte foi construída em mil novecentos e sessenta e seis."]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"32d278ed-b1f5-4bf1-b8d3-0ac163ce3ef1","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"여름","correct_answer":"Summer","options":["Hot","Cold","Summer","Soccer"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-c009-000000000000","distractors":["Soccer","Cold","Hot"]},"after":{"prompt":"기타","correct_answer":"Guitar","options":["To cook","Soccer","Guitar","To read"],"card_id":null,"distractors":["To cook","Soccer","To read"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"3578b223-fbbd-48e4-8db1-b5a2a90513d8","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-1005-0001-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"Chaud","correct_answer":"Hot","options":["Cold","Hot","To read","Doctor"],"distractors":["Cold","Doctor","To read"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-2222-1005-c007-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Cuisinier","correct_answer":"Cook","options":["Teacher","Cook","Doctor","Driver"],"distractors":["Teacher","Doctor","Driver"],"card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"36406a75-c064-41aa-af25-9cf0dd9bee47","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","explanation":"The respectful pattern is お + stem + になる: お帰りになりました. お帰りされました and お帰りをしました wrongly mix する into the respectful slot, and plain 帰りました shows no respect at all."},"after":{"explanation":"The requested subject-honorific pattern is お + verb stem + になる: お帰りになりました. 帰りました is polite to the listener through ます, but does not itself elevate the president as the subject. Use the taught お帰りになる pattern here."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"36830ba8-a4a1-40d3-9a82-6c080e02ac0d","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-4005-0001-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","hint_text":"To pull someones leg"},"after":{"hint_text":"To pull someone's leg"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"3720c172-42d7-4804-99f2-0740ccb924e3","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4006-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","hint_text":"To be right = avere ragione; remember the mood after penso che.","explanation":"Penso che (or credo che) requires the subjunctive: abbia ragione, not ha ragione. Italian uses avere ragione (to have reason) where English uses to be right.","prompt":"Translate to Italian: I think Marco is right."},"after":{"hint_text":"Use formal Italian with the subjunctive after penso che or credo che; to be right = avere ragione.","explanation":"Use abbia ragione in this formal subjunctive exercise. Avere ragione means to be right. Colloquial indicative usage is outside the construction requested here.","prompt":"Translate to formal Italian, using the subjunctive: I think Marco is right."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"37d1044d-db5a-4815-97ab-92c39f39eb35","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1005-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"办公室","correct_answer":"办公室","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":"Office","card_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1005-c003-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"我喜欢画画。","correct_answer":"我喜欢画画。","accepted_answers":["我喜歡畫畫。"],"hint_text":"I like drawing.","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"394a406f-3d0b-4f0a-bc2a-c6a8b1bfb028","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4006-0003-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"Elle a dit : « Je suis fatiguée. » → Elle a dit qu'elle ___ fatiguée.","explanation":"After a past reporting verb (« a dit »), the present backshifts to the imparfait: était. Keeping « est » copies English, where backshift is optional; in French it is obligatory."},"after":{"prompt":"Apply tense backshift (present to imparfait) from a past-time viewpoint: Elle a dit : « Je suis fatiguée. » → Elle a dit qu'elle ___ fatiguée.","explanation":"For the requested past-time backshift, suis becomes était. After a passé composé reporting verb, French can also retain the original tense when the report keeps its current relevance; backshift is not universally obligatory."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"3ab267e8-0721-4882-8fde-32ac26c69581","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0006-b10000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["Meanwhile","Next","Ending","Then"],"distractors":["Then","Meanwhile","Ending"]},"after":{"options":["Meanwhile","Next","Ending","Before"],"distractors":["Before","Meanwhile","Ending"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"3ab6f2cc-6cdc-4678-8792-922029b63a8d","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4006-0002-b20000000000","type":"error_correction","metadata":{},"accepted_answers":["도둑이 경찰한테 잡혔어요"]},"after":{"metadata":{"error_sentence":"도둑이 경찰을 잡았어요.","correction_instruction":"Rewrite so that the thief was caught by the police, using a passive verb. The original instead says that the thief caught the police."},"accepted_answers":["도둑이 경찰한테 잡혔어요","도둑은 경찰에게 잡혔어요","경찰에게 도둑이 잡혔어요"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"3bbc3807-131a-470e-a62a-77dc61855d11","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-1005-0004-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"Lire","correct_answer":"To read","card_id":"aabbccdd-2222-1005-c004-000000000000","options":["Summer","Office","To read","Cold"],"distractors":["Summer","Office","Cold"]},"after":{"prompt":"Il pleut","correct_answer":"It is raining","card_id":null,"options":["It is cold","It is hot","It is raining","It is snowing"],"distractors":["It is cold","It is hot","It is snowing"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"3c2c7173-ad4d-482a-94d4-cbfac4a1d3e1","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4006-0003-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"Which is the correct reported form? Ils ont annoncé : « Nous avons fini le projet. »","explanation":"The passé composé backshifts to the plus-que-parfait in reported speech: avaient fini. The pronoun also shifts from nous to ils because the reporter is no longer the original speaker."},"after":{"prompt":"You are outside the group that spoke. Apply tense backshift (passé composé to plus-que-parfait): Ils ont annoncé : « Nous avons fini le projet. » Which report fits?","explanation":"The requested backshift changes avons fini to avaient fini. Because the reporter is outside the original group, nous becomes ils here. Keeping the original tense can be possible in a report with current relevance, but it is not the transformation requested."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"3d1b9aa5-47b8-4efa-9067-142d4aba27c0","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":["Der Professor sagt, dass die Prüfung schwierig sei","Der Professor sagt die Prüfung sei schwierig","Der Professor sagt, die Pruefung sei schwierig","Der Professor sagt, dass die Pruefung schwierig sei"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Der Professor sagt, dass die Prüfung schwierig sei","Der Professor sagt die Prüfung sei schwierig","Der Professor sagt, die Pruefung sei schwierig","Der Professor sagt, dass die Pruefung schwierig sei","Die Professorin sagt, die Prüfung sei schwierig.","Die Professorin sagt, dass die Prüfung schwierig sei."]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"3e6198db-7732-4901-a8e9-fef801015a61","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4006-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":["вчера я купила хлеб","я купил хлеб вчера","я купила хлеб вчера","я вчера купил хлеб","я вчера купила хлеб"],"prompt":"Translate to Russian: \"Yesterday I bought bread.\" (start with «Вчера»)","explanation":"A single completed purchase takes the perfective past: «купил» (or «купила» for a female speaker). Imperfective «покупал» would mean repeated or unfinished buying, which the English sentence does not express."},"after":{"accepted_answers":["вчера я купила хлеб","Вчера я купил хлеба.","Вчера я купила хлеба."],"prompt":"Translate to Russian: \"Yesterday I bought bread.\" Use the perfective past of «купить» and start with «Вчера».","explanation":"For the perfective purchase explicitly requested in the hint, use «Вчера я купил хлеб» (female speaker: «купила»). The partitive «хлеба» is also possible. Imperfective «покупал» can state a general past fact in a suitable context; it does not necessarily mean the purchase was unfinished or repeated."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"3ee4f709-0b94-4550-bd11-064d801f590f","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":["明日、書類をお送りいたします","明日書類をお送りいたします。","明日書類をお送りいたします","あした、しょるいをおおくりいたします。","あしたしょるいをおおくりいたします","書類は明日お送りいたします。","書類は明日お送りいたします"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["明日、書類をお送りいたします","明日書類をお送りいたします。","明日書類をお送りいたします","あした、しょるいをおおくりいたします。","あしたしょるいをおおくりいたします","書類は明日お送りいたします。","書類は明日お送りいたします","明日、書類をお送りします。","明日書類をお送りします。","書類は明日お送りします。","あした、しょるいをおおくりします。","あしたしょるいをおおくりします。"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"3eff6bc0-f742-420f-8e28-001ee0686a41","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4006-0005-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","hint_text":"'Much taller' = 高多了 / 高得多. Never use 很 in a 比-sentence.","explanation":"Degree words like 很/非常 are banned in 比-sentences; a big difference is shown AFTER the adjective with 多了 or 得多: 哥哥比我高多了. Reversing 哥哥 and 我 reverses the meaning."},"after":{"hint_text":"Express much taller after 高 with 多了, 得多 or 很多; do not use 比我很高.","explanation":"The offered correct answer is 哥哥比我高多了. A large difference can be expressed after the adjective with 多了, 得多 or 很多. Bare 很 before 高 does not form this comparison; swapping the brothers reverses its meaning."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"3f0a8a1b-9b69-42f1-a51c-fc505a0629a9","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-1005-0001-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Quente","correct_answer":"Quente","hint_text":"Hot","card_id":"aabbccdd-5555-1005-c007-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Cozinheiro","correct_answer":"Cozinheiro","hint_text":"Cook","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"3febc703-c5da-4b54-bf66-156dacedc6de","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0002-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["せつぞくし"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"416f3540-d0a8-41dc-baa2-fd6f137e3883","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4006-0003-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","hint_text":"Use -거든, not -(으)면 — the main clause is a request.","explanation":"-거든 attaches directly to the stem: 만나거든 = \"if you happen to meet Minsu.\" It is preferred over -(으)면 when the condition is uncertain and the main clause is a command or request."},"after":{"hint_text":"Use the specifically requested connective -거든 after the stem 만나-.","explanation":"만나다 + -거든 gives 만나거든, “if you happen to meet.” The following clause requests that the listener pass on a book. -(으)면 can also occur before a request; this exercise specifically asks you to practise -거든."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"41902e82-99f4-43fd-8903-159e7415c401","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"Ils ont dit : « Nous avons gagné. » → Ils ont dit qu'ils ___ gagné.","explanation":"In reported speech after a past verb, the passé composé backshifts to the plus-que-parfait: avaient gagné. The pronoun shifts from nous to ils as the point of view changes."},"after":{"prompt":"You are outside the group that spoke. Apply passé composé-to-plus-que-parfait backshift: Ils ont dit : « Nous avons gagné. » → Ils ont dit qu'ils ___ gagné.","explanation":"For this requested past-time backshift, avons gagné becomes avaient gagné. Nous becomes ils because the reporter is outside the original group. Other reporting contexts can retain the original tense."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"428e4b88-e545-4a85-b3e2-cff9bac91e7a","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["ふていし"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"429842b2-6096-4fbd-aa26-96cf2522f9ae","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4006-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":["衣服洗好了。","衣服洗完了","衣服洗完了。","衣服已经洗好了","衣服已经洗好了。","衣服洗干净了","衣服洗干净了。"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["衣服洗好了。","衣服洗完了","衣服洗完了。","衣服已经洗好了","衣服已经洗好了。","衣服洗干净了","衣服洗干净了。","衣服已经洗完了","衣服已经洗干净了"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"43180ea4-f3b2-4bd9-b0e7-511bc07cf93e","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1004-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"Hora","correct_answer":"Time","options":["Blue","To pay","Expensive","Time"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1004-c009-000000000000","distractors":["Blue","Expensive","To pay"]},"after":{"prompt":"Vestido","correct_answer":"Dress","options":["Shirt","Shoes","Dress","Coat"],"card_id":null,"distractors":["Shirt","Shoes","Coat"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"43aec50c-2768-4a12-a1d3-17ee2ffd4eaf","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0005-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["じせい"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"464afb60-b9be-4ed4-a2f5-783da509d336","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4006-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":["请把门打开。","把门打开","把门打开。","请你把门打开","请你把门打开。"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["请把门打开。","把门打开","把门打开。","请你把门打开","请你把门打开。","请把门开开","请您把门打开"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"46c7c0b3-1367-4b5b-8f68-458902a48905","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-1001-0001-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["Hello","Goodbye","Good night","Excuse me"]},"after":{"options":["Hello","Thank you","Good night","Excuse me"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"4730d47d-cbc1-4797-b3d1-e53cce0321c9","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3008-0001-b10000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["Cool","Formal","Awesome","Sincerely"],"distractors":["Cool","Sincerely","Formal"]},"after":{"options":["Goodbye","Formal","Awesome","Sincerely"],"distractors":["Goodbye","Sincerely","Formal"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"4772ed43-ede6-466e-9ac6-819757ed3e59","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3008-0004-b10000000000","type":"listening_type","hint_text":"Regards"},"after":{"hint_text":"Please give my regards"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"4779fe09-b776-4d8f-abd0-c434dfccfb3f","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-3007-0003-b10000000000","type":"listening_choice","correct_answer":"Instead","options":["Instead","Should","Suppose","Otherwise"]},"after":{"correct_answer":"Instead of","options":["Instead of","Should","Suppose","Otherwise"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"47f283c0-4972-47a2-860e-d433c5cd5ffd","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"조각","correct_answer":"Sculpture","options":["Painting","Novel","Metaphor","Sculpture"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4004-c004-b20000000000","distractors":["Painting","Metaphor","Novel"]},"after":{"prompt":"선율","correct_answer":"Melody","options":["Harmony","Silence","Melody","Rhythm"],"card_id":null,"distractors":["Harmony","Silence","Rhythm"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"49808db9-4fd1-4fb9-9bc3-de572eb78e92","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["No","Good night","Sorry","Excuse me"],"distractors":["Sorry","No","Good night"]},"after":{"options":["No","Good night","Good morning","Excuse me"],"distractors":["Good morning","No","Good night"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"4a9ff9d7-2c46-4c27-b1e0-2fa0fd573d45","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3008-0004-b10000000000","type":"listening_choice","correct_answer":"Regards","options":["Kind of","Dude","Cool","Regards"]},"after":{"correct_answer":"Please give my regards","options":["Kind of","Dude","Cool","Please give my regards"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"4b0f1b6b-1bf9-4ed6-ac78-ec831d13fbc4","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Skulptur","correct_answer":"Skulptur","hint_text":"Sculpture","card_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4004-c004-b20000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Das Tempo wird schneller.","correct_answer":"Das Tempo wird schneller.","hint_text":"The music gets faster.","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"4b94d1e2-bd63-44a7-80b9-a2812bd94b0b","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0002-b10000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["While","Then","Next","Suddenly"],"distractors":["Suddenly","Next","While"]},"after":{"options":["While","Then","Before","Suddenly"],"distractors":["Suddenly","Before","While"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"4cd96507-2818-4fb7-8eb0-a821bb252473","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4005-0001-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","hint_text":"To pull someones leg"},"after":{"hint_text":"To pull someone's leg"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"4d7260a9-dd5a-43a4-84d5-a6be5b1db642","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-1005-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"Офис","correct_answer":"Office","options":["Teacher","Office","Soccer","Doctor"],"distractors":["Soccer","Teacher","Doctor"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-9999-1005-c003-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Я люблю рисовать.","correct_answer":"I like drawing.","options":["I like cooking.","I like reading.","I like drawing.","I like swimming."],"distractors":["I like cooking.","I like reading.","I like swimming."],"card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"4fb9f4d2-94f3-43d1-bdd1-75d805790f51","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"error_correction","metadata":{},"hint_text":"Negated belief — check the mood.","explanation":"« Ne pas croire que » expresses doubt and takes the subjunctive: puisse. The indicative « peut » is only correct in the affirmative « je crois qu'il peut »."},"after":{"metadata":{"correction_instruction":"Express doubt by rewriting pouvoir in the present subjunctive after Je ne crois pas que. Keep the rest of the sentence unchanged."},"hint_text":"For the requested doubtful subjunctive reading, use puisse.","explanation":"The requested subjunctive expresses doubt: Je ne crois pas qu’il puisse résoudre ce problème seul. Negative croire can also take an indicative or conditional in other contexts; the indicative is not limited to affirmative croire."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"517d3618-8290-4d43-abf1-308879650bca","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4006-0005-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","explanation":"«Хотел бы» + infinitive is the polite, softened way to express a wish, like English «would like». The distractor «хочу» cannot combine with «бы» — the particle only attaches to past-tense forms."},"after":{"explanation":"«Хотел бы» plus an infinitive politely softens a wish, like English «would like». For this finite conditional form of хотеть, use «хотел», not present «хочу». Other constructions allow бы with an infinitive or a predicative; the particle is not universally limited to past-tense forms."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"528550d0-34c0-4ad9-bc5b-019899e2a13d","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"Escultura","correct_answer":"Sculpture","options":["Plot twist","Review","Sculpture","Symbolism"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4004-c004-b20000000000","distractors":["Review","Plot twist","Symbolism"]},"after":{"prompt":"Melodía","correct_answer":"Melody","options":["Melody","Rhythm","Harmony","Silence"],"card_id":null,"distractors":["Rhythm","Harmony","Silence"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"546bd4a2-a52a-4d33-8cc5-95e7c06a04e6","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-1005-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"Bureau","correct_answer":"Office","options":["Teacher","Office","To read","Summer"],"distractors":["Teacher","Summer","To read"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-2222-1005-c003-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"J’aime dessiner.","correct_answer":"I like drawing.","options":["I like reading.","I like cooking.","I like drawing.","I like swimming."],"distractors":["I like reading.","I like cooking.","I like swimming."],"card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"54b09fab-3a72-4746-89bd-5af47fd98b9c","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4006-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":["Der Freund, mit dem ich gereist bin, lebt in Berlin","Der Freund mit dem ich gereist bin wohnt in Berlin","Der Freund, mit dem ich gereist bin, wohnt in Berlin"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Der Freund, mit dem ich gereist bin, lebt in Berlin","Der Freund mit dem ich gereist bin wohnt in Berlin","Der Freund, mit dem ich gereist bin, wohnt in Berlin","Der Freund, mit welchem ich gereist bin, wohnt in Berlin.","Der Freund, mit welchem ich gereist bin, lebt in Berlin.","Der Freund, mit dem ich reiste, wohnt in Berlin.","Der Freund, mit dem ich reiste, lebt in Berlin."]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"55eb7244-578c-4dea-b5ec-ff02e9fa4cc1","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-1005-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"事務所","correct_answer":"事務所","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":"Office","card_id":"aabbccdd-6666-1005-c003-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"泳ぐ","correct_answer":"泳ぐ","accepted_answers":["およぐ"],"hint_text":"To swim","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"567a6b8a-5cf9-4fef-96b7-47bf060f2dfd","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-2003-0006-a20000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"씨다"},"after":{"prompt":"씻다"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"56c8aaaf-a6f6-4801-a9f6-474c758cd41a","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":["바쁘시면 내일 전화하세요","바쁘면 내일 전화해 주세요","바쁘시면 내일 전화해 주세요"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["바쁘시면 내일 전화하세요","바쁘면 내일 전화해 주세요","바쁘시면 내일 전화해 주세요","바쁘시면 내일 저에게 전화하세요","바쁘면 내일 제게 전화하세요","바쁘시면 내일 저에게 전화해 주세요"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"57ec9d2c-06e6-4243-84ad-a44d4ff322d8","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-1005-0004-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"Читать","correct_answer":"To read","options":["Cold","Winter","Teacher","To read"],"distractors":["Teacher","Cold","Winter"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-9999-1005-c004-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Идёт дождь.","correct_answer":"It is raining.","options":["It is cold.","It is hot.","It is snowing.","It is raining."],"distractors":["It is cold.","It is hot.","It is snowing."],"card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"58c2b6c7-7ff1-48b5-9150-7d33f44937ec","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["じょうけんけい"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"59b513f8-37c2-42ab-ac62-906c4bf7ce31","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":"听不 + 清楚 (qīngchu) = cannot hear clearly."},"after":{"accepted_answers":["清"],"hint_text":"Complete the potential complement meaning cannot hear clearly: 听不…"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"59da1c6a-0312-4b5c-82d1-c61790add219","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","prompt":"Le nouveau pont ___ inauguré par la maire la semaine prochaine.","explanation":"In the passive, tense is carried entirely by « être »: sera inauguré is the future passive (« va être inauguré » also works). « La semaine prochaine » rules out any past or present form."},"after":{"prompt":"Use a future passive form (futur simple or futur proche): Le nouveau pont ___ inauguré par la maire la semaine prochaine.","explanation":"The futur simple passive is sera inauguré; the futur proche is va être inauguré. The prompt specifically requests one of these future forms. A present tense can refer to a scheduled future event in French, so la semaine prochaine alone does not ban every present form."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"5b05cf07-d376-4371-96b3-614927cdefdb","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","explanation":"In «para as crianças comerem», the personal infinitive marks its own subject («as crianças») with the ending -em — a purpose-clause structure unique to Portuguese."},"after":{"explanation":"In «para as crianças comerem», the personal infinitive marks its own subject («as crianças») with the ending -em."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"5e83c046-b3ab-4a3d-9435-0ab7ac6cbbb5","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"Escultura","correct_answer":"Sculpture","options":["Plot twist","Sculpture","Genre","Inspiration"],"distractors":["Inspiration","Plot twist","Genre"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-5555-4004-c004-b20000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"O andamento acelera.","correct_answer":"The music gets faster.","options":["The music gets quieter.","The music starts again.","The music gets faster.","The music gets slower."],"distractors":["The music gets quieter.","The music starts again.","The music gets slower."],"card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"5efe7098-50fc-4dfc-97c4-d868840a1bbc","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4006-0003-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","hint_text":"A finished past event needs the compound passive."},"after":{"hint_text":"Among these choices, select the past passive; its participles agree with feminine plural scarpe."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"5f44217a-f420-4f10-9956-809d0630e997","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0005-b20000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["Morality","Ethics","Freedom","Doubt"],"distractors":["Doubt","Freedom","Morality"]},"after":{"options":["Wealth","Ethics","Freedom","Doubt"],"distractors":["Doubt","Freedom","Wealth"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"6029cb32-52ab-4090-920d-7bd83efddde8","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":["安かったら、買います","安かったら買います。","安かったら買います","やすかったら、かいます。","やすかったらかいます","安ければ、買います。","安ければ買います","やすければかいます","安いなら買います","安かったら買う","安ければ買う","やすければかう"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["安かったら、買います","安かったら買います。","安かったら買います","やすかったら、かいます。","やすかったらかいます","安ければ、買います。","安ければ買います","やすければかいます","安いなら買います","安かったら買う","安ければ買う","やすければかう","安いなら買う"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"604e173b-998e-49ad-8d26-8c254f17b2a8","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0001-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","explanation":"なら takes up the other person's statement (\"if it's Kyoto you're going to…\") and lets the speaker comment before the trip happens. と, ば, and たら would make the advice hinge on the trip already taking place."},"after":{"explanation":"行くなら takes up the other speaker’s stated plan and introduces advice about it. Here the reply recommends autumn before the trip is arranged. The uses of と, ば and たら differ with the predicates and context; they do not all require a trip already to have happened."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"612a6a30-614f-4b55-b628-51b52fe15d4f","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4006-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":["공부를 열심히 했는데도 시험이 어려웠어요","열심히 공부를 했는데도 시험이 어려웠어요"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["공부를 열심히 했는데도 시험이 어려웠어요","열심히 공부를 했는데도 시험이 어려웠어요","열심히 공부했는데도 시험은 어려웠어요"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"626f79e9-1320-45e4-918d-ab034fd6c658","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4006-0005-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","explanation":"« Où » is the relative pronoun for place: le quartier où j'ai grandi. English speakers often write « que » here because 'the neighborhood that I grew up in' uses 'that'.","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"explanation":"Où introduces the place where the speaker grew up. Dans lequel is also grammatical with masculine singular quartier. A bare que does not express the required location relation here.","accepted_answers":["dans lequel"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"62a58e0d-88a1-42e8-a05f-376048ce1edc","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":["Ela disse que vivia no Porto.","Disse que morava no Porto.","Disse que vivia no Porto.","Ela disse que ela morava no Porto."]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Ela disse que vivia no Porto.","Disse que morava no Porto.","Disse que vivia no Porto.","Ela disse que ela morava no Porto.","Ela disse que ela vivia no Porto."]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"62cfed6e-b129-4f95-9deb-3d3c728a2151","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-2004-0003-a20000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"慰概","correct_answer":"慰概"},"after":{"prompt":"慷慨","correct_answer":"慷慨"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"63072253-50e0-45b2-b0b2-7f850521ab6e","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_transformation","accepted_answers":["Se construyó este puente en 1990"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Se construyó este puente en 1990","En 1990 se construyó este puente","Se construyó en 1990 este puente"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"6310f463-98f4-4887-be8e-192d8a9f9deb","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4006-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":["听得清楚","我听得清楚。","听得清楚。","我听得很清楚","我听得很清楚。"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["听得清楚","我听得清楚。","听得清楚。","我听得很清楚","我听得很清楚。","我听得清","我能听得清楚","你的话我听得清楚","我听你的话听得清楚"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"64b53f94-16d3-42e1-bb62-2c15c070329e","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"error_correction","hint_text":"Two verbs must shift to Konjunktiv I.","explanation":"Reported speech continues across coordinated clauses: both verbs shift to Konjunktiv I — ist becomes sei and arbeitet becomes arbeite. Leaving them indicative would present the claim as the narrator's own fact.","metadata":{"error_sentence":"Die Nachbarin erzählte, ihr Sohn ist jetzt in Kanada und arbeitet dort als Koch."}},"after":{"hint_text":"Rewrite both verbs in Konjunktiv I for the formal reported-speech style practised here.","explanation":"In this formal reported-speech exercise, change ist to sei and arbeitet to arbeite across the coordinated clauses. Indicative reported speech is possible in other registers; the task specifically practises Konjunktiv I.","metadata":{"error_sentence":"Die Nachbarin erzählte, ihr Sohn ist jetzt in Kanada und arbeitet dort als Koch.","correction_instruction":"Rewrite the report in formal German using Konjunktiv I for both reported verbs. Keep the rest of the meaning unchanged."}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"6514286f-d1da-42b3-bd49-b77a264161dd","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-0001-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"더운","correct_answer":"더운","hint_text":"Hot","card_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-c007-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"엔지니어","correct_answer":"엔지니어","hint_text":"Engineer","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"67ec7712-2f18-4954-9f7d-a5726f839bd1","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-3007-0002-b10000000000","type":"listening_type","hint_text":"Would"},"after":{"hint_text":"Would do / would make"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"68edf821-d23c-46fb-b7c9-8abf2344f8f9","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4006-0003-b20000000000","type":"word_form","explanation":"Past passive of arrestare in the passato prossimo: è stato arrestato. With a recent time expression like ieri sera, avoid the passato remoto (fu/venne arrestato), which is reserved for the distant, narrative past.","prompt":"Il ladro ___ (arrestare) dalla polizia ieri sera."},"after":{"explanation":"The explicitly requested passato prossimo passive is è stato arrestato. Passato remoto forms such as fu arrestato are not excluded merely by ieri sera: aspect, discourse and regional usage influence that choice. They are outside the tense specified by this drill.","prompt":"Complete with the passato prossimo passive of arrestare: Il ladro ___ dalla polizia ieri sera."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"6a585e3c-8449-4677-b65e-9f97c84300d8","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"word_form","accepted_answers":["おいでになります","来られます","こられます","お見えになります","おみえになります","見えます","みえます"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["おいでになります","来られます","こられます","お見えになります","おみえになります","見えます","みえます","お越しになります","おこしになります"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"6a67d025-99b5-4871-9c67-3a1ee40d0282","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Escultura","correct_answer":"Escultura","hint_text":"Sculpture","card_id":"aabbccdd-5555-4004-c004-b20000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"O andamento acelera.","correct_answer":"O andamento acelera.","hint_text":"The music gets faster.","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"6cf4a965-6f49-4737-b3d2-420417326894","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-1005-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"夏","correct_answer":"夏","hint_text":"Summer","card_id":"aabbccdd-6666-1005-c009-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"ギター","correct_answer":"ギター","hint_text":"Guitar","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"6d2e4ef1-31c5-47f8-ac0c-70677799d422","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-3005-0005-b10000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["To upload","To download","Website","Screen"],"distractors":["Website","Screen","To upload"]},"after":{"options":["To delete","To download","Website","Screen"],"distractors":["Website","Screen","To delete"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"6d4f156a-1de9-4df8-9ebe-2c1b5eb5887a","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4006-0005-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","explanation":"Both halves of an unreal conditional carry «бы»: «Если бы я знал…, я БЫ сказал…». The particle usually stands before or right after the verb, and always combines with the past-tense form."},"after":{"explanation":"In this finite unreal conditional, both clauses use «бы»: «Если бы я знал…, я бы сказал…». Here it combines with the past-form verb «сказал» and may stand before or after it. Other constructions allow бы with an infinitive, as in «мне бы отдохнуть»."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"6d568516-5cb6-4c8c-bd2e-6d4cb1bbc8f9","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0003-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","explanation":"遊ばせた is the causative of 遊ぶ: \"let/made someone play.\" With an intransitive verb the causee takes を: 子どもを遊ばせた. Only one kana separates it from passive 遊ばれた — a completely different meaning."},"after":{"explanation":"遊ばせた is the causative of 遊ぶ: someone caused or allowed the child to play. In this sentence 子どもを marks the child. Intransitive causatives can also use に in suitable contexts; を is not an absolute rule. Passive 遊ばれた has a different meaning."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"71f32edc-87e3-43e2-95f4-fc9a66cbd013","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["いっち"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"723dd777-a4ba-4628-bf1e-daeca66f5d29","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4006-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_transformation","prompt":"Put into reported speech: Paul a dit : « Je peux t'aider. »","hint_text":"Shift the pronouns and backshift the present tense.","explanation":"« Je » becomes « il », « te » becomes « me », and the present « peux » backshifts to the imparfait « pouvait ». Every deictic element must shift to the reporter's point of view."},"after":{"prompt":"Paul said to you: « Je peux t’aider. » Report his words as yourself, beginning « Paul a dit », and backshift peux to the imparfait.","hint_text":"Paul is il; you are the person offered help, so t’aider becomes m’aider. Use pouvait.","explanation":"Paul becomes il, and his original addressee is now the reporter, so t’aider becomes m’aider. The requested present-to-imparfait backshift gives pouvait. These pronoun and tense choices follow the stated reporting situation, not an automatic shift of every deictic word."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"72a391f7-664f-4823-aef3-22991cb52721","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0001-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"Heiß","correct_answer":"Hot","options":["To cook","Hot","Winter","Teacher"],"distractors":["To cook","Teacher","Winter"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-c007-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Koch","correct_answer":"Cook","options":["Teacher","Cook","Doctor","Driver"],"distractors":["Teacher","Doctor","Driver"],"card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"73863ade-b4b2-4209-9ea2-9b1f8dfe7029","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1004-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"시간","correct_answer":"Time","options":["To pay","Time","Money","Shirt"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1004-c009-000000000000","distractors":["Money","To pay","Shirt"]},"after":{"prompt":"원피스","correct_answer":"Dress","options":["Shirt","Dress","Shoes","Coat"],"card_id":null,"distractors":["Shirt","Shoes","Coat"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"7474a84b-072a-4fd4-8067-17f70b8f106c","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Scultura","correct_answer":"Scultura","hint_text":"Sculpture","card_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4004-c004-b20000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Il tempo diventa più rapido.","correct_answer":"Il tempo diventa più rapido.","hint_text":"The music gets faster.","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"76a2ef37-b8be-4300-88d2-5a7c8d86ffb0","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4006-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":["친구는 요즘 바쁘다고 했어요","친구가 요즘 바쁘다고 말했어요","친구는 요즘 바쁘다고 말했어요"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["친구는 요즘 바쁘다고 했어요","친구가 요즘 바쁘다고 말했어요","친구는 요즘 바쁘다고 말했어요","제 친구가 요즘 바쁘다고 했어요","제 친구는 요즘 바쁘다고 했어요"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"779b132b-d860-4820-89fd-3b1e076c513f","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0001-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Heiß","correct_answer":"Heiß","hint_text":"Hot","card_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-c007-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Koch","correct_answer":"Koch","hint_text":"Cook","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"77a576b8-9ef1-462a-b29b-a2409625ed17","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-1007-0002-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["Bedroom","Bed","Table","Room"],"distractors":["Bedroom","Table","Bed"]},"after":{"options":["Window","Bed","Table","Room"],"distractors":["Window","Table","Bed"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"77d81200-95d6-48e9-a487-311eb7476492","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0002-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["かんせつわほう"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"78dfb4a4-7a08-4060-9544-309f8ddab966","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-1001-0002-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["Thank you","Please","Sorry","Good evening"],"distractors":["Excuse me","Please","Good evening"]},"after":{"options":["Good morning","Please","Sorry","Good evening"],"distractors":["Good morning","Please","Good evening"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"79242741-89b4-4a32-89e9-b8c25ea3ee8b","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0005-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["どうめいし"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"793dde56-07f2-42d7-85e0-6e047c280dc6","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0003-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","hint_text":"走らせる = causative of 走る; the causee of an intransitive verb takes を.","explanation":"走る is intransitive, so the people made to run take を: 私たちを走らせた. Coercive causatives prefer を; に would suggest permission. Passive 走られた — one kana away — would mean the coach was affected by our running."},"after":{"hint_text":"走らせる is the causative of 走る. Here 私たちを identifies the people the coach made run.","explanation":"コーチ is the causer, and 私たちを identifies the runners. The causative 走らせた supports “made us run” here. を is common in coercive intransitive causatives; に is also possible with suitable verbs and contexts. Passive 走られた would express being affected by someone’s running."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"7a878ed6-483d-41f6-84ac-21c58a85bfe3","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","hint_text":"Place words shift away from the speaker in reported speech.","explanation":"In reported speech, deictics shift away from the original speaker: qui → lì/là, and venire → andare. The present vengo also backshifts to the imperfect andava.","prompt":"Direct: 'Vengo qui ogni giorno.' → Ha detto che andava ___ ogni giorno."},"after":{"hint_text":"Assume the report is made from a different place: change here to there.","explanation":"For the changed reporting location specified here, qui becomes lì or là, alongside andava. Place words and venire/andare depend on the reporter’s perspective; they do not change automatically when that perspective stays the same.","prompt":"Report from a different location (here becomes there): 'Vengo qui ogni giorno.' → Ha detto che andava ___ ogni giorno."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"7ae4a765-3936-4b2f-9e54-feb86f548b98","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"조각","correct_answer":"조각","hint_text":"Sculpture","card_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4004-c004-b20000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"선율","correct_answer":"선율","hint_text":"Melody","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"7bb6fdc5-fbb9-4ddf-bb63-841467cd3e2c","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4006-0001-b20000000000","type":"error_correction","hint_text":"A duration phrase cannot combine with a perfective verb.","explanation":"The duration phrase «весь день» is incompatible with the perfective «прочитал», which presents the action as one completed whole. Ongoing activity measured by time requires the imperfective «читал»."},"after":{"hint_text":"For reading as an activity throughout the day, use imperfective читал. A completed reading can instead be timed with за день.","explanation":"«Я весь день читал статьи» describes the reading activity throughout the day. To present completion within that time, «Я за день прочитал статьи» is also possible. This читать/прочитать contrast does not ban all perfective verbs with duration phrases: «проспал весь день» is grammatical."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"7c7a2d67-cdc9-4cd3-8d4f-601be6990d21","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4006-0003-b20000000000","type":"error_correction","metadata":{},"hint_text":"The reporting verb is in the past — check the tense that follows.","explanation":"After « elle a dit », the present must backshift to the imparfait: était. This concordance des temps is obligatory in French, unlike English where 'she said she is sick' can pass in speech."},"after":{"metadata":{"correction_instruction":"Rewrite from a past-time viewpoint, using the imparfait for her illness. Keep the reporting clause and the rest of the wording unchanged."},"hint_text":"Use était for the illness viewed at the time of her statement.","explanation":"The requested past-time viewpoint gives Elle a dit qu'elle était malade. The original present est can be grammatical if the report presents the illness as still current; this is a contextual tense rewrite, not a universal error."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"7d2d7162-98ea-4092-99e9-cef4421c43cc","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0006-b10000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["Dear Sir","Awesome","Cool","Sincerely"],"distractors":["Sincerely","Dear Sir","Awesome"]},"after":{"options":["Dear Sir","Boring","Cool","Sincerely"],"distractors":["Sincerely","Dear Sir","Boring"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"7df4d0ac-1150-41b5-b787-bc86b4375770","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-1004-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Время","correct_answer":"Время","hint_text":"Time","card_id":"aabbccdd-9999-1004-c009-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Юбка","correct_answer":"Юбка","hint_text":"Skirt","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"80792050-a4d0-4fa8-a05e-71803b74a711","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4006-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_transformation","explanation":"Ability tied to a result uses the potential complement, not 能: insert 不 between verb and result — 看不懂 = cannot (manage to) understand by reading."},"after":{"explanation":"This transformation specifically requests the potential complement: insert 不 between 看 and 懂 to form 看不懂. 能/不能 can combine with resultative predicates in other constructions; the source sentence is being rewritten, not declared universally ungrammatical."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"83011d99-b746-4600-8a41-758235a4f9f0","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","prompt":"«Falo português.» → Ela disse que ___ português.","hint_text":"Present → imperfeito after «disse que».","explanation":"The present indicative «falo» backshifts to the imperfeito «falava» when reported with a past verb: «Ela disse que falava português»."},"after":{"prompt":"Report from a past viewpoint using tense backshift to the imperfeito: «Falo português.» → Ela disse que ___ português.","hint_text":"For the requested backshift, falo becomes falava.","explanation":"With the past viewpoint explicitly requested here, «falo» becomes «falava». A present-tense report can also be appropriate when presenting a statement as still current; backshift is not obligatory in every context."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"8354ea71-79b9-4b0a-8310-94287c2bc289","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"error_correction","metadata":{},"hint_text":"She left AFTER finishing — the verbal adverb must be perfective.","explanation":"Imperfective «заканчивая» claims she went home while still finishing the work — a contradiction. A completed prior action requires the perfective verbal adverb «закончив»: first the work ended, then she left."},"after":{"metadata":{"correction_instruction":"She finished the work before leaving for home. Keep the rest of the sentence and replace заканчивая with the perfective verbal adverb of закончить."},"hint_text":"For completion before departure, use закончив.","explanation":"«Заканчивая» presents the finishing and departure as simultaneous, which can be possible in context. This task explicitly places completion before departure, so it requires «Закончив работу, она пошла домой»."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"8361c5a0-875c-440d-9524-7af8778535e6","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4006-0005-b20000000000","type":"sentence_transformation","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Ce film dont je te parlais passe au cinéma."]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"85e4c014-8d26-4b16-91ad-c325cf722ca3","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"Скульптура","correct_answer":"Sculpture","options":["Inspiration","Masterpiece","Sculpture","Protagonist"],"distractors":["Masterpiece","Protagonist","Inspiration"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-c004-b20000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Музыка звучит всё быстрее.","correct_answer":"The music gets faster.","options":["The music gets quieter.","The music starts again.","The music gets faster.","The music gets slower."],"distractors":["The music gets quieter.","The music starts again.","The music gets slower."],"card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"86070b23-f20a-4389-aadf-59869d7276b8","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"Büro","correct_answer":"Office","options":["Cold","Office","Hot","To cook"],"distractors":["To cook","Hot","Cold"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-c003-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Ich zeichne gern.","correct_answer":"I like drawing.","options":["I like reading.","I like cooking.","I like drawing.","I like swimming."],"distractors":["I like reading.","I like cooking.","I like swimming."],"card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"87a76e53-e4ee-406b-bcaa-6c858eb345fb","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-1004-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Hora","correct_answer":"Hora","hint_text":"Time","card_id":"aabbccdd-5555-1004-c009-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Saia","correct_answer":"Saia","hint_text":"Skirt","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"89d3fdcb-7629-468e-9c7e-4346833dbfc7","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"error_correction","explanation":"Location phrases with 在 precede the verb: 在上海住过, not 住过在上海. English \"lived in Shanghai\" order cannot be copied into Chinese."},"after":{"explanation":"With 过 in this experiential sentence, put the setting 在上海 before 住过: 我以前在上海住过. This does not mean every 在 phrase must precede its verb; 住在上海 is grammatical in other constructions."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"8a170103-eb1e-4b7b-b30d-64b0967c2c7a","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4006-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_transformation","accepted_answers":["열심히 공부했다면 시험에 합격했을 거예요","열심히 공부했더라면 시험에 합격했을 텐데요","열심히 공부했다면 시험에 합격했을 텐데요"],"explanation":"Past counterfactuals need past marking on both clauses: 공부했더라면 (\"if I had studied\") and 합격했을 거예요 (\"would have passed\"). Plain 공부하면 ... 합격할 거예요 would be a real future condition instead."},"after":{"accepted_answers":["열심히 공부했더라면 시험에 합격했을 텐데요"],"explanation":"This task asks for -았/었더라면 and a past unreal result: 공부했더라면 ... 합격했을 거예요 or 합격했을 텐데요. Both studying and passing refer to the imagined past here. Other counterfactual contexts can have present results; past marking in both clauses is not a universal requirement."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"8ab4b38d-4667-4d6d-9ec5-dd5497e107bc","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"Skulptur","correct_answer":"Sculpture","options":["Review","Novel","Metaphor","Sculpture"],"distractors":["Metaphor","Novel","Review"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4004-c004-b20000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Das Tempo wird schneller.","correct_answer":"The music gets faster.","options":["The music gets quieter.","The music gets slower.","The music gets faster.","The music starts again."],"distractors":["The music gets quieter.","The music gets slower.","The music starts again."],"card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"8c60951b-ff5d-43a5-8970-40a861b97466","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Escultura","correct_answer":"Escultura","hint_text":"Sculpture","card_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4004-c004-b20000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Melodía","correct_answer":"Melodía","hint_text":"Melody","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"8ccf67d5-56f0-4392-b4bb-d961d86b09a8","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4005-0001-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","hint_text":"To pull someones leg"},"after":{"hint_text":"To pull someone's leg"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"8d52cb00-05e5-4aa5-886d-49db787a96f0","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3008-0003-b10000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["Formal","Sincerely","Regards","Dude"],"distractors":["Regards","Formal","Dude"]},"after":{"options":["Formal","Sincerely","Tomorrow","Dude"],"distractors":["Tomorrow","Formal","Dude"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"8e00b6ea-a1c9-4b1d-88d5-a82b72b09509","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-1005-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"Escritório","correct_answer":"Office","options":["Hot","Summer","Winter","Office"],"distractors":["Winter","Hot","Summer"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-5555-1005-c003-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Gosto de desenhar.","correct_answer":"I like drawing.","options":["I like cooking.","I like reading.","I like drawing.","I like swimming."],"distractors":["I like cooking.","I like reading.","I like swimming."],"card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"8e553f1e-d805-445c-9143-50c01637b6ec","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0002-b10000000000","type":"listening_choice","correct_answer":"Would","options":["Would","If","Suppose","Could"]},"after":{"correct_answer":"Would do / would make","options":["Would do / would make","If","Suppose","Could"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"8ea6a035-1ef6-4fff-b9b5-bafdf9eb1714","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4006-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_transformation","accepted_answers":["Dijo que no podía ir a la reunión"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Marta dijo que ella no podía ir a la reunión"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"8f9be607-4551-4f1d-980f-a1773a5b0a32","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3002-0001-b10000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["Manager","Interview","Meeting","Project"],"distractors":["Project","Meeting","Manager"]},"after":{"options":["Manager","Interview","Salary","Project"],"distractors":["Project","Salary","Manager"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"8ffef473-5ee8-4a41-ae31-4b98716f3cdd","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-1005-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"事務所","correct_answer":"Office","options":["Cold","Doctor","Friend","Office"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-6666-1005-c003-000000000000","distractors":["Doctor","Cold","Friend"]},"after":{"prompt":"泳ぐ","correct_answer":"To swim","options":["To read","To cook","To swim","To run"],"card_id":null,"distractors":["To read","To cook","To run"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"912bf229-6733-4dd8-8064-f20c9306f7bc","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4004-0003-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"絵画","correct_answer":"絵画","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":"Painting","card_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4004-c003-b20000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"観客","correct_answer":"観客","accepted_answers":["かんきゃく"],"hint_text":"Audience","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"914d3ab8-1af6-44d1-a2b0-d530816b3856","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4006-0002-b20000000000","type":"error_correction","explanation":"A 被-sentence must begin with the receiver: 我的钱包被小偷偷走了. The affected noun cannot appear after the verb as in English word order."},"after":{"explanation":"In this neutral passive, 我的钱包 is the affected subject and precedes 被: 我的钱包被小偷偷走了. A time or setting phrase could precede that subject in a longer sentence, so the receiver need not be the first words of every 被-sentence."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"916e57d6-a989-4667-b70a-8e047ae84a25","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Sculpture","correct_answer":"Sculpture","hint_text":"Sculpture","card_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-c004-b20000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Le tempo s’accélère.","correct_answer":"Le tempo s’accélère.","hint_text":"The music gets faster.","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"9278b88e-f774-4356-8c67-9454743c0fd1","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4006-0001-b20000000000","type":"sentence_transformation","correct_answer":"수진 씨가 머리가 아픈고 했어요","accepted_answers":["수진씨가 머리가 아프다고 했어요","수진 씨가 머리가 아프다고 말했어요","수진씨가 머리가 아프다고 말했어요"]},"after":{"correct_answer":"수진 씨가 머리가 아프다고 했어요","accepted_answers":[]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"938e8517-0e5b-491b-9583-7930c959fddb","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4006-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_transformation","accepted_answers":["Der Roman den ich gerade lese ist spannend"],"hint_text":"ihn (accusative masculine) becomes the relative pronoun den.","explanation":"The pronoun ihn shows that the relative pronoun must be accusative masculine: den. The relative clause follows its antecedent directly, with the verb lese at the clause end and commas on both sides."},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Der Roman den ich gerade lese ist spannend","Der Roman, welchen ich gerade lese, ist spannend."],"hint_text":"Use an accusative masculine relative pronoun: den or the more formal welchen.","explanation":"The role of ihn requires an accusative masculine relative pronoun: den or the more formal welchen. Place the relative clause after Der Roman, with lese at its end and a comma on each side."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"948b66ef-2a07-41b4-b115-4dfbb59f32c2","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4006-0003-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","explanation":"The source phrase 从书包里 precedes the verb, and the object follows verb + direction: 他从书包里拿出了一本词典. An indefinite object (一本词典) cannot move before the verb."},"after":{"explanation":"The neutral new-information order here is 他从书包里拿出了一本词典: source phrase before the verb, then the newly introduced dictionary. Other discourse contexts can use topicalized objects; they do not make the displayed rearrangements the neutral answer to this prompt."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"94eefc44-0f4d-4cbe-b071-84c47a9e8600","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-1005-0001-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"暑い","correct_answer":"暑い","hint_text":"Hot","card_id":"aabbccdd-6666-1005-c007-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"エンジニア","correct_answer":"エンジニア","hint_text":"Engineer","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"969d3e8c-d849-4f84-a3c0-828c49e45371","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["Goodbye","Yes","Excuse me","Sorry"],"distractors":["Yes","Goodbye","Sorry"]},"after":{"options":["Goodbye","Yes","Excuse me","Good morning"],"distractors":["Yes","Goodbye","Good morning"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"98142994-4e7c-4d8c-8c50-aed36238a406","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"Scultura","correct_answer":"Sculpture","options":["Protagonist","Sculpture","Novel","Painting"],"distractors":["Protagonist","Novel","Painting"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4004-c004-b20000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Il tempo diventa più rapido.","correct_answer":"The music gets faster.","options":["The music gets quieter.","The music gets slower.","The music gets faster.","The music starts again."],"distractors":["The music gets quieter.","The music gets slower.","The music starts again."],"card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"99b16ebd-bb92-429f-b704-2af79ac1a8be","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Büro","correct_answer":"Büro","hint_text":"Office","card_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-c003-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Ich zeichne gern.","correct_answer":"Ich zeichne gern.","hint_text":"I like drawing.","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"9b65f13b-9be0-4100-b01b-40a205adfee0","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"사무실","correct_answer":"Office","options":["Office","Doctor","Teacher","Friend"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-c003-000000000000","distractors":["Doctor","Friend","Teacher"]},"after":{"prompt":"수영하다","correct_answer":"To swim","options":["To swim","To run","To read","To cook"],"card_id":null,"distractors":["To run","To read","To cook"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"9d35e142-5c86-4688-9a7a-ca59bf0c1011","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4006-0005-b20000000000","type":"error_correction","hint_text":"Remove 很; put 多了 (or 得多) AFTER 冷 to say 'much colder'.","explanation":"很 can never modify the adjective in a 比-sentence. Degree of difference goes after the adjective: 冷多了 / 冷得多 = much colder.","metadata":{"error_sentence":"今天比昨天很冷。"},"accepted_answers":["今天比昨天冷多了。","今天比昨天冷得多","今天比昨天冷得多。"]},"after":{"hint_text":"Remove 很 before 冷 and express much colder after 冷 with 多了, 得多 or 很多.","explanation":"Use 今天比昨天冷多了, 冷得多 or 冷很多. The degree-of-difference expression follows 冷, unlike the erroneous 很冷 placement in the source.","metadata":{"error_sentence":"今天比昨天很冷。","correction_instruction":"Rewrite to say: Today is much colder than yesterday. Keep the comparison with 比 and express much colder after 冷."},"accepted_answers":["今天比昨天冷多了。","今天比昨天冷得多","今天比昨天冷得多。","今天比昨天冷很多"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"9dc545cf-e813-40f6-9a04-3683fc6db24b","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_transformation","accepted_answers":["私は母に部屋を掃除させられた","わたしはははにへやをそうじさせられた。","わたしはははにへやをそうじさせられた","私は母に部屋をそうじさせられた。","私は母に部屋をそうじさせられた"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["私は母に部屋を掃除させられた","わたしはははにへやをそうじさせられた。","わたしはははにへやをそうじさせられた","私は母に部屋をそうじさせられた。","私は母に部屋をそうじさせられた","私は部屋を母に掃除させられた"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"9de38852-2cf4-4a22-a1aa-4a1369b22138","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","explanation":"For elders and superiors, use honorific vocabulary: 연세 replaces 나이, and the verb takes -(으)세요. 나이가 몇 살이에요? is fine for peers, and 반말 forms like 몇 살이야? are only for close friends."},"after":{"explanation":"연세가 어떻게 되세요? uses honorific age vocabulary and an honorific polite verb, fitting the professor-directed question. Casual 몇 살이야? can be used where informal speech is appropriate, such as with close friends or children; it is not the respectful choice requested here."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"9de8e3aa-ba71-4f97-8a41-a9a66727f2db","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-1004-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"時間","correct_answer":"時間","hint_text":"Time","card_id":"aabbccdd-6666-1004-c009-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"ワンピース","correct_answer":"ワンピース","hint_text":"Dress","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"9f53a4f3-3da9-4c34-a28f-5af817cf0f06","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4006-0005-b20000000000","type":"word_form","explanation":"Russian has no special subjunctive conjugation: the unreal mood is always past tense + бы. So «if he were here» is «если бы он был здесь», with the ordinary past «был» of быть."},"after":{"explanation":"The finite conditional construction here uses the ordinary past-form verb with бы: «если бы он был здесь». The masculine form «был» agrees with «он»; no separate subjunctive ending is needed."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"9fdbe85c-2869-4074-9396-04029cb90e3f","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-1005-0004-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Ler","correct_answer":"Ler","hint_text":"To read","card_id":"aabbccdd-5555-1005-c004-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Está chovendo.","correct_answer":"Está chovendo.","hint_text":"It is raining.","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"a13b3c4d-8430-4dfd-945d-fc7db4c7c1bc","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0001-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"Caldo","correct_answer":"Hot","options":["To read","Office","Hot","Friend"],"distractors":["Friend","To read","Office"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-c007-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Cuoco","correct_answer":"Cook","options":["Teacher","Cook","Doctor","Driver"],"distractors":["Teacher","Doctor","Driver"],"card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"a4483806-ecaa-4bd3-b001-539f645247b1","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3008-0002-b10000000000","type":"listening_type","hint_text":"Dear Sir"},"after":{"hint_text":"Respected ... (before a name or title)"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"a492b0a6-9fae-454f-a924-1a90b7d41b51","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"word_form","hint_text":"Reflexive verbs form the verbal adverb with -вшись."},"after":{"hint_text":"For this perfective reflexive verb, вернуться, form the verbal adverb with -вшись."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"a7923058-050b-419b-b406-adac5165c18b","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","explanation":"了 reports a completed event (he went — possibly still there); 过 reports a detached past experience (he has been there at least once, and is not there now)."},"after":{"explanation":"去了 reports the going event; 去过 presents a prior experience of visiting. A completed earlier visit does not determine where the person is now: they could have returned for another visit."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"a7cabd31-1e6f-4ba6-b371-3b4a7b01d7ef","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-3007-0003-b10000000000","type":"listening_choice","correct_answer":"Instead","options":["Regret","Consequence","Instead","If"]},"after":{"correct_answer":"Instead of","options":["Regret","Consequence","Instead of","If"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"a8268c0a-0de3-4eec-980b-2debda139c9f","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1005-0004-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Leer","correct_answer":"Leer","hint_text":"To read","card_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1005-c004-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Lluvia","correct_answer":"Lluvia","hint_text":"Rain","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"a8507887-b7a8-4634-815f-763cbc40f167","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4006-0002-b20000000000","type":"error_correction","hint_text":"One of the two verbs is in the wrong mood after se.","explanation":"The conditional never follows se: se sarei must become se fossi (imperfect subjunctive). The conditional accetterei is correct in the main clause. Se sarei is a stigmatized error even for natives."},"after":{"hint_text":"In this hypothetical if-clause, change sarei to the imperfect subjunctive.","explanation":"Use se fossi in te for this hypothetical condition and retain accetterei in the main clause. This does not prohibit a conditional after se meaning whether in an indirect question."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"a8b07669-fa0d-4b3b-80b1-97f36bddfbfe","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4006-0002-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","explanation":"Arrival is expressed with при-: «приходит» = arrives. «Уходит» means leaves for good, «выходит» means exits or steps out, and «заходит» means drops in briefly — none of them matches «arrives at the office»."},"after":{"explanation":"Arrival is expressed with при-: «приходит» = arrives. «Уходит» means leaves, «выходит» means exits or steps out, and «заходит» means drops in briefly — none of them matches «arrives at the office»."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"a930f388-e507-40db-9289-1f57901e52fc","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4006-0003-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","explanation":"The relative pronoun takes its case from its role INSIDE the relative clause. Geben requires a dative recipient (ich gebe dem Mann das Buch), so masculine singular dative dem is correct. Dessen is genitive (whose), while denen and deren belong to plural antecedents — der Mann is singular."},"after":{"explanation":"Geben takes a dative recipient, so the masculine singular relative pronoun is dem. Dessen is genitive masculine/neuter singular; denen is dative plural; deren is genitive feminine singular or plural. None of those fits the masculine singular dative role here."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aa9841b6-5ede-436c-845c-7ee761c9786c","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-1004-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"時間","correct_answer":"Time","options":["Time","To pay","Money","Breakfast"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-6666-1004-c009-000000000000","distractors":["Breakfast","Money","To pay"]},"after":{"prompt":"ワンピース","correct_answer":"Dress","options":["Dress","Coat","Shirt","Shoes"],"card_id":null,"distractors":["Coat","Shirt","Shoes"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Chao","Chau","Hasta luego"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0001-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0001-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","options":["Good night","Goodbye","Good morning","Good evening"]},"after":{"options":["Good night","Goodbye","Good morning","Thank you"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0001-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Thanks"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Buen día"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Good evening"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0002-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["I am sorry","I’m sorry"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Buenas tardes"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Good evening"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0003-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Perdón","Disculpa","Disculpe"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0003-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Sorry","Pardon me","I beg your pardon"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0004-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Perdón","Con permiso"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0005-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0005-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Buenas noches\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Good night","options":["Good morning","Good night","Good evening","Goodbye"],"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read the short introduction: «Hola. Me llamo Ana. Mi amigo se llama Luis». Who is the speaker’s friend?","correct_answer":"Luis","options":["Ana","Marta","Luis","Pablo"],"explanation":"Me llamo Ana identifies the speaker. Mi amigo se llama Luis says that the speaker’s friend is named Luis.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0005-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Thanks"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["I am sorry","I’m sorry"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0006-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1001-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Hi"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1002-0004-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1002-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Tasty"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1002-0005-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1002-0005-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Leche\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Milk","options":["Rice","Chicken","Milk","Bread"],"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read the restaurant order. Cliente: «Quiero pescado con arroz y agua, por favor». Camarero: «Muy bien». Which order did the customer request?","correct_answer":"Fish, rice and water.","options":["Chicken, rice and water.","Fish, bread and water.","Fish, rice and coffee.","Fish, rice and water."],"explanation":"Pescado is fish, arroz is rice and agua is water. Quiero …, por favor is the customer’s request, not just a list of food vocabulary.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1002-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1002-0005-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","prompt":"Translate to Spanish: Coffee","correct_answer":"Café","accepted_answers":[],"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"At a restaurant, translate using Quiero and por favor: Chicken with rice and water, please.","correct_answer":"Quiero pollo con arroz y agua, por favor.","accepted_answers":["Quiero pollo con arroz y agua por favor.","Yo quiero pollo con arroz y agua, por favor.","Yo quiero pollo con arroz y agua por favor.","Por favor, quiero pollo con arroz y agua.","Por favor quiero pollo con arroz y agua.","Por favor, yo quiero pollo con arroz y agua.","Por favor yo quiero pollo con arroz y agua.","Quiero agua y pollo con arroz, por favor.","Quiero agua y pollo con arroz por favor.","Yo quiero agua y pollo con arroz, por favor.","Yo quiero agua y pollo con arroz por favor.","Por favor, quiero agua y pollo con arroz.","Por favor quiero agua y pollo con arroz.","Por favor, yo quiero agua y pollo con arroz.","Por favor yo quiero agua y pollo con arroz."],"explanation":"Quiero makes the request explicit; por favor adds please. Pollo con arroz is chicken with rice, and agua is water. The meal and drink may be listed in either order. Other request formulas are possible in Spanish; this task practises Quiero.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"Quiero + meal request + por favor"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1002-0005-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1002-0005-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Rico","Rica","Sabroso","Sabrosa","Exquisito","Exquisita"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1002-0006-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1002-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Carta"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1003-0001-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1003-0001-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Izquierda\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Left","options":["Station","Straight","Left","Bus"],"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read the directions. Visitor: «¿Dónde está la estación?» Local: «Sigue recto y gira a la izquierda». What should the visitor do after going straight?","correct_answer":"Turn left.","options":["Turn right.","Turn left.","Take a bus.","Wait at the bank."],"explanation":"Sigue recto means go straight; gira a la izquierda gives the next step, turn left. The question asks about the second action, not just the meaning of estación.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1003-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1003-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["A la derecha"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1003-0001-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1003-0001-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["ocar"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1003-0001-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1003-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Boleto","Pasaje"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1003-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1003-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Recto","Todo recto"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1003-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1003-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Bus","Ómnibus","Colectivo","Camión","Guagua","Autocar"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1003-0004-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1003-0004-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Autobús\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Bus","options":["Station","Ticket","Hospital","Bus"],"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"At the ticket office, a customer says: «Quiero dos billetes para Madrid, por favor». What does the customer request?","correct_answer":"Two tickets to Madrid.","options":["One ticket to Madrid.","Two tickets to Barcelona.","Two tickets to Madrid.","One ticket to Barcelona."],"explanation":"Dos billetes gives the quantity, two tickets; para Madrid gives the destination. Both details must match the request.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1003-0004-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1003-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Drugstore","Chemist’s"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1003-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1003-0005-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Boleto","Pasaje"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1003-0005-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1003-0005-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Botica"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1004-0001-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1004-0001-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Desayuno\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Breakfast","options":["Blue","Time","Shirt","Breakfast"],"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read Ana’s routine: «Todos los días desayuno a las siete y voy al trabajo a las ocho». What does Ana do at seven?","correct_answer":"She eats breakfast.","options":["She goes to work.","She eats lunch.","She goes to bed.","She eats breakfast."],"explanation":"Desayuno a las siete places breakfast at seven. Going to work happens at eight;