ith long hair.","Tall, with long hair.","Short, with short hair.","Tall, with short hair."],"explanation":"Alta describes her height, tall. Tiene el pelo corto says she has short hair; both features matter.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1006-0002-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1006-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Abuelita"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1006-0002-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1006-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Grandpa","Granddad","Grandad"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1006-0003-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1006-0003-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Hermana\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Sister","options":["Brother","Family","Daughter","Sister"],"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Read: «Mi hermana tiene doce años». How old is my sister?","correct_answer":"Twelve years old","options":["Twenty years old","Two years old","Twelve years old","Ten years old"],"explanation":"Doce means twelve. Tiene doce años states that she is twelve years old; Spanish uses tener to state age.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"tener + age + años"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-1006-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1006-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","prompt":"Translate to Spanish: Brother","correct_answer":"Hermano","accepted_answers":[],"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to Spanish using tener: I am twenty years old.","correct_answer":"Tengo veinte años.","accepted_answers":["Yo tengo veinte años.","Tengo 20 años.","Yo tengo 20 años."],"explanation":"Tengo veinte años expresses “I am twenty years old.” Yo 