he city.","This is the city's cheapest hotel.","In the city, this hotel is the cheapest.","In the city this hotel is the cheapest.","In the city, this is the cheapest hotel.","In the city this is the cheapest hotel.","In the city, this hotel is the least expensive.","In the city this hotel is the least expensive.","In the city, this is the least expensive hotel.","In the city this is the least expensive hotel."],"explanation":"El más barato de la ciudad identifies this hotel as the cheapest in the city, not merely cheaper than one other hotel.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"relative superlative with a location group"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-2007-0003-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-2007-0003-a20000000000","type":"fill_blank","prompt":"Más _____ (More expensive)","correct_answer":"caro","explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Complete “This is the most expensive of these three hotels” with más or menos: De estos tres hoteles, este es el ___ caro.","correct_answer":"más","explanation":"El más caro means “the most expensive”; el menos caro would mean “the least expensive.” The accent in más is part of the word.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"el más + adjective"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-2007-0003-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-2007-0003-a20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Más alta"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-2007-0003-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-2007-0003-a20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Más despacio","Más lentamente"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-1111-2007-0004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-2007-0004-a20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Más económico","Más económica"]}},{"table":"exer