istinguions les faits de nos interprétations.","metadata":{"tiles":["La","recherche","de","la","vérité","exige","que","nous","distinguions","les","faits","de","nos","interprétations."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4001-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4001-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Objectif","Finalité"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4001-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4001-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Awareness","Conscience"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4001-0002-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4001-0002-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Wisdom","correct_answer":"Sagesse","metadata":{"tiles":["Sagesse"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “Wisdom consists not only in knowing, but also in recognizing the limits of one’s knowledge.” Use ordinary subject-before-verb order in declarative clauses. Start with “La sagesse” and end with “ses connaissances.”.","correct_answer":"La sagesse ne consiste pas seulement à savoir, mais aussi à reconnaître les limites de ses connaissances.","metadata":{"tiles":["La","sagesse","ne","consiste","pas","seulement","à","savoir,","mais","aussi","à","reconnaître","les","limites","de","ses","connaissances."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4001-0003-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4001-0003-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["le"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4001-0003-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4001-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Belief","correct_answer":"Croyance","metadata":{"tiles":["Croyance"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “A belief can give meaning to life without constituting proof of what it asserts.” Use ordinary subject-before-verb order in declarative clauses. Start with “Une croyance” and end with “qu’elle affirme.”.","correct_answer":"Une croyance peut donner un sens à la vie sans constituer une preuve de ce qu’elle affirme.","metadata":{"tiles":["Une","croyance","peut","donner","un","sens","à","la","vie","sans","constituer","une","preuve","de","ce","qu’elle","affirme."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4001-0004-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4001-0004-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Conviction"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4001-0004-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4001-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Doubt","correct_answer":"Doute","metadata":{"tiles":["Doute"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “Doubt becomes useful when it drives us to examine the evidence rather than reject every new idea.” Use ordinary subject-before-verb order in declarative clauses. Start with “Le doute” and end with “idée nouvelle.”.","correct_answer":"Le doute devient utile lorsqu’il nous pousse à examiner les preuves plutôt qu’à rejeter toute idée nouvelle.","metadata":{"tiles":["Le","doute","devient","utile","lorsqu’il","nous","pousse","à","examiner","les","preuves","plutôt","qu’à","rejeter","toute","idée","nouvelle."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4001-0005-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4001-0005-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Freedom","correct_answer":"Liberté","metadata":{"tiles":["Liberté"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “Individual freedom cannot justify acts that threaten the safety of others.” Use ordinary subject-before-verb order in declarative clauses. Start with “La liberté” and end with “des autres.”.","correct_answer":"La liberté individuelle ne saurait justifier des actes qui menacent la sécurité des autres.","metadata":{"tiles":["La","liberté","individuelle","ne","saurait","justifier","des","actes","qui","menacent","la","sécurité","des","autres."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4001-0006-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4001-0006-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Justice","correct_answer":"Justice","metadata":{"tiles":["Justice"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “A society committed to justice must ensure that everyone can assert their rights.” Use ordinary subject-before-verb order in declarative clauses. Start with “Une société” and end with “ses droits.”.","correct_answer":"Une société attachée à la justice doit veiller à ce que chacun puisse faire valoir ses droits.","metadata":{"tiles":["Une","société","attachée","à","la","justice","doit","veiller","à","ce","que","chacun","puisse","faire","valoir","ses","droits."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Convaincre"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Proof"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0001-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0001-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Claim","correct_answer":"Affirmation","metadata":{"tiles":["Affirmation"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “This assertion remains questionable as long as it is not based on verifiable data.” Use ordinary subject-before-verb order in declarative clauses. Start with “Cette affirmation” and end with “données vérifiables.”.","correct_answer":"Cette affirmation reste contestable tant qu’elle ne s’appuie pas sur des données vérifiables.","metadata":{"tiles":["Cette","affirmation","reste","contestable","tant","qu’elle","ne","s’appuie","pas","sur","des","données","vérifiables."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0002-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0002-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Assertion"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0002-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0002-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Fallacy","correct_answer":"Sophisme","metadata":{"tiles":["Sophisme"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “This fallacy presents two possibilities as the only options, whereas other solutions exist.” Use ordinary subject-before-verb order in declarative clauses. Start with “Ce sophisme” and end with “solutions existent.”.","correct_answer":"Ce sophisme présente deux possibilités comme les seules options, alors que d’autres solutions existent.","metadata":{"tiles":["Ce","sophisme","présente","deux","possibilités","comme","les","seules","options,","alors","que","d’autres","solutions","existent."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Nevertheless"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0003-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Rhetoric","correct_answer":"Rhétorique","metadata":{"tiles":["Rhétorique"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “Convincing rhetoric does not relieve the speaker of the need to provide evidence in support of their thesis.” Use ordinary subject-before-verb order in declarative clauses. Start with “Une rhétorique” and end with “sa thèse.”.","correct_answer":"Une rhétorique convaincante ne dispense pas l’orateur de fournir des preuves à l’appui de sa thèse.","metadata":{"tiles":["Une","rhétorique","convaincante","ne","dispense","pas","l’orateur","de","fournir","des","preuves","à","l’appui","de","sa","thèse."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Toutefois","Néanmoins"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0004-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Nonetheless","However"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0004-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Bias","correct_answer":"Préjugé","metadata":{"tiles":["Préjugé"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “This reasoning is based on a prejudice, since it attributes the same behavior to all members of a group.” Use ordinary subject-before-verb order in declarative clauses. Start with “Ce raisonnement” and end with “d’un groupe.”.","correct_answer":"Ce raisonnement repose sur un préjugé, puisqu’il attribue le même comportement à tous les membres d’un groupe.","metadata":{"tiles":["Ce","raisonnement","repose","sur","un","préjugé,","puisqu’il","attribue","le","même","comportement","à","tous","les","membres","d’un","groupe."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0005-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","options":["To refute","Bias","However","Nevertheless"]},"after":{"options":["To refute","Bias","However","Therefore"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Cependant","Pourtant"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Moreover","In addition"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0005-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Biais","Partialité"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0005-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Argument","correct_answer":"Argument","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["Argument"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “To evaluate this argument, one should examine whether the conclusion really follows from the premises.” Use ordinary subject-before-verb order in declarative clauses. Start with “Pour évaluer” and end with “des prémisses.”.","correct_answer":"Pour évaluer cet argument, il convient d’examiner si la conclusion découle réellement des prémisses.","accepted_answers":["Pour évaluer cet argument, il convient d’examiner si réellement la conclusion découle des prémisses."],"metadata":{"tiles":["Pour","évaluer","cet","argument,","il","convient","d’examiner","si","la","conclusion","découle","réellement","des","prémisses."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0006-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0006-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","options":["Counterargument","Bias","Nevertheless","However"]},"after":{"options":["Counterargument","Bias","Nevertheless","Therefore"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["En outre"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0006-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4002-0006-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: To persuade","correct_answer":"Persuader","metadata":{"tiles":["Persuader"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “To persuade a skeptical audience, one must address its objections instead of ignoring them.” Use ordinary subject-before-verb order in declarative clauses. Start with “Pour persuader” and end with “les ignorer.”.","correct_answer":"Pour persuader un public sceptique, il faut répondre à ses objections au lieu de les ignorer.","metadata":{"tiles":["Pour","persuader","un","public","sceptique,","il","faut","répondre","à","ses","objections","au","lieu","de","les","ignorer."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4003-0001-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4003-0001-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["en place"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4003-0002-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4003-0002-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Procès-verbal"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4003-0002-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4003-0002-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: To delegate","correct_answer":"Déléguer","metadata":{"tiles":["Déléguer"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “Before presenting the schedule, I will specify which tasks we can delegate to an external team.” Use ordinary subject-before-verb order in declarative clauses. Start with “Avant de” and end with “équipe externe.”.","correct_answer":"Avant de présenter le calendrier, je préciserai quelles tâches nous pourrons déléguer à une équipe externe.","metadata":{"tiles":["Avant","de","présenter","le","calendrier,","je","préciserai","quelles","tâches","nous","pourrons","déléguer","à","une","équipe","externe."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4003-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4003-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Mettre en place"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4003-0003-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4003-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Efficiency","correct_answer":"Efficacité","metadata":{"tiles":["Efficacité"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “We could accept this compromise provided that the effectiveness of the service is not compromised.” Use ordinary subject-before-verb order in declarative clauses. Start with “Nous pourrions” and end with “pas compromise.”.","correct_answer":"Nous pourrions accepter ce compromis à condition que l’efficacité du service ne soit pas compromise.","metadata":{"tiles":["Nous","pourrions","accepter","ce","compromis","à","condition","que","l’efficacité","du","service","ne","soit","pas","compromise."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4003-0004-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4003-0004-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Efficience"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4003-0004-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4003-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Deadline","correct_answer":"Échéance","metadata":{"tiles":["Échéance"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “The report recommends postponing the deadline so that each team can check the results.” Use ordinary subject-before-verb order in declarative clauses. Start with “Le rapport” and end with “les résultats.”.","correct_answer":"Le rapport recommande de repousser l’échéance afin que chaque équipe puisse vérifier les résultats.","metadata":{"tiles":["Le","rapport","recommande","de","repousser","l’échéance","afin","que","chaque","équipe","puisse","vérifier","les","résultats."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4003-0005-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4003-0005-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Date limite"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4003-0005-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4003-0005-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Negotiation","correct_answer":"Négociation","metadata":{"tiles":["Négociation"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “During this professional gathering, I proposed continuing the negotiation after consulting my partners.” Use ordinary subject-before-verb order in declarative clauses. Start with “Lors de” and end with “mes partenaires.”.","correct_answer":"Lors de cette rencontre professionnelle, j’ai proposé de poursuivre la négociation après avoir consulté mes partenaires.","metadata":{"tiles":["Lors","de","cette","rencontre","professionnelle,","j’ai","proposé","de","poursuivre","la","négociation","après","avoir","consulté","mes","partenaires."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4003-0006-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4003-0006-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Proposal","correct_answer":"Proposition","metadata":{"tiles":["Proposition"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “This proposal offers a realistic solution, provided that the additional costs are covered.” Use ordinary subject-before-verb order in declarative clauses. Start with “Cette proposition” and end with “en charge.”.","correct_answer":"Cette proposition offre une solution réaliste, sous réserve que les coûts supplémentaires soient pris en charge.","metadata":{"tiles":["Cette","proposition","offre","une","solution","réaliste,","sous","réserve","que","les","coûts","supplémentaires","soient","pris","en","charge."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0001-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0001-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Personnage principal"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0001-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0001-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Plot twist","correct_answer":"Rebondissement","metadata":{"tiles":["Rebondissement"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “In this film, the final plot twist forces the viewer to reinterpret the images of the opening scene.” Use ordinary subject-before-verb order in declarative clauses. Start with “Dans ce” and end with “scène d’ouverture.”.","correct_answer":"Dans ce film, le dernier rebondissement oblige le spectateur à réinterpréter les images de la scène d’ouverture.","metadata":{"tiles":["Dans","ce","film,","le","dernier","rebondissement","oblige","le","spectateur","à","réinterpréter","les","images","de","la","scène","d’ouverture."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Tableau"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0002-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0002-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Coup de théâtre"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0002-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0002-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Review","correct_answer":"Critique","metadata":{"tiles":["Critique"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “This review highlights the richness of the style while regretting that the characters lack depth.” Use ordinary subject-before-verb order in declarative clauses. Start with “Cette critique” and end with “de profondeur.”.","correct_answer":"Cette critique souligne la richesse du style tout en regrettant que les personnages manquent de profondeur.","metadata":{"tiles":["Cette","critique","souligne","la","richesse","du","style","tout","en","regrettant","que","les","personnages","manquent","de","profondeur."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0002-e00000000010","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0002-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Chef-d''œuvre\" mean in English?"},"after":{"prompt":"What does \"Chef-d'œuvre\" mean in English?"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0003-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0003-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Compte rendu"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0003-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Masterpiece","correct_answer":"Chef-d'œuvre","metadata":{"tiles":["Chef-d'œuvre"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “Although the staging divides the audience, some consider this film a masterpiece.” Use ordinary subject-before-verb order in declarative clauses. Start with “Bien que” and end with “un chef-d’œuvre.”.","correct_answer":"Bien que la mise en scène divise le public, certains considèrent ce film comme un chef-d’œuvre.","metadata":{"tiles":["Bien","que","la","mise","en","scène","divise","le","public,","certains","considèrent","ce","film","comme","un","chef-d’œuvre."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0004-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Sculpture\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Sculpture","options":["Sculpture","Metaphor","Symbolism","Genre"],"distractors":[]},"after":{"prompt":"Read this concert review: « Dans le dernier passage, l’orchestre joue de moins en moins fort, tandis que la mélodie principale revient plusieurs fois. » What change in volume does the reviewer describe?","correct_answer":"The orchestra gradually plays more softly.","options":["The orchestra gradually plays more loudly.","The orchestra suddenly stops playing.","The orchestra maintains exactly the same volume.","The orchestra gradually plays more softly."],"distractors":["The orchestra gradually plays more loudly.","The orchestra suddenly stops playing.","The orchestra maintains exactly the same volume."]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0004-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Inspiration","correct_answer":"Inspiration","metadata":{"tiles":["Inspiration"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “The composer draws inspiration from traditional melodies, transforming their rhythms to create an original work.” Use ordinary subject-before-verb order in declarative clauses. Start with “Le compositeur” and end with “œuvre originale.”.","correct_answer":"Le compositeur puise son inspiration dans les mélodies traditionnelles, dont il transforme les rythmes pour créer une œuvre originale.","metadata":{"tiles":["Le","compositeur","puise","son","inspiration","dans","les","mélodies","traditionnelles,","dont","il","transforme","les","rythmes","pour","créer","une","œuvre","originale."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0004-e00000000010","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Roman\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Novel","options":["Novel","Protagonist","Poem","Inspiration"],"distractors":[]},"after":{"prompt":"Which change does « le tempo s’accélère » describe in a music review?","correct_answer":"The music gets faster.","options":["The music gets quieter.","The music gets slower.","The music gets faster.","The music starts again."],"distractors":["The music gets quieter.","The music gets slower.","The music starts again."]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0005-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0005-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Novel","correct_answer":"Roman","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["Roman"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “In my novel, I would like to alternate points of view so that the reader gradually discovers the characters’ motivations.” Use ordinary subject-before-verb order in declarative clauses. Start with “Dans mon” and end with “des personnages.”.","correct_answer":"Dans mon roman, je voudrais alterner les points de vue afin que le lecteur découvre progressivement les motivations des personnages.","accepted_answers":["Dans mon roman, je voudrais alterner les points de vue afin que progressivement le lecteur découvre les motivations des personnages."],"metadata":{"tiles":["Dans","mon","roman,","je","voudrais","alterner","les","points","de","vue","afin","que","le","lecteur","découvre","progressivement","les","motivations","des","personnages."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Main character"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0006-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0006-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Poem","correct_answer":"Poème","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["Poème"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “This poem evokes solitude through contrasting images, without ever directly naming the feeling it expresses.” Use ordinary subject-before-verb order in declarative clauses. Start with “Ce poème” and end with “qu’il exprime.”.","correct_answer":"Ce poème évoque la solitude au moyen d’images contrastées, sans jamais nommer directement le sentiment qu’il exprime.","accepted_answers":["Ce poème évoque la solitude au moyen d’images contrastées, sans jamais directement nommer le sentiment qu’il exprime."],"metadata":{"tiles":["Ce","poème","évoque","la","solitude","au","moyen","d’images","contrastées,","sans","jamais","nommer","directement","le","sentiment","qu’il","exprime."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4005-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4005-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Taper dans le mille"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4005-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4005-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["It's a piece of cake","It is a piece of cake"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4005-0001-e00000000010","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4005-0001-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Faire d''une pierre deux coups\" mean in English?"},"after":{"prompt":"What does \"Faire d'une pierre deux coups\" mean in English?"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4005-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4005-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Du gâteau"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4005-0003-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4005-0003-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"C''est du gâteau\" mean in English?"},"after":{"prompt":"What does \"C'est du gâteau\" mean in English?"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4005-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4005-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Coûter un bras"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4005-0004-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4005-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["To be over the moon"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4005-0004-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4005-0004-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["La balle est dans votre camp"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4005-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4005-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Être au septième ciel"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4005-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4005-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Very rarely"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4005-0006-e00000000010","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4005-0006-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"C''est du gâteau\" mean in English?"},"after":{"prompt":"What does \"C'est du gâteau\" mean in English?"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Tschüss"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0001-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Thanks"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0001-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0001-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["ldigen Sie"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0002-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Vielen Dank","Danke schön"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0002-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0002-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["digung"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0003-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Es tut mir leid","Tut mir leid"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0003-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Pardon me","Sorry","I'm sorry"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0004-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["You're welcome","You are welcome"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0004-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Entschuldigung","Entschuldige"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0005-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0005-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Gute Nacht\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Good night","options":["Please","No","Good night","Sorry"],"distractors":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read this short introduction:\nHallo! Ich heiße Lea. Ich komme aus Berlin.\n\nWhat is the writer’s name?","correct_answer":"Lea","options":["Marco","Anna","Lea","Lukas"],"distractors":["Marco","Anna","Lukas"],"hint_text":"Look for the phrase Ich heiße, which introduces a name.","explanation":"The writer says Ich heiße Lea: My name is Lea. Hallo is the greeting; the final sentence states where Lea is from.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0005-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Thanks"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0005-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0005-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["ldigen Sie"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0005-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0005-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Entschuldigen Sie\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Excuse me","options":["Good evening","Excuse me","Good night","Good morning"],"distractors":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read this short introduction:\nHallo! Ich heiße Lea. Ich komme aus Berlin.\n\nWhere is Lea from?","correct_answer":"Berlin","options":["Rome","Berlin","Paris","London"],"distractors":["Rome","Paris","London"],"hint_text":"Look for Ich komme aus, which introduces a place of origin.","explanation":"Ich komme aus Berlin means I come from Berlin. The passage names Berlin as Lea’s place of origin; it does not state an address or current location.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Vielen Dank","Danke schön"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0006-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0006-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["digung"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0006-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1001-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Hi"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1002-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1002-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Huhn"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1002-0004-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1002-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Tasty"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1002-0005-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1002-0005-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Milch\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Milk","options":["Milk","Fish","Chicken","Cheese"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"At a restaurant, you want fish with rice and a glass of water. Which sentence places that order politely?","correct_answer":"Ich möchte bitte Fisch mit Reis und ein Glas Wasser.","options":["Ich möchte bitte Hähnchen mit Reis und ein Glas Wasser.","Ich möchte bitte Fisch mit Reis und ein Glas Wasser.","Ich möchte bitte Fisch mit Brot und ein Glas Wasser.","Ich möchte bitte Fisch mit Reis und ein Glas Milch."],"hint_text":"Möchte expresses would like; bitte means please. Check both the food and the drink.","explanation":"Ich möchte bitte Fisch mit Reis und ein Glas Wasser means I would like fish with rice and a glass of water, please. The other orders change the fish, rice or water. This is one useful polite ordering pattern, not the only possible wording.","distractors":["Ich möchte bitte Hähnchen mit Reis und ein Glas Wasser.","Ich möchte bitte Fisch mit Brot und ein Glas Wasser.","Ich möchte bitte Fisch mit Reis und ein Glas Milch."],"skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1002-0005-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1002-0005-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","prompt":"Re_____ (Rice)","correct_answer":"is","hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Complete the restaurant request with möchte (would like) or habe (have): Ich ___ bitte Fisch mit Reis und ein Glas Wasser.","correct_answer":"möchte","hint_text":"The customer is asking to receive the meal, not stating what they already have.","explanation":"Ich möchte bitte Fisch mit Reis und ein Glas Wasser places an order. Of the two offered forms, möchte expresses the requested wish; habe states possession. The visible two-form instruction selects this ordering pattern without ruling out other polite requests in unrestricted conversation.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"polite_meal_request"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1002-0005-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1002-0005-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Fisch\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Fish","options":["Rice","Delicious","Bread","Fish"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"A customer says: Ich möchte bitte Hähnchen mit Reis und ein Glas Wasser. What does the customer order?","correct_answer":"Chicken with rice and a glass of water.","options":["Chicken with bread and a glass of water.","Fish with rice and a glass of water.","Chicken with rice and a glass of milk.","Chicken with rice and a glass of water."],"hint_text":"Hähnchen is chicken, Reis is rice and Wasser is water.","explanation":"The complete order is chicken with rice and a glass of water. Bitte makes the request polite; mit connects the chicken with its rice accompaniment, and und adds the drink.","distractors":["Chicken with bread and a glass of water.","Fish with rice and a glass of water.","Chicken with rice and a glass of milk."],"skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1002-0005-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1002-0005-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Köstlich"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1002-0006-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1002-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Karte"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1003-0001-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1003-0001-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Links\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Left","options":["Bank","Left","Airport","Right"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"You want someone to explain how to get to the railway station. Which question asks for those directions?","correct_answer":"Entschuldigung, wie komme ich zum Bahnhof?","options":["Entschuldigung, wie viel kostet die Fahrkarte?","Entschuldigung, wie komme ich zum Bahnhof?","Entschuldigung, wann fährt der nächste Zug?","Entschuldigung, ist das meine Fahrkarte?"],"hint_text":"Wie komme ich zu ...? asks how to get to a place. Zum combines zu and dem.","explanation":"Entschuldigung, wie komme ich zum Bahnhof? means Excuse me, how do I get to the railway station? The other questions ask the ticket price, the next train’s departure time and whether a ticket belongs to the speaker. They do not ask for a route.","distractors":["Entschuldigung, wie viel kostet die Fahrkarte?","Entschuldigung, wann fährt der nächste Zug?","Entschuldigung, ist das meine Fahrkarte?"],"skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1003-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1003-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Straight ahead"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1003-0001-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1003-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Ticket","Fahrschein"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1003-0001-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1003-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Train station","Railway station"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1003-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1003-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Gerade"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1003-0002-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1003-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Station","Haltestelle"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1003-0003-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1003-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Bench"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1003-0004-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1003-0004-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Bus\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Bus","options":["Bus","Train","Ticket","Station"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"At a ticket counter, you want one one-way ticket to Berlin. Which request matches?","correct_answer":"Eine einfache Fahrkarte nach Berlin, bitte.","options":["Eine Fahrkarte nach Berlin und zurück, bitte.","Zwei einfache Fahrkarten nach Berlin, bitte.","Eine einfache Fahrkarte nach Hamburg, bitte.","Eine einfache Fahrkarte nach Berlin, bitte."],"hint_text":"Eine einfache Fahrkarte is one ticket without a return journey. Nach introduces the destination.","explanation":"Eine einfache Fahrkarte nach Berlin, bitte requests one one-way ticket to Berlin. The other requests include a return journey, two tickets or a different destination. A noun phrase followed by bitte is a normal concise request at a ticket counter.","distractors":["Eine Fahrkarte nach Berlin und zurück, bitte.","Zwei einfache Fahrkarten nach Berlin, bitte.","Eine einfache Fahrkarte nach Hamburg, bitte."],"skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1003-0004-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1003-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Chemist's","Chemist"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1003-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1003-0005-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Ticket","Fahrschein"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1003-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1003-0005-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Train station","Railway station"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1003-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1003-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Station","Haltestelle"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1004-0001-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1004-0001-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Frühstück\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Breakfast","options":["Shoes","Shirt","Tomorrow","Breakfast"],"distractors":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read this sentence:\nLina frühstückt jeden Morgen zu Hause.\n\nWhich routine is described?","correct_answer":"Eating breakfast at home every morning.","options":["Eating breakfast at home every morning.","Eating dinner at home every evening.","Eating breakfast at a café every morning.","Eating breakfast at home only on Sundays."],"distractors":["Eating dinner at home every evening.","Eating breakfast at a café every morning.","Eating breakfast at home only on Sundays."],"hint_text":"Jeden Morgen means every morning; zu Hause means at home.","explanation":"Lina eats breakfast at home every morning. Frühstückt is the finite verb for eating breakfast, and jeden Morgen makes this a regular routine rather than a single meal.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1004-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1004-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Inexpensive"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1004-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1004-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Günstig","Preiswert"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1004-0002-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1004-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Pay"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1004-0004-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1004-0004-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Rot\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Red","options":["Red","Money","Breakfast","Shoes"],"distractors":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read this sentence:\nDer Laden öffnet morgens um neun Uhr.\n\nAt what time does the shop open?","correct_answer":"At 9 a.m.","options":["At 8 a.m.","At 9 p.m.","At 9 a.m.","At 10 a.m."],"distractors":["At 8 a.m.","At 9 p.m.","At 10 a.m."],"hint_text":"Neun is nine; morgens selects the morning, not the evening.","explanation":"The shop opens at 9 a.m. Um neun Uhr gives the clock time and morgens identifies the morning. Öffnet describes opening, not closing.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1004-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1004-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Pay"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Ärztin"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0001-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","prompt":"Translate to German: Soccer","correct_answer":"Fußball","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to German: waiter (a man who serves customers in a restaurant). Give a noun without an article.","correct_answer":"Kellner","accepted_answers":["Ober","Bedienung","Servicekraft","Servierer"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0001-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","prompt":"Translate to English: Heiß","correct_answer":"Hot","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to English: Koch (a person whose job is to prepare food). Give the noun without an article.","correct_answer":"Cook","accepted_answers":["Chef"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0001-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0001-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","prompt":"Ka_____ (Cold)","correct_answer":"lt","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null},"after":{"prompt":"Bäck_____ (Baker: enter the missing ending of the singular masculine or feminine noun.)","correct_answer":"er","accepted_answers":["erin"],"hint_text":"Both Bäcker and Bäckerin name a person who makes baked goods for a living."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0002-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0002-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Arzt\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Doctor","options":["Doctor","Friend","Hot","Teacher"],"distractors":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read this sentence:\nMorgen treffe ich Lea im Park.\n\nWhat plan is described?","correct_answer":"Meeting Lea in the park tomorrow.","options":["Meeting Lea at a café tomorrow.","Meeting Lea in the park today.","Staying at home tomorrow.","Meeting Lea in the park tomorrow."],"distractors":["Meeting Lea at a café tomorrow.","Meeting Lea in the park today.","Staying at home tomorrow."],"hint_text":"Morgen means tomorrow here; treffe ich Lea means I am meeting Lea.","explanation":"The speaker plans to meet Lea in the park tomorrow. German can use the present tense with a future time phrase for a planned meeting. Im Park identifies the agreed place.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Read"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0003-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0003-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Büro\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Office","options":["Doctor","Teacher","Cold","Office"],"distractors":[]},"after":{"prompt":"Read: „Im Sommer zeichne ich gern im Park.“ Which hobby does the speaker enjoy?","correct_answer":"Drawing","options":["Swimming","Cooking","Drawing","Reading"],"distractors":["Swimming","Cooking","Reading"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Cook"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0004-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Football"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0004-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0004-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["undin"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0005-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0005-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["rerin"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0006-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1005-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Freundin"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Papa"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0001-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Grandma"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0002-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0002-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Vater\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Father","options":["Cat","Father","Son","Grandfather"],"distractors":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read this sentence:\nMein Vater hat braune Augen und kurze Haare.\n\nWhich description matches the sentence?","correct_answer":"The father has brown eyes and short hair.","options":["The father has blue eyes and short hair.","The father has brown eyes and short hair.","The father has brown eyes and long hair.","The father has green eyes and long hair."],"distractors":["The father has blue eyes and short hair.","The father has brown eyes and long hair.","The father has green eyes and long hair."],"hint_text":"Braune Augen means brown eyes; kurze Haare means short hair.","explanation":"The speaker’s father has brown eyes and short hair. The adjectives describe eye colour and hair length, not a family relationship alone.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0002-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Oma"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0002-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Grandpa"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0003-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0003-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Schwester\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Sister","options":["Sister","Grandmother","Daughter","Brother"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"You are speaking directly to a child named Lea. Which question asks how old she is?","correct_answer":"Wie alt bist du?","options":["Wie heißt du?","Wann hast du Geburtstag?","Wie alt bist du?","Wo wohnst du?"],"hint_text":"To ask an age, use Wie alt ...?","explanation":"Wie alt bist du? asks the child’s age. Wie heißt du? asks her name; Wann hast du Geburtstag? asks the birthday date; Wo wohnst du? asks where she lives.","distractors":["Wie heißt du?","Wann hast du Geburtstag?","Wo wohnst du?"],"skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"age_expressions"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","prompt":"Translate to German: Brother","correct_answer":"Bruder","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to German: I am eight years old. Use Jahre alt and write the number as a word.","correct_answer":"Ich bin acht Jahre alt.","accepted_answers":["Acht Jahre alt bin ich."],"hint_text":"Use a present-tense form of sein with the age expression.","explanation":"Ich bin acht Jahre alt. German normally states age with sein: ich bin. Acht means eight; Jahre alt means years old.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"age_expressions"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","prompt":"Translate to English: Tochter","correct_answer":"Daughter","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to English: Lea ist acht Jahre alt.","correct_answer":"Lea is eight years old.","accepted_answers":["Lea is eight.","Lea's eight years old.","Lea's eight.","Lea is 8 years old.","Lea is 8.","Lea's 8 years old.","Lea's 8."],"hint_text":"Acht gives Lea’s age, not a calendar date.","explanation":"Lea is eight years old. The expression ist ... Jahre alt states how old someone is. The shorter English Lea is eight is also natural.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"age_expressions"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0003-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0003-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","prompt":"So_____ (Son)","correct_answer":"hn","hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Complete with the present-tense form of sein: Ben ___ zehn Jahre alt.","correct_answer":"ist","hint_text":"Ben is one person, like er.","explanation":"Ben ist zehn Jahre alt. Use ist with the third-person singular subject Ben. The sentence says that Ben is ten years old.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"age_expressions"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0003-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0003-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Großmutter\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Grandmother","options":["Grandmother","Father","Family","Cat"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Lea hat am dritten Mai Geburtstag. Ben hat am achten Juni Geburtstag. When is Ben’s birthday?","correct_answer":"On June 8.","options":["On May 3.","On June 8.","On June 3.","On May 8."],"hint_text":"Find Ben’s sentence. Juni is June, and achten refers to the eighth.","explanation":"Ben’s birthday is on June 8; Lea’s is on May 3. With a date after am, German uses the ordinal form: am achten Juni.","distractors":["On May 3.","On June 3.","On May 8."],"skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"birthday_dates"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0003-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","prompt":"Translate to German: Grandfather","correct_answer":"Großvater","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to German: My birthday is on June eighth. Use Geburtstag and write the date in words.","correct_answer":"Ich habe am achten Juni Geburtstag.","accepted_answers":["Am achten Juni habe ich Geburtstag.","Mein Geburtstag ist am achten Juni.","Am achten Juni ist mein Geburtstag.","Ich habe Geburtstag am achten Juni."],"hint_text":"You can use Ich habe ... Geburtstag or Mein Geburtstag ist ... .","explanation":"Ich habe am achten Juni Geburtstag and Mein Geburtstag ist am achten Juni both state the birthday date. Use am achten Juni for on June eighth.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"birthday_dates"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0005-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0005-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Tochter\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Daughter","options":["Brother","Sister","Daughter","Family"],"distractors":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read this sentence:\nJeden Sonntag koche ich mit meiner Tochter.\n\nWhich shared family activity is described?","correct_answer":"Cooking with the speaker’s daughter every Sunday.","options":["Cooking with the speaker’s daughter every Sunday.","Reading with the speaker’s daughter every Sunday.","Cooking with the speaker’s mother every Sunday.","Cooking with the speaker’s daughter every Friday."],"distractors":["Reading with the speaker’s daughter every Sunday.","Cooking with the speaker’s mother every Sunday.","Cooking with the speaker’s daughter every Friday."],"hint_text":"Koche means cook; mit meiner Tochter means with my daughter.","explanation":"The speaker cooks with their daughter every Sunday. Mit introduces the family member taking part, while jeden Sonntag gives the recurring day.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0005-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Grandma"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Oma"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Grandpa"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0006-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1006-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Mom","Mum"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1007-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1007-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Raum"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1007-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1007-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","prompt":"Translate to German: Bathroom","correct_answer":"Badezimmer"},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to German: spoon. Give the noun without an article.","correct_answer":"Löffel"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1007-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1007-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","prompt":"Translate to English: Schlafzimmer","correct_answer":"Bedroom","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to English: Teller (the item you eat from). Give the noun without an article.","correct_answer":"Plate","accepted_answers":["Dish"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1007-0003-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1007-0003-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","prompt":"Be_____ (Bed)","correct_answer":"tt"},"after":{"prompt":"Ga_____ (Fork: enter the missing ending of the singular noun.)","correct_answer":"bel"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1007-0005-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1007-0005-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Schlafzimmer\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Bedroom","options":["Door","Bedroom","House","Kitchen"],"distractors":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read this sentence:\nMein Haus hat zwei Schlafzimmer und einen Garten.\n\nWhich description matches the stated details?","correct_answer":"The home has two bedrooms and a garden.","options":["The home has one bedroom and a garden.","The home has two bedrooms but no garden.","The home has two bedrooms and a garden.","The home has three bedrooms and a garden."],"distractors":["The home has one bedroom and a garden.","The home has two bedrooms but no garden.","The home has three bedrooms and a garden."],"hint_text":"Zwei Schlafzimmer means two bedrooms; einen Garten means a garden.","explanation":"The home has two bedrooms and a garden. The sentence states both the number of bedrooms and the presence of a garden; the other offered descriptions change one of those facts.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1008-0001-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1008-0001-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["merzen"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1008-0002-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1008-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Medikament","Arznei","Arzneimittel"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1008-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1008-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Bauch"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1008-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1008-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Ill"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1008-0004-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1008-0004-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["ikament"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1008-0005-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1008-0005-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Krank\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Sick","options":["Fever","Pain","Head","Sick"],"distractors":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read this sentence:\nIch gehe jeden Tag spazieren.\n\nWhich habit does the speaker describe?","correct_answer":"Going for a walk every day.","options":["Going swimming every day.","Going for a walk once a week.","Drinking water every morning.","Going for a walk every day."],"distractors":["Going swimming every day.","Going for a walk once a week.","Drinking water every morning."],"hint_text":"Spazieren gehen means to go for a walk; jeden Tag means every day.","explanation":"The speaker goes for a walk every day. This sentence describes a recurring personal activity. It does not prescribe a medical treatment, duration or exercise target.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1008-0005-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1008-0005-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["merzen"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-1008-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-1008-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Medikament","Arznei","Arzneimittel"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0001-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0001-a20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Husband","correct_answer":"Ehemann","metadata":{"tiles":["Ehemann"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “My husband has two sisters.” Start with “Mein” and end with “Schwestern.”.","correct_answer":"Mein Ehemann hat zwei Schwestern.","metadata":{"tiles":["Mein","Ehemann","hat","zwei","Schwestern."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0002-a20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Kusine","Vetter"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0002-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0002-a20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Mann"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0002-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0002-a20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Wife","correct_answer":"Ehefrau","metadata":{"tiles":["Ehefrau"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “His wife is my best friend.” Start with “Seine” and end with “Freundin.”.","correct_answer":"Seine Ehefrau ist meine beste Freundin.","metadata":{"tiles":["Seine","Ehefrau","ist","meine","beste","Freundin."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0003-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0003-a20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Cousin\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Cousin","options":["Cousin","Nephew","Niece","Husband"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Lukas ist fünfundzwanzig Jahre alt. Sofia ist zweiundzwanzig. Which sentence correctly compares their ages?","correct_answer":"Lukas ist drei Jahre älter als Sofia.","options":["Lukas ist drei Jahre jünger als Sofia.","Lukas ist drei Jahre älter als Sofia.","Lukas und Sofia sind gleich alt.","Lukas ist zwei Jahre älter als Sofia."],"hint_text":"Älter means older; jünger means younger. Compare twenty-five with twenty-two.","explanation":"Lukas ist drei Jahre älter als Sofia. The difference is three years, and Lukas is older. German uses älter als to compare ages; drei Jahre states the difference.","distractors":["Lukas ist drei Jahre jünger als Sofia.","Lukas und Sofia sind gleich alt.","Lukas ist zwei Jahre älter als Sofia."],"skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"age_comparison"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0003-a20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","prompt":"Translate to German: Nephew","correct_answer":"Neffe","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to German: My brother is three years older than me. Use Bruder and älter; write three as a word.","correct_answer":"Mein Bruder ist drei Jahre älter als ich.","accepted_answers":["Mein Bruder ist um drei Jahre älter als ich.","Mein Bruder ist drei Jahre älter als ich bin.","Mein Bruder ist um drei Jahre älter als ich bin.","Drei Jahre älter als ich ist mein Bruder.","Um drei Jahre älter als ich ist mein Bruder.","Mein Bruder ist älter als ich, und zwar um drei Jahre."],"hint_text":"Use drei Jahre älter als ich. The comparison can also include um before the age difference.","explanation":"Mein Bruder ist drei Jahre älter als ich. The number describes an age difference, not the brother’s total age. Als ich is the shortened form of als ich bin; um drei Jahre is also possible.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"age_comparison"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0003-a20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","prompt":"Translate to English: Nichte","correct_answer":"Niece","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to English using turned: Lea ist gestern zweiundzwanzig geworden.","correct_answer":"Lea turned twenty-two yesterday.","accepted_answers":["Lea turned 22 yesterday.","Yesterday Lea turned twenty-two.","Yesterday, Lea turned twenty-two.","Yesterday Lea turned 22.","Yesterday, Lea turned 22.","Lea turned twenty-two years old yesterday.","Lea turned 22 years old yesterday.","Yesterday Lea turned twenty-two years old.","Yesterday, Lea turned twenty-two years old.","Yesterday Lea turned 22 years old.","Yesterday, Lea turned 22 years old."],"hint_text":"Ist ... geworden describes reaching the new age, and gestern means yesterday.","explanation":"Lea turned twenty-two yesterday. Here werden is a main verb meaning become; its perfect form is ist ... geworden. This is a birthday event, not merely a statement that Lea was already twenty-two.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"reaching_an_age"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0003-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0003-a20000000000","type":"fill_blank","prompt":"Ehe_____ (Husband)","correct_answer":"mann","hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Lukas ist fünfundzwanzig, Sofia zweiundzwanzig. Complete with the comparative form of alt: Lukas ist drei Jahre ___ als Sofia.","correct_answer":"älter","hint_text":"The comparative of alt changes a to ä and adds -er.","explanation":"Lukas ist drei Jahre älter als Sofia. Älter is the comparative of alt. The explicit ages select older, not younger, and the als frame calls for a comparative rather than a superlative.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"age_comparison"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0003-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0003-a20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Frau"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0003-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0003-a20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Boyfriend","correct_answer":"Freund","metadata":{"tiles":["Freund"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “My boyfriend is twenty years old.” Start with “Mein” and end with “alt.”.","correct_answer":"Mein Freund ist zwanzig Jahre alt.","metadata":{"tiles":["Mein","Freund","ist","zwanzig","Jahre","alt."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0003-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0003-a20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Freundin\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Girlfriend","options":["Niece","Uncle","Married","Girlfriend"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"You are chatting with a friend about the friend’s adult sister. Which question asks the sister’s age?","correct_answer":"Wie alt ist deine Schwester?","options":["Wie heißt deine Schwester?","Was macht deine Schwester beruflich?","Wann hat deine Schwester Geburtstag?","Wie alt ist deine Schwester?"],"hint_text":"The sister is a third-person subject, so the age question uses ist.","explanation":"Wie alt ist deine Schwester? asks her age. The other questions ask her name, occupation and birthday date. A birthday date is not the same information as an age.","distractors":["Wie heißt deine Schwester?","Was macht deine Schwester beruflich?","Wann hat deine Schwester Geburtstag?"],"skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"age_questions"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0003-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0003-a20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","prompt":"Translate to German: Neighbor","correct_answer":"Nachbar","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to German in the Perfekt: Yesterday I turned twenty-two. Use werden and write the age as a word.","correct_answer":"Gestern bin ich zweiundzwanzig geworden.","accepted_answers":["Ich bin gestern zweiundzwanzig geworden.","Gestern bin ich zweiundzwanzig Jahre alt geworden.","Ich bin gestern zweiundzwanzig Jahre alt geworden."],"hint_text":"Use bin ... geworden. With gestern first, bin comes before ich.","explanation":"Gestern bin ich zweiundzwanzig geworden. The requested perfect uses sein plus geworden for main-verb werden. Jahre alt may be included after the age number. This is not the passive participle worden.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"reaching_an_age"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0004-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0004-a20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Girlfriend","correct_answer":"Freundin","metadata":{"tiles":["Freundin"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “My girlfriend moved to Berlin last year.” Start with “Meine Freundin” and end with “Berlin gezogen.”.","correct_answer":"Meine Freundin ist letztes Jahr nach Berlin gezogen.","metadata":{"tiles":["Meine","Freundin","ist","letztes","Jahr","nach","Berlin","gezogen."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0005-a20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Mann"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0005-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0005-a20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Neighbor","correct_answer":"Nachbar","metadata":{"tiles":["Nachbar"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “Our neighbor visits his parents every Sunday.” Start with “Unser” and end with “Sonntag.”.","correct_answer":"Unser Nachbar besucht seine Eltern jeden Sonntag.","metadata":{"tiles":["Unser","Nachbar","besucht","seine","Eltern","jeden","Sonntag."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0006-a20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Frau"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0006-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0006-a20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Nachbarin"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0006-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2001-0006-a20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Wedding","correct_answer":"Hochzeit","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["Hochzeit"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “The wedding takes place next Saturday.” Start with “Die” and end with “statt.”.","correct_answer":"Die Hochzeit findet am nächsten Samstag statt.","accepted_answers":["Die Hochzeit am nächsten Samstag findet statt."],"metadata":{"tiles":["Die","Hochzeit","findet","am","nächsten","Samstag","statt."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2002-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2002-0001-a20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Kopfweh"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2002-0001-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2002-0001-a20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Nurse","correct_answer":"Krankenschwester","metadata":{"tiles":["Krankenschwester"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “The nurse asks me about my pain.” Start with “Die” and end with “Schmerzen.”.","correct_answer":"Die Krankenschwester fragt mich nach meinen Schmerzen.","metadata":{"tiles":["Die","Krankenschwester","fragt","mich","nach","meinen","Schmerzen."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2002-0002-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2002-0002-a20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Krankenpfleger","Pflegekraft","Pflegefachkraft"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2002-0002-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2002-0002-a20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Dentist","correct_answer":"Zahnarzt","metadata":{"tiles":["Zahnarzt"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “Tomorrow I have an appointment with the dentist.” Start with “Morgen” and end with “Zahnarzt.”.","correct_answer":"Morgen habe ich einen Termin beim Zahnarzt.","metadata":{"tiles":["Morgen","habe","ich","einen","Termin","beim","Zahnarzt."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2002-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2002-0003-a20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Verschreibung"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2002-0003-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2002-0003-a20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Zahnärztin"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2002-0003-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2002-0003-a20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Stress","correct_answer":"Stress","metadata":{"tiles":["Stress"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “At the pharmacy, I ask for help with stress.” Start with “In der” and end with “gegen Stress.”.","correct_answer":"In der Apotheke frage ich nach Hilfe gegen Stress.","metadata":{"tiles":["In","der","Apo