pt":"Für eine Nacht: Hotel A kostet 60 Euro, Hotel B 80 Euro und Hotel C 100 Euro. Which sentence identifies the cheapest of these three hotels?","correct_answer":"Hotel A ist am billigsten.","options":["Hotel B ist am billigsten.","Hotel A ist am teuersten.","Hotel C ist am billigsten.","Hotel A ist am billigsten."],"hint_text":"The cheapest hotel has the lowest price. Look for am billigsten.","explanation":"Hotel A has the lowest price, so it is am billigsten, the cheapest. Billiger compares prices; am billigsten identifies the minimum price in this set of three hotels.","distractors":["Hotel B ist am billigsten.","Hotel A ist am teuersten.","Hotel C ist am billigsten."],"skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"superlative_comparison"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2007-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2007-0003-a20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","prompt":"Translate to German: Worse","correct_answer":"Schlechter","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to German: Hotel A is the cheapest of the three hotels. Use billig and write three as a word.","correct_answer":"Hotel A ist das billigste der drei Hotels.","accepted_answers":["Von den drei Hotels ist Hotel A am billigsten.","Hotel A ist von den drei Hotels am billigsten.","Unter den drei Hotels ist Hotel A am billigsten.","Hotel A ist unter den drei Hotels am billigsten.","Hotel A ist das billigste von den drei Hotels.","Hotel A ist von den drei Hotels das billigste.","Von den drei Hotels ist Hotel A das billigste.","Unter den drei Hotels ist Hotel A das billigste.","Hotel A ist unter den drei Hotels das billigste."],"hint_text":"Use das billigste with an understood Hotel, or am billigsten in the predicate.","explanation":"Das billigste der drei Hotels means the cheapest of the three hotels. A predicate version is Von den drei Hotels ist Hotel A am billigsten. Both express a superlative, not merely cheaper than one other hotel.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"superlative_comparison"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2007-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2007-0003-a20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","prompt":"Translate to English: Billiger","correct_answer":"Cheaper","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"We are comparing three hotels. Translate to English: Hotel C ist das teuerste Hotel.","correct_answer":"Hotel C is the most expensive hotel.","accepted_answers":["Hotel C is the most expensive.","Hotel C is the priciest hotel.","Hotel C is the priciest.","Hotel C is the costliest hotel.","Hotel C is the costliest."],"hint_text":"Teuerste is a superlative, not the comparative teurer.","explanation":"Hotel C is the most expensive hotel in the comparison. The superlative teuerste expresses the highest price; more expensive would only express a comparative.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"superlative_comparison"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2007-0003-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2007-0003-a20000000000","type":"fill_blank","prompt":"Teu_____ (More expensive)","correct_answer":"rer","hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Complete with the superlative form of billig: Von den drei Hotels ist Hotel A am ___.","correct_answer":"billigsten","hint_text":"The predicate pattern is am + adjective ending in -sten.","explanation":"Von den drei Hotels ist Hotel A am billigsten. The supplied am takes billigsten here, not comparative billiger or attributive billigste.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"superlative_comparison"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2007-0003-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2007-0003-a20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Shorter","correct_answer":"Kleiner","metadata":{"tiles":["Kleiner"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “This apartment is smaller, but it has the biggest balcony.” Start with “Diese Wohnung” and end with “größten Balkon.”.","correct_answer":"Diese Wohnung ist kleiner, aber sie hat den größten Balkon.","metadata":{"tiles":["Diese","Wohnung","ist","kleiner,","aber","sie","hat","den","größten","Balkon."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2007-0003-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2007-0003-a20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Schneller\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Faster","options":["Smaller","Taller","Faster","Slower"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Zug A braucht 50 Minuten, Zug B 40 und Zug C 30. Alle fahren dieselbe Strecke. Which sentence names the slowest of the three trains?","correct_answer":"Zug A ist am langsamsten.","options":["Zug C ist am langsamsten.","Zug A ist am langsamsten.","Zug B ist am langsamsten.","Zug A ist am schnellsten."],"hint_text":"For the same route, the train taking the most time is the slowest.","explanation":"Zug A takes 50 minutes, the longest time for the same route, so it is am langsamsten. Zug C takes the least time and is am schnellsten.","distractors":["Zug C ist am langsamsten.","Zug B ist am langsamsten.","Zug A ist am schnellsten."],"skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"superlative_comparison"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2007-0003-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2007-0003-a20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","prompt":"Translate to German: Slower","correct_answer":"Langsamer","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to German: Of the three trains, train C is the fastest. Use Zug and schnell; write three as a word.","correct_answer":"Von den drei Zügen ist Zug C am schnellsten.","accepted_answers":["Zug C ist von den drei Zügen am schnellsten.","Unter den drei Zügen ist Zug C am schnellsten.","Zug C ist unter den drei Zügen am schnellsten.","Zug C ist der schnellste der drei Züge.","Zug C ist der schnellste von den drei Zügen.","Von den drei Zügen ist Zug C der schnellste.","Zug C ist von den drei Zügen der schnellste.","Unter den drei Zügen ist Zug C der schnellste.","Zug C ist unter den drei Zügen der schnellste."],"hint_text":"The predicate superlative is am schnellsten. After von den, the plural is Zügen.","explanation":"Von den drei Zügen ist Zug C am schnellsten. Der schnellste der drei Züge is also valid. The superlative identifies C as fastest within the stated three-train set.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"superlative_comparison"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2007-0004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2007-0004-a20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Günstiger","Preiswerter"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2007-0004-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2007-0004-a20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Kürzer"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2007-0004-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2007-0004-a20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Faster","correct_answer":"Schneller","metadata":{"tiles":["Schneller"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “The more expensive computer is faster and has a better screen.” Start with “Der teurere” and end with “besseren Bildschirm.”.","correct_answer":"Der teurere Computer ist schneller und hat einen besseren Bildschirm.","metadata":{"tiles":["Der","teurere","Computer","ist","schneller","und","hat","einen","besseren","Bildschirm."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2007-0005-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2007-0005-a20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Slower","correct_answer":"Langsamer","metadata":{"tiles":["Langsamer"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “I prefer to drive more slowly because I want to see the scenery.” Start with “Ich fahre” and end with “sehen möchte.”.","correct_answer":"Ich fahre lieber langsamer, weil ich die Landschaft sehen möchte.","metadata":{"tiles":["Ich","fahre","lieber","langsamer,","weil","ich","die","Landschaft","sehen","möchte."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2008-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2008-0001-a20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["New Year's Day"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2008-0001-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2008-0001-a20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Gift","correct_answer":"Geschenk","metadata":{"tiles":["Geschenk"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “At Christmas, my daughter gets a present from her grandmother.” Start with “Zu Weihnachten” and end with “ihrer Oma.”.","correct_answer":"Zu Weihnachten bekommt meine Tochter ein Geschenk von ihrer Oma.","metadata":{"tiles":["Zu","Weihnachten","bekommt","meine","Tochter","ein","Geschenk","von","ihrer","Oma."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2008-0002-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2008-0002-a20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Weihnachten\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Christmas","options":["Music","To celebrate","Christmas","Holiday"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Mia describes her family: „Zum Geburtstag backen wir immer einen Kuchen.“ What food do they traditionally prepare for birthdays?","correct_answer":"Cake","options":["Rice","Fish","Cake","Bread"],"hint_text":"Kuchen names the food; immer marks the recurring custom.","explanation":"They bake a cake for birthdays. The sentence describes Mia’s family custom, not a rule for every German-speaking family.","distractors":["Rice","Fish","Bread"],"skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"habitual_food_customs"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2008-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2008-0002-a20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","prompt":"Translate to German: New Year","correct_answer":"Neujahr","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"A speaker describes their family custom. Translate to German: On New Year’s Day, we always eat soup. Use an Neujahr, essen and Suppe.","correct_answer":"An Neujahr essen wir immer Suppe.","accepted_answers":["Wir essen an Neujahr immer Suppe.","Wir essen immer an Neujahr Suppe.","Wir essen immer Suppe an Neujahr.","An Neujahr essen wir immer eine Suppe.","Wir essen an Neujahr immer eine Suppe.","Wir essen immer an Neujahr eine Suppe.","Wir essen immer eine Suppe an Neujahr."],"hint_text":"When An Neujahr comes first, the finite verb essen comes before wir.","explanation":"An Neujahr essen wir immer Suppe states a recurring family meal. Immer means always. Wir essen an Neujahr immer Suppe is another natural word order.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"habitual_food_customs"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2008-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2008-0002-a20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","prompt":"Translate to English: Geburtstag","correct_answer":"Birthday","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to English: Wir essen jedes Jahr Geburtstagskuchen.","correct_answer":"We eat birthday cake every year.","accepted_answers":["Every year, we eat birthday cake.","We eat a birthday cake every year.","Every year, we eat a birthday cake.","We eat birthday cake each year.","Each year, we eat birthday cake.","We eat a birthday cake each year.","Each year, we eat a birthday cake.","Every year we eat birthday cake.","Every year we eat a birthday cake.","Each year we eat birthday cake.","Each year we eat a birthday cake."],"hint_text":"Jedes Jahr means every year; Geburtstagskuchen is birthday cake.","explanation":"We eat birthday cake every year. The present-tense statement and jedes Jahr describe a repeated custom, not one completed past meal.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"habitual_food_customs"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2008-0002-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2008-0002-a20000000000","type":"fill_blank","prompt":"Trad_____ (Tradition)","correct_answer":"ition","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Complete with a present-tense form of backen: Meine Oma ___ zu meinem Geburtstag einen Kuchen.","correct_answer":"backt","accepted_answers":["bäckt"],"hint_text":"Meine Oma is third-person singular. Both standard present-tense variants are accepted.","explanation":"Meine Oma backt zu meinem Geburtstag einen Kuchen. Bäckt is also a standard third-person singular form of backen. Both say that my grandmother bakes a cake for my birthday.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"habitual_food_customs"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2008-0002-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2008-0002-a20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Party","correct_answer":"Party","metadata":{"tiles":["Party"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “At our party, there is always my grandmother’s cake.” Start with “Bei unserer” and end with “meiner Oma.”.","correct_answer":"Bei unserer Party gibt es immer den Kuchen meiner Oma.","metadata":{"tiles":["Bei","unserer","Party","gibt","es","immer","den","Kuchen","meiner","Oma."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2008-0002-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2008-0002-a20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Feiern\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"To celebrate","options":["Costume","To celebrate","Festival","Dance"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Mia says: „An Neujahr kocht mein Vater Suppe. Meine Mutter backt Brot.“ Who makes the soup?","correct_answer":"Mia’s father","options":["Mia’s mother","Mia’s brother","Mia’s father","Mia’s grandmother"],"hint_text":"Match Suppe with the person named in the same sentence.","explanation":"Mia’s father cooks the soup; her mother bakes bread. These roles belong to this particular family account, not a cultural rule about who cooks.","distractors":["Mia’s mother","Mia’s brother","Mia’s grandmother"],"skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"habitual_food_customs"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2008-0002-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2008-0002-a20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","prompt":"Translate to German: Music","correct_answer":"Musik","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to German: My grandmother always bakes a cake for my birthday. Use meine Oma, backen, Kuchen and zu meinem Geburtstag.","correct_answer":"Meine Oma backt zu meinem Geburtstag immer einen Kuchen.","accepted_answers":["Meine Oma bäckt zu meinem Geburtstag immer einen Kuchen.","Meine Oma backt immer zu meinem Geburtstag einen Kuchen.","Meine Oma bäckt immer zu meinem Geburtstag einen Kuchen.","Meine Oma backt immer einen Kuchen zu meinem Geburtstag.","Meine Oma bäckt immer einen Kuchen zu meinem Geburtstag.","Zu meinem Geburtstag backt meine Oma immer einen Kuchen.","Zu meinem Geburtstag bäckt meine Oma immer einen Kuchen.","Immer backt meine Oma zu meinem Geburtstag einen Kuchen.","Immer bäckt meine Oma zu meinem Geburtstag einen Kuchen."],"hint_text":"State the person, recurring action, occasion and food. Backt and bäckt are both accepted.","explanation":"Meine Oma backt zu meinem Geburtstag immer einen Kuchen describes a personal family custom. The occasion can also be fronted: Zu meinem Geburtstag backt meine Oma immer einen Kuchen. Bäckt is another standard form.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"habitual_food_customs"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2008-0003-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2008-0003-a20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Feier"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2008-0003-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2008-0003-a20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: To celebrate","correct_answer":"Feiern","metadata":{"tiles":["Feiern"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “We celebrate the festival with music and traditional dances.” Start with “Wir feiern” and end with “traditionellen Tänzen.”.","correct_answer":"Wir feiern das Fest mit Musik und traditionellen Tänzen.","metadata":{"tiles":["Wir","feiern","das","Fest","mit","Musik","und","traditionellen","Tänzen."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2008-0004-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2008-0004-a20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Present"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-2008-0004-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-2008-0004-a2000