look for the missing house.” Start with “Zuerst fanden” and end with “zu suchen.”.","correct_answer":"Zuerst fanden wir eine alte Karte, und dann begannen wir, nach dem verschwundenen Haus zu suchen.","metadata":{"tiles":["Zuerst","fanden","wir","eine","alte","Karte,","und","dann","begannen","wir,","nach","dem","verschwundenen","Haus","zu","suchen."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0002-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Auf einmal"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0002-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["During"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0002-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0002-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Danach","Als Nächstes"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0002-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0002-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Finally","correct_answer":"Schließlich","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["Schließlich"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “We looked for the way for several hours and finally reached the village before it became dark.” Start with “Wir suchten” and end with “dunkel wurde.”.","correct_answer":"Wir suchten mehrere Stunden nach dem Weg und erreichten schließlich das Dorf, bevor es dunkel wurde.","accepted_answers":["Wir suchten nach dem Weg mehrere Stunden und erreichten schließlich das Dorf, bevor es dunkel wurde."],"metadata":{"tiles":["Wir","suchten","mehrere","Stunden","nach","dem","Weg","und","erreichten","schließlich","das","Dorf,","bevor","es","dunkel","wurde."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0003-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0003-b10000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Plötzlich\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Suddenly","options":["Next","Finally","Suddenly","Meanwhile"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Gestern Abend las Lea gerade ein Buch, als das Telefon klingelte. What was in progress when the phone rang?","correct_answer":"She was reading a book.","options":["She was reading a book.","She had finished the book.","She was cooking a meal.","She had not started reading."],"hint_text":"Las is the past form of lesen. Gerade marks the reading as in progress at that moment.","explanation":"Lea was reading a book. The ringing occurs during the reading; the sentence does not say that she had finished the book. German can express an ongoing past scene with a simple past form plus context or an adverb such as gerade.","distractors":["She had finished the book.","She was cooking a meal.","She had not started reading."],"skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"ongoing_past_scene"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0003-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","prompt":"Translate to German: While","correct_answer":"Während","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to German using the Präteritum for both verbs: I was reading a book when Marco arrived. Use lesen, Buch, als and ankommen; use gerade to mark the reading as in progress.","correct_answer":"Ich las gerade ein Buch, als Marco ankam.","accepted_answers":["Als Marco ankam, las ich gerade ein Buch.","Gerade las ich ein Buch, als Marco ankam.","Ein Buch las ich gerade, als Marco ankam.","Ich las gerade in einem Buch, als Marco ankam.","Als Marco ankam, las ich gerade in einem Buch.","Gerade las ich in einem Buch, als Marco ankam.","In einem Buch las ich gerade, als Marco ankam."],"hint_text":"Lesen becomes las; ankommen becomes ankam at the end of the als clause.","explanation":"Ich las gerade ein Buch, als Marco ankam. Gerade highlights the ongoing reading, while als introduces the arrival. The fronted version Als Marco ankam, las ich gerade ein Buch is also valid. This is a selected German past-narration pattern, not a rule requiring an English-style progressive auxiliary.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"ongoing_past_scene"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0003-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","prompt":"Translate to English: Zuerst","correct_answer":"First","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to English using eating: Gestern um acht Uhr aßen wir noch.","correct_answer":"We were still eating at eight yesterday.","accepted_answers":["We were still eating yesterday at eight.","Yesterday at eight, we were still eating.","Yesterday at eight we were still eating.","At eight yesterday, we were still eating.","At eight yesterday we were still eating.","Yesterday, we were still eating at eight.","Yesterday we were still eating at eight.","We were still eating at 8 yesterday.","We were still eating yesterday at 8.","Yesterday at 8, we were still eating.","Yesterday at 8 we were still eating.","At 8 yesterday, we were still eating.","At 8 yesterday we were still eating.","Yesterday, we were still eating at 8.","Yesterday we were still eating at 8.","We were still eating at eight o'clock yesterday.","We were still eating yesterday at eight o'clock.","Yesterday at eight o'clock, we were still eating.","Yesterday at eight o'clock we were still eating.","At eight o'clock yesterday, we were still eating.","At eight o'clock yesterday we were still eating.","Yesterday, we were still eating at eight o'clock.","Yesterday we were still eating at eight o'clock.","We were still eating at 8 o'clock yesterday.","We were still eating yesterday at 8 o'clock.","Yesterday at 8 o'clock, we were still eating.","Yesterday at 8 o'clock we were still eating.","At 8 o'clock yesterday, we were still eating.","At 8 o'clock yesterday we were still eating.","Yesterday, we were still eating at 8 o'clock.","Yesterday we were still eating at 8 o'clock."],"hint_text":"Noch means still. The specified past time locates the meal while it was in progress.","explanation":"We were still eating at eight yesterday. Aßen is the simple past of essen; noch shows that the activity was continuing at the stated time. The sentence does not specify morning or evening.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"ongoing_past_scene"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0003-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0003-b10000000000","type":"fill_blank","prompt":"Da_____ (Next)","correct_answer":"nn","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Complete with the Präteritum form of essen: Wir ___ noch, als Marco ankam.","correct_answer":"aßen","accepted_answers":["assen"],"hint_text":"The wir past form is aßen in German and Austrian spelling; Swiss spelling uses assen.","explanation":"Wir aßen noch, als Marco ankam. Aßen agrees with wir. Noch and the arrival clause locate the eating as still in progress at that past moment.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"ongoing_past_scene"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0003-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0003-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Endlich","Zuletzt"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0003-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0003-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Meanwhile","correct_answer":"Inzwischen","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["Inzwischen"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “The father was in the middle of cooking, and meanwhile the children were playing outside in the garden.” Start with “Der Vater” and end with “im Garten.”.","correct_answer":"Der Vater war gerade beim Kochen, und inzwischen spielten die Kinder draußen im Garten.","accepted_answers":["Der Vater war gerade beim Kochen, und die Kinder spielten inzwischen draußen im Garten.","Der Vater war gerade beim Kochen, und inzwischen spielten draußen die Kinder im Garten."],"metadata":{"tiles":["Der","Vater","war","gerade","beim","Kochen,","und","inzwischen","spielten","die","Kinder","draußen","im","Garten."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0003-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0003-b10000000000","type":"error_correction","prompt":"Find and correct the error: Chxrakter","metadata":{"error_sentence":"Chxrakter"},"correct_answer":"Charakter","hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Correct the past form of lesen in the sentence.","metadata":{"error_sentence":"Ich leste gerade ein Buch, als Marco ankam.","correction_instruction":"This describes a past scene. Correct only the Präteritum form of lesen; keep every other word and the word order unchanged."},"correct_answer":"Ich las gerade ein Buch, als Marco ankam.","hint_text":"Lesen is irregular: its first-person singular Präteritum is las, not leste.","explanation":"Ich las gerade ein Buch, als Marco ankam. Replace only the incorrect leste with las. The rest already gives the ongoing reading and the arrival event in the requested order.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"ongoing_past_scene"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0003-e00000000010","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0003-b10000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Ende\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Ending","options":["Finally","Ending","Plot","Character"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Yesterday we started dinner at eight. Marco arrived at half past eight, before we finished. Which sentence describes our meal at his arrival?","correct_answer":"Als Marco ankam, aßen wir noch.","options":["Als Marco ankam, hatten wir schon fertig gegessen.","Als Marco ankam, aßen wir noch.","Wir werden erst morgen mit dem Essen anfangen.","Als Marco ankam, aßen wir nicht."],"hint_text":"The meal had begun but was not finished. Noch marks still.","explanation":"Als Marco ankam, aßen wir noch. The eating was already underway and continued at the arrival time. Hatten wir schon fertig gegessen would mean that we had already finished, contrary to the stated scene.","distractors":["Als Marco ankam, hatten wir schon fertig gegessen.","Wir werden erst morgen mit dem Essen anfangen.","Als Marco ankam, aßen wir nicht."],"skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"ongoing_past_scene"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0004-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Zunächst"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0004-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0004-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Währenddessen","Unterdessen"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0004-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0004-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Character","correct_answer":"Charakter","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["Charakter"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “The character was just about to open the letter when someone suddenly knocked on the door.” Start with “Der Charakter” and end with “Tür klopfte.”.","correct_answer":"Der Charakter wollte gerade den Brief öffnen, als plötzlich jemand an die Tür klopfte.","accepted_answers":["Der Charakter wollte gerade den Brief öffnen, als jemand plötzlich an die Tür klopfte."],"metadata":{"tiles":["Der","Charakter","wollte","gerade","den","Brief","öffnen,","als","plötzlich","jemand","an","die","Tür","klopfte."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0005-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Danach","Als Nächstes"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0005-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Eventually"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0005-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0005-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Figur"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0005-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0005-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Plot","correct_answer":"Handlung","metadata":{"tiles":["Handlung"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “The plot is set in a small village where the houses stand right beside a wide river.” Start with “Die Handlung” and end with “Fluss stehen.”.","correct_answer":"Die Handlung spielt in einem kleinen Dorf, wo die Häuser direkt an einem breiten Fluss stehen.","metadata":{"tiles":["Die","Handlung","spielt","in","einem","kleinen","Dorf,","wo","die","Häuser","direkt","an","einem","breiten","Fluss","stehen."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0006-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Endlich","Zuletzt"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0006-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["In the meantime"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0006-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0006-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Beginning","correct_answer":"Anfang","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["Anfang"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “At the beginning of the story, nobody knew why the stranger waited outside the station every night.” Start with “Am Anfang” and end with “Bahnhof wartete.”.","correct_answer":"Am Anfang der Geschichte wusste niemand, warum der Fremde jede Nacht vor dem Bahnhof wartete.","accepted_answers":["Am Anfang der Geschichte wusste niemand, warum jede Nacht der Fremde vor dem Bahnhof wartete."],"metadata":{"tiles":["Am","Anfang","der","Geschichte","wusste","niemand,","warum","der","Fremde","jede","Nacht","vor","dem","Bahnhof","wartete."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0001-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0001-b10000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Wenn\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"If","options":["Consequence","Imagine","Would","If"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"We have not decided what to do tomorrow. Our plan is: „Wenn es morgen regnet, bleiben wir zu Hause.“ What condition is stated for staying at home?","correct_answer":"If it rains tomorrow.","options":["If it rains tomorrow.","If it is sunny tomorrow.","If it rained yesterday.","If we leave home."],"hint_text":"Wenn introduces the condition; morgen locates it tomorrow.","explanation":"The stated condition is rain tomorrow. Staying at home is the planned result if that condition holds. The sentence does not claim that it will definitely rain or state what we will do if it is sunny.","distractors":["If it is sunny tomorrow.","If it rained yesterday.","If we leave home."],"skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"possible_future_condition"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0001-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","prompt":"Translate to German: Would","correct_answer":"Würde","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to German using the Präsens in both clauses: If it rains tomorrow, we will stay at home. Use wenn, regnen and bleiben.","correct_answer":"Wenn es morgen regnet, bleiben wir zu Hause.","accepted_answers":["Wenn es morgen regnet, bleiben wir zuhause.","Wenn es morgen regnet, dann bleiben wir zu Hause.","Wenn es morgen regnet, dann bleiben wir zuhause.","Wir bleiben zu Hause, wenn es morgen regnet.","Wir bleiben zuhause, wenn es morgen regnet.","Wir bleiben dann zu Hause, wenn es morgen regnet.","Wir bleiben dann zuhause, wenn es morgen regnet.","Wenn es morgen regnet, so bleiben wir zu Hause.","Wenn es morgen regnet, so bleiben wir zuhause.","Wir bleiben, wenn es morgen regnet, zu Hause.","Wir bleiben, wenn es morgen regnet, zuhause."],"hint_text":"In the wenn clause, regnet goes last. After a fronted condition, use bleiben wir, optionally preceded by dann.","explanation":"Wenn es morgen regnet, bleiben wir zu Hause. Present forms naturally express this future plan with morgen. A future-tense wording is possible in other tasks, but the visible instruction selects the Präsens here. Zu Hause and zuhause are both standard spellings.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"possible_future_condition"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0001-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","prompt":"Translate to English: Könnte","correct_answer":"Could","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to English using will and walk, beginning with If the bus: Wenn der Bus morgen zu spät kommt, gehen wir zu Fuß zur Schule.","correct_answer":"If the bus is late tomorrow, we will walk to school.","accepted_answers":["If the bus is late tomorrow we will walk to school.","If the bus is late tomorrow, we'll walk to school.","If the bus is late tomorrow we'll walk to school.","If the bus arrives late tomorrow, we will walk to school.","If the bus arrives late tomorrow we will walk to school.","If the bus arrives late tomorrow, we'll walk to school.","If the bus arrives late tomorrow we'll walk to school.","If the bus is running late tomorrow, we will walk to school.","If the bus is running late tomorrow we will walk to school.","If the bus is running late tomorrow, we'll walk to school.","If the bus is running late tomorrow we'll walk to school.","If the bus is delayed tomorrow, we will walk to school.","If the bus is delayed tomorrow we will walk to school.","If the bus is delayed tomorrow, we'll walk to school.","If the bus is delayed tomorrow we'll walk to school.","If the bus is late tomorrow, then we will walk to school.","If the bus is late tomorrow then we will walk to school.","If the bus is late tomorrow, then we'll walk to school.","If the bus is late tomorrow then we'll walk to school.","If the bus arrives late tomorrow, then we will walk to school.","If the bus arrives late tomorrow then we will walk to school.","If the bus arrives late tomorrow, then we'll walk to school.","If the bus arrives late tomorrow then we'll walk to school.","If the bus is running late tomorrow, then we will walk to school.","If the bus is running late tomorrow then we will walk to school.","If the bus is running late tomorrow, then we'll walk to school.","If the bus is running late tomorrow then we'll walk to school.","If the bus is delayed tomorrow, then we will walk to school.","If the bus is delayed tomorrow then we will walk to school.","If the bus is delayed tomorrow, then we'll walk to school.","If the bus is delayed tomorrow then we'll walk to school."],"hint_text":"Zu spät gives the condition; zu Fuß zur Schule gives the planned consequence.","explanation":"If the bus is late tomorrow, we will walk to school. The present-tense German verbs describe a possible future plan in this context. The consequence is conditional, not an unconditional promise to walk.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"possible_future_condition"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0001-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0001-b10000000000","type":"fill_blank","prompt":"Sol_____ (Should)","correct_answer":"lte","hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Complete with the Präsens form of regnen: Wenn es morgen ___, bleiben wir zu Hause.","correct_answer":"regnet","hint_text":"Use the third-person singular form with weather subject es.","explanation":"Wenn es morgen regnet, bleiben wir zu Hause. Regnet agrees with es and stands at the end of the wenn clause. Morgen makes the future reference clear despite the present form.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"possible_future_condition"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0001-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0001-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Perhaps","correct_answer":"Vielleicht","metadata":{"tiles":["Vielleicht"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “If it rains tomorrow, perhaps we will stay at home and watch a film together.” Start with “Wenn es” and end with “Film an.”.","correct_answer":"Wenn es morgen regnet, bleiben wir vielleicht zu Hause und sehen uns gemeinsam einen Film an.","metadata":{"tiles":["Wenn","es","morgen","regnet,","bleiben","wir","vielleicht","zu","Hause","und","sehen","uns","gemeinsam","einen","Film","an."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0001-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0001-b10000000000","type":"error_correction","prompt":"Find and correct the error: Stxll dir vor","metadata":{"error_sentence":"Stxll dir vor"},"correct_answer":"Stell dir vor","hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Correct the main-clause word order after the fronted condition.","metadata":{"error_sentence":"Wenn es morgen regnet, wir bleiben zu Hause.","correction_instruction":"Correct only the main-clause word order after the initial wenn clause. Keep every word; do not add or remove any words."},"correct_answer":"Wenn es morgen regnet, bleiben wir zu Hause.","hint_text":"The fronted condition occupies the first position, so the finite main verb comes before wir.","explanation":"Wenn es morgen regnet, bleiben wir zu Hause. Swap wir and bleiben. No tense change or extra dann is needed in this keep-every-word correction.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"possible_future_condition"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0001-e00000000010","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0001-b10000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Andernfalls\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Otherwise","options":["Could","I wish","Otherwise","Imagine"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Our plan is: „Wenn der Bus morgen zu spät kommt, gehen wir zu Fuß zur Schule.“ If the bus is late tomorrow, what does this plan say we will do?","correct_answer":"We will walk to school.","options":["We will take a taxi to school.","We will stay at home.","We will walk to school.","We will cancel school."],"hint_text":"The result is in the main clause: gehen wir zu Fuß zur Schule.","explanation":"We will walk to school if the bus is late. The plan does not mention a taxi, staying home or canceling school, and it does not state what happens if the bus is on time.","distractors":["We will take a taxi to school.","We will stay at home.","We will cancel school."],"skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"possible_future_condition"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0002-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0002-b10000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Würde\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Would","options":["Should","Regret","Perhaps","Would"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"The speaker does not own a car now and imagines a different situation: „Wenn ich ein Auto hätte, würde ich ans Meer fahren.“ What is the imagined result?","correct_answer":"The speaker would go to the seaside by car.","options":["The speaker would go to the seaside by car.","The speaker already owns a car.","The speaker took a train yesterday.","The speaker would stay at home."],"hint_text":"Hätte sets up the imagined possession; würde ... fahren gives the result.","explanation":"The imagined result is driving to the seaside. The context says that the speaker does not currently own a car. The conditional sentence does not report a completed journey or an actual purchase.","distractors":["The speaker already owns a car.","The speaker took a train yesterday.","The speaker would stay at home."],"skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"hypothetical_present_condition"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0002-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","prompt":"Translate to German: Could","correct_answer":"Könnte","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"I have little free time now. Translate this imagined alternative to German: If I had more time, I would read more. Use wenn, the one-word Konjunktiv II form of haben, and lesen for the result.","correct_answer":"Wenn ich mehr Zeit hätte, würde ich mehr lesen.","accepted_answers":["Wenn ich mehr Zeit hätte, dann würde ich mehr lesen.","Wenn ich mehr Zeit hätte, so würde ich mehr lesen.","Wenn ich mehr Zeit hätte, läse ich mehr.","Wenn ich mehr Zeit hätte, dann läse ich mehr.","Wenn ich mehr Zeit hätte, so läse ich mehr.","Ich würde mehr lesen, wenn ich mehr Zeit hätte.","Ich würde dann mehr lesen, wenn ich mehr Zeit hätte.","Ich läse mehr, wenn ich mehr Zeit hätte.","Ich läse dann mehr, wenn ich mehr Zeit hätte.","Mehr würde ich lesen, wenn ich mehr Zeit hätte.","Mehr läse ich, wenn ich mehr Zeit hätte.","Ich würde, wenn ich mehr Zeit hätte, mehr lesen.","Ich läse, wenn ich mehr Zeit hätte, mehr.","Wenn ich mehr Zeit hätte, würde ich dann mehr lesen.","Wenn ich mehr Zeit hätte, läse ich dann mehr."],"hint_text":"Use hätte in the wenn clause. The result can use würde ... lesen or the one-word form läse.","explanation":"Wenn ich mehr Zeit hätte, würde ich mehr lesen. Hätte and würde lesen express the imagined present condition and result; they do not mean that the situation happened in the past. Läse is a valid synthetic alternative to würde lesen. The visible instruction selects the one-word condition form without banning würde constructions generally.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"hypothetical_present_condition"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0002-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","prompt":"Translate to English: Sollte","correct_answer":"Should","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"The speaker is not rich now. Translate the imagined alternative to English using would, work and less: Wenn ich reich wäre, würde ich weniger arbeiten.","correct_answer":"If I were rich, I would work less.","accepted_answers":["If I were rich, then I would work less.","I would work less, if I were rich.","If I were rich I would work less.","If I were rich then I would work less.","I would work less if I were rich.","If I were rich, I'd work less.","If I were rich, then I'd work less.","I'd work less, if I were rich.","If I were rich I'd work less.","If I were rich then I'd work less.","I'd work less if I were rich.","If I were wealthy, I would work less.","If I were wealthy, then I would work less.","I would work less, if I were wealthy.","If I were wealthy I would work less.","If I were wealthy then I would work less.","I would work less if I were wealthy.","If I were wealthy, I'd work less.","If I were wealthy, then I'd work less.","I'd work less, if I were wealthy.","If I were wealthy I'd work less.","If I were wealthy then I'd work less.","I'd work less if I were wealthy.","If I was rich, I would work less.","If I was rich, then I would work less.","I would work less, if I was rich.","If I was rich I would work less.","If I was rich then I would work less.","I would work less if I was rich.","If I was rich, I'd work less.","If I was rich, then I'd work less.","I'd work less, if I was rich.","If I was rich I'd work less.","If I was rich then I'd work less.","I'd work less if I was rich.","If I was wealthy, I would work less.","If I was wealthy, then I would work less.","I would work less, if I was wealthy.","If I was wealthy I would work less.","If I was wealthy then I would work less.","I would work less if I was wealthy.","If I was wealthy, I'd work less.","If I was wealthy, then I'd work less.","I'd work less, if I was wealthy.","If I was wealthy I'd work less.","If I was wealthy then I'd work less.","I'd work less if I was wealthy."],"hint_text":"Reich means rich; weniger arbeiten means work less. The context is an imagined present, not a past event.","explanation":"If I were rich, I would work less. Were is the traditional hypothetical form; ordinary informal English with was is also accepted. The statement does not say that the speaker is rich or has already reduced their work.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"hypothetical_present_condition"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0002-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0002-b10000000000","type":"fill_blank","prompt":"Ich wü_____ (I wish)","correct_answer":"nschte","hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"The speaker has no car now. Complete with the one-word Konjunktiv II form of haben: Wenn ich ein Auto ___, würde ich ans Meer fahren.","correct_answer":"hätte","hint_text":"Use hätte, with an umlaut, for this imagined possession.","explanation":"Wenn ich ein Auto hätte, würde ich ans Meer fahren. Hätte is the requested Konjunktiv II form. Hatte would be an indicative past form and would not supply the selected hypothetical condition.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"hypothetical_present_condition"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0002-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0002-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Möglicherweise","Eventuell"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0002-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0002-b10000000000","type":"error_correction","prompt":"Find and correct the error: Anxenommen","metadata":{"error_sentence":"Anxenommen"},"correct_answer":"Angenommen","hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Correct the verb form after würde in this imagined present situation.","metadata":{"error_sentence":"Wenn ich mehr Zeit hätte, würde ich mehr liest.","correction_instruction":"The speaker imagines having more time now. Correct only the form of lesen after würde. Keep every other word and the word order unchanged."},"correct_answer":"Wenn ich mehr Zeit hätte, würde ich mehr lesen.","hint_text":"Würde takes the infinitive lesen here, not the finite form liest.","explanation":"Wenn ich mehr Zeit hätte, würde ich mehr lesen. Replace liest with lesen. The condition already has hätte; only the result-clause infinitive needs correction.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"hypothetical_present_condition"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0002-e00000000010","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0002-b10000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Bedauern\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Regret","options":["If","Regret","Could","Consequence"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Lea has very little time today and says: „Wenn ich jetzt mehr Zeit hätte, würde ich dich besuchen.“ What kind of situation is she describing?","correct_answer":"An imagined situation with more time now.","options":["An imagined situation with more time now.","A completed trip last year.","A confirmed appointment tomorrow.","A statement that the speaker already has plenty of time."],"hint_text":"Jetzt means now; hätte and würde frame an imagined alternative to the stated current situation.","explanation":"Lea imagines having more time now and visiting under that condition. She does not describe a completed past visit or make an unconditional appointment for tomorrow. The modal past-stem form is not itself a past-time report.","distractors":["A completed trip last year.","A confirmed appointment tomorrow.","A statement that the speaker already has plenty of time."],"skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"hypothetical_present_condition"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0003-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0003-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Stelle dir vor","Stellen Sie sich vor","Stellt euch vor"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0003-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0003-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Suppose","correct_answer":"Angenommen","metadata":{"tiles":["Angenommen"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “Suppose you lose your passport abroad; then you should contact the embassy.” Start with “Angenommen, du” and end with “Botschaft wenden.”.","correct_answer":"Angenommen, du verlierst deinen Pass im Ausland, dann solltest du dich an die Botschaft wenden.","metadata":{"tiles":["Angenommen,","du","verlierst","deinen","Pass","im","Ausland,","dann","solltest","du","dich","an","die","Botschaft","wenden."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0004-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0004-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Maybe"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0004-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0004-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Instead","correct_answer":"Stattdessen","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["Stattdessen"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “I have to work today, but I would rather go to the seaside with my friends instead.” Start with “Ich muss” and end with “Meer fahren.”.","correct_answer":"Ich muss heute arbeiten, aber ich würde stattdessen lieber mit meinen Freunden ans Meer fahren.","accepted_answers":["Ich muss heute arbeiten, aber ich würde lieber stattdessen mit meinen Freunden ans Meer fahren.","Ich muss heute arbeiten, aber ich würde mit meinen Freunden stattdessen lieber ans Meer fahren."],"metadata":{"tiles":["Ich","muss","heute","arbeiten,","aber","ich","würde","stattdessen","lieber","mit","meinen","Freunden","ans","Meer","fahren."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0005-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Möglicherweise","Eventuell"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0005-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0005-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Otherwise","correct_answer":"Andernfalls","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["Andernfalls"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “I should have declined the invitation; otherwise I would have had to arrange a ticket in good time.” Start with “Ich hätte” and end with “kümmern müssen.”.","correct_answer":"Ich hätte die Einladung ablehnen sollen; andernfalls hätte ich mich rechtzeitig um eine Fahrkarte kümmern müssen.","accepted_answers":["Ich hätte die Einladung ablehnen sollen; andernfalls hätte ich mich um eine Fahrkarte rechtzeitig kümmern müssen."],"metadata":{"tiles":["Ich","hätte","die","Einladung","ablehnen","sollen;","andernfalls","hätte","ich","mich","rechtzeitig","um","eine","Fahrkarte","kümmern","müssen."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0006-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Stellen Sie sich vor","Stellt euch vor"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0006-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Assuming","Supposing"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0006-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0006-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Sonst"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0006-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0006-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Regret","correct_answer":"Bedauern","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["Bedauern"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “To my regret, I rejected the offer, although I would actually have liked to accept the position.” Start with “Zu meinem” and end with “angenommen hätte.”.","correct_answer":"Zu meinem Bedauern habe ich das Angebot abgelehnt, obwohl ich die Stelle eigentlich gern angenommen hätte.","accepted_answers":["Zu meinem Bedauern habe ich das Angebot abgelehnt, obwohl ich eigentlich gern die Stelle angenommen hätte."],"metadata":{"tiles":["Zu","meinem","Bedauern","habe","ich","das","Angebot","abgelehnt,","obwohl","ich","die","Stelle","eigentlich","gern","angenommen","hätte."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0001-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Kind regards","Best regards","Yours sincerely"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0001-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0001-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Cool","correct_answer":"Cool","metadata":{"tiles":["Cool"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “In a formal inquiry, I would ask for a reply and avoid the word cool.” Start with “In einer” and end with “„cool“ vermeiden.”.","correct_answer":"In einer formellen Anfrage würde ich um eine Antwort bitten und das Wort „cool“ vermeiden.","metadata":{"tiles":["In","einer","formellen","Anfrage","würde","ich","um","eine","Antwort","bitten","und","das","Wort","„cool“","vermeiden."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0002-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Greetings"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0002-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0002-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Awesome","correct_answer":"Toll","metadata":{"tiles":["Toll"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “Your concert was great, and I am really glad that I was able to be there!” Start with “Dein Konzert” and end with “sein konnte!”.","correct_answer":"Dein Konzert war toll, und ich bin wirklich froh, dass ich dabei sein konnte!","metadata":{"tiles":["Dein","Konzert","war","toll,","und","ich","bin","wirklich","froh,","dass","ich","dabei","sein","konnte!"],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0003-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Viele Grüße"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0003-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Somehow","Sort of"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0003-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0003-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Großartig","Fantastisch","Super"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0003-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0003-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Whatever","correct_answer":"Egal","metadata":{"tiles":["Egal"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “In a polite email, I prefer writing “Both dates work” rather than “I do not care”.” Start with “In einer” and end with “mir egal“.”.","correct_answer":"In einer höflichen E-Mail schreibe ich lieber „Beide Termine passen“ als „Das ist mir egal“.","metadata":{"tiles":["In","einer","höflichen","E-Mail","schreibe","ich","lieber","„Beide","Termine","passen“","als","„Das","ist","mir","egal“."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0004-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0004-b10000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["p"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0005-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Great","Fantastic"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0005-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0005-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Keine Sorge"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0005-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0005-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Dude","correct_answer":"Alter","metadata":{"tiles":["Alter"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “Among friends, addressing someone as dude is possible, but I would avoid it in a job interview.” Start with “Unter Freunden” and end with “sie vermeiden.”.","correct_answer":"Unter Freunden ist die Anrede „Alter“ möglich, aber in einem Bewerbungsgespräch würde ich sie vermeiden.","metadata":{"tiles":["Unter","Freunden","ist","die","Anrede","„Alter“","möglich,","aber","in","einem","Bewerbungsgespräch","würde","ich","sie","vermeiden."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0006-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0006-b10000000000","type":"multiple_choice","options":["Cool","Awesome","Whatever","No problem"]},"after":{"options":["Cool","Boring","Whatever","No problem"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0006-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Großartig","Fantastisch","Super"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0006-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["It doesn't matter","It does not matter","Never mind"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0006-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0006-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Kumpel"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0006-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0006-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Formal","correct_answer":"Formell","metadata":{"tiles":["Formell"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “When I write to an authority, I phrase my request formally and avoid colloquial expressions.” Start with “Wenn ich” and end with “umgangssprachliche Ausdrücke.”.","correct_answer":"Wenn ich an eine Behörde schreibe, formuliere ich meine Bitte formell und vermeide umgangssprachliche Ausdrücke.","metadata":{"tiles":["Wenn","ich","an","eine","Behörde","schreibe,","formuliere","ich","meine","Bitte","formell","und","vermeide","umgangssprachliche","Ausdrücke."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Aim"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0001-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0001-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Truth","correct_answer":"Wahrheit","metadata":{"tiles":["Wahrheit"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “Although we seek the truth, our experiences influence which explanations initially seem plausible to us.” Start with “Obwohl wir” and end with “plausibel erscheinen.”.","correct_answer":"Obwohl wir nach der Wahrheit suchen, beeinflussen unsere Erfahrungen, welche Erklärungen uns zunächst plausibel erscheinen.","metadata":{"tiles":["Obwohl","wir","nach","der","Wahrheit","suchen,","beeinflussen","unsere","Erfahrungen,","welche","Erklärungen","uns","zunächst","plausibel","erscheinen."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Sinn","Absicht"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Awareness"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0002-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0002-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Wisdom","correct_answer":"Weisheit","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["Weisheit"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “For me, wisdom reveals itself in questioning one’s own convictions without prematurely giving up every judgment.” Start with “Für mich” and end with “vorschnell aufzugeben.”.","correct_answer":"Für mich zeigt sich Weisheit darin, die eigenen Überzeugungen zu hinterfragen, ohne jedes Urteil vorschnell aufzugeben.","accepted_answers":["Für mich zeigt Weisheit sich darin, die eigenen Überzeugungen zu hinterfragen, ohne jedes Urteil vorschnell aufzugeben."],"metadata":{"tiles":["Für","mich","zeigt","sich","Weisheit","darin,","die","eigenen","Überzeugungen","zu","hinterfragen,","ohne","jedes","Urteil","vorschnell","aufzugeben."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0003-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0003-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["ralität"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0003-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Belief","correct_answer":"Glaube","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["Glaube"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “Even a deeply rooted belief can change when new experiences fundamentally call previous assumptions into question.” Start with “Auch ein” and end with “infrage stellen.”.","correct_answer":"Auch ein fest verankerter Glaube kann sich verändern, wenn neue Erfahrungen die bisherigen Annahmen grundsätzlich infrage stellen.","accepted_answers":["Auch ein fest verankerter Glaube kann sich verändern, wenn neue Erfahrungen grundsätzlich die bisherigen Annahmen infrage stellen."],"metadata":{"tiles":["Auch","ein","fest","verankerter","Glaube","kann","sich","verändern,","wenn","neue","Erfahrungen","die","bisherigen","Annahmen","grundsätzlich","infrage","stellen."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0004-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Morals"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0004-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0004-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Überzeugung"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0004-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Doubt","correct_answer":"Zweifel","metadata":{"tiles":["Zweifel"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “Doubts about this conclusion are justified as long as the available data allow several different explanations.” Start with “Die Zweifel” and end with “Erklärungen zulassen.”.","correct_answer":"Die Zweifel an dieser Schlussfolgerung sind berechtigt, solange die verfügbaren Daten mehrere unterschiedliche Erklärungen zulassen.","metadata":{"tiles":["Die","Zweifel","an","dieser","Schlussfolgerung","sind","berechtigt,","solange","die","verfügbaren","Daten","mehrere","unterschiedliche","Erklärungen","zulassen."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Sittlichkeit","Moralität"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0005-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0005-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Freedom","correct_answer":"Freiheit","metadata":{"tiles":["Freiheit"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “Personal freedom cannot be considered independently of the responsibility we have toward other people.” Start with “Persönliche Freiheit” and end with “Menschen haben.”.","correct_answer":"Persönliche Freiheit lässt sich nicht unabhängig von der Verantwortung betrachten, die wir gegenüber anderen Menschen haben.","metadata":{"tiles":["Persönliche","Freiheit","lässt","sich","nicht","unabhängig","von","der","Verantwortung","betrachten,","die","wir","gegenüber","anderen","Menschen","haben."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0006-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0006-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","options":["Doubt","Freedom","Morality","Ethics"]},"after":{"options":["Doubt","Freedom","Morality","Wealth"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Dasein"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0006-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0006-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Justice","correct_answer":"Gerechtigkeit","metadata":{"tiles":["Gerechtigkeit"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “A rule does not automatically create justice just because it applies to everyone; its actual effects must also be considered.” Start with “Eine Regel” and end with “berücksichtigt werden.”.","correct_answer":"Eine Regel schafft nicht automatisch Gerechtigkeit, nur weil sie für alle gilt; auch ihre tatsächlichen Auswirkungen müssen berücksichtigt werden.","metadata":{"tiles":["Eine","Regel","schafft","nicht","automatisch","Gerechtigkeit,","nur","weil","sie","für","alle","gilt;","auch","ihre","tatsächlichen","Auswirkungen","müssen","berücksichtigt","werden."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Überreden"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Proof"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0001-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0001-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Entkräften"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0001-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0001-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Claim","correct_answer":"Behauptung","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["Behauptung"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “A claim is only convincing when it is supported by verifiable evidence and withstands possible objections.” Start with “Eine Behauptung” and end with “Einwänden standhält.”.","correct_answer":"Eine Behauptung ist erst dann überzeugend, wenn sie durch überprüfbare Belege gestützt wird und möglichen Einwänden standhält.","accepted_answers":["Eine Behauptung ist dann erst überzeugend, wenn sie durch überprüfbare Belege gestützt wird und möglichen Einwänden standhält."],"metadata":{"tiles":["Eine","Behauptung","ist","erst","dann","überzeugend,","wenn","sie","durch","überprüfbare","Belege","gestützt","wird","und","möglichen","Einwänden","standhält."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Belege","Beweismaterial","Nachweis","Beleg"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0002-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0002-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["These"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0002-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0002-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Fallacy","correct_answer":"Trugschluss","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["Trugschluss"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “It would be a fallacy to derive a general rule from a single example without carefully checking possible counterexamples.” Start with “Es wäre” and end with “zu prüfen.”.","correct_answer":"Es wäre ein Trugschluss, aus einem einzelnen Beispiel eine allgemeine Regel abzuleiten, ohne mögliche Gegenbeispiele sorgfältig zu prüfen.","accepted_answers":["Es wäre ein Trugschluss, eine allgemeine Regel aus einem einzelnen Beispiel abzuleiten, ohne mögliche Gegenbeispiele sorgfältig zu prüfen."],"metadata":{"tiles":["Es","wäre","ein","Trugschluss,","aus","einem","einzelnen","Beispiel","eine","allgemeine","Regel","abzuleiten,","ohne","mögliche","Gegenbeispiele","sorgfältig","zu","prüfen."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["But"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0003-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0003-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Fehlschluss"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0003-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Rhetoric","correct_answer":"Rhetorik","metadata":{"tiles":["Rhetorik"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “The speaker’s rhetoric sounds convincing, although he leaves the crucial question of financing his proposal unanswered.” Start with “Die Rhetorik” and end with “unbeantwortet lässt.”.","correct_answer":"Die Rhetorik des Redners wirkt überzeugend, obwohl er die entscheidende Frage nach der Finanzierung seines Vorschlags unbeantwortet lässt.","metadata":{"tiles":["Die","Rhetorik","des","Redners","wirkt","überzeugend,","obwohl","er","die","entscheidende","Frage","nach","der","Finanzierung","seines","Vorschlags","unbeantwortet","lässt."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0004-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Gegenargument\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Counterargument","options":["Argument","Counterargument","Bias","Nevertheless"],"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","hint_text":null,"explanation":null},"after":{"prompt":"Read this argument:\nDie Firma hat hundert Mitarbeiter. Zwei von ihnen waren heute unfreundlich zu mir. Daher sind alle Mitarbeiter dieser Firma unfreundlich.\n\nWhich criticism identifies the reasoning error?","correct_answer":"It judges all one hundred employees from the behaviour of only two.","options":["It attacks a person’s origin instead of examining their evidence.","It judges all one hundred employees from the behaviour of only two.","It treats a later event as the cause of an earlier event.","It claims that an opinion is true because most people believe it."],"distractors":["It attacks a person’s origin instead of examining their evidence.","It treats a later event as the cause of an earlier event.","It claims that an opinion is true because most people believe it."],"skill_type":"mixed","hint_text":"Compare the number of people actually observed with the number covered by the conclusion.","explanation":"Zwei von ihnen refers to two of the hundred employees; daher introduces the conclusion about alle, all of them. The observation concerns only two of one hundred employees and does not justify a categorical judgment about all of them: this is a hasty generalization. The problem is insufficient support; it does not prove that the opposite conclusion is true."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Aber","Allerdings","Indes"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0004-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Nonetheless","Even so","Still"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0004-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Bias","correct_answer":"Voreingenommenheit","metadata":{"tiles":["Voreingenommenheit"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “Anyone who rejects a study solely because of its author’s origin replaces an objective examination with bias.” Start with “Wer eine” and end with “durch Voreingenommenheit.”.","correct_answer":"Wer eine Studie allein wegen der Herkunft ihres Autors ablehnt, ersetzt eine sachliche Prüfung durch Voreingenommenheit.","metadata":{"tiles":["Wer","eine","Studie","allein","wegen","der","Herkunft","ihres","Autors","ablehnt,","ersetzt","eine","sachliche","Prüfung","durch","Voreingenommenheit."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0004-e00000000010","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Argument\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Argument","options":["Argument","Counterargument","However","Nevertheless"],"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","hint_text":null,"explanation":null},"after":{"prompt":"Read this argument:\nDie Stadt hat neue Straßenlampen aufgestellt. Einen Monat später stieg die Zahl der Besucher. Das beweist, dass die neuen Lampen diesen Anstieg verursacht haben.\n\nWhich response directly addresses the reasoning error?","correct_answer":"The increase came later, but that timing alone does not establish its cause.","options":["The timing alone proves that the new lamps caused the increase.","The increase proves that the lamps could not have had any effect.","The passage says that visitor numbers rose before the lamps were installed.","The increase came later, but that timing alone does not establish its cause."],"distractors":["The timing alone proves that the new lamps caused the increase.","The increase proves that the lamps could not have had any effect.","The passage says that visitor numbers rose before the lamps were installed."],"skill_type":"mixed","hint_text":"Separate the order of events from evidence about what caused the change.","explanation":"Einen Monat später expresses time order; das beweist, dass introduces the speaker’s claim of proof. Later does not by itself mean caused by: this is a post hoc causal inference. The lamps might have contributed, but the passage provides no evidence separating their effect from other possible causes. The justified response questions the claimed proof, not the possibility of an effect."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0005-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","options":["Fallacy","Nevertheless","Rhetoric","However"]},"after":{"options":["Fallacy","Therefore","Rhetoric","However"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Trotzdem","Gleichwohl","Nichtsdestoweniger"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Moreover","In addition"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0005-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Befangenheit"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0005-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Argument","correct_answer":"Argument","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["Argument"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “Before I reject your argument, I would like to make sure that I have correctly understood the underlying assumptions and your conclusion.” Start with “Bevor ich” and end with “verstanden habe.”.","correct_answer":"Bevor ich Ihr Argument zurückweise, möchte ich sicherstellen, dass ich die zugrunde liegenden Annahmen und Ihre Schlussfolgerung richtig verstanden habe.","accepted_answers":["Bevor ich Ihr Argument zurückweise, möchte ich sicherstellen, dass ich Ihre Schlussfolgerung und die zugrunde liegenden Annahmen richtig verstanden habe."],"metadata":{"tiles":["Bevor","ich","Ihr","Argument","zurückweise,","möchte","ich","sicherstellen,","dass","ich","die","zugrunde","liegenden","Annahmen","und","Ihre","Schlussfolgerung","richtig","verstanden","habe."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Außerdem","Zudem","Ferner"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["To disprove"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0006-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4002-0006-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: To persuade","correct_answer":"Überzeugen","metadata":{"tiles":["Überzeugen"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “To convince a skeptical audience, you should anticipate possible objections and explain how your evidence supports the central thesis.” Start with “Um ein” and end with “These stützen.”.","correct_answer":"Um ein skeptisches Publikum zu überzeugen, sollten Sie mögliche Einwände vorwegnehmen und erklären, wie Ihre Belege die zentrale These stützen.","metadata":{"tiles":["Um","ein","skeptisches","Publikum","zu","überzeugen,","sollten","Sie","mögliche","Einwände","vorwegnehmen","und","erklären,","wie","Ihre","Belege","die","zentrale","These","stützen."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4003-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4003-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Agreement"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4003-0001-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4003-0001-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Minutes","correct_answer":"Protokoll","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["Protokoll"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “I am sending you the minutes of our meeting attached, with a request to check the recorded decisions carefully before approval.” Start with “Anbei übersende” and end with “zu prüfen.”.","correct_answer":"Anbei übersende ich Ihnen das Protokoll unserer Sitzung mit der Bitte, die festgehaltenen Beschlüsse vor der Freigabe sorgfältig zu prüfen.","accepted_answers":["Anbei übersende ich Ihnen das Protokoll unserer Sitzung mit der Bitte, die festgehaltenen Beschlüsse sorgfältig vor der Freigabe zu prüfen."],"metadata":{"tiles":["Anbei","übersende","ich","Ihnen","das","Protokoll","unserer","Sitzung","mit","der","Bitte,","die","festgehaltenen","Beschlüsse","vor","der","Freigabe","sorgfältig","zu","prüfen."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4003-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4003-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["To put into practice","To carry out"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4003-0002-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4003-0002-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Sitzungsprotokoll"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4003-0002-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4003-0002-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: To delegate","correct_answer":"Delegieren","metadata":{"tiles":["Delegieren"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “In my presentation, I will explain why we should delegate tasks without losing sight of responsibility for the overall result.” Start with “In meiner” and end with “zu verlieren.”.","correct_answer":"In meiner Präsentation werde ich erläutern, warum wir Aufgaben delegieren sollten, ohne die Verantwortung für das Gesamtergebnis aus den Augen zu verlieren.","metadata":{"tiles":["In","meiner","Präsentation","werde","ich","erläutern,","warum","wir","Aufgaben","delegieren","sollten,","ohne","die","Verantwortung","für","das","Gesamtergebnis","aus","den","Augen","zu","verlieren."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4003-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4003-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Implementieren"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4003-0003-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4003-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Efficiency","correct_answer":"Effizienz","metadata":{"tiles":["Effizienz"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “We would be willing to accept the proposed date provided that the new process increases efficiency and continues to meet the agreed quality standards.” Start with “Wir wären” and end with “weiterhin erfüllt.”.","correct_answer":"Wir wären bereit, den vorgeschlagenen Termin zu akzeptieren, sofern das neue Verfahren die Effizienz erhöht und die vereinbarten Qualitätsstandards weiterhin erfüllt.","metadata":{"tiles":["Wir","wären","bereit,","den","vorgeschlagenen","Termin","zu","akzeptieren,","sofern","das","neue","Verfahren","die","Effizienz","erhöht","und","die","vereinbarten","Qualitätsstandards","weiterhin","erfüllt."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4003-0004-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4003-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Deadline","correct_answer":"Frist","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["Frist"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “We propose extending the deadline by two weeks so that the specialist department can carefully assess the risks before a final decision.” Start with “Wir schlagen” and end with “bewerten kann.”.","correct_answer":"Wir schlagen vor, die Frist um zwei Wochen zu verlängern, damit die Fachabteilung die Risiken vor einer endgültigen Entscheidung sorgfältig bewerten kann.","accepted_answers":["Wir schlagen vor, um zwei Wochen die Frist zu verlängern, damit die Fachabteilung die Risiken vor einer endgültigen Entscheidung sorgfältig bewerten kann.","Wir schlagen vor, die Frist um zwei Wochen zu verlängern, damit die Fachabteilung vor einer endgültigen Entscheidung die Risiken sorgfältig bewerten kann.","Wir schlagen vor, um zwei Wochen die Frist zu verlängern, damit die Fachabteilung vor einer endgültigen Entscheidung die Risiken sorgfältig bewerten kann."],"metadata":{"tiles":["Wir","schlagen","vor,","die","Frist","um","zwei","Wochen","zu","verlängern,","damit","die","Fachabteilung","die","Risiken","vor","einer","endgültigen","Entscheidung","sorgfältig","bewerten","kann."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4003-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4003-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Etat"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4003-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4003-0005-b200