o","Addio"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Hello","Good day"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0001-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Per piacere","Per cortesia"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0001-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Thanks"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0002-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["I'm sorry","I am sorry"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0002-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0002-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["usa","usami","usatemi"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0003-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Scusa","Scusi"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0003-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Sorry","Pardon"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0004-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Scusami","Scusatemi","Scusa"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0005-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0005-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Buonanotte\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Good night","options":["Good night","Excuse me","Goodbye","Please"],"distractors":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read this short introduction:\nCiao! Mi chiamo Lea. Sono di Roma.\n\nWhat is the writer’s name?","correct_answer":"Lea","options":["Marco","Anna","Lea","Luca"],"distractors":["Marco","Anna","Luca"],"hint_text":"Look for Mi chiamo, which introduces a name.","explanation":"The writer says Mi chiamo Lea: My name is Lea. Ciao is the greeting; the final sentence states where Lea is from.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0005-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Per piacere","Per cortesia"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0005-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Thanks"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0005-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0005-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Scusi\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Excuse me","options":["Hello","Goodbye","Excuse me","Good night"],"distractors":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read this short introduction:\nCiao! Mi chiamo Lea. Sono di Roma.\n\nWhere is Lea from?","correct_answer":"Rome","options":["Berlin","Rome","Paris","London"],"distractors":["Berlin","Paris","London"],"hint_text":"Sono di introduces a place of origin here; Roma is Rome.","explanation":"Sono di Roma means I am from Rome. With this city name, Italian uses di without an article. The passage states origin, not a current address.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["I'm sorry","I am sorry"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0006-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0006-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["usa","usami","usatemi"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0006-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":["Goodbye","Bye"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Goodbye","Bye","Hi"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0006-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0006-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["ederLa"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1002-0004-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1002-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Tasty"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1002-0005-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1002-0005-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Latte\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Milk","options":["Apple","Milk","Cheese","Water"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"At a restaurant, you want fish with rice and a glass of water. Which sentence places that order politely?","correct_answer":"Vorrei del pesce con riso e un bicchiere d’acqua, per favore.","options":["Vorrei del pollo con riso e un bicchiere d’acqua, per favore.","Vorrei del pesce con riso e un bicchiere d’acqua, per favore.","Vorrei del pesce con pane e un bicchiere d’acqua, per favore.","Vorrei del pesce con riso e un bicchiere di latte, per favore."],"hint_text":"Vorrei expresses I would like; per favore means please. Check both the food and the drink.","explanation":"Vorrei del pesce con riso e un bicchiere d’acqua, per favore means I would like fish with rice and a glass of water, please. The other orders change the fish, rice or water. Vorrei is a useful polite request formula, not the only possible way to order.","distractors":["Vorrei del pollo con riso e un bicchiere d’acqua, per favore.","Vorrei del pesce con pane e un bicchiere d’acqua, per favore.","Vorrei del pesce con riso e un bicchiere di latte, per favore."],"skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1002-0005-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1002-0005-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","prompt":"Ri_____ (Rice)","correct_answer":"so","hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Complete the restaurant request with vorrei (I would like) or ho (I have): ___ del pesce con riso e un bicchiere d’acqua, per favore.","correct_answer":"vorrei","hint_text":"The customer is asking to receive the meal, not stating what they already have.","explanation":"Vorrei del pesce con riso e un bicchiere d’acqua, per favore places an order. Of the two offered forms, vorrei expresses the request; ho states possession. Vorrei is first-person singular; Italian does not need an explicit io here.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"polite_meal_request"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1002-0005-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1002-0005-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Pesce\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Fish","options":["Fish","Coffee","Delicious","Menu"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"A customer says: Vorrei del pollo con riso e un bicchiere d’acqua, per favore. What does the customer order?","correct_answer":"Chicken with rice and a glass of water.","options":["Chicken with bread and a glass of water.","Fish with rice and a glass of water.","Chicken with rice and a glass of milk.","Chicken with rice and a glass of water."],"hint_text":"Pollo is chicken, riso is rice and acqua is water.","explanation":"The complete order is chicken with rice and a glass of water. Per favore makes the request polite; con connects the chicken with its rice accompaniment, and e adds the drink.","distractors":["Chicken with bread and a glass of water.","Fish with rice and a glass of water.","Chicken with rice and a glass of milk."],"skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1002-0005-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1002-0005-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Squisito","Squisita","Deliziosa"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1003-0001-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1003-0001-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Sinistra\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Left","options":["Bus","Station","Straight","Left"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"You want someone to explain how to get to the railway station. Which question asks for those directions?","correct_answer":"Mi scusi, come arrivo alla stazione?","options":["Mi scusi, quanto costa il biglietto?","Mi scusi, come arrivo alla stazione?","Mi scusi, quando parte il prossimo treno?","Mi scusi, questo è il mio biglietto?"],"hint_text":"Come arrivo a ...? asks how to get to a place. Alla combines a and la.","explanation":"Mi scusi, come arrivo alla stazione? means Excuse me, how do I get to the station? The other questions ask the ticket price, the next train’s departure time and whether a ticket belongs to the speaker. Mi scusi is a polite way to address one person.","distractors":["Mi scusi, quanto costa il biglietto?","Mi scusi, quando parte il prossimo treno?","Mi scusi, questo è il mio biglietto?"],"skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1003-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1003-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Straight ahead"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1003-0004-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1003-0004-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Autobus\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Bus","options":["Bus","Ticket","Pharmacy","Right"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"At a ticket counter, you want one one-way ticket to Rome. Which request matches?","correct_answer":"Un biglietto di sola andata per Roma, per favore.","options":["Un biglietto di andata e ritorno per Roma, per favore.","Due biglietti di sola andata per Roma, per favore.","Un biglietto di sola andata per Milano, per favore.","Un biglietto di sola andata per Roma, per favore."],"hint_text":"Sola andata means one-way; andata e ritorno includes the journey back.","explanation":"Un biglietto di sola andata per Roma, per favore requests one one-way ticket to Rome. The other requests include a return journey, two tickets or a different destination. Per favore makes the concise counter request polite.","distractors":["Un biglietto di andata e ritorno per Roma, per favore.","Due biglietti di sola andata per Roma, per favore.","Un biglietto di sola andata per Milano, per favore."],"skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1003-0004-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1003-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Chemist's","Drugstore"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1004-0001-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1004-0001-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Colazione\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Breakfast","options":["Breakfast","Cheap","Blue","Expensive"],"distractors":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read this sentence:\nLina fa colazione a casa ogni mattina.\n\nWhich routine is described?","correct_answer":"Eating breakfast at home every morning.","options":["Eating breakfast at home every morning.","Eating dinner at home every evening.","Eating breakfast at a café every morning.","Eating breakfast at home only on Sundays."],"distractors":["Eating dinner at home every evening.","Eating breakfast at a café every morning.","Eating breakfast at home only on Sundays."],"hint_text":"Ogni mattina means every morning; a casa means at home.","explanation":"Lina eats breakfast at home every morning. Fa colazione describes eating breakfast, and ogni mattina makes this a regular routine rather than a single meal.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1004-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1004-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Caro","Cara","Costosa"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1004-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1004-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Inexpensive","Economical"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1004-0001-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1004-0001-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["ssa"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1004-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1004-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Poco costoso","A buon mercato","Economica"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1004-0003-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1004-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Hour","Now"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1004-0004-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1004-0004-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Rosso\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Red","options":["Expensive","Time","Cheap","Red"],"distractors":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read this sentence:\nIl negozio apre alle nove di mattina.\n\nAt what time does the shop open?","correct_answer":"At 9 a.m.","options":["At 8 a.m.","At 9 p.m.","At 9 a.m.","At 10 a.m."],"distractors":["At 8 a.m.","At 9 p.m.","At 10 a.m."],"hint_text":"Nove is nine; di mattina selects the morning, not the evening.","explanation":"The shop opens at 9 a.m. Alle nove gives the clock time and di mattina identifies the morning. Apre describes opening, not closing.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1004-0004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1004-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Azzurro"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1004-0004-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1004-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Tempo"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1004-0005-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1004-0005-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Cash"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1004-0006-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1004-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Denaro"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Medico"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0001-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","prompt":"Translate to Italian: Soccer","correct_answer":"Calcio","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to Italian: waiter (a man who serves customers in a restaurant). Give the noun without an article.","correct_answer":"Cameriere","accepted_answers":["Cameriere di sala"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0001-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","prompt":"Translate to English: Caldo","correct_answer":"Hot","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to English: cuoco (a person whose job is to prepare food). Give the noun without an article.","correct_answer":"Cook","accepted_answers":["Chef"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0001-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0001-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","prompt":"Fre_____ (Cold)","correct_answer":"ddo","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null},"after":{"prompt":"Panett_____ (Baker: enter the missing ending of the singular masculine or feminine noun.)","correct_answer":"iere","accepted_answers":["iera"],"hint_text":"The masculine singular is panettiere; the feminine singular is panettiera."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0002-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0002-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Dottore\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Doctor","options":["Doctor","Hot","To read","Friend"],"distractors":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read this sentence:\nDomani incontro Lea al parco.\n\nWhat plan is described?","correct_answer":"Meeting Lea in the park tomorrow.","options":["Meeting Lea at a café tomorrow.","Meeting Lea in the park today.","Staying at home tomorrow.","Meeting Lea in the park tomorrow."],"distractors":["Meeting Lea at a café tomorrow.","Meeting Lea in the park today.","Staying at home tomorrow."],"hint_text":"Domani means tomorrow; incontro Lea means I am meeting Lea.","explanation":"The speaker plans to meet Lea in the park tomorrow. Italian can use the present tense with a future time phrase for a planned meeting. Al parco identifies the place.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0003-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0003-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Ufficio\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Office","options":["To cook","Friend","Cold","Office"],"distractors":[]},"after":{"prompt":"Read: «D’estate mi piace disegnare al parco.» Which hobby does the speaker enjoy?","correct_answer":"Drawing","options":["Swimming","Cooking","Drawing","Reading"],"distractors":["Swimming","Cooking","Reading"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Cuocere"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0004-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Football"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0004-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0004-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["lda"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0004-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0004-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["ica"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0005-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Warm"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0005-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0005-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["dda"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0005-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0005-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":["Dude"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Dude","Buddy","Pal"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0006-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0006-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["toressa"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Papà"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0001-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Grandma","Granny"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0002-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0002-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Padre\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Father","options":["Family","Father","Son","Brother"],"distractors":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read this sentence:\nMio padre ha gli occhi marroni e i capelli corti.\n\nWhich description matches the sentence?","correct_answer":"The father has brown eyes and short hair.","options":["The father has blue eyes and short hair.","The father has brown eyes and short hair.","The father has brown eyes and long hair.","The father has green eyes and long hair."],"distractors":["The father has blue eyes and short hair.","The father has brown eyes and long hair.","The father has green eyes and long hair."],"hint_text":"Gli occhi marroni means brown eyes; i capelli corti means short hair.","explanation":"The speaker’s father has brown eyes and short hair. Italian uses the articles gli and i with these body-part descriptions; marroni and corti agree with the plural nouns.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0002-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Grandpa","Granddad"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0003-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0003-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Sorella\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Sister","options":["Sister","Grandmother","Cat","Brother"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"You are speaking directly to a child named Lea. Which question asks how old she is?","correct_answer":"Quanti anni hai?","options":["Come ti chiami?","Quando è il tuo compleanno?","Quanti anni hai?","Dove abiti?"],"hint_text":"Anni means years. The age question uses avere.","explanation":"Quanti anni hai? asks the child’s age. Come ti chiami? asks her name; Quando è il tuo compleanno? asks the birthday date; Dove abiti? asks where she lives.","distractors":["Come ti chiami?","Quando è il tuo compleanno?","Dove abiti?"],"skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"age_expressions"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","prompt":"Translate to Italian: Brother","correct_answer":"Fratello","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to Italian: I am eight years old. Use avere and anni; write the number as a word.","correct_answer":"Ho otto anni.","accepted_answers":["Io ho otto anni."],"hint_text":"Use ho, the first-person singular of avere.","explanation":"Ho otto anni. Italian normally states age with avere, literally have eight years. Io is optional because ho already identifies the first-person singular.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"age_expressions"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","prompt":"Translate to English: Figlia","correct_answer":"Daughter","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to English: Lea ha otto anni.","correct_answer":"Lea is eight years old.","accepted_answers":["Lea is eight.","Lea's eight years old.","Lea's eight.","Lea is 8 years old.","Lea is 8.","Lea's 8 years old.","Lea's 8."],"hint_text":"Otto gives Lea’s age, not a calendar date.","explanation":"Lea is eight years old. Italian uses ha ... anni, but English normally uses is ... years old. Lea is eight is also natural English.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"age_expressions"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0003-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0003-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","prompt":"Fig_____ (Son)","correct_answer":"lio","hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Complete with the present-tense form of avere: Ben ___ dieci anni.","correct_answer":"ha","hint_text":"Ben is one person, like lui.","explanation":"Ben ha dieci anni. Use ha with the third-person singular subject Ben. The sentence says that Ben is ten years old.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"age_expressions"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0003-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0003-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Nonna\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Grandmother","options":["Mother","Father","Daughter","Grandmother"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Il compleanno di Lea è il tre maggio. Il compleanno di Ben è l’otto giugno. When is Ben’s birthday?","correct_answer":"On June 8.","options":["On May 3.","On June 8.","On June 3.","On May 8."],"hint_text":"Find Ben’s sentence. Giugno is June, and otto is eight.","explanation":"Ben’s birthday is on June 8; Lea’s is on May 3. Italian normally uses a cardinal number for a day such as eight: l’otto giugno. The article elides before otto.","distractors":["On May 3.","On June 3.","On May 8."],"skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"birthday_dates"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0003-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","prompt":"Translate to Italian: Grandfather","correct_answer":"Nonno","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to Italian: My birthday is on June eighth. Use essere and il mio compleanno; write the date in words.","correct_answer":"Il mio compleanno è l'otto giugno.","accepted_answers":["L'otto giugno è il mio compleanno."],"hint_text":"Use è with il mio compleanno. Italian dates use otto here, not ottavo.","explanation":"Il mio compleanno è l’otto giugno. The birthday date uses l’otto giugno; the English ordinal eighth corresponds to the cardinal otto in this Italian date.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"birthday_dates"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0004-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Child"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0004-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0004-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["tta"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0005-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0005-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Figlia\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Daughter","options":["Grandmother","Son","Dog","Daughter"],"distractors":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read this sentence:\nOgni domenica cucino con mia figlia.\n\nWhich shared family activity is described?","correct_answer":"Cooking with the speaker’s daughter every Sunday.","options":["Cooking with the speaker’s daughter every Sunday.","Reading with the speaker’s daughter every Sunday.","Cooking with the speaker’s mother every Sunday.","Cooking with the speaker’s daughter every Friday."],"distractors":["Reading with the speaker’s daughter every Sunday.","Cooking with the speaker’s mother every Sunday.","Cooking with the speaker’s daughter every Friday."],"hint_text":"Cucino means I cook; con mia figlia means with my daughter.","explanation":"The speaker cooks with their daughter every Sunday. Con introduces the family member taking part, while ogni domenica gives the recurring day.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0005-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Grandma","Granny"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0005-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0005-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["mma"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Grandpa","Granddad"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0006-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Mom","Mum"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0006-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1006-0006-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["pà"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1007-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1007-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Camera"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1007-0001-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1007-0001-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["ola"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1007-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1007-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Toilet","Restroom"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1007-0002-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1007-0002-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["ggiola"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1007-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1007-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","prompt":"Translate to Italian: Bathroom","correct_answer":"Bagno"},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to Italian: spoon. Give the noun without an article.","correct_answer":"Cucchiaio"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1007-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1007-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","prompt":"Translate to English: Camera da letto","correct_answer":"Bedroom","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to English: piatto (the item you eat from). Give the noun without an article.","correct_answer":"Plate","accepted_answers":["Dish"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1007-0003-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1007-0003-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","prompt":"Le_____ (Bed)","correct_answer":"tto"},"after":{"prompt":"For_____ (Fork: enter the missing ending of the singular noun.)","correct_answer":"chetta"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1007-0004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1007-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Stanza da letto"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1007-0004-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1007-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Seggiola"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1007-0005-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1007-0005-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Camera da letto\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Bedroom","options":["Window","Chair","Bedroom","Bed"],"distractors":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read this sentence:\nLa mia casa ha due camere da letto e un giardino.\n\nWhich description matches the stated details?","correct_answer":"The home has two bedrooms and a garden.","options":["The home has one bedroom and a garden.","The home has two bedrooms but no garden.","The home has two bedrooms and a garden.","The home has three bedrooms and a garden."],"distractors":["The home has one bedroom and a garden.","The home has two bedrooms but no garden.","The home has three bedrooms and a garden."],"hint_text":"Due camere da letto means two bedrooms; un giardino means a garden.","explanation":"The home has two bedrooms and a garden. The sentence states both the number of bedrooms and the presence of a garden; the other offered descriptions change one of those facts.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1007-0005-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1007-0005-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["ola"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1007-0006-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1007-0006-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["ggiola"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1007-0006-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1007-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Home"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0001-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["In salute","Sana"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0001-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Medication"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0002-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0002-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["ata"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0002-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Farmaco"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0002-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Ache"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Ill","Unwell"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0003-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0003-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["na"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0003-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Male"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Ammalato","Ammalata","Malata"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0004-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Well"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0004-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0004-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["cinale"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0005-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0005-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Malato\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Sick","options":["Leg","Head","Medicine","Sick"],"distractors":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read this sentence:\nFaccio una passeggiata ogni giorno.\n\nWhich habit does the speaker describe?","correct_answer":"Going for a walk every day.","options":["Going swimming every day.","Going for a walk once a week.","Drinking water every morning.","Going for a walk every day."],"distractors":["Going swimming every day.","Going for a walk once a week.","Drinking water every morning."],"hint_text":"Fare una passeggiata means to go for a walk; ogni giorno means every day.","explanation":"The speaker goes for a walk every day. This sentence describes a recurring personal activity. It does not prescribe a medical treatment, duration or exercise target.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0005-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["In salute","Sana"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0005-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Medication"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Farmaco"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1008-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Ache"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0001-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0001-a20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Husband","correct_answer":"Marito","metadata":{"tiles":["Marito"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “My husband has two older sisters.” Start with “Mio” and end with “maggiori.”.","correct_answer":"Mio marito ha due sorelle maggiori.","metadata":{"tiles":["Mio","marito","ha","due","sorelle","maggiori."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0001-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0001-a20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Fidanzato"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0002-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0002-a20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Sposo"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0002-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0002-a20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Wife","correct_answer":"Moglie","metadata":{"tiles":["Moglie"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “My wife is also my best friend.” Start with “Mia moglie” and end with “migliore amica.”.","correct_answer":"Mia moglie è anche la mia migliore amica.","metadata":{"tiles":["Mia","moglie","è","anche","la","mia","migliore","amica."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0002-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0002-a20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Fidanzata"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0003-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0003-a20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Cugino\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Cousin","options":["Married","Neighbor","Wife","Cousin"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Luca ha venticinque anni. Sofia ne ha ventidue. Which sentence correctly compares their ages?","correct_answer":"Luca ha tre anni più di Sofia.","options":["Luca ha tre anni meno di Sofia.","Luca ha tre anni più di Sofia.","Luca e Sofia hanno la stessa età.","Luca ha due anni più di Sofia."],"hint_text":"Compare twenty-five with twenty-two. Più means more; meno means less.","explanation":"Luca ha tre anni più di Sofia. Luca is three years older. In this age comparison, avere ... anni più di expresses having that many more years of age, not a total age of three.","distractors":["Luca ha tre anni meno di Sofia.","Luca e Sofia hanno la stessa età.","Luca ha due anni più di Sofia."],"skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"age_comparison"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0003-a20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","prompt":"Translate to Italian: Nephew","correct_answer":"Nipote","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to Italian: My brother is three years older than me. Use fratello, avere, anni and più; write three as a word.","correct_answer":"Mio fratello ha tre anni più di me.","accepted_answers":["Mio fratello ha tre anni in più di me.","Mio fratello ha tre anni più di quanti ne ho io.","Mio fratello ha tre anni in più di quanti ne ho io."],"hint_text":"Use ha tre anni più di me. In più is also possible.","explanation":"Mio fratello ha tre anni più di me. The visible instruction selects an avere age comparison. Ha tre anni in più di me is also valid. An essere construction with più grande could convey the same age relation, but is not the requested avere pattern.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"age_comparison"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0003-a20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","prompt":"Translate to English: Nipote","correct_answer":"Niece","accepted_answers":["Nephew"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to English using turned: Lea ha compiuto ventidue anni ieri.","correct_answer":"Lea turned twenty-two yesterday.","accepted_answers":["Lea turned 22 yesterday.","Yesterday Lea turned twenty-two.","Yesterday, Lea turned twenty-two.","Yesterday Lea turned 22.","Yesterday, Lea turned 22.","Lea turned twenty-two years old yesterday.","Lea turned 22 years old yesterday.","Yesterday Lea turned twenty-two years old.","Yesterday, Lea turned twenty-two years old.","Yesterday Lea turned 22 years old.","Yesterday, Lea turned 22 years old."],"hint_text":"Ha compiuto ... anni describes reaching the age on a birthday.","explanation":"Lea turned twenty-two yesterday. Compiere ... anni describes reaching that age; ha compiuto is the passato prossimo. The sentence states a birthday event, not merely a static age.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"reaching_an_age"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0003-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0003-a20000000000","type":"fill_blank","prompt":"Mar_____ (Husband)","correct_answer":"ito","hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Luca ha venticinque anni e Sofia ne ha ventidue. Complete with più or meno: Luca ha tre anni ___ di Sofia.","correct_answer":"più","hint_text":"Luca’s age is greater by three years.","explanation":"Luca ha tre anni più di Sofia. The ages select più, more, rather than meno, less. Più has an accent on ù.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"age_comparison"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0003-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0003-a20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Sposa"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0003-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0003-a20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Boyfriend","correct_answer":"Ragazzo","metadata":{"tiles":["Ragazzo"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “My boyfriend has just turned twenty years old.” Start with “Il mio” and end with “venti anni.”.","correct_answer":"Il mio ragazzo ha appena compiuto venti anni.","metadata":{"tiles":["Il","mio","ragazzo","ha","appena","compiuto","venti","anni."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0003-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0003-a20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Ragazza\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Girlfriend","options":["Girlfriend","Neighbor","Cousin","Niece"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"You are chatting with a friend about the friend’s adult sister. Which question asks the sister’s age?","correct_answer":"Quanti anni ha tua sorella?","options":["Come si chiama tua sorella?","Che lavoro fa tua sorella?","Quando è il compleanno di tua sorella?","Quanti anni ha tua sorella?"],"hint_text":"The sister is the third-person singular subject, so use ha.","explanation":"Quanti anni ha tua sorella? asks her age. The other questions ask her name, occupation and birthday date. Italian uses avere in this age question.","distractors":["Come si chiama tua sorella?","Che lavoro fa tua sorella?","Quando è il compleanno di tua sorella?"],"skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"age_questions"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0003-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0003-a20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","prompt":"Translate to Italian: Neighbor","correct_answer":"Vicino","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to Italian in the passato prossimo: Yesterday I turned twenty-two. Use compiere and anni; write the age as a word.","correct_answer":"Ieri ho compiuto ventidue anni.","accepted_answers":["Io ieri ho compiuto ventidue anni.","Ieri io ho compiuto ventidue anni.","Ho compiuto ventidue anni ieri.","Io ho compiuto ventidue anni ieri.","Ho compiuto ieri ventidue anni.","Io ho compiuto ieri ventidue anni.","Ho ieri compiuto ventidue anni.","Io ho ieri compiuto ventidue anni."],"hint_text":"Use ho compiuto. The subject pronoun io is optional.","explanation":"Ieri ho compiuto ventidue anni. The requested passato prossimo uses ho plus compiuto. Io may be included, and ieri may come before or after the birthday statement.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"reaching_an_age"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0004-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-2001-0004-a20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Fidanzato"]}},{"table":"exercises