cepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Dopo","Allora"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0001-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["All of a sudden"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0001-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0001-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Primo","Per prima cosa","Innanzitutto"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0001-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0001-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Next","correct_answer":"Dopo","metadata":{"tiles":["Dopo"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “First we found an old map, and immediately afterward we began looking for the house hidden in the woods.” Start with “Prima abbiamo” and end with “nel bosco.”.","correct_answer":"Prima abbiamo trovato una vecchia mappa, e subito dopo abbiamo cominciato a cercare la casa nascosta nel bosco.","metadata":{"tiles":["Prima","abbiamo","trovato","una","vecchia","mappa,","e","subito","dopo","abbiamo","cominciato","a","cercare","la","casa","nascosta","nel","bosco."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0002-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0002-b10000000000","type":"multiple_choice","options":["While","Next","Then","Suddenly"]},"after":{"options":["While","Before","Then","Suddenly"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0002-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Improvvisamente","D'un tratto"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0002-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Whereas"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0002-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0002-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Poi","Successivamente"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0002-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0002-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Finally","correct_answer":"Infine","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["Infine"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “We walked along the river for hours and finally reached the village before it got dark.” Start with “Abbiamo camminato” and end with “facesse buio.”.","correct_answer":"Abbiamo camminato per ore lungo il fiume e infine siamo arrivati al villaggio prima che facesse buio.","accepted_answers":["Abbiamo camminato lungo il fiume per ore e infine siamo arrivati al villaggio prima che facesse buio."],"metadata":{"tiles":["Abbiamo","camminato","per","ore","lungo","il","fiume","e","infine","siamo","arrivati","al","villaggio","prima","che","facesse","buio."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0003-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0003-b10000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"All''improvviso\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Suddenly","options":["Next","Meanwhile","Suddenly","First"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Ieri sera Lea stava leggendo un libro quando ha suonato il telefono. What was in progress when the phone rang?","correct_answer":"She was reading a book.","options":["She was reading a book.","She had finished the book.","She was cooking a meal.","She had not started reading."],"hint_text":"Stava leggendo focuses on the reading in progress; ha suonato supplies the ringing event.","explanation":"Lea was reading a book. Stava leggendo is the progressive construction with imperfetto stare and a gerund. The ringing occurs during the reading, not after an explicitly completed book.","distractors":["She had finished the book.","She was cooking a meal.","She had not started reading."],"skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"ongoing_past_scene"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0003-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","prompt":"Translate to Italian: While","correct_answer":"Mentre","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to Italian: I was reading a book when Marco arrived. Use stare in the imperfetto + the gerund of leggere for the reading, quando, and arrivare in the passato prossimo.","correct_answer":"Stavo leggendo un libro quando Marco è arrivato.","accepted_answers":["Io stavo leggendo un libro quando Marco è arrivato.","Stavo leggendo un libro, quando Marco è arrivato.","Io stavo leggendo un libro, quando Marco è arrivato.","Quando Marco è arrivato, stavo leggendo un libro.","Quando Marco è arrivato stavo leggendo un libro.","Quando Marco è arrivato, io stavo leggendo un libro.","Quando Marco è arrivato io stavo leggendo un libro.","Stavo leggendo un libro quando è arrivato Marco.","Io stavo leggendo un libro quando è arrivato Marco.","Stavo leggendo un libro, quando è arrivato Marco.","Io stavo leggendo un libro, quando è arrivato Marco.","Quando è arrivato Marco, stavo leggendo un libro.","Quando è arrivato Marco stavo leggendo un libro.","Quando è arrivato Marco, io stavo leggendo un libro.","Quando è arrivato Marco io stavo leggendo un libro."],"hint_text":"Use stavo leggendo for I was reading and Marco è arrivato for Marco arrived.","explanation":"Stavo leggendo un libro quando Marco è arrivato. Stavo leggendo foregrounds the reading in progress; è arrivato gives the arrival event. The plain imperfetto leggevo can also describe a background in appropriate contexts, but this task visibly requests stare + gerund.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"ongoing_past_scene"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0003-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","prompt":"Translate to English: Prima","correct_answer":"First","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to English using eating: Ieri alle otto stavamo ancora mangiando.","correct_answer":"We were still eating at eight yesterday.","accepted_answers":["We were still eating yesterday at eight.","Yesterday at eight, we were still eating.","Yesterday at eight we were still eating.","At eight yesterday, we were still eating.","At eight yesterday we were still eating.","Yesterday, we were still eating at eight.","Yesterday we were still eating at eight.","We were still eating at 8 yesterday.","We were still eating yesterday at 8.","Yesterday at 8, we were still eating.","Yesterday at 8 we were still eating.","At 8 yesterday, we were still eating.","At 8 yesterday we were still eating.","Yesterday, we were still eating at 8.","Yesterday we were still eating at 8.","We were still eating at eight o'clock yesterday.","We were still eating yesterday at eight o'clock.","Yesterday at eight o'clock, we were still eating.","Yesterday at eight o'clock we were still eating.","At eight o'clock yesterday, we were still eating.","At eight o'clock yesterday we were still eating.","Yesterday, we were still eating at eight o'clock.","Yesterday we were still eating at eight o'clock.","We were still eating at 8 o'clock yesterday.","We were still eating yesterday at 8 o'clock.","Yesterday at 8 o'clock, we were still eating.","Yesterday at 8 o'clock we were still eating.","At 8 o'clock yesterday, we were still eating.","At 8 o'clock yesterday we were still eating.","Yesterday, we were still eating at 8 o'clock.","Yesterday we were still eating at 8 o'clock."],"hint_text":"Ancora means still; stavamo mangiando describes the meal in progress.","explanation":"We were still eating at eight yesterday. Imperfetto stavamo plus mangiando presents the ongoing activity at that past time. Morning or evening is not specified.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"ongoing_past_scene"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0003-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0003-b10000000000","type":"fill_blank","prompt":"Do_____ (Next)","correct_answer":"po","hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Complete with the imperfetto indicative form of stare: Ieri alle otto noi ___ ancora mangiando.","correct_answer":"stavamo","hint_text":"Use the first-person plural form of stare in the imperfetto.","explanation":"Ieri alle otto noi stavamo ancora mangiando. Stavamo agrees with noi; the following gerund mangiando gives the action in progress.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"ongoing_past_scene"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0003-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0003-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Finalmente","Alla fine"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0003-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0003-b10000000000","type":"error_correction","prompt":"Find and correct the error: Pexsonaggio","metadata":{"error_sentence":"Pexsonaggio"},"correct_answer":"Personaggio","hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Correct the gerund of leggere in the sentence.","metadata":{"error_sentence":"Stavo leggiendo un libro quando Marco è arrivato.","correction_instruction":"Correct only the gerund of leggere in this past progressive sentence; keep every other word and the word order unchanged."},"correct_answer":"Stavo leggendo un libro quando Marco è arrivato.","hint_text":"The gerund is leggendo, without an i between gg and e.","explanation":"Stavo leggendo un libro quando Marco è arrivato. Replace leggiendo with leggendo. Stavo is already the correct imperfetto auxiliary for the requested first-person progressive.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"ongoing_past_scene"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0003-e00000000010","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0003-b10000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Fine\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Ending","options":["Ending","Plot","Next","While"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Yesterday we started dinner at eight. Marco arrived at half past eight, before we finished. Which sentence describes our meal at his arrival?","correct_answer":"Quando Marco è arrivato, stavamo ancora mangiando.","options":["Quando Marco è arrivato, avevamo già finito di mangiare.","Quando Marco è arrivato, stavamo ancora mangiando.","Cominceremo a mangiare soltanto domani.","Quando Marco è arrivato, non stavamo mangiando."],"hint_text":"The meal had begun but was not finished. Ancora means still.","explanation":"Quando Marco è arrivato, stavamo ancora mangiando. The progressive describes the ongoing meal. Avevamo già finito di mangiare would place its completion before the arrival, contrary to the stated scene.","distractors":["Quando Marco è arrivato, avevamo già finito di mangiare.","Cominceremo a mangiare soltanto domani.","Quando Marco è arrivato, non stavamo mangiando."],"skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"ongoing_past_scene"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0004-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Per prima cosa","Innanzitutto","Primo"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0004-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0004-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["After","Afterwards","Later"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0004-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0004-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Intanto","Frattanto"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0004-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0004-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Character","correct_answer":"Personaggio","metadata":{"tiles":["Personaggio"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “The character was about to open the letter when someone knocked on the door, breaking the room’s silence.” Start with “Il personaggio” and end with “della stanza.”.","correct_answer":"Il personaggio stava per aprire la lettera quando qualcuno ha bussato alla porta, interrompendo il silenzio della stanza.","metadata":{"tiles":["Il","personaggio","stava","per","aprire","la","lettera","quando","qualcuno","ha","bussato","alla","porta,","interrompendo","il","silenzio","della","stanza."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0004-e00000000010","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0004-b10000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"C''era una volta\" mean in English?"},"after":{"prompt":"What does \"C'era una volta\" mean in English?"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0005-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Poi","Successivamente"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0005-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Lastly","In the end"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0005-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0005-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Plot","correct_answer":"Trama","metadata":{"tiles":["Trama"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “The plot is set in a small village, where the houses overlook a river and everyone knows one another.” Start with “La trama” and end with “si conoscono.”.","correct_answer":"La trama si svolge in un piccolo paese, dove le case si affacciano su un fiume e tutti si conoscono.","metadata":{"tiles":["La","trama","si","svolge","in","un","piccolo","paese,","dove","le","case","si","affacciano","su","un","fiume","e","tutti","si","conoscono."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0006-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Finalmente","Alla fine"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0006-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["In the meantime"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0006-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0006-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Beginning","correct_answer":"Inizio","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["Inizio"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “At the beginning of the story, nobody knew why the stranger waited outside the station every night without speaking to anyone.” Start with “All'inizio della” and end with “con nessuno.”.","correct_answer":"All'inizio della storia nessuno sapeva perché lo sconosciuto aspettasse ogni notte davanti alla stazione senza parlare con nessuno.","accepted_answers":["All'inizio della storia nessuno sapeva perché lo sconosciuto aspettasse davanti alla stazione ogni notte senza parlare con nessuno.","All'inizio della storia nessuno sapeva perché lo sconosciuto ogni notte aspettasse davanti alla stazione senza parlare con nessuno."],"metadata":{"tiles":["All'inizio","della","storia","nessuno","sapeva","perché","lo","sconosciuto","aspettasse","ogni","notte","davanti","alla","stazione","senza","parlare","con","nessuno."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0006-e00000000010","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0006-b10000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"All''improvviso\" mean in English?"},"after":{"prompt":"What does \"All'improvviso\" mean in English?"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0001-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0001-b10000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Se\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"If","options":["Instead","Would","Perhaps","If"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"We have not decided what to do tomorrow. Our plan is: «Se domani piove, restiamo a casa». What condition is stated for staying at home?","correct_answer":"If it rains tomorrow.","options":["If it rains tomorrow.","If it is sunny tomorrow.","If it rained yesterday.","If we leave home."],"hint_text":"Se introduces the condition; domani locates it tomorrow.","explanation":"The condition is rain tomorrow; staying at home is the planned consequence. This plausible condition is not a claim that rain is certain, and the sentence does not state a sunny-weather plan.","distractors":["If it is sunny tomorrow.","If it rained yesterday.","If we leave home."],"skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"possible_future_condition"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0001-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","prompt":"Translate to Italian: Would","correct_answer":"Farebbe","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to Italian using the presente indicativo in both clauses: If it rains tomorrow, we will stay at home. Begin with Se and use piovere and restare.","correct_answer":"Se domani piove, restiamo a casa.","accepted_answers":["Se domani piove restiamo a casa.","Se piove domani, restiamo a casa.","Se piove domani restiamo a casa.","Se domani piove, noi restiamo a casa.","Se domani piove noi restiamo a casa.","Se piove domani, noi restiamo a casa.","Se piove domani noi restiamo a casa.","Se domani piove, allora restiamo a casa.","Se domani piove allora restiamo a casa.","Se piove domani, allora restiamo a casa.","Se piove domani allora restiamo a casa.","Se domani piove, allora noi restiamo a casa.","Se domani piove allora noi restiamo a casa.","Se piove domani, allora noi restiamo a casa.","Se piove domani allora noi restiamo a casa.","Se domani piove, noi allora restiamo a casa.","Se domani piove noi allora restiamo a casa.","Se piove domani, noi allora restiamo a casa.","Se piove domani noi allora restiamo a casa."],"hint_text":"Use piove in the condition and restiamo in the result. Noi is optional.","explanation":"Se domani piove, restiamo a casa. The present indicative can express this future plan because domani gives the time. Future forms are also possible in Italian conditional plans generally; this particular exercise explicitly selects present forms.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"possible_future_condition"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0001-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","prompt":"Translate to English: Potrebbe","correct_answer":"Could","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to English using will and walk, beginning with If the bus: Se domani l’autobus arriva in ritardo, andiamo a scuola a piedi.","correct_answer":"If the bus is late tomorrow, we will walk to school.","accepted_answers":["If the bus is late tomorrow we will walk to school.","If the bus is late tomorrow, we'll walk to school.","If the bus is late tomorrow we'll walk to school.","If the bus arrives late tomorrow, we will walk to school.","If the bus arrives late tomorrow we will walk to school.","If the bus arrives late tomorrow, we'll walk to school.","If the bus arrives late tomorrow we'll walk to school.","If the bus is running late tomorrow, we will walk to school.","If the bus is running late tomorrow we will walk to school.","If the bus is running late tomorrow, we'll walk to school.","If the bus is running late tomorrow we'll walk to school.","If the bus is delayed tomorrow, we will walk to school.","If the bus is delayed tomorrow we will walk to school.","If the bus is delayed tomorrow, we'll walk to school.","If the bus is delayed tomorrow we'll walk to school.","If the bus is late tomorrow, then we will walk to school.","If the bus is late tomorrow then we will walk to school.","If the bus is late tomorrow, then we'll walk to school.","If the bus is late tomorrow then we'll walk to school.","If the bus arrives late tomorrow, then we will walk to school.","If the bus arrives late tomorrow then we will walk to school.","If the bus arrives late tomorrow, then we'll walk to school.","If the bus arrives late tomorrow then we'll walk to school.","If the bus is running late tomorrow, then we will walk to school.","If the bus is running late tomorrow then we will walk to school.","If the bus is running late tomorrow, then we'll walk to school.","If the bus is running late tomorrow then we'll walk to school.","If the bus is delayed tomorrow, then we will walk to school.","If the bus is delayed tomorrow then we will walk to school.","If the bus is delayed tomorrow, then we'll walk to school.","If the bus is delayed tomorrow then we'll walk to school."],"hint_text":"In ritardo gives the condition; a piedi gives the way we will go to school.","explanation":"If the bus is late tomorrow, we will walk to school. The present indicative describes the conditional future plan in this context; it does not mean that we have already walked to school.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"possible_future_condition"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0001-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0001-b10000000000","type":"fill_blank","prompt":"Dovr_____ (Should)","correct_answer":"ebbe","hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Complete with the presente indicativo form of piovere: Se domani ___, restiamo a casa.","correct_answer":"piove","hint_text":"The impersonal weather verb uses the third-person singular form.","explanation":"Se domani piove, restiamo a casa. Piove is the requested present form of piovere. The future time comes from domani; no obligatory future-tense suffix is imposed by English will.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"possible_future_condition"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0001-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0001-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Desidero","Mi auguro"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0001-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0001-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Perhaps","correct_answer":"Forse","metadata":{"tiles":["Forse"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “If it rains tomorrow, perhaps we will stay at home and watch a film together instead of going to the park.” Start with “Se domani” and end with “al parco.”.","correct_answer":"Se domani pioverà, forse resteremo a casa e guarderemo un film insieme, invece di andare al parco.","metadata":{"tiles":["Se","domani","pioverà,","forse","resteremo","a","casa","e","guarderemo","un","film","insieme,","invece","di","andare","al","parco."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0001-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0001-b10000000000","type":"error_correction","prompt":"Find and correct the error: Imxagina","metadata":{"error_sentence":"Imxagina"},"correct_answer":"Immagina","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Correct the agreement of restare in the result clause.","metadata":{"error_sentence":"Se domani piove, noi resta a casa.","correction_instruction":"Correct only the presente indicativo form of restare so that it agrees with noi. Keep every other word and the word order unchanged."},"correct_answer":"Se domani piove, noi restiamo a casa.","accepted_answers":["Se domani piove noi restiamo a casa."],"hint_text":"The first-person plural present form is restiamo, not resta.","explanation":"Se domani piove, noi restiamo a casa. Restiamo agrees with the explicitly stated noi. The condition and the planned result otherwise already fit the selected present-indicative pattern.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"possible_future_condition"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0001-e00000000010","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0001-b10000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Altrimenti\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Otherwise","options":["Consequence","Otherwise","Perhaps","I wish"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Our plan is: «Se domani l’autobus arriva in ritardo, andiamo a scuola a piedi». If the bus is late tomorrow, what does this plan say we will do?","correct_answer":"We will walk to school.","options":["We will take a taxi to school.","We will stay at home.","We will walk to school.","We will cancel school."],"hint_text":"The result is andiamo a scuola a piedi.","explanation":"We will walk to school if the bus is late. No taxi, home stay or school cancellation is stated; neither is the plan for an on-time bus.","distractors":["We will take a taxi to school.","We will stay at home.","We will cancel school."],"skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"possible_future_condition"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0002-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0002-b10000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Farebbe\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Would","options":["Could","Instead","I wish","Would"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"The speaker does not own a car now and imagines a different situation: «Se avessi una macchina, andrei al mare in macchina». What is the imagined result?","correct_answer":"The speaker would go to the seaside by car.","options":["The speaker would go to the seaside by car.","The speaker already owns a car.","The speaker took a train yesterday.","The speaker would stay at home."],"hint_text":"Avessi sets up the imagined possession; andrei gives the conditional result.","explanation":"The imagined result is going to the seaside by car. The context says that the speaker does not currently own a car. This is not a report of a completed journey or a claim of actual ownership.","distractors":["The speaker already owns a car.","The speaker took a train yesterday.","The speaker would stay at home."],"skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"hypothetical_present_condition"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0002-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","prompt":"Translate to Italian: Could","correct_answer":"Potrebbe","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"I have little free time now. Translate this imagined alternative to Italian using avere in the congiuntivo imperfetto and leggere in the condizionale presente: If I had more time, I would read more.","correct_answer":"Se avessi più tempo, leggerei di più.","accepted_answers":["Se avessi più tempo, io leggerei di più.","Se avessi più tempo, allora leggerei di più.","Se avessi più tempo, allora io leggerei di più.","Se avessi più tempo, io allora leggerei di più.","Leggerei di più, se avessi più tempo.","Io leggerei di più, se avessi più tempo.","Se avessi più tempo leggerei di più.","Se avessi più tempo io leggerei di più.","Se avessi più tempo allora leggerei di più.","Se avessi più tempo allora io leggerei di più.","Se avessi più tempo io allora leggerei di più.","Leggerei di più se avessi più tempo.","Io leggerei di più se avessi più tempo.","Se avessi più tempo, leggerei più.","Se avessi più tempo, io leggerei più.","Se avessi più tempo, allora leggerei più.","Se avessi più tempo, allora io leggerei più.","Se avessi più tempo, io allora leggerei più.","Leggerei più, se avessi più tempo.","Io leggerei più, se avessi più tempo.","Se avessi più tempo leggerei più.","Se avessi più tempo io leggerei più.","Se avessi più tempo allora leggerei più.","Se avessi più tempo allora io leggerei più.","Se avessi più tempo io allora leggerei più.","Leggerei più se avessi più tempo.","Io leggerei più se avessi più tempo.","Se io avessi più tempo, leggerei di più.","Se io avessi più tempo, io leggerei di più.","Se io avessi più tempo, allora leggerei di più.","Se io avessi più tempo, allora io leggerei di più.","Se io avessi più tempo, io allora leggerei di più.","Leggerei di più, se io avessi più tempo.","Io leggerei di più, se io avessi più tempo.","Se io avessi più tempo leggerei di più.","Se io avessi più tempo io leggerei di più.","Se io avessi più tempo allora leggerei di più.","Se io avessi più tempo allora io leggerei di più.","Se io avessi più tempo io allora leggerei di più.","Leggerei di più se io avessi più tempo.","Io leggerei di più se io avessi più tempo.","Se io avessi più tempo, leggerei più.","Se io avessi più tempo, io leggerei più.","Se io avessi più tempo, allora leggerei più.","Se io avessi più tempo, allora io leggerei più.","Se io avessi più tempo, io allora leggerei più.","Leggerei più, se io avessi più tempo.","Io leggerei più, se io avessi più tempo.","Se io avessi più tempo leggerei più.","Se io avessi più tempo io leggerei più.","Se io avessi più tempo allora leggerei più.","Se io avessi più tempo allora io leggerei più.","Se io avessi più tempo io allora leggerei più.","Leggerei più se io avessi più tempo.","Io leggerei più se io avessi più tempo."],"hint_text":"Use avessi for the condition and leggerei for the result. Io is optional.","explanation":"Se avessi più tempo, leggerei di più. In this explicitly selected hypothetical-present pattern, the se clause uses congiuntivo imperfetto and the result uses condizionale presente. The same form names do not make this a past event. Other registers and conditional constructions are not universally excluded.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"hypothetical_present_condition"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0002-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","prompt":"Translate to English: Dovrebbe","correct_answer":"Should","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Marco is not rich now. Translate his imagined alternative to English using would, work and less: Se fossi ricco, lavorerei di meno.","correct_answer":"If I were rich, I would work less.","accepted_answers":["If I were rich, then I would work less.","I would work less, if I were rich.","If I were rich I would work less.","If I were rich then I would work less.","I would work less if I were rich.","If I were rich, I'd work less.","If I were rich, then I'd work less.","I'd work less, if I were rich.","If I were rich I'd work less.","If I were rich then I'd work less.","I'd work less if I were rich.","If I were wealthy, I would work less.","If I were wealthy, then I would work less.","I would work less, if I were wealthy.","If I were wealthy I would work less.","If I were wealthy then I would work less.","I would work less if I were wealthy.","If I were wealthy, I'd work less.","If I were wealthy, then I'd work less.","I'd work less, if I were wealthy.","If I were wealthy I'd work less.","If I were wealthy then I'd work less.","I'd work less if I were wealthy.","If I was rich, I would work less.","If I was rich, then I would work less.","I would work less, if I was rich.","If I was rich I would work less.","If I was rich then I would work less.","I would work less if I was rich.","If I was rich, I'd work less.","If I was rich, then I'd work less.","I'd work less, if I was rich.","If I was rich I'd work less.","If I was rich then I'd work less.","I'd work less if I was rich.","If I was wealthy, I would work less.","If I was wealthy, then I would work less.","I would work less, if I was wealthy.","If I was wealthy I would work less.","If I was wealthy then I would work less.","I would work less if I was wealthy.","If I was wealthy, I'd work less.","If I was wealthy, then I'd work less.","I'd work less, if I was wealthy.","If I was wealthy I'd work less.","If I was wealthy then I'd work less.","I'd work less if I was wealthy."],"hint_text":"Fossi ricco gives the imagined condition; lavorerei di meno gives the result.","explanation":"If I were rich, I would work less. The male speaker Marco accounts for ricco; the first-person forms report his own hypothetical alternative. Both hypothetical were and ordinary informal was are accepted in English.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"hypothetical_present_condition"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0002-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0002-b10000000000","type":"fill_blank","prompt":"Vor_____ (I wish)","correct_answer":"rei","hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"The speaker has little free time now. Complete with the first-person singular congiuntivo imperfetto of avere: Se io ___ più tempo, leggerei di più.","correct_answer":"avessi","hint_text":"The requested io form is avessi, not the conditional avrei.","explanation":"Se io avessi più tempo, leggerei di più. Avessi supplies the selected subjunctive form for this imagined present condition; leggerei is already the conditional result. This is not a rule about se meaning whether in an indirect question.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"hypothetical_present_condition"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0002-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0002-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Magari"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0002-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0002-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Imagine","correct_answer":"Immagina","metadata":{"tiles":["Immagina"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “Imagine what you would do if you had a whole year free to travel and did not have to worry about expenses.” Start with “Immagina che” and end with “delle spese.”.","correct_answer":"Immagina che cosa faresti se avessi un anno libero per viaggiare e non dovessi preoccuparti delle spese.","metadata":{"tiles":["Immagina","che","cosa","faresti","se","avessi","un","anno","libero","per","viaggiare","e","non","dovessi","preoccuparti","delle","spese."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0002-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0002-b10000000000","type":"error_correction","prompt":"Find and correct the error: Suxponiamo","metadata":{"error_sentence":"Suxponiamo"},"correct_answer":"Supponiamo","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Correct the agreement of the conditional result with io.","metadata":{"error_sentence":"Se io avessi più tempo, io leggerebbe di più.","correction_instruction":"The speaker imagines having more time now. Correct only the condizionale presente form of leggere so that it agrees with io. Keep every other word and the word order unchanged."},"correct_answer":"Se io avessi più tempo, io leggerei di più.","accepted_answers":["Se io avessi più tempo io leggerei di più."],"hint_text":"Io takes leggerei; leggerebbe is the third-person singular.","explanation":"Se io avessi più tempo, io leggerei di più. Change leggerebbe to leggerei. The repeated io is permitted and must remain because this task requests correction of only the verb form.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"hypothetical_present_condition"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0002-e00000000010","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0002-b10000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Rimpianto\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Regret","options":["Regret","Would","Instead","I wish"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Lea has very little time today and says: «Se avessi più tempo adesso, ti verrei a trovare». What kind of situation is she describing?","correct_answer":"An imagined situation with more time now.","options":["An imagined situation with more time now.","A completed trip last year.","A confirmed appointment tomorrow.","A statement that the speaker already has plenty of time."],"hint_text":"Adesso means now; avessi and verrei describe an imagined alternative to the stated facts.","explanation":"Lea imagines having more time now and visiting under that condition. Congiuntivo imperfetto avessi does not make the hypothesis a past-time event here. She is not confirming a future appointment or claiming abundant current time.","distractors":["A completed trip last year.","A confirmed appointment tomorrow.","A statement that the speaker already has plenty of time."],"skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"hypothetical_present_condition"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0003-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Dovrei","Dovresti","Dovremmo"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0003-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["I would like","I'd like"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0003-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0003-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Immagini","Immaginate","Immaginiamo","Immaginare"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0003-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0003-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Suppose","correct_answer":"Supponiamo","metadata":{"tiles":["Supponiamo"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “Suppose you lose your passport abroad: it would be better to contact the consulate and ask which documents are needed.” Start with “Supponiamo che” and end with “documenti servono.”.","correct_answer":"Supponiamo che tu perda il passaporto all'estero: sarebbe meglio contattare il consolato e chiedere quali documenti servono.","metadata":{"tiles":["Supponiamo","che","tu","perda","il","passaporto","all'estero:","sarebbe","meglio","contattare","il","consolato","e","chiedere","quali","documenti","servono."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0004-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Desidero","Mi auguro"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0004-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0004-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Maybe"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0004-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0004-b10000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["ginate","giniamo","ginare"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0004-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0004-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Supponi","Supponete","Supponga","Supporre"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0004-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0004-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Instead","correct_answer":"Invece","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["Invece"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “I have to study for the exam, but instead I would like to spend the afternoon at the seaside with my friends.” Start with “Devo studiare” and end with “miei amici.”.","correct_answer":"Devo studiare per l'esame, ma invece vorrei passare il pomeriggio al mare con i miei amici.","accepted_answers":["Devo studiare per l'esame, ma vorrei invece passare il pomeriggio al mare con i miei amici.","Devo studiare per l'esame, ma vorrei passare invece il pomeriggio al mare con i miei amici."],"metadata":{"tiles":["Devo","studiare","per","l'es