r experiences influence how we interpret facts and choose which explanations to consider plausible.” Start with “Sebbene cerchiamo” and end with “considerare plausibili.”.","correct_answer":"Sebbene cerchiamo la verità, le nostre esperienze influenzano il modo in cui interpretiamo i fatti e scegliamo quali spiegazioni considerare plausibili.","metadata":{"tiles":["Sebbene","cerchiamo","la","verità,","le","nostre","esperienze","influenzano","il","modo","in","cui","interpretiamo","i","fatti","e","scegliamo","quali","spiegazioni","considerare","plausibili."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Fine","Finalità","Obiettivo"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Conscience","Awareness"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0002-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0002-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Wisdom","correct_answer":"Saggezza","metadata":{"tiles":["Saggezza"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “Wisdom does not consist in having all the answers, but in recognizing the limits of one’s convictions and knowing how to question them.” Start with “La saggezza” and end with “in discussione.”.","correct_answer":"La saggezza non consiste nel possedere tutte le risposte, ma nel riconoscere i limiti delle proprie convinzioni e nel saperle mettere in discussione.","metadata":{"tiles":["La","saggezza","non","consiste","nel","possedere","tutte","le","risposte,","ma","nel","riconoscere","i","limiti","delle","proprie","convinzioni","e","nel","saperle","mettere","in","discussione."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Consapevolezza"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Morality"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0003-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0003-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Sapienza"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0003-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Belief","correct_answer":"Credenza","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["Credenza"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “A deeply rooted belief can withstand even contrary evidence, especially when it helps define a person’s or a group’s identity.” Start with “Una credenza” and end with “un gruppo.”.","correct_answer":"Una credenza profondamente radicata può resistere anche a prove contrarie, soprattutto quando contribuisce a definire l'identità di una persona o di un gruppo.","accepted_answers":["Una credenza profondamente radicata può anche resistere a prove contrarie, soprattutto quando contribuisce a definire l'identità di una persona o di un gruppo."],"metadata":{"tiles":["Una","credenza","profondamente","radicata","può","resistere","anche","a","prove","contrarie,","soprattutto","quando","contribuisce","a","definire","l'identità","di","una","persona","o","di","un","gruppo."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0004-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0004-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Convinzione","Fede"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0004-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Doubt","correct_answer":"Dubbio","metadata":{"tiles":["Dubbio"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “The doubt raised by these data requires us to reexamine the initial conclusion rather than defend it merely because it matches our expectations.” Start with “Il dubbio” and end with “nostre aspettative.”.","correct_answer":"Il dubbio sollevato da questi dati ci impone di riesaminare la conclusione iniziale, anziché difenderla soltanto perché coincide con le nostre aspettative.","metadata":{"tiles":["Il","dubbio","sollevato","da","questi","dati","ci","impone","di","riesaminare","la","conclusione","iniziale,","anziché","difenderla","soltanto","perché","coincide","con","le","nostre","aspettative."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Morale","Etica"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0005-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0005-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Incertezza"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0005-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0005-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Freedom","correct_answer":"Libertà","metadata":{"tiles":["Libertà"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “Individual freedom must be considered together with responsibility toward others, since a personal choice can have consequences affecting the whole community.” Start with “La libertà” and end with “l'intera comunità.”.","correct_answer":"La libertà individuale va considerata insieme alla responsabilità verso gli altri, poiché una scelta personale può avere conseguenze che riguardano l'intera comunità.","metadata":{"tiles":["La","libertà","individuale","va","considerata","insieme","alla","responsabilità","verso","gli","altri,","poiché","una","scelta","personale","può","avere","conseguenze","che","riguardano","l'intera","comunità."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0006-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0006-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Justice","correct_answer":"Giustizia","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["Giustizia"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “For there to be justice, applying the same rule to everyone is not enough: we must also assess whether their starting conditions are truly comparable.” Start with “Perché ci” and end with “davvero comparabili.”.","correct_answer":"Perché ci sia giustizia, non basta applicare la stessa regola a tutti: occorre valutare anche se le condizioni di partenza siano davvero comparabili.","accepted_answers":["Perché ci sia giustizia, non basta applicare la stessa regola a tutti: occorre anche valutare se le condizioni di partenza siano davvero comparabili."],"metadata":{"tiles":["Perché","ci","sia","giustizia,","non","basta","applicare","la","stessa","regola","a","tutti:","occorre","valutare","anche","se","le","condizioni","di","partenza","siano","davvero","comparabili."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Convincere"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Proof"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0001-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0001-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["rgomentazione"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0001-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0001-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Smentire"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0001-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0001-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Claim","correct_answer":"Affermazione","metadata":{"tiles":["Affermazione"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “This claim is convincing only if it is supported by verifiable evidence and takes account of objections that could call its validity into question.” Start with “Questa affermazione” and end with “la validità.”.","correct_answer":"Questa affermazione risulta convincente soltanto se è sostenuta da prove verificabili e se tiene conto delle obiezioni che potrebbero metterne in dubbio la validità.","metadata":{"tiles":["Questa","affermazione","risulta","convincente","soltanto","se","è","sostenuta","da","prove","verificabili","e","se","tiene","conto","delle","obiezioni","che","potrebbero","metterne","in","dubbio","la","validità."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Elementi di prova"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0002-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0002-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Asserzione","Tesi"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0002-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0002-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Fallacy","correct_answer":"Fallacia","metadata":{"tiles":["Fallacia"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “Attacking the person presenting a thesis instead of examining the reasons supporting it is a fallacy and does not constitute a real counterargument.” Start with “Attaccare la” and end with “vero controargomento.”.","correct_answer":"Attaccare la persona che presenta una tesi, invece di esaminare le ragioni che la sostengono, è una fallacia e non costituisce un vero controargomento.","metadata":{"tiles":["Attaccare","la","persona","che","presenta","una","tesi,","invece","di","esaminare","le","ragioni","che","la","sostengono,","è","una","fallacia","e","non","costituisce","un","vero","controargomento."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Controargomentazione","Obiezione"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Nevertheless","Nonetheless","Yet"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0003-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0003-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Sofisma","Errore logico"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0003-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Rhetoric","correct_answer":"Retorica","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["Retorica"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “Although the speech’s rhetoric is persuasive, the speaker has not yet explained how he intends to finance the project without reducing existing services.” Start with “Sebbene la” and end with “servizi esistenti.”.","correct_answer":"Sebbene la retorica del discorso sia persuasiva, il relatore non ha ancora spiegato come intenda finanziare il progetto senza ridurre i servizi esistenti.","accepted_answers":["Sebbene la retorica del discorso sia persuasiva, il relatore non ha spiegato ancora come intenda finanziare il progetto senza ridurre i servizi esistenti."],"metadata":{"tiles":["Sebbene","la","retorica","del","discorso","sia","persuasiva,","il","relatore","non","ha","ancora","spiegato","come","intenda","finanziare","il","progetto","senza","ridurre","i","servizi","esistenti."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0004-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Controargomento\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Counterargument","options":["To persuade","Rhetoric","Counterargument","To refute"],"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","hint_text":null,"explanation":null},"after":{"prompt":"Read this argument:\nL’azienda ha cento dipendenti. Due di loro oggi sono stati scortesi con me. Quindi tutti i dipendenti dell’azienda sono scortesi.\n\nWhich criticism identifies the reasoning error?","correct_answer":"It judges all one hundred employees from the behaviour of only two.","options":["It attacks a person’s origin instead of examining their evidence.","It judges all one hundred employees from the behaviour of only two.","It treats a later event as the cause of an earlier event.","It claims that an opinion is true because most people believe it."],"distractors":["It attacks a person’s origin instead of examining their evidence.","It treats a later event as the cause of an earlier event.","It claims that an opinion is true because most people believe it."],"skill_type":"mixed","hint_text":"Compare the number of people actually observed with the number covered by the conclusion.","explanation":"Due di loro refers to two of the hundred employees; quindi introduces the conclusion about tutti, all of them. The observation concerns only two of one hundred employees and does not justify a categorical judgment about all of them: this is a hasty generalization. The problem is insufficient support; it does not prove that the opposite conclusion is true."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Però","Nondimeno","Ciononostante"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0004-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Nonetheless","However"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0004-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Bias","correct_answer":"Pregiudizio","metadata":{"tiles":["Pregiudizio"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “A prejudice can lead us to dismiss testimony based on the speaker’s identity instead of assessing its content and reliability.” Start with “Un pregiudizio” and end with “e l'attendibilità.”.","correct_answer":"Un pregiudizio può portarci a scartare una testimonianza sulla base dell'identità di chi parla, invece di valutarne il contenuto e l'attendibilità.","metadata":{"tiles":["Un","pregiudizio","può","portarci","a","scartare","una","testimonianza","sulla","base","dell'identità","di","chi","parla,","invece","di","valutarne","il","contenuto","e","l'attendibilità."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0004-e00000000010","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Argomento\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Argument","options":["Fallacy","Bias","Nevertheless","Argument"],"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","hint_text":null,"explanation":null},"after":{"prompt":"Read this argument:\nIl Comune ha installato nuovi lampioni. Un mese dopo è aumentato il numero dei visitatori. Questo dimostra che i nuovi lampioni hanno causato l’aumento.\n\nWhich response directly addresses the reasoning error?","correct_answer":"The increase came later, but that timing alone does not establish its cause.","options":["The timing alone proves that the new lamps caused the increase.","The increase proves that the lamps could not have had any effect.","The passage says that visitor numbers rose before the lamps were installed.","The increase came later, but that timing alone does not establish its cause."],"distractors":["The timing alone proves that the new lamps caused the increase.","The increase proves that the lamps could not have had any effect.","The passage says that visitor numbers rose before the lamps were installed."],"skill_type":"mixed","hint_text":"Separate the order of events from evidence about what caused the change.","explanation":"Un mese dopo expresses time order; questo dimostra che introduces the speaker’s claim of proof. Later does not by itself mean caused by: this is a post hoc causal inference. The lamps might have contributed, but the passage provides no evidence separating their effect from other possible causes. The justified response questions the claimed proof, not the possibility of an effect."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Tuttavia","Ciononostante","Ciò nonostante"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Moreover","Also"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0005-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Parzialità","Preconcetto"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0005-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Argument","correct_answer":"Argomento","metadata":{"tiles":["Argomento"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “Before rejecting your argument, I would like to clarify which premises you consider indispensable and how they lead to the conclusion you propose to us.” Start with “Prima di” and end with “ci propone.”.","correct_answer":"Prima di respingere il suo argomento, vorrei chiarire quali premesse ritenga indispensabili e in che modo esse conducano alla conclusione che ci propone.","metadata":{"tiles":["Prima","di","respingere","il","suo","argomento,","vorrei","chiarire","quali","premesse","ritenga","indispensabili","e","in","che","modo","esse","conducano","alla","conclusione","che","ci","propone."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Oltretutto","Per di più"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["To disprove"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0006-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0006-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Argomentazione"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0006-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0006-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: To persuade","correct_answer":"Persuadere","metadata":{"tiles":["Persuadere"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “To persuade a skeptical audience, it is useful to anticipate possible objections and respond with verifiable reasons, without confusing a confident tone with solid evidence.” Start with “Per persuadere” and end with “delle prove.”.","correct_answer":"Per persuadere un pubblico scettico, è utile anticipare le possibili obiezioni e rispondere con ragioni verificabili, senza confondere la sicurezza del tono con la solidità delle prove.","metadata":{"tiles":["Per","persuadere","un","pubblico","scettico,","è","utile","anticipare","le","possibili","obiezioni","e","rispondere","con","ragioni","verificabili,","senza","confondere","la","sicurezza","del","tono","con","la","solidità","delle","prove."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4003-0001-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4003-0001-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Programma"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4003-0001-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4003-0001-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Minutes","correct_answer":"Verbale","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["Verbale"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “I am sending you the meeting minutes attached so that you can verify the agreements reached and point out any inaccuracies before the document’s final approval.” Start with “Le invio” and end with “del documento.”.","correct_answer":"Le invio in allegato il verbale della riunione affinché possa verificare gli accordi raggiunti e segnalare eventuali inesattezze prima dell'approvazione definitiva del documento.","accepted_answers":["Le invio il verbale della riunione in allegato affinché possa verificare gli accordi raggiunti e segnalare eventuali inesattezze prima dell'approvazione definitiva del documento."],"metadata":{"tiles":["Le","invio","in","allegato","il","verbale","della","riunione","affinché","possa","verificare","gli","accordi","raggiunti","e","segnalare","eventuali","inesattezze","prima","dell'approvazione","definitiva","del","documento."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4003-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4003-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["To carry out","To put into practice"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4003-0002-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4003-0002-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Verbali"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4003-0002-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4003-0002-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: To delegate","correct_answer":"Delegare","metadata":{"tiles":["Delegare"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “In the presentation, I will explain why delegating some tasks does not mean giving up responsibility for the result, but distributing work to make the most of everyone’s skills.” Start with “Nella presentazione” and end with “di ciascuno.”.","correct_answer":"Nella presentazione spiegherò perché delegare alcuni compiti non significa rinunciare alla responsabilità del risultato, ma distribuire il lavoro valorizzando le competenze di ciascuno.","metadata":{"tiles":["Nella","presentazione","spiegherò","perché","delegare","alcuni","compiti","non","significa","rinunciare","alla","responsabilità","del","risultato,","ma","distribuire","il","lavoro","valorizzando","le","competenze","di","ciascuno."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4003-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4003-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Attuare","Mettere in pratica","Realizzare"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4003-0003-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4003-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Efficiency","correct_answer":"Efficienza","metadata":{"tiles":["Efficienza"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “We would be willing to accept the proposed deadline provided that the new process improves efficiency without compromising quality and allows the results obtained to be checked.” Start with “Saremmo disposti” and end with “risultati ottenuti.”.","correct_answer":"Saremmo disposti ad accettare la scadenza proposta, purché il nuovo processo migliori l'efficienza senza compromettere la qualità e permetta di verificare i risultati ottenuti.","metadata":{"tiles":["Saremmo","disposti","ad","accettare","la","scadenza","proposta,","purché","il","nuovo","processo","migliori","l'efficienza","senza","compromettere","la","qualità","e","permetta","di","verificare","i","risultati","ottenuti."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4003-0004-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4003-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Deadline","correct_answer":"Scadenza","metadata":{"tiles":["Scadenza"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “I propose extending the deadline by two weeks so that the team can assess the outstanding risks before formulating a final recommendation.” Start with “Propongo di” and end with “raccomandazione definitiva.”.","correct_answer":"Propongo di prorogare la scadenza di due settimane, in modo che il gruppo possa valutare i rischi ancora aperti prima di formulare una raccomandazione definitiva.","metadata":{"tiles":["Propongo","di","prorogare","la","scadenza","di","due","settimane,","in","modo","che","il","gruppo","possa","valutare","i","rischi","ancora","aperti","prima","di","formulare","una","raccomandazione","definitiva."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4003-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4003-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Bilancio preventivo"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4003-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4003-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Interested party"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4003-0005-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4003-0005-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Termine"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4003-0005-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4003-0005-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Negotiation","correct_answer":"Negoziazione","metadata":{"tiles":["Negoziazione"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “Following our meeting at the conference, I would like to continue negotiating the terms of possible cooperation, also involving the leaders of our respective teams.” Start with “Dopo il” and end with “di lavoro.”.","correct_answer":"Dopo il nostro incontro al convegno, mi piacerebbe proseguire la negoziazione sulle condizioni di una possibile collaborazione, coinvolgendo anche i responsabili dei rispettivi gruppi di lavoro.","metadata":{"tiles":["Dopo","il","nostro","incontro","al","convegno,","mi","piacerebbe","proseguire","la","negoziazione","sulle","condizioni","di","una","possibile","col