duction is controversial, many critics consider the play a masterpiece of contemporary theater.” Use ordinary subject-before-verb order in declarative clauses when a noun or pronoun subject is supplied. Start with “Embora a” and end with “teatro contemporâneo.”.","correct_answer":"Embora a montagem seja controversa, muitos críticos consideram a peça uma obra-prima do teatro contemporâneo.","metadata":{"tiles":["Embora","a","montagem","seja","controversa,","muitos","críticos","consideram","a","peça","uma","obra-prima","do","teatro","contemporâneo."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-5555-4004-0004-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Escultura\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Sculpture","options":["Poem","Sculpture","Plot twist","Masterpiece"],"distractors":[]},"after":{"prompt":"Read this concert review: « No trecho final, a intensidade sonora da orquestra diminui gradualmente, enquanto a melodia principal se repete. » What change in volume does the reviewer describe?","correct_answer":"The orchestra gradually plays more softly.","options":["The orchestra maintains exactly the same volume.","The orchestra gradually plays more softly.","The orchestra gradually plays more loudly.","The orchestra suddenly stops playing."],"distractors":["The orchestra maintains exactly the same volume.","The orchestra gradually plays more loudly.","The orchestra suddenly stops playing."]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-5555-4004-0004-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Inspiration","correct_answer":"Inspiração","metadata":{"tiles":["Inspiração"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “The musician found inspiration in local rhythms, which he reinterpreted to create his own sound.” Use ordinary subject-before-verb order in declarative clauses when a noun or pronoun subject is supplied. Start with “O músico” and end with “sonoridade própria.”.","correct_answer":"O músico encontrou inspiração nos ritmos locais, que reinterpretou para criar uma sonoridade própria.","metadata":{"tiles":["O","músico","encontrou","inspiração","nos","ritmos","locais,","que","reinterpretou","para","criar","uma","sonoridade","própria."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-5555-4004-0004-e00000000010","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Romance\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Novel","options":["Genre","Novel","Symbolism","Protagonist"],"distractors":[]},"after":{"prompt":"Which change does « o andamento acelera » describe in a music review?","correct_answer":"The music gets faster.","options":["The music starts again.","The music gets slower.","The music gets quieter.","The music gets faster."],"distractors":["The music starts again.","The music gets slower.","The music gets quieter."]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-5555-4004-0005-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-4004-0005-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Novel","correct_answer":"Romance","metadata":{"tiles":["Romance"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “In my novel, I intend to alternate narrators so that the reader notices the contradictions between their accounts.” Use ordinary subject-before-verb order in declarative clauses when a noun or pronoun subject is supplied. Start with “No meu” and end with “suas versões.”.","correct_answer":"No meu romance, pretendo alternar os narradores para que o leitor perceba as contradições entre suas versões.","metadata":{"tiles":["No","meu","romance,","pretendo","alternar","os","narradores","para","que","o","leitor","perceba","as","contradições","entre","suas","versões."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":