}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “This robot can move on its own even without human instructions.” Start with “このロボットは、” and end with “自分で動けます。”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"このロボットは、人の指示がなくても自分で動けます。","metadata":{"tiles":["この","ロボットは、","人の","指示が","なくても","自分で","動けます。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-0001-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["その後","そして"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-0001-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["All of a sudden","Abruptly"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-0001-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-0001-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["最初に","初めに","第一に"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-0001-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-0001-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Next","correct_answer":"次に","metadata":{"tiles":["次に"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “Next, the main character noticed a voice coming from the other side of the door.” Start with “次に主人公は” and end with “声に気づきました。”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"次に主人公は扉の向こうから聞こえる声に気づきました。","metadata":{"tiles":["次に","主人公は","扉の","向こうから","聞こえる","声に","気づきました。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-0002-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["急に"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-0002-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["During"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-0002-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-0002-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["その次に"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-0002-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-0002-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Finally","correct_answer":"最後に","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["最後に"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “Finally, we were able to return the wallet we had found to its owner.” Start with “最後に、私たちは” and end with “返すことができました。”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"最後に、私たちは見つけた財布を持ち主に返すことができました。","accepted_answers":["最後に、私たちは持ち主に見つけた財布を返すことができました。"],"metadata":{"tiles":["最後に、","私たちは","見つけた","財布を","持ち主に","返すことが","できました。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-0003-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-0003-b10000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"突然\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Suddenly","options":["While","Finally","Suddenly","Then"],"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"昨夜八時、ミナは本を読んでいました。九時に本を閉じました。八時にミナは何をしていましたか。","correct_answer":"Mina was reading a book.","options":["Mina was closing the book.","Mina was buying a book.","Mina was writing a book.","Mina was reading a book."],"explanation":"読んでいました describes the reading in progress at eight. The separate closing event, 本を閉じました, happens at nine.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"past -ていました for an action in progress"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-0003-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","prompt":"Translate to Japanese: While","correct_answer":"の間に","accepted_answers":[],"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to Japanese: At eight last night, I was reading a book. Use 昨夜八時に and 本を; put 読む into the polite -ていました form and omit the understood subject.","correct_answer":"昨夜八時に本を読んでいました。","accepted_answers":["昨夜八時に、本を読んでいました。","本を昨夜八時に読んでいました。","昨夜8時に本を読んでいました。","昨夜８時に本を読んでいました。","昨夜八時に本をよんでいました。","昨夜8時に本をよんでいました。","昨夜８時に本をよんでいました。","昨夜8時に、本を読んでいました。","昨夜８時に、本を読んでいました。","昨夜八時に、本をよんでいました。","昨夜8時に、本をよんでいました。","昨夜８時に、本をよんでいました。","本を昨夜8時に読んでいました。","本を昨夜８時に読んでいました。","本を昨夜八時によんでいました。","本を昨夜8時によんでいました。","本を昨夜８時によんでいました。"],"explanation":"読む takes the て-form 読んで, producing 読んでいました for the requested polite past progressive. The reader is understood as the speaker in this translation context, so no explicit 私 is needed. The provided time and object phrases bound this form-focused task.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"読む → 読んでいました"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-0003-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","prompt":"Translate to English: まず","correct_answer":"First","accepted_answers":[],"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to English: 私が一冊の本を読んでいたとき、電話が鳴りました。","correct_answer":"I was reading a book when the phone rang.","accepted_answers":["When the phone rang, I was reading a book.","When the phone rang I was reading a book.","The phone rang while I was reading a book.","While I was reading a book, the phone rang.","While I was reading a book the phone rang.","The phone rang when I was reading a book.","When I was reading a book, the phone rang.","When I was reading a book the phone rang.","I was reading a book when a phone rang.","When a phone rang, I was reading a book.","When a phone rang I was reading a book.","A phone rang while I was reading a book.","While I was reading a book, a phone rang.","While I was reading a book a phone rang.","A phone rang when I was reading a book.","When I was reading a book, a phone rang.","When I was reading a book a phone rang.","I was reading one book when the phone rang.","When the phone rang, I was reading one book.","When the phone rang I was reading one book.","The phone rang while I was reading one book.","While I was reading one book, the phone rang.","While I was reading one book the phone rang.","The phone rang when I was reading one book.","When I was reading one book, the phone rang.","When I was reading one book the phone rang.","I was reading one book when a phone rang.","When a phone rang, I was reading one book.","When a phone rang I was reading one book.","A phone rang while I was reading one book.","While I was reading one book, a phone rang.","While I was reading one book a phone rang.","A phone rang when I was reading one book.","When I was reading one book, a phone rang.","When I was reading one book a phone rang."],"explanation":"読んでいたとき sets the ongoing reading as the time background for 電話が鳴りました, “the phone rang.” 一冊の本 is one book. Japanese does not mark an English definite or indefinite article on 電話, so both “the phone” and “a phone” are possible.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"past action in progress + とき event"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-0003-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-0003-b10000000000","type":"fill_blank","prompt":"次_____ (Next)","correct_answer":"に","explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Complete with the past form of います: 電話が鳴ったとき、私は本を読んで___。","correct_answer":"いました","explanation":"The past form of います is いました. 読んでいました describes the reading in progress at the time the phone rang.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"polite past -ていました"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-0003-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-0003-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":