":"真実","metadata":{"tiles":["真実"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “What we believe to be true is not necessarily based on fact.” Start with “私たちが真実だと” and end with “事実に基づいているとは限りません。”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"私たちが真実だと信じていることが、必ずしも事実に基づいているとは限りません。","metadata":{"tiles":["私たちが","真実だと","信じている","ことが、","必ずしも","事実に","基づいているとは限りません。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Awareness"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0002-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0002-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["理学"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0002-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0002-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["真理"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0002-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0002-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Wisdom","correct_answer":"知恵","metadata":{"tiles":["知恵"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “Wisdom is reflected not only in the amount of knowledge one has, but also in a willingness to understand different values.” Start with “知恵とは、知識の” and end with “姿勢にも表れるものです。”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"知恵とは、知識の量だけでなく、異なる価値観を理解する姿勢にも表れるものです。","metadata":{"tiles":["知恵とは、","知識の","量だけでなく、","異なる価値観を","理解する","姿勢にも","表れるものです。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Morals"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0003-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0003-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["徳性"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0003-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Belief","correct_answer":"信念","metadata":{"tiles":["信念"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “Holding strong convictions is compatible with being open to new evidence.” Start with “強い信念を” and end with “姿勢は両立します。”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"強い信念を持つことと、新しい証拠を受け入れる姿勢は両立します。","metadata":{"tiles":["強い","信念を","持つことと、","新しい証拠を","受け入れる","姿勢は","両立します。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["倫理学"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0004-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Morals"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0004-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0004-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["信仰"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0004-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Doubt","correct_answer":"疑い","metadata":{"tiles":["疑い"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “It is precisely because we doubted that conclusion that we need to reconsider the assumptions.” Start with “その結論に” and end with “見直す必要があるのです。”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"その結論に疑いを持ったからこそ、前提を見直す必要があるのです。","metadata":{"tiles":["その","結論に","疑いを","持ったからこそ、","前提を","見直す必要が","あるのです。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["道徳性"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Being","Presence"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0005-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0005-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["疑念"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0005-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0005-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Freedom","correct_answer":"自由","metadata":{"tiles":["自由"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “Individual freedom cannot be separated from the responsibility to respect the rights of others.” Start with “個人の自由は、” and end with “責任と切り離せません。”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"個人の自由は、他者の権利を尊重する責任と切り離せません。","metadata":{"tiles":["個人の","自由は、","他者の","権利を","尊重する","責任と","切り離せません。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0006-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0006-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","options":["Purpose","Freedom","Morality","Ethics"]},"after":{"options":["Purpose","Freedom","Morality","Existence"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0006-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0006-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Justice","correct_answer":"正義","metadata":{"tiles":["正義"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “The meaning of justice can vary depending on whose perspective one adopts.” Start with “正義の意味は、” and end with “よって変わり得ます。”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"正義の意味は、誰の立場から考えるかによって変わり得ます。","metadata":{"tiles":["正義の","意味は、","誰の","立場から","考えるかに","よって","変わり得ます。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["説き伏せる"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Proof"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0001-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0001-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["論破する","反証する"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0001-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0001-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Claim","correct_answer":"主張","metadata":{"tiles":["主張"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “Making a persuasive claim requires presenting specific evidence.” Start with “説得力のある主張には、” and end with “ことが求められます。”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"説得力のある主張には、具体的な根拠を示すことが求められます。","metadata":{"tiles":["説得力のある","主張には、","具体的な","根拠を","示す","ことが","求められます。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Rebuttal","Objection"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0002-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0002-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["かしながら"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0002-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0002-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["言い分"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0002-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0002-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Fallacy","correct_answer":"詭弁","metadata":{"tiles":["詭弁"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “Even if you feel that the other person’s explanation is sophistry, you should show specifically where the problem lies.” Start with “相手の説明が” and end with “具体的に示すべきです。”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"相手の説明が詭弁だと感じても、どこに問題があるのかを具体的に示すべきです。","metadata":{"tiles":["相手の","説明が","詭弁だと","感じても、","どこに問題があるのかを","具体的に","示すべきです。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["対論"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["But","Yet"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0003-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0003-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["にもかかわらず"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0003-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0003-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["誤謬"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0003-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Rhetoric","correct_answer":"修辞学","metadata":{"tiles":["修辞学"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “By studying rhetoric, you can analyze the effectiveness of expressions that appeal to the listener’s emotions.” Start with “修辞学を学ぶことで、” and end with “表現の効果を分析できます。”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"修辞学を学ぶことで、聞き手の感情に訴える表現の効果を分析できます。","metadata":{"tiles":["修辞学を","学ぶことで、","聞き手の","感情に","訴える","表現の効果を","分析できます。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0004-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"反論\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Counterargument","options":["Fallacy","Counterargument","However","To refute"],"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Evaluate this argument:「このカフェを二度利用したが、どちらも料理が出てくるまで長く待った。だから、この町のカフェはどこも、いつ行っても料理が出てくるのが遅いはずだ。」 Why do the observations not justify the conclusion?","correct_answer":"It generalizes from two visits to one café to every café in the town.","options":["It treats a low price as proof of fast service.","It generalizes from two visits to one café to every café in the town.","It treats a popular belief as proof that the belief is true.","It rejects a claim solely because of the person who made it."],"explanation":"Two visits to one café do not establish what happens at every café, every time. This is an unsupported generalization from a very limited sample. The claim might happen to be true or false; these observations do not justify it.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["しかしながら","だが"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0004-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Nonetheless","Still","Even so","All the same"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0004-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["らには"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0004-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["レトリック"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0004-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Bias","correct_answer":"偏見","metadata":{"tiles":["偏見"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “Judging an entire group from a single case can end up reinforcing prejudice.” Start with “一つの事例だけで” and end with “強めることにつながりかねません。”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"一つの事例だけで集団全体を判断するのは、偏見を強めることにつながりかねません。","metadata":{"tiles":["一つの","事例だけで","集団全体を","判断するのは、","偏見を","強めることに","つながりかねません。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["それにもかかわらず","にもかかわらず"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Moreover","In addition","Further"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0005-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["バイアス","先入観"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0005-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Argument","correct_answer":"議論","metadata":{"tiles":["議論"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “To deepen the discussion, it is important not only to answer counterarguments but also to confirm shared assumptions.” Start with “議論を深めるためには、” and end with “確認することも重要です。”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"議論を深めるためには、反論に答えるだけでなく、共通の前提を確認することも重要です。","metadata":{"tiles":["議論を","深めるためには、","反論に","答えるだけでなく、","共通の前提を","確認することも","重要です。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["その上","加えて"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Refute","Rebut"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0006-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0006-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: To persuade","correct_answer":"説得する","metadata":{"tiles":["説得する"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “I think that simply repeating that you are right is not enough to persuade someone.” Start with “相手を説得するには、” and end with “不十分だと思います。”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"相手を説得するには、自分が正しいと繰り返すだけでは不十分だと思います。","metadata":{"tiles":["相手を","説得するには、","自分が","正しいと","繰り返すだけでは","不十分だと","思います。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["提議"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0001-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0001-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["議事日程","アジェンダ"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0001-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0001-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Minutes","correct_answer":"議事録","metadata":{"tiles":["議事録"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “Please review the attached meeting minutes and let me know by tomorrow which parts need correction.” Start with “添付の議事録を” and end with “明日までにお知らせください。”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"添付の議事録をご確認のうえ、修正が必要な箇所を明日までにお知らせください。","metadata":{"tiles":["添付の","議事録を","ご確認のうえ、","修正が","必要な箇所を","明日までに","お知らせください。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["契約書"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Implement","To carry out","Carry out","To conduct","To execute"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0002-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0002-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["会議録"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0002-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0002-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: To delegate","correct_answer":"委任する","metadata":{"tiles":["委任する"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “Next, I will explain the effects of delegating authority to the people in charge on site.” Start with “次に、権限を” and end with “得られる効果をご説明します。”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"次に、権限を現場の責任者に委任することで得られる効果をご説明します。","metadata":{"tiles":["次に、","権限を","現場の","責任者に","委任することで","得られる効果を","ご説明します。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0003-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0003-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["任せる","委ねる","委譲する"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0003-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Efficiency","correct_answer":"効率","metadata":{"tiles":["効率"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “To improve operational efficiency for both sides, could you consider a proposal to reduce the number of deliveries?” Start with “双方の業務効率を” and end with “減らす案をご検討いただけますか。”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"双方の業務効率を高めるために、納品の回数を減らす案をご検討いただけますか。","metadata":{"tiles":["双方の","業務効率を","高めるために、","納品の","回数を","減らす案を","ご検討いただけますか。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["方策","作戦"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0004-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0004-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["能率"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0004-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Deadline","correct_answer":"締め切り","metadata":{"tiles":["締め切り"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “To demonstrate the need to extend the deadline, I summarized the causes of the delay and measures for improvement in a report.” Start with “締め切りを延ばす” and end with “改善策を報告書にまとめました。”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"締め切りを延ばす必要性を示すため、遅れの原因と改善策を報告書にまとめました。","metadata":{"tiles":["締め切りを","延ばす","必要性を","示すため、","遅れの原因と","改善策を","報告書にまとめました。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Interested party"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0005-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0005-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["事日程"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0005-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0005-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["期限","期日"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0005-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0005-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Negotiation","correct_answer":"交渉","metadata":{"tiles":["交渉"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “The relationship of trust with the contact I met at a networking event made the later negotiations go smoothly.” Start with “交流会で知り合った” and end with “交渉を円滑にしました。”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"交流会で知り合った担当者との信頼関係が、その後の交渉を円滑にしました。","metadata":{"tiles":["交流会で","知り合った","担当者との","信頼関係が、","その後の","交渉を","円滑にしました。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["ステークホルダー"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answer