n_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4005-0003-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["一挙両得"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4005-0003-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4005-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: The ball is in your court","correct_answer":"あなた次第","metadata":{"tiles":["あなた次第"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “Which path you choose is up to you, but decisions come with responsibility.” Start with “どの道を” and end with “責任が伴います。”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"どの道を選ぶかはあなた次第ですが、決断には責任が伴います。","metadata":{"tiles":["どの","道を","選ぶかは","あなた次第ですが、","決断には","責任が","伴います。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4005-0004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4005-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["遅れてもやらないよりはまし"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4005-0004-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4005-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["To be over the moon","To be elated","To be in seventh heaven"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4005-0004-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4005-0004-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["今度はあなたの番です"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4005-0004-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4005-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Bite off more than you can chew","correct_answer":"能力以上のことをする","metadata":{"tiles":["能力以上のことをする"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “If you overreach by taking on more than you can handle, you may end up inviting failure instead.” Start with “能力以上のことを” and end with “かえって失敗を招きかねません。”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"能力以上のことを引き受けて背伸びをしすぎると、かえって失敗を招きかねません。","metadata":{"tiles":["能力以上の","ことを","引き受けて","背伸びを","しすぎると、","かえって失敗を","招きかねません。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4005-0005-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4005-0005-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"遅くてもしないよりまし\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Better late than never","options":["A piece of cake","To break the ice","To hit the nail on the head","Better late than never"],"explanation":null},"after":{"prompt":"Read the English sentence: “We’ll have to put off the meeting until next week.” Which Japanese sentence renders “put off” naturally here?","correct_answer":"会議を来週に延期しなければなりません。","options":["会議を来週に延期しなければなりません。","来週の会議を中止しなければなりません。","来週の会議まで我慢しなければなりません。","来週までに会議室を片付けなければなりません。"],"explanation":"Put off here means postpone: 延期する (先延ばしにする is also natural). 中止する is call off, 我慢する is put up with, and 片付ける is put away. Japanese has no English-style verb-plus-particle category; one verb carries the whole phrasal sense."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4005-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4005-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["天にも昇る気持ちになる","有頂天になる","大喜びする"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4005-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4005-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["To tease","Tease","To kid","To joke with someone"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4005-0005-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4005-0005-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["手に余ることを引き受ける","無理な仕事を引き受ける"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4005-0005-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4005-0005-b20000000000","type":