ine: “토요일에는 요리해요. 일요일에는 책을 읽어요.” What does Luis do on Sundays?","correct_answer":"He reads a book.","options":["He cooks.","He plays soccer.","He goes to the office.","He reads a book."],"explanation":"일요일에는 책을 읽어요 says he reads a book on Sundays. The cooking activity is assigned to 토요일, Saturday.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-0005-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-0005-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Pal","Buddy"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-0005-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-0005-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["생"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["뜨거운"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Chilly"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-0006-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["벗"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-0006-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Instructor"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["아빠","부친"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0001-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Grandma","Granny"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0002-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0002-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"아버지\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Father","options":["Mother","Son","Grandfather","Father"],"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read the description: “제 여동생은 키가 크고 머리가 짧아요.” Which description matches the sister?","correct_answer":"Tall, with short hair.","options":["Tall, with short hair.","Short, with long hair.","Tall, with long hair.","Short, with short hair."],"explanation":"키가 크다 describes being tall, and 머리가 짧다 describes short hair in this appearance context. 여동생 identifies the speaker’s younger sister.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Siblings"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0002-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Grandpa","Granddad"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0003-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0003-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"자매\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Sister","options":["Father","Brother","Sister","Grandfather"],"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Read: 제 여동생은 열두 살이에요. How old is my younger sister?","correct_answer":"Twelve years old","options":["Two years old","Twenty years old","Ten years old","Twelve years old"],"explanation":"열두 is twelve and 살 counts years of age. The sentence says that my younger sister is twelve years old.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"native Korean number + 살이에요"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","prompt":"Translate to Korean: Brother","correct_answer":"형제","accepted_answers":[],"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to Korean. Begin with 저는, use the age counter 살, and use polite -요 speech: I am twenty years old.","correct_answer":"저는 스무 살이에요.","accepted_answers":["저는 20살이에요.","저는 20 살이에요.","저는 스무 살이어요.","저는 20살이어요.","저는 20 살이어요.","저는 나이가 스무 살이에요.","저는 나이가 스무 살이어요.","저는 나이가 20살이에요.","저는 나이가 20살이어요.","저는 나이가 20 살이에요.","저는 나이가 20 살이어요.","저는 스무 살 먹었어요.","저는 스무 살을 먹었어요.","저는 20살 먹었어요.","저는 20살을 먹었어요.","저는 20 살 먹었어요.","저는 20 살을 먹었어요."],"explanation":"Before 살, the native Korean number 스물 takes the form 스무: 스무 살이에요. 저는 is the requested introduction frame, not an obligatory topic in every Korean age statement. 이에요 and 이어요 are both valid polite endings.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"저는 + age + 살이에요"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","prompt":"Translate to English: 딸","correct_answer":"Daughter","accepted_answers":[],"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to English: 제 생일은 5월이에요.","correct_answer":"My birthday is in May.","accepted_answers":["My birthday's in May.","My birthday falls in May.","I have my birthday in May.","May is my birthday month.","My birthday is in the month of May."],"explanation":"제 생일 means “my birthday”; 5월 is May. The sentence states the month of the birthday.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"birthday month statement"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0003-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0003-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","prompt":"아_____ (Son)","correct_answer":"들","explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Complete “My younger sibling is ten years old” with the age counter: 동생은 열 ___이에요.","correct_answer":"살","explanation":"열 is the native Korean number ten. With the age counter 살, 열 살 means ten years old.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"native Korean number + 살"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0003-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["조부"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0003-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Family members"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0004-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["식구"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0004-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Dogs"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0005-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0005-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"딸\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Daughter","options":["Brother","Sister","Daughter","Mother"],"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read about a family: “일요일에는 가족이 집에서 함께 밥을 먹어요.” What does the family do on Sundays?","correct_answer":"They eat together at home.","options":["They work at the office.","They eat together at home.","They play soccer in the park.","They study at school."],"explanation":"가족이 identifies the family, 집에서 gives at home, and 함께 밥을 먹어요 says they eat together.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-1006-0005-e00000000003","before":{"les