 to translate: “If artificial intelligence develops, people may be able to focus on more creative work.” Start with “인공지능이 발달하면” and end with “있을지도 몰라요.”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"인공지능이 발달하면 사람들은 더 창의적인 일에 집중할 수 있을지도 몰라요.","accepted_answers":["인공지능이 발달하면 더 창의적인 일에 사람들은 집중할 수 있을지도 몰라요."],"metadata":{"tiles":["인공지능이","발달하면","사람들은","더","창의적인","일에","집중할","수","있을지도","몰라요."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3005-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3005-0006-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["스크린"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3005-0006-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3005-0006-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["AI"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3005-0006-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3005-0006-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Robot","correct_answer":"로봇","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["로봇"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “This robot can move on its own even without human instructions.” Start with “이 로봇은” and end with “수 있어요.”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"이 로봇은 사람의 지시가 없어도 스스로 움직일 수 있어요.","accepted_answers":["이 로봇은 스스로 사람의 지시가 없어도 움직일 수 있어요."],"metadata":{"tiles":["이","로봇은","사람의","지시가","없어도","스스로","움직일","수","있어요."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0001-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["그런 다음"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0001-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["All of a sudden","Abruptly","Unexpectedly"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0001-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0001-b10000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["사이에"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0001-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0001-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["처음에","첫째로","우선"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0001-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0001-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Next","correct_answer":"다음에","metadata":{"tiles":["다음에"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “Next, the main character stopped after hearing an unfamiliar voice coming from outside the door.” Start with “다음에 주인공은” and end with “듣고 멈췄어요.”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"다음에 주인공은 문밖에서 들려오는 낯선 목소리를 듣고 멈췄어요.","metadata":{"tiles":["다음에","주인공은","문밖에서","들려오는","낯선","목소리를","듣고","멈췄어요."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0002-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["돌연","느닷없이","문득"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0002-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["While doing","During"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0002-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0002-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["그다음에","다음으로"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0002-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0002-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Finally","correct_answer":"마침내","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["마침내"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “Finally, we were able to return the wallet we had found to its original owner.” Start with “마침내 우리는” and end with “수 있었어요.”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"마침내 우리는 찾아낸 지갑을 원래 주인에게 돌려줄 수 있었어요.","accepted_answers":["마침내 우리는 원래 주인에게 찾아낸 지갑을 돌려줄 수 있었어요."],"metadata":{"tiles":["마침내","우리는","찾아낸","지갑을","원래","주인에게","돌려줄","수","있었어요."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0003-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0003-b10000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"갑자기\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Suddenly","options":["Suddenly","Beginning","Finally","Once upon a time"],"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"어젯밤 여덟 시에 민아는 책을 읽고 있었어요. 아홉 시에 책을 덮었어요. 여덟 시에 민아는 무엇을 하고 있었어요?","correct_answer":"Mina was reading a book.","options":["Mina was reading a book.","Mina was buying a book.","Mina was closing the book.","Mina was writing a book."],"explanation":"읽고 있었어요 describes the reading in progress at eight. The book was closed later, at nine: 아홉 시에 책을 덮었어요.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"past -고 있었다 for an action in progress"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0003-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","prompt":"Translate to Korean: While","correct_answer":"하는 동안","accepted_answers":[],"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to Korean: At eight last night, I was reading a book. Use 어젯밤 여덟 시에 and 책을; put 읽다 into the polite -고 있었어요 form and omit the understood subject.","correct_answer":"어젯밤 여덟 시에 책을 읽고 있었어요.","accepted_answers":["책을 어젯밤 여덟 시에 읽고 있었어요.","어젯밤 여덟 시에, 책을 읽고 있었어요.","어젯밤 8시에 책을 읽고 있었어요.","어젯밤 8 시에 책을 읽고 있었어요.","책을 어젯밤 8시에 읽고 있었어요.","책을 어젯밤 8 시에 읽고 있었어요.","어젯밤 8시에, 책을 읽고 있었어요.","어젯밤 8 시에, 책을 읽고 있었어요."],"explanation":"Attach -고 있었어요 to the stem 읽- to describe the reading in progress at that past time. The speaker is understood as the reader here; an explicit 저는 is not required. The task supplies the time and object phrases and requests this particular progressive ending.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"읽다 → 읽고 있었어요"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0003-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","prompt":"Translate to English: 먼저","correct_answer":"First","accepted_answers":[],"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Translate to English: 제가 책 한 권을 읽고 있을 때 전화가 울렸어요.","correct_answer":"I was reading a book when the phone rang.","accepted_answers":["When the phone rang, I was reading a book.","When the phone rang I was reading a book.","The phone rang while I was reading a book.","While I was reading a book, the phone rang.","While I was reading a book the phone rang.","The phone rang when I was reading a book.","When I was reading a book, the phone rang.","When I was reading a book the phone rang.","I was reading a book when a phone rang.","When a phone rang, I was reading a book.","When a phone rang I was reading a book.","A phone rang while I was reading a book.","While I was reading a book, a phone rang.","While I was reading a book a phone rang.","A phone rang when I was reading a book.","When I was reading a book, a phone rang.","When I was reading a book a phone rang.","I was reading one book when the phone rang.","When the phone rang, I was reading one book.","When the phone rang I was reading one book.","The phone rang while I was reading one book.","While I was reading one book, the phone rang.","While I was reading one book the phone rang.","The phone rang when I was reading one book.","When I was reading one book, the phone rang.","When I was reading one book the phone rang.","I was reading one book when a phone rang.","When a phone rang, I was reading one book.","When a phone rang I was reading one book.","A phone rang while I was reading one book.","While I was reading one book, a phone rang.","While I was reading one book a phone rang.","A phone rang when I was reading one book.","When I was reading one book, a phone rang.","When I was reading one book a phone rang."],"explanation":"The reading is in progress when the phone rings; 울렸어요 places that event in the past. Korean can use -고 있을 때 for an action ongoing relative to that past event, without copying an English past-tense ending into every clause. 한 권 specifies one book; 전화 does not itself select “the” versus “a” in English.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"ongoing -고 있을 때 action with a past event"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0003-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0003-b10000000000","type":"fill_blank","prompt":"다_____ (Next)","correct_answer":"음에","explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Complete with the -어요 polite past form of 있다: 전화가 울렸을 때 저는 책을 읽고 ___.","correct_answer":"있었어요","explanation":"The requested polite past form of 있다 is 있었어요. 읽고 있었어요 describes the reading in progress at the past time when the phone rang.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"polite past -고 있었어요"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0003-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0003-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["드디어","결국","끝내","마지막으로"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0004-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["처음에","첫째로","우선"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0004-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0004-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Later","Afterwards","Afterward"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0004-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0004-b10000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["지막으로"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0004-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0004-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["한편","그동안","그 동안에"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0004-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0004-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Character","correct_answer":"등장인물","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["등장인물"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “Just as a character was about to reveal a secret, the phone suddenly started ringing.” Start with “등장인물이 비밀을” and end with “울리기 시작했어요.”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"등장인물이 비밀을 말하려던 순간 갑자기 전화가 울리기 시작했어요.","accepted_answers":["등장인물이 비밀을 말하려던 순간 전화가 갑자기 울리기 시작했어요."],"metadata":{"tiles":["등장인물이","비밀을","말하려던","순간","갑자기","전화가","울리기","시작했어요."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0005-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["그다음에","다음으로"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0005-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["At last","Eventually","In the end","Ultimately"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0005-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0005-b10000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["동안에"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0005-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0005-b10000000000","type":"cl