,{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4001-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4001-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Being","Presence"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4001-0005-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4001-0005-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["의혹"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4001-0005-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4001-0005-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Freedom","correct_answer":"자유","metadata":{"tiles":["자유"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “Individual freedom cannot be separated from the duty to respect other people’s rights.” Start with “개인의 자유는” and end with “수 없습니다.”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"개인의 자유는 타인의 권리를 존중해야 할 책임과 분리할 수 없습니다.","metadata":{"tiles":["개인의","자유는","타인의","권리를","존중해야","할","책임과","분리할","수","없습니다."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4001-0006-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4001-0006-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","options":["Ethics","Morality","Equality","Consciousness"]},"after":{"options":["Purpose","Morality","Equality","Consciousness"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4001-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4001-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["실존"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4001-0006-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4001-0006-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["리"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4001-0006-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4001-0006-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Justice","correct_answer":"정의","metadata":{"tiles":["정의"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “The meaning of justice can vary depending on whose perspective one adopts.” Start with “정의의 의미는” and end with “수 있습니다.”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"정의의 의미는 누구의 관점에서 바라보느냐에 따라 달라질 수 있습니다.","metadata":{"tiles":["정의의","의미는","누구의","관점에서","바라보느냐에","따라","달라질","수","있습니다."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Proof"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0001-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0001-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["박"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0001-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0001-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["논박하다"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0001-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0001-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Claim","correct_answer":"주장","metadata":{"tiles":["주장"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “To make a persuasive claim, you must be able to present specific evidence.” Start with “설득력 있는” and end with “있어야 합니다.”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"설득력 있는 주장을 하려면 구체적인 근거를 제시할 수 있어야 합니다.","metadata":{"tiles":["설득력","있는","주장을","하려면","구체적인","근거를","제시할","수","있어야","합니다."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["근거"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Rebuttal","Counterclaim"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0002-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0002-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["렇지만","런데"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0002-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0002-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Fallacy","correct_answer":"오류","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["오류"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “Even if you feel that there is an error in the other person’s explanation, you should identify specifically what the problem is.” Start with “상대의 설명에” and end with “밝혀야 합니다.”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"상대의 설명에 오류가 있다고 느껴지더라도 무엇이 문제인지 구체적으로 밝혀야 합니다.","accepted_answers":["상대의 설명에 오류가 있다고 느껴지더라도 구체적으로 무엇이 문제인지 밝혀야 합니다."],"metadata":{"tiles":["상대의","설명에","오류가","있다고","느껴지더라도","무엇이","문제인지","구체적으로","밝혀야","합니다."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["반박"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["But","Yet"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0003-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0003-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["논리적 오류"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0003-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Rhetoric","correct_answer":"수사학","metadata":{"tiles":["수사학"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “By studying rhetoric, you can analyze the effectiveness of expressions that appeal to the listener’s emotions.” Start with “수사학을 공부하면” and end with “수 있습니다.”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"수사학을 공부하면 듣는 이의 감정에 호소하는 표현의 효과를 분석할 수 있습니다.","metadata":{"tiles":["수사학을","공부하면","듣는","이의","감정에","호소하는","표현의","효과를","분석할","수","있습니다."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0004-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"반론\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Counterargument","options":["Counterargument","Claim","To persuade","Argument"],"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Evaluate this argument: “이 카페에 두 번 갔는데 두 번 모두 음식이 늦게 나왔어요. 그러니 이 도시의 모든 카페에서는 언제나 음식이 늦게 나와요.” Why do the observations not justify the conclusion?","correct_answer":"It generalizes from two visits to one café to every café in the city.","options":["It rejects a claim solely because of the person who made it.","It treats a popular belief as proof that the belief is true.","It generalizes from two visits to one café to every café in the city.","It treats a low price as proof of fast service."],"explanation":"Two visits to one café do not establish what happens at every café, every time. This is an unsupported generalization from a very limited sample. The claim might happen to be true or false; these observations do not justify it.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["하지만","그렇지만","그런데"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0004-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Nonetheless","Even so","Despite that","Despite this","All the same"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0004-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["군다나","구나","나아가"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0004-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["수사"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0004-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Bias","correct_answer":"편견","metadata":{"tiles":["편견"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “Judging an entire group from a single case risks reinforcing existing prejudice.” Start with “하나의 사례만으로” and end with “우려가 있습니다.”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"하나의 사례만으로 집단 전체를 판단하면 기존의 편견을 강화할 우려가 있습니다.","metadata":{"tiles":["하나의","사례만으로","집단","전체를","판단하면","기존의","편견을","강화할","우려가","있습니다."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0005-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","options":["Nevertheless","However","Evidence","Fallacy"]},"after":{"options":["Therefore","However","Evidence","Fallacy"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["그래도"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Moreover","Additionally","Besides","In addition"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0005-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["을 하다"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0005-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["편향"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0005-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Argument","correct_answer":"논쟁","metadata":{"tiles":["논쟁"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “To advance a debate, it is important not only to answer counterarguments but also to confirm shared premises.” Start with “논쟁을 발전시키려면” and end with “것도 중요합니다.”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"논쟁을 발전시키려면 반론에 답할 뿐 아니라 공통의 전제를 확인하는 것도 중요합니다.","metadata":{"tiles":["논쟁을","발전시키려면","반론에","답할","뿐","아니라","공통의","전제를","확인하는","것도","중요합니다."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["게다가","또한","더군다나","더구나","나아가"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Refute","Rebut","To contradict","Contradict"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0006-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0006-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["논증","논거"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0006-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0006-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: To persuade","correct_answer":"설득하다","metadata":{"tiles":["설득하다"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “I think that simply repeating that you are right is not enough to persuade someone.” Start with “상대를 설득하려면” and end with “않다고 생각합니다.”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"상대를 설득하려면 자신이 옳다고 반복하는 것만으로는 충분하지 않다고 생각합니다.","metadata":{"tiles":["상대를","설득하려면","자신이","옳다고","반복하는","것만으로는","충분하지","않다고","생각합니다."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["제의","제안서"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0001-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0001-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["을 하다"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0001-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0001-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["의제","의사일정","회의 안건"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0001-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0001-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Minutes","correct_answer":"회의록","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["회의록"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “Please review the attached meeting minutes and let me know by tomorrow which parts need correction.” Start with “첨부된 회의록을” and end with “알려주시기 바랍니다.”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"첨부된 회의록을 검토하신 후 수정이 필요한 부분을 내일까지 알려주시기 바랍니다.","accepted_answers":["첨부된 회의록을 검토하신 후 내일까지 수정이 필요한 부분을 알려주시기 바랍니다."],"metadata":{"tiles":["첨부된","회의록을","검토하신","후","수정이","필요한","부분을","내일까지","알려주시기","바랍니다."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["계약서"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Implement","To execute","Execute","To carry out","Carry out"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0002-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0002-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["회의 기록"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0002-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0002-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: To delegate","correct_answer":"위임하다","metadata":{"tiles":["위임하다"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “Next, I will explain the potential effects of delegating authority to the people in charge on site.” Start with “다음으로 권한을” and end with “효과를 설명하겠습니다.”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"다음으로 권한을 현장 책임자에게 위임함으로써 얻을 수 있는 효과를 설명하겠습니다.","metadata":{"tiles":["다음으로","권한을","현장","책임자에게","위임함으로써","얻을","수","있는","효과를","설명하겠습니다."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["이행하다","실시하다"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0003-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0003-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["맡기다","위탁하다"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0003-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Efficiency","correct_answer":"효율","metadata":{"tiles":["효율"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “To improve operational efficiency for both sides, could you consider a proposal to reduce the number of deliveries?” Start with “양측의 업무” and end with “검토해 주시겠습니까?”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"양측의 업무 효율을 높이기 위해 납품 횟수를 줄이는 방안을 검토해 주시겠습니까?","metadata":{"tiles":["양측의","업무","효율을","높이기","위해","납품","횟수를","줄이는","방안을","검토해","주시겠습니까?"],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0004-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0004-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["관계인"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0004-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0004-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["효율성"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0004-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Deadline","correct_answer":"마감일","metadata":{"tiles":["마감일"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “To explain the need to extend the deadline, I summarized the causes of the delay and measures for improvement in a report.” Start with “마감일을 연장할” and end with “보고서에 정리했습니다.”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"마감일을 연장할 필요성을 설명하기 위해 지연 원인과 개선책을 보고서에 정리했습니다.","metadata":{"tiles":["마감일을","연장할","필요성을","설명하기","위해","지연","원인과","개선책을","보고서에","정리했습니다."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Interested party"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0005-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0005-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["기한","마감 기한","마감 시간"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0005-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0005-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Negotiation","correct_answer":"협상","metadata":{"tiles":["협상"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “The relationship of trust with the contact I met at a networking event made the later negotiations go smoothly.” Start with “교류회에서 만난” and end with “원활하게 만들었습니다.”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"교류회에서 만난 담당자와의 신뢰관계가 이후 협상을 원활하게 만들었습니다.","metadata":{"tiles":["교류회에서","만난","담당자와의","신뢰관계가","이후","협상을","원활하게","만들었습니다."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["이해 당사자","이해관계인"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Agenda item","Item on the agenda","Motion"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0006-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0006-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["의 기록"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0006-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0006-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["교섭"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0006-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0006-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Proposal","correct_answer":"제안","metadata":{"tiles":["제안"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “This proposal aims to reduce costs while also maintaining quality.” Start with “이번 제안은” and end with “목표로 합니다.”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"이번 제안은 비용을 줄이는 한편 품질도 유지하는 것을 목표로 합니다.","metadata":{"tiles":["이번","제안은","비용을","줄이는","한편","품질도","유지하는","것을","목표로","합니다."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4004-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4004-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Picture","Drawing"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4004-0001-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4004-0001-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["각품","각상"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4004-0001-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4004-0001-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Plot twist","correct_answer":"반전","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["반전"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “In this video artwork, the final plot twist greatly changes the audience’s interpretation.” Start with “이 영상” and end with “크게 바꿉니다.”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"이 영상 작품은 마지막 반전을 통해 관객의 해석을 크게 바꿉니다.","accepted_answers":["이 영상 작품은 관객의 해석을 마지막 반전을 통해 크게 바꿉니다."],"metadata":{"tiles":["이","영상","작품은","마지막","반전을","통해","관객의","해석을","크게","바꿉니다."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4004-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4004-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["회화"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4004-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4004-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Carving"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4004-0002-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4004-0002-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["유법"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4004-0002-e00000000008","before":{"le