adata":{"tiles":["비밀을","누설하다"],"distractors":["얼음을","정곱을"]}},"after":{"metadata":{"tiles":["비밀을","누설하다"],"distractors":["얼음을","정곡을"]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["누워서 떡 먹기"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Cost an arm and a leg","To be extremely expensive","Extremely expensive","Eye-wateringly expensive"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0002-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0002-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["비밀을 털어놓다","비밀을 밝히다"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0002-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0002-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: To kill two birds with one stone","correct_answer":"일석이조","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["일석이조"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every tile to translate: “Walking to work saves on transport costs and also gives you exercise: it really is killing two birds with one stone.” Start with “걸어서 출근하면” and end with “그야말로 일석이조입니다.”. Use each tile once.","correct_answer":"걸어서 출근하면 교통비를 아끼면서 운동도 할 수 있으니 그야말로 일석이조입니다.","accepted_answers":["걸어서 출근하면 운동도 교통비를 아끼면서 할 수 있으니 그야말로 일석이조입니다."],"metadata":{"tiles":["걸어서","출근하면","교통비를","아끼면서","운동도","할","수","있으니","그야말로","일석이조입니다."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["엄청나게 비싸다","값이 엄청나다","눈이 휘둥그레질 정도로 비싸다"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0003-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0003-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["에 떠 있는 기분이다","에 떠 있는 것 같다"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0003-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0003-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["일거양득"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["늦게라도 하는 것이 안 하는 것보다 낫다","늦더라도 안 하는 것보다 낫다"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0004-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Be on cloud nine","On cloud nine","Over the moon","Feel like flying","To be overjoyed"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0004-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0004-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":["이제 결정하실 차례입니다"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["이제 결정하실 차례입니다","이제 네가 결정할 차례다","이제 당신 차례입니다"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0005-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0005-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"늦어도 안 하는 것보다 낫다\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Better late than never","options":["To kill two birds with one stone","A piece of cake","Better late than never","To let the cat out of the bag"],"explanation":null},"after":{"prompt":"Read the English sentence: “We’ll have to put off the meeting until next week.” Which Korean sentence renders “put off” naturally here?","correct_answer":"회의를 다음 주로 미뤄야 해요.","options":["다음 주 회의를 취소해야 해요.","다음 주 회의까지 참아야 해요.","회의를 다음 주로 미뤄야 해요.","다음 주까지 회의실을 치워야 해요."],"explanation":"Put off here means postpone: 미루다 (연기하다 is also natural). 취소하다 is call off, 참다 is put up with, and 치우다 is put away. Korean has no English-style verb-plus-particle category; one verb carries the whole phrasal sense."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["기분이 날아갈 것 같다","너무나 기쁘다","기쁘기 그지없다"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Pull someone’s leg","To tease someone","Tease someone","To joke with someone"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0005-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0005-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["능력 밖의 일을 벌이다","감당하지 못할 일을 맡다"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["장난치다","농담하다"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Very rarely","Rarely","Hardly ever"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0006-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0006-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["털어놓다","밝히다"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0006-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0006-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["어색함을 풀다","서먹한 분위기를 깨다","어색한 분위기를 풀다"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["拜拜","再会"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0001-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Thanks"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["早安","早"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0002-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["谢谢你","多谢"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0002-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["I am sorry","I'm sorry"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0003-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["抱歉"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0003-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Embarrassed"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0003-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0003-000000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["是的","对"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0004-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0004-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","options":["Excuse me","No","Sorry","Good morning"]},"after":{"options":["Good night","No","Sorry","Good morning"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0004-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["劳驾","打扰一下"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0004-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["To be","Is"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0004-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0004-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["对"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0005-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0005-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"晚安\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Good night","options":["Good night","Thank you","Hello","Good morning"],"distractors":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read this short introduction:\n你好！我叫小红。我是北京人。\n\nWhat is the writer’s name?","correct_answer":"Xiaohong","options":["Xiaoming","Xiaowang","Xiaohong","Xiaolin"],"distractors":["Xiaoming","Xiaowang","Xiaolin"],"hint_text":"我叫 introduces a name. 小红 is written Xiaohong in pinyin.","explanation":"The writer says 我叫小红: My name is Xiaohong. 你好 is the greeting; the final sentence states where Xiaohong is from.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0005-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Thanks"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0005-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0005-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"不好意思\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Excuse me","options":["Goodbye","Hello","Excuse me","Yes"],"distractors":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read this short introduction:\n你好！我叫小红。我是北京人。\n\nWhere is Xiaohong from?","correct_answer":"Beijing","options":["Shanghai","Beijing","Paris","London"],"distractors":["Shanghai","Paris","London"],"hint_text":"北京 is Beijing. A place name followed by 人 can describe a person from that place.","explanation":"我是北京人 means I am from Beijing, literally I am a Beijing person. It identifies Xiaohong’s origin, not an address or necessarily the current location.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0005-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0005-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["是的","对"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["多谢","谢谢你"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["I am sorry","I'm sorry"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0006-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["不","不对"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0006-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1001-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Hi"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1002-0002-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1002-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["干酪","芝士"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1002-0002-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1002-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Cooked rice"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1002-0003-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1002-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["米","大米"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1002-0004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1002-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["奶"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1002-0004-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1002-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Tasty","Good to eat"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1002-0005-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1002-0005-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"牛奶\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Milk","options":["Apple","Water","Menu","Milk"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"At a restaurant, you want fish, rice and a glass of water. Which sentence places that order politely?","correct_answer":"请给我鱼、米饭和一杯水。","options":["请给我鸡肉、米饭和一杯水。","请给我鱼、米饭和一杯水。","请给我鱼、面包和一杯水。","请给我鱼、米饭和一杯牛奶。"],"hint_text":"请给我 means please give me. Check both the food items and the drink.","explanation":"请给我鱼、米饭和一杯水 means Please give me fish, rice and a glass of water. The other orders change the fish, rice or water. 请 makes the request polite; 一杯水 specifies one cup or glass of water.","distractors":["请给我鸡肉、米饭和一杯水。","请给我鱼、面包和一杯水。","请给我鱼、米饭和一杯牛奶。"],"skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1002-0005-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1002-0005-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","prompt":"米_____ (Rice)","correct_answer":"饭","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary","target_grammar":null},"after":{"prompt":"Complete the positive restaurant request with 请 (please) or 不 (not): ___给我鱼、米饭和一杯水。","correct_answer":"请","accepted_answers":["請"],"hint_text":"The customer is politely asking to receive these items, not refusing them.","explanation":"请给我鱼、米饭和一杯水 is a polite request for fish, rice and a glass of water. Of the two offered characters, 请 supplies please; 不 would negate the verb instead. 請 is the traditional form of 请.","skill_type":"grammar","target_grammar":"polite_meal_request"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1002-0005-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1002-0005-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"鱼\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Fish","options":["Rice","Fish","Apple","Chicken"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"A customer says: 请给我鸡肉、米饭和一杯水。What does the customer order?","correct_answer":"Chicken, rice and a glass of water.","options":["Chicken, bread and a glass of water.","Fish, rice and a glass of water.","Chicken, rice and a glass of milk.","Chicken, rice and a glass of water."],"hint_text":"鸡肉 is chicken, 米饭 is cooked rice and 水 is water.","explanation":"The complete order is chicken, rice and a glass of water. 请给我 introduces the polite request, and 和 links the last item in the list. 杯 can refer to a cup or glass; the offered answer correctly identifies the drink as water.","distractors":["Chicken, bread and a glass of water.","Fish, rice and a glass of water.","Chicken, rice and a glass of milk."],"skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1002-0005-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1002-0005-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["美味","可口"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1002-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1002-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["干酪","芝士"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1002-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1002-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Cooked rice"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0001-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0001-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"左\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Left","options":["Left","Station","Straight","Pharmacy"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"You want someone to explain how to get to the railway station. Which question asks for those directions?","correct_answer":"请问，去火车站怎么走？","options":["请问，这张车票多少钱？","请问，去火车站怎么走？","请问，下一班火车什么时候开？","请问，这是我的车票吗？"],"hint_text":"怎么走 asks how to get there; 请问 politely introduces a question.","explanation":"请问，去火车站怎么走？ means Excuse me, how do I get to the railway station? The other questions ask the ticket price, the next train’s departure time and whether a ticket belongs to the speaker. This supplies an asking frame; the existing valid direction 直走 remains useful and unchanged.","distractors":["请问，这张车票多少钱？","请问，下一班火车什么时候开？","请问，这是我的车票吗？"],"skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["右边","右侧"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["直","一直走"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0002-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["站"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["公交车","巴士"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0003-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0003-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["房"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0004-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0004-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"公共汽车\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Bus","options":["Hospital","Bus","Airport","Straight"],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"At a ticket counter, you want one one-way ticket to Beijing. Which request matches?","correct_answer":"请给我一张去北京的单程票。","options":["请给我一张去北京的往返票。","请给我两张去北京的单程票。","请给我一张去上海的单程票。","请给我一张去北京的单程票。"],"hint_text":"单程票 is a one-way ticket. 一张 specifies one ticket; 去北京 gives its destination.","explanation":"请给我一张去北京的单程票 means Please give me one one-way ticket to Beijing. The other requests include a round trip, two tickets or a different destination. 张 is the measure word for the ticket; no particular operator’s fare rules or product availability is asserted.","distractors":["请给我一张去北京的往返票。","请给我两张去北京的单程票。","请给我一张去上海的单程票。"],"skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["列车"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0004-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Drugstore","Chemist's"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0005-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0005-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["药房"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0005-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0005-000000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["左边","左侧"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["站"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0006-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0006-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["飞机场"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0006-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1003-0006-000000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["右边","右侧"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0001-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0001-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"早餐\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Breakfast","options":["Expensive","Blue","Tomorrow","Breakfast"],"distractors":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read this sentence:\n小林每天早上在家吃早饭。\n\nWhich routine is described?","correct_answer":"Eating breakfast at home every morning.","options":["Eating breakfast at home every morning.","Eating dinner at home every evening.","Eating breakfast at a café every morning.","Eating breakfast at home only on Sundays."],"distractors":["Eating dinner at home every evening.","Eating breakfast at a café every morning.","Eating breakfast at home only on Sundays."],"hint_text":"每天早上 means every morning; 在家 means at home; 吃早饭 means eat breakfast.","explanation":"Xiaolin eats breakfast at home every morning. 每天早上 makes this a regular routine rather than a single meal. The sentence states the activity, time and place.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["昂贵"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Inexpensive"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0001-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0001-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["衬衣"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0001-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0001-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["款","费"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["廉价","低廉"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0002-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["鞋"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0002-e00000000007","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0002-000000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["To pay money"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0002-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0002-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["刻"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["红"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0003-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0003-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["衣"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0003-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0003-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["付款","支付","付费"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0003-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0003-000000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["日"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0004-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0004-000000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"红色\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Red","options":["Red","Breakfast","Shirt","To pay"],"distractors":[],"hint_text":null,"explanation":null,"skill_type":"vocabulary"},"after":{"prompt":"Read this sentence:\n商店上午九点开门。\n\nAt what time does the shop open?","correct_answer":"At 9 a.m.","options":["At 8 a.m.","At 9 p.m.","At 9 a.m.","At 10 a.m."],"distractors":["At 8 a.m.","At 9 p.m.","At 10 a.m."],"hint_text":"九点 is nine o’clock; 上午 selects the morning, not the evening.","explanation":"The shop opens at 9 a.m. 上午九点 gives an unambiguous morning clock time. 开门 describes opening, not closing.","skill_type":"mixed"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["蓝"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0004-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0004-000000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["时刻"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0004-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0004-000000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["金钱"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1004-0005-000000000000",