004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-3008-0004-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["有点儿","有些","有一点"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-3008-0004-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-3008-0004-b10000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["好了","赞了"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-3008-0004-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-3008-0004-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["随你","无所谓"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-3008-0004-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-3008-0004-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: No worries","correct_answer":"没关系","metadata":{"tiles":["没关系"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “When the other person apologizes for being late on the phone, you can say, “It is all right, we have not started the meeting yet.”” Start with “对方” and end with “开会呢”。”.","correct_answer":"对方在电话里为迟到道歉时，你可以说“没关系，我们还没开始开会呢”。","metadata":{"tiles":["对方","在电话里","为迟到","道歉时，","你","可以","说","“没关系，","我们","还没","开始","开会呢”。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-3008-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-3008-0005-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Great","Fantastic","Wonderful"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-3008-0005-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-3008-0005-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["不用担心","没事","没问题","别担心"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-3008-0005-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-3008-0005-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Dude","correct_answer":"哥们","metadata":{"tiles":["哥们"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: ““哥们” can be used to address a familiar male friend, but it is best not to address the other person that way in a formal interview.” Start with ““哥们”” and end with “对方。”.","correct_answer":"“哥们”可以用来称呼熟悉的男性朋友，但是在正式面试中最好不要这样称呼对方。","metadata":{"tiles":["“哥们”","可以","用来","称呼","熟悉的男性朋友，","但是","在正式面试中","最好","不要","这样","称呼","对方。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-3008-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-3008-0006-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["棒极了","真棒","太好了","了不起"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-3008-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-3008-0006-b10000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["As you like","Whatever you like","Casually"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-3008-0006-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-3008-0006-b10000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["事","问题"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-3008-0006-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-3008-0006-b10000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["哥们儿","老兄","伙计"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-3008-0006-e00000000006","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-3008-0006-b10000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Formal","correct_answer":"正式","metadata":{"tiles":["正式"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “When writing an email to an unfamiliar client, I use relatively formal expressions to avoid seeming too casual.” Start with “给” and end with “过于随便。”.","correct_answer":"给不熟悉的客户写邮件时，我会使用比较正式的表达，避免让人觉得过于随便。","metadata":{"tiles":["给","不熟悉的客户","写邮件时，","我","会","使用","比较正式的","表达，","避免","让人","觉得","过于随便。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["公正"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Aim","Goal","Objective"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0001-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0001-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Truth","correct_answer":"真理","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["真理"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “Although different people may understand truth differently, we still need to distinguish verifiable facts from unexamined personal judgments.” Start with “尽管” and end with “个人判断。”.","correct_answer":"尽管不同的人可能对真理有不同的理解，我们仍然需要区分可以验证的事实和未经检验的个人判断。","accepted_answers":["尽管不同的人对真理可能有不同的理解，我们仍然需要区分可以验证的事实和未经检验的个人判断。"],"metadata":{"tiles":["尽管","不同的人","可能","对","真理","有","不同的理解，","我们","仍然","需要","区分","可以验证的事实","和","未经检验的","个人判断。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["目标","宗旨"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Awareness"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0002-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0002-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["理学"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0002-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0002-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Wisdom","correct_answer":"智慧","metadata":{"tiles":["智慧"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “In my view, wisdom is not just accumulating knowledge; more important is being able to reflect on one’s beliefs and defer conclusions when evidence is insufficient.” Start with “在我看来，” and end with “作出结论。”.","correct_answer":"在我看来，智慧并不只是积累知识，更重要的是能够反思自己的信念，并在证据不足时暂缓作出结论。","metadata":{"tiles":["在我看来，","智慧","并不只是","积累知识，","更重要的是","能够","反思","自己的信念，","并在","证据不足时","暂缓","作出结论。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Morals"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0003-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Belief","correct_answer":"信仰","metadata":{"tiles":["信仰"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “A person’s religious faith may give life meaning, but that personal experience does not automatically justify requiring others to accept the same values.” Start with “一个人的” and end with “理由。”.","correct_answer":"一个人的宗教信仰可能为生活提供意义，但这种个人体验并不能自动成为要求他人接受同一套价值观的理由。","metadata":{"tiles":["一个人的","宗教信仰","可能","为生活","提供","意义，","但","这种个人体验","并不能","自动成为","要求他人","接受","同一套","价值观的","理由。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["伦理学"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0004-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Morals"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0004-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0004-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["信念"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0004-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Doubt","correct_answer":"疑惑","metadata":{"tiles":["疑惑"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “As long as the available evidence still allows several reasonable explanations, retaining appropriate doubt does not mean refusing to think, but acknowledging the limits of the conclusion.” Start with “只要” and end with “局限。”.","correct_answer":"只要现有的证据仍然允许多种合理的解释，保留适当的疑惑就不意味着拒绝思考，而是承认结论的局限。","metadata":{"tiles":["只要","现有的证据","仍然","允许","多种合理的解释，","保留","适当的","疑惑","就","不意味着","拒绝","思考，","而是","承认","结论的","局限。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["To exist","Exist","Being"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0005-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0005-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["怀疑","疑问"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0005-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0005-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Freedom","correct_answer":"自由","metadata":{"tiles":["自由"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “If we emphasize only individual freedom while ignoring the effects of choices on others, it is difficult to discuss fully the relationship between freedom and responsibility.” Start with “如果” and end with “关系。”.","correct_answer":"如果只强调个人自由，却忽视选择对他人的影响，我们就很难完整地讨论自由与责任之间的关系。","metadata":{"tiles":["如果","只强调","个人自由，","却","忽视","选择对他人的影响，","我们","就很难","完整地","讨论","自由","与","责任","之间的","关系。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Equal"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0006-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0006-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Justice","correct_answer":"正义","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["正义"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “Justice requires not only that rules treat everyone equally in form, but also that we carefully examine the different consequences those rules cause in practice.” Start with “正义” and end with “不同后果。”.","correct_answer":"正义不仅要求规则在形式上对所有人一视同仁，也要求我们认真考察这些规则在现实中造成的不同后果。","accepted_answers":["正义不仅要求规则对所有人在形式上一视同仁，也要求我们认真考察这些规则在现实中造成的不同后果。"],"metadata":{"tiles":["正义","不仅","要求","规则","在形式上","对所有人","一视同仁，","也要求","我们","认真","考察","这些规则","在现实中","造成的","不同后果。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Proof"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0001-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0001-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["驳斥","批驳","驳倒"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0001-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0001-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Claim","correct_answer":"声明","metadata":{"tiles":["声明"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “Before supporting this public statement, we should check whether the data it cites are reliable rather than accepting its conclusion merely because its wording is powerful.” Start with “在” and end with “它的结论。”.","correct_answer":"在支持这份公开声明之前，我们应当核实其中引用的数据是否可靠，而不能仅仅因为措辞有力就接受它的结论。","metadata":{"tiles":["在","支持","这份公开声明","之前，","我们","应当","核实","其中引用的数据","是否","可靠，","而不能","仅仅","因为","措辞有力","就","接受","它的结论。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["论据","依据"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":["To refute"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["To refute","Refutation","Rebuttal"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0002-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0002-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["声称","主张","断言"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0002-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0002-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Fallacy","correct_answer":"谬误","metadata":{"tiles":["谬误"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “Inferring directly from one successful case that a method works for everyone without examining failures is a fallacy of overgeneralization.” Start with “从” and end with “谬误。”.","correct_answer":"从一个成功的个案直接推断某种方法对所有人都有效，却不考察失败的情况，这是一种以偏概全的谬误。","metadata":{"tiles":["从","一个成功的个案","直接","推断","某种方法","对所有人","都有效，","却不","考察","失败的情况，","这","是一种","以偏概全的","谬误。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["反论点"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Yet","But"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0003-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0003-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["这样"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0003-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0003-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["谬论"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0003-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Rhetoric","correct_answer":"修辞","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["修辞"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “Even if the speaker uses vivid rhetoric to move the audience, he still needs to explain how his proposal can be implemented within a limited budget.” Start with “即使” and end with “落实。”.","correct_answer":"即使演讲者运用了生动的修辞来打动听众，他仍然需要解释自己的建议如何在有限的预算内得到落实。","accepted_answers":["即使演讲者运用了生动的修辞来打动听众，他仍然需要解释自己的建议在有限的预算内如何得到落实。"],"metadata":{"tiles":["即使","演讲者","运用了","生动的修辞","来","打动听众，","他","仍然","需要","解释","自己的建议","如何","在","有限的预算内","得到","落实。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0004-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"反驳\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Counterargument","options":["Argument","To persuade","However","Counterargument"],"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","hint_text":null,"explanation":null},"after":{"prompt":"Read this argument:\n这家公司有一百名员工。其中两个人今天对我不友好。所以，这家公司的所有员工都不友好。\n\nWhich criticism identifies the reasoning error?","correct_answer":"It judges all one hundred employees from the behaviour of only two.","options":["It attacks a person’s origin instead of examining their evidence.","It judges all one hundred employees from the behaviour of only two.","It treats a later event as the cause of an earlier event.","It claims that an opinion is true because most people believe it."],"distractors":["It attacks a person’s origin instead of examining their evidence.","It treats a later event as the cause of an earlier event.","It claims that an opinion is true because most people believe it."],"skill_type":"mixed","hint_text":"Compare the number of people actually observed with the number covered by the conclusion.","explanation":"其中两个人 refers to two of the hundred employees; 所以 introduces the conclusion about 所有员工, all employees. The observation concerns only two of one hundred employees and does not justify a categorical judgment about all of them: this is a hasty generalization. The problem is insufficient support; it does not prove that the opposite conclusion is true."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["不过","但是","可是"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0004-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Nonetheless","Even so"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0004-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["修辞学"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0004-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Bias","correct_answer":"偏见","metadata":{"tiles":["偏见"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “If a study is rejected solely because of its author’s background without analyzing its methods and evidence, that judgment may be influenced by bias.” Start with “如果” and end with “偏见的影响。”.","correct_answer":"如果仅仅因为作者的背景就否定一项研究，而不分析它的方法和证据，这种判断就可能受到偏见的影响。","metadata":{"tiles":["如果","仅仅","因为","作者的背景","就","否定","一项研究，","而不","分析","它的方法","和证据，","这种判断","就","可能","受到","偏见的影响。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0004-e00000000010","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0004-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"论点\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Argument","options":["Rhetoric","Argument","To refute","To persuade"],"distractors":[],"skill_type":"vocabulary","hint_text":null,"explanation":null},"after":{"prompt":"Read this argument:\n市里安装了新的路灯。一个月后，游客人数增加了。所以，一定是这些新路灯使游客人数增加了。\n\nWhich response directly addresses the reasoning error?","correct_answer":"The increase came later, but that timing alone does not establish its cause.","options":["The timing alone proves that the new lamps caused the increase.","The increase proves that the lamps could not have had any effect.","The passage says that visitor numbers rose before the lamps were installed.","The increase came later, but that timing alone does not establish its cause."],"distractors":["The timing alone proves that the new lamps caused the increase.","The increase proves that the lamps could not have had any effect.","The passage says that visitor numbers rose before the lamps were installed."],"skill_type":"mixed","hint_text":"Separate the order of events from evidence about what caused the change.","explanation":"一个月后 expresses time order; 一定是 states the speaker’s certainty about the cause. Later does not by itself mean caused by: this is a post hoc causal inference. The lamps might have contributed, but the passage provides no evidence separating their effect from other possible causes. The justified response questions the claimed proof, not the possibility of an effect."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["即便如此","尽管这样"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Moreover","Besides"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0005-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["偏向","偏倚","成见"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0005-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0005-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Argument","correct_answer":"论点","metadata":{"tiles":["论点"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “Before refuting your argument, I want first to confirm whether I have accurately understood its underlying assumptions and final conclusion.” Start with “在” and end with “最终结论。”.","correct_answer":"在反驳您的论点之前，我想先确认自己是否准确地理解了您所依据的假设和最终结论。","metadata":{"tiles":["在","反驳","您的论点","之前，","我","想","先","确认","自己","是否","准确地","理解了","您所依据的","假设","和","最终结论。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["而且","另外","再者","并且"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":["Counterargument"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Counterargument","Refutation","Rebuttal"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0006-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0006-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["称"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0006-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0006-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: To persuade","correct_answer":"说服","metadata":{"tiles":["说服"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “To persuade an audience with different views, we need not only to state our position clearly but also to respond carefully to the questions that concern them most.” Start with “要想” and end with “疑问。”.","correct_answer":"要想说服持不同意见的听众，我们不仅要清楚地提出主张，还需要认真地回应他们最关心的疑问。","metadata":{"tiles":["要想","说服","持不同意见的听众，","我们","不仅","要","清楚地","提出主张，","还需要","认真地","回应","他们","最关心的","疑问。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["提议","建议","方案","建议书"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Agreement"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0001-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0001-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["行"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0001-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0001-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["日程","议事日程","会议议程"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0001-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0001-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Minutes","correct_answer":"会议记录","metadata":{"tiles":["会议记录"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “The minutes of this meeting are attached; please carefully check the listed decisions before formally confirming them, and let us know promptly if anything is missing.” Start with “随信附上” and end with “告知。”.","correct_answer":"随信附上本次会议的会议记录，敬请各位在正式确认之前仔细核对所列的决定，如有遗漏请及时告知。","metadata":{"tiles":["随信附上","本次会议的","会议记录，","敬请","各位","在正式确认之前","仔细","核对","所列的决定，","如有遗漏","请","及时","告知。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["契约","合约"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Implementation","To carry out"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0002-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0002-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["会议纪要","纪要"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0002-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0002-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: To delegate","correct_answer":"委派","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["委派"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “In this presentation, I will explain how to appoint suitable colleagues to handle different tasks while retaining responsibility for the project’s overall progress and quality.” Start with “在” and end with “负责。”.","correct_answer":"在这次报告中，我将说明如何委派合适的同事负责不同的任务，同时继续对项目整体进度和质量负责。","accepted_answers":["在这次报告中，我将说明如何委派合适的同事负责不同的任务，同时继续对质量和项目整体进度负责。"],"metadata":{"tiles":["在","这次报告中，","我","将","说明","如何","委派","合适的同事","负责","不同的任务，","同时","继续","对","项目整体进度","和","质量","负责。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["实行","执行","落实"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Tactics"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0003-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0003-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["委托","授权"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0003-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Efficiency","correct_answer":"效率","metadata":{"tiles":["效率"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “Provided that the new process really can improve efficiency without lowering the agreed quality standards, we are willing to make appropriate concessions on delivery time.” Start with “只要” and end with “让步。”.","correct_answer":"只要新流程确实能够提高效率，并且不降低已经约定的质量标准，我们就愿意在交付时间上作出适当的让步。","metadata":{"tiles":["只要","新流程","确实","能够","提高效率，","并且","不降低","已经约定的","质量标准，","我们","就愿意","在","交付时间上","作出","适当的","让步。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["战略","谋略","方略"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0004-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["To budget"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0004-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0004-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["相关方","攸关方"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0004-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Deadline","correct_answer":"截止日期","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["截止日期"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “We suggest moving the deadline back two weeks so that the assessment team can fully analyze potential risks before making a final decision instead of submitting a report hastily.” Start with “我们建议” and end with “报告。”.","correct_answer":"我们建议把截止日期推迟两周，以便负责评估的团队能够在作出最终决定之前充分分析潜在的风险，而不是仓促提交报告。","accepted_answers":["我们建议把截止日期推迟两周，以便在作出最终决定之前负责评估的团队能够充分分析潜在的风险，而不是仓促提交报告。"],"metadata":{"tiles":["我们建议","把截止日期","推迟两周，","以便","负责评估的团队","能够","在","作出最终决定之前","充分","分析","潜在的风险，","而不是","仓促","提交","报告。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0005-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0005-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["期限","最后期限","截止日","截止时间"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0005-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0005-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Negotiation","correct_answer":"谈判","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["谈判"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “After exchanging views at the conference, I hope to continue negotiations with you to explore further the areas in which we could establish long-term cooperation.” Start with “在会议上” and end with “合作关系。”.","correct_answer":"在会议上交换意见之后，我希望能与您继续谈判，进一步探讨双方在哪些领域可以建立长期的合作关系。","accepted_answers":["在会议上交换意见之后，我希望能与您继续谈判，进一步探讨双方可以在哪些领域建立长期的合作关系。"],"metadata":{"tiles":["在会议上","交换意见之后，","我","希望","能与您","继续","谈判，","进一步","探讨","双方","在哪些领域","可以","建立","长期的","合作关系。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["利益攸关方"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0006-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0006-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["纪要"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0006-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0006-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["协商","商谈","洽谈"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0006-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0006-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Proposal","correct_answer":"提案","metadata":{"tiles":["提案"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “Although this proposal is feasible in principle, we still need to clarify further the extra costs that might arise during implementation and who will bear the corresponding funding responsibility.” Start with “尽管” and end with “资金责任。”.","correct_answer":"尽管这份提案原则上具有可行性，我们仍需进一步明确实施过程中可能产生的额外费用，以及由谁承担相应的资金责任。","metadata":{"tiles":["尽管","这份提案","原则上","具有可行性，","我们","仍需","进一步","明确","实施过程中","可能产生的","额外费用，","以及","由谁","承担","相应的","资金责任。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["诗歌","诗篇","诗作"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Drawing","To paint","To draw"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0001-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0001-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["刻","像"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0001-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0001-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["主人公"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0001-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0001-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Plot twist","correct_answer":"情节转折","metadata":{"tiles":["情节转折"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “Through a strong contrast between light and dark colors, this painting suggests a plot twist in the story without directly explaining why the character suddenly changed their choice.” Start with “这幅画” and end with “自己的选择。”.","correct_answer":"这幅画通过明暗色彩的强烈对比暗示了故事中的情节转折，却没有直接说明人物为何突然改变了自己的选择。","metadata":{"tiles":["这幅画","通过","明暗色彩的","强烈对比","暗示了","故事中的","情节转折，","却","没有","直接","说明","人物","为何","突然","改变了","自己的选择。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["画","画作"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Statue","Sculpting"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0002-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0002-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["剧情反转","情节反转","剧情转折"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0002-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0002-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Review","correct_answer":"评论","metadata":{"tiles":["评论"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “In this review, I specifically point out that the novel’s contradictory memories force the reader to keep reassessing whether the narrator deserves trust.” Start with “在这篇评论中，” and end with “信任。”.","correct_answer":"在这篇评论中，我特别指出，小说里相互矛盾的回忆迫使读者不断重新判断叙述者是否值得信任。","metadata":{"tiles":["在这篇评论中，","我","特别","指出，","小说里","相互矛盾的","回忆","迫使读者","不断","重新","判断","叙述者","是否","值得","信任。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["雕刻","雕像"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0003-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Analogy","Figure of speech","Simile"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0003-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0003-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["手法"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0003-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0003-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["评述","评价"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0003-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Masterpiece","correct_answer":"杰作","metadata":{"tiles":["杰作"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “The film is regarded as a masterpiece not because it provides simple answers, but because it lets the audience see the complex circumstances behind the conflict.” Start with “这部电影” and end with “复杂处境。”.","correct_answer":"这部电影之所以被视为杰作，并不是因为它给出了简单的答案，而是因为它让观众看见了冲突背后的复杂处境。","metadata":{"tiles":["这部电影","之所以","被","视为","杰作，","并不是","因为","它","给出了","简单的答案，","而是","因为","它","让观众","看见了","冲突背后的","复杂处境。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0004-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"雕塑\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Sculpture","options":["Novel","Review","Symbolism","Sculpture"],"distractors":[]},"after":{"prompt":"Read this concert review: “在最后一段中，管弦乐队的音量逐渐降低，而主旋律反复出现。” What change in volume does the reviewer describe?","correct_answer":"The orchestra gradually plays more softly.","options":["The orchestra gradually plays more loudly.","The orchestra suddenly stops playing.","The orchestra maintains exactly the same volume.","The orchestra gradually plays more softly."],"distractors":["The orchestra gradually plays more loudly.","The orchestra suddenly stops playing.","The orchestra maintains exactly the same volume."]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["隐喻","暗喻"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0004-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["名作"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0004-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Inspiration","correct_answer":"灵感","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["灵感"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “The composer drew inspiration from traditional melodies and then gave those familiar sounds entirely new meaning through changing rhythms and unexpected harmonies.” Start with “作曲家” and end with “意义。”.","correct_answer":"作曲家从传统旋律中获得了灵感，又通过变化的节奏和出人意料的和声赋予这些熟悉的声音全新的意义。","accepted_answers":["作曲家从传统旋律中获得了灵感，又通过出人意料的和声和变化的节奏赋予这些熟悉的声音全新的意义。"],"metadata":{"tiles":["作曲家","从","传统旋律中","获得了","灵感，","又","通过","变化的节奏","和","出人意料的和声","赋予","这些熟悉的声音","全新的","意义。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0004-e00000000010","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"小说\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Novel","options":["Inspiration","Masterpiece","Novel","Plot twist"],"distractors":[]},"after":{"prompt":"Which change does “音乐的速度加快了” describe in a music review?","correct_answer":"The music gets faster.","options":["The music gets quieter.","The music gets slower.","The music gets faster.","The music starts again."],"distractors":["The music gets quieter.","The music gets slower.","The music starts again."]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["象征手法"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0005-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0005-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["人公"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0005-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0005-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Novel","correct_answer":"小说","metadata":{"tiles":["小说"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “If I were to write a novel, I would have two characters take turns recounting the same past events, allowing the reader gradually to discover that their memories do not entirely agree.” Start with “如果” and end with “完全一致。”.","correct_answer":"如果我要写一部小说，我会让两个人物轮流讲述同一段往事，使读者逐渐发现他们的记忆并不完全一致。","metadata":{"tiles":["如果","我","要写","一部小说，","我","会","让","两个人物","轮流","讲述","同一段往事，","使读者","逐渐","发现","他们的记忆","并不","完全一致。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["类型","文体","文类"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Main character","Leading character","Lead"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0006-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0006-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["反转"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0006-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0006-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["长篇小说"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0006-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0006-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Poem","correct_answer":"诗","metadata":{"tiles":["诗"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “The poem does not explicitly identify the source of its sense of loss, but leaves room for interpretation through recurring imagery, so different readers may reach different understandings.” Start with “这首诗” and end with “理解。”.","correct_answer":"这首诗并未明确交代失落感的来源，而是通过反复出现的意象保留了解释的空间，因此不同的读者可能产生不同的理解。","metadata":{"tiles":["这首诗","并未","明确","交代","失落感的来源，","而是","通过","反复出现的","意象","保留了","解释的空间，","因此","不同的读者","可能","产生","不同的","理解。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["一语中的","说到点子上","切中要害"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Very easy","Easy","A cinch"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0001-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0001-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["昂贵","高昂"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0001-e00000000005","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0001-b20000000000","type":"error_correction","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["迟到比不到好"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0001-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0001-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: To let the cat out of the bag","correct_answer":"说漏嘴","metadata":{"tiles":["说漏嘴"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “To avoid letting the secret slip early, he kept avoiding the topic of the birthday party and spoke only when all the guests were ready to surprise her.” Start with “为了” and end with “开口。”.","correct_answer":"为了不提前说漏嘴，他一直避开生日派对的话题，直到所有客人都准备好给她一个惊喜才开口。","metadata":{"tiles":["为了","不","提前","说漏嘴，","他","一直","避开","生日派对的话题，","直到","所有客人","都","准备好","给她","一个惊喜","才","开口。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["易如反掌","轻而易举"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Very expensive","Costly","Expensive"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0002-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0002-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["泄露秘密","泄密"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0002-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0002-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: To kill two birds with one stone","correct_answer":"一石二鸟","metadata":{"tiles":["一石二鸟"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “Taking advantage of a meeting downtown to drop off books at the library both saves a separate trip and returns the books on time: it really is killing two birds with one stone.” Start with “趁着” and end with “一石二鸟。”.","correct_answer":"趁着去市中心参加会议的机会，顺便把需要归还的书带到图书馆，既少跑了一趟路，又按时还了书，真是一石二鸟。","metadata":{"tiles":["趁着","去市中心","参加会议的机会，","顺便","把","需要归还的书","带到图书馆，","既","少跑了","一趟路，","又","按时还了书，","真是","一石二鸟。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["花一大笔钱","贵得要命","价格昂贵"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0003-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0003-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["一举两得"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0003-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: The ball is in your court","correct_answer":"球在你手上","metadata":{"tiles":["球在你手上"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “Since we have already put forward a concrete proposal, it is now your turn to make a decision; you still need to consider carefully whether to accept it.” Start with “既然” and end with “考虑。”.","correct_answer":"既然我们已经提出了具体的方案，接下来就轮到你作出决定，是否接受还需要由你认真考虑。","metadata":{"tiles":["既然","我们","已经","提出了","具体的方案，","接下来","就","轮到你","作出决定，","是否","接受","还需要","由你","认真","考虑。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0004-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["晚做总比不做好","晚来总比不来好"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0004-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Overjoyed","Ecstatic","To be overjoyed"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0004-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0004-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["轮到你了","现在就看你的了","由你决定"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0004-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Bite off more than you can chew","correct_answer":"贪多嚼不烂","metadata":{"tiles":["贪多嚼不烂"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “Taking on too many projects at once often leaves people unable to attend to everything; as the saying goes, do not bite off more than you can chew, so it is better to finish the work at hand first than hastily accept every request.” Start with “同时” and end with “做好。”.","correct_answer":"同时承担太多项目往往会让人顾此失彼，正所谓贪多嚼不烂，与其仓促答应所有请求，不如先把手头的工作做好。","metadata":{"tiles":["同时","承担","太多项目","往往","会","让人","顾此失彼，","正所谓","贪多嚼不烂，","与其","仓促","答应所有请求，","不如","先","把","手头的工作","做好。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["喜出望外","乐不可支","心花怒放"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["To joke","To kid","To tease","Joking"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0005-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0005-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["难遇"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0005-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0005-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: To break the ice","correct_answer":"打破僵局","metadata":{"tiles":["打破僵局"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word or phrase tile to translate: “To break the deadlock, the moderator first asked both sides to list the points they had already agreed on and then gradually discuss the key issues on which they still disagreed.” Start with “为了” and end with “关键问题。”.","correct_answer":"为了打破僵局，主持人先请双方列出已经达成共识的事项，然后再逐步讨论仍然存在分歧的关键问题。","metadata":{"tiles":["为了","打破僵局，","主持人","先","请","双方","列出","已经达成共识的事项，","然后","再","逐步","讨论","仍然","存在分歧的","关键问题。"],"distractors":[],"tile_joiner":""}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0006-e00000000002","before":{"less