d_answers":["Передавать полномочия"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4003-0003-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4003-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Efficiency","correct_answer":"Эффективность","metadata":{"tiles":["Эффективность"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “We are ready to review the contract terms if the effectiveness of the work does not decrease and expenses remain predictable.” For this task, use neutral prose order. Outside questions and relative clauses, put explicit subjects before finite verbs and direct objects after their verbs. Keep each preposition with its following phrase. Start with “Мы готовы” and end with “останутся предсказуемыми.”.","correct_answer":"Мы готовы пересмотреть условия договора, если эффективность работы не снизится, а расходы останутся предсказуемыми.","metadata":{"tiles":["Мы","готовы","пересмотреть","условия","договора,","если","эффективность","работы","не","снизится,","а","расходы","останутся","предсказуемыми."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4003-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4003-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Interested party"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4003-0005-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4003-0005-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["стка дня"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4003-0005-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4003-0005-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Дедлайн"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4003-0005-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4003-0005-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Negotiation","correct_answer":"Переговоры","metadata":{"tiles":["Переговоры"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “After the meeting with potential partners, we will continue negotiations, taking account of the priorities that we managed to identify during the discussion.” For this task, use neutral prose order. Outside questions and relative clauses, put explicit subjects before finite verbs and direct objects after their verbs. Keep each preposition with its following phrase. Start with “После встречи” and end with “ходе обсуждения.”.","correct_answer":"После встречи с потенциальными партнёрами мы продолжим переговоры, учитывая приоритеты, которые удалось определить в ходе обсуждения.","metadata":{"tiles":["После","встречи","с","потенциальными","партнёрами","мы","продолжим","переговоры,","учитывая","приоритеты,","которые","удалось","определить","в","ходе","обсуждения."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4003-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4003-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Заинтересованное лицо","Стейкхолдер"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4003-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4003-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Meeting agenda"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4003-0006-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4003-0006-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["окол заседания"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4003-0006-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4003-0006-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Ведение переговоров"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4003-0006-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4003-0006-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Proposal","correct_answer":"Предложение","metadata":{"tiles":["Предложение"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “The proposal provides for a gradual reduction in costs, but its implementation depends on whether it is possible to agree on the initial investment.” For this task, use neutral prose order. Outside questions and relative clauses, put explicit subjects before finite verbs and direct objects after their verbs. Keep each preposition with its following phrase. Start with “Предложение предусматривает” and end with “первоначальные инвестиции.”.","correct_answer":"Предложение предусматривает постепенное сокращение затрат, однако его реализация зависит от того, удастся ли согласовать первоначальные инвестиции.","metadata":{"tiles":["Предложение","предусматривает","постепенное","сокращение","затрат,","однако","его","реализация","зависит","от","того,","удастся","ли","согласовать","первоначальные","инвестиции."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Стих"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Picture"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0001-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0001-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Главная героиня","Главный персонаж","Протагонист"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Живопись"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Statue"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0002-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0002-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Сюжетный поворот"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0002-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0002-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Review","correct_answer":"Рецензия","metadata":{"tiles":["Рецензия"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “The review notes the expressiveness of the language, but questions the plausibility of the ending toward which the author leads the reader.” For this task, use neutral prose order. Outside questions and relative clauses, put explicit subjects before finite verbs and direct objects after their verbs. Keep each preposition with its following phrase. Start with “Рецензия отмечает” and end with “подводит читателя.”.","correct_answer":"Рецензия отмечает выразительность языка, но ставит под сомнение правдоподобие развязки, к которой автор подводит читателя.","metadata":{"tiles":["Рецензия","отмечает","выразительность","языка,","но","ставит","под","сомнение","правдоподобие","развязки,","к","которой","автор","подводит","читателя."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Изваяние"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0003-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0003-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Отзыв"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0003-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0003-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Masterpiece","correct_answer":"Шедевр","metadata":{"tiles":["Шедевр"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “Despite mixed reviews, many critics consider this production a masterpiece because it offers a new interpretation of a classic play.” For this task, use neutral prose order. Outside questions and relative clauses, put explicit subjects before finite verbs and direct objects after their verbs. Keep each preposition with its following phrase. Start with “Несмотря на” and end with “классической пьесы.”.","correct_answer":"Несмотря на противоречивые отзывы, многие критики считают этот спектакль шедевром, поскольку он предлагает новое прочтение классической пьесы.","metadata":{"tiles":["Несмотря","на","противоречивые","отзывы,","многие","критики","считают","этот","спектакль","шедевром,","поскольку","он","предлагает","новое","прочтение","классической","пьесы."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0004-e00000000001","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Скульптура\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Sculpture","options":["Protagonist","Symbolism","Sculpture","Review"],"distractors":[]},"after":{"prompt":"Read this concert review: «В финале оркестр играет всё тише, а основная мелодия повторяется». What change in volume does the reviewer describe?","correct_answer":"The orchestra gradually plays more softly.","options":["The orchestra maintains exactly the same volume.","The orchestra gradually plays more softly.","The orchestra gradually plays more loudly.","The orchestra suddenly stops playing."],"distractors":["The orchestra maintains exactly the same volume.","The orchestra gradually plays more loudly.","The orchestra suddenly stops playing."]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0004-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Inspiration","correct_answer":"Вдохновение","metadata":{"tiles":["Вдохновение"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “The composer finds inspiration in folk melodies, transforming familiar rhythms so that they sound unexpected to the modern listener.” For this task, use neutral prose order. Outside questions and relative clauses, put explicit subjects before finite verbs and direct objects after their verbs. Keep each preposition with its following phrase. Start with “Композитор находит” and end with “современного слушателя.”.","correct_answer":"Композитор находит вдохновение в народных мелодиях, преобразуя знакомые ритмы так, чтобы они звучали неожиданно для современного слушателя.","metadata":{"tiles":["Композитор","находит","вдохновение","в","народных","мелодиях,","преобразуя","знакомые","ритмы","так,","чтобы","они","звучали","неожиданно","для","современного","слушателя."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0004-e00000000010","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What does \"Роман\" mean in English?","correct_answer":"Novel","options":["Metaphor","Poem","Plot twist","Novel"],"distractors":[]},"after":{"prompt":"Which change does «оркестр постепенно ускоряет темп» describe in a concert review?","correct_answer":"The music gets faster.","options":["The music starts again.","The music gets slower.","The music gets quieter.","The music gets faster."],"distractors":["The music starts again.","The music gets slower.","The music gets quieter."]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0005-e00000000004","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0005-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["й персонаж"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0005-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0005-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Novel","correct_answer":"Роман","metadata":{"tiles":["Роман"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “In my novel, I intend to alternate narrators so that the reader notices the contradictions between their accounts of the same events.” For this task, use neutral prose order. Outside questions and relative clauses, put explicit subjects before finite verbs and direct objects after their verbs. Keep each preposition with its following phrase. Start with “В своём” and end with “же событий.”.","correct_answer":"В своём романе я намерен чередовать рассказчиков, чтобы читатель заметил противоречия между их версиями одних и тех же событий.","metadata":{"tiles":["В","своём","романе","я","намерен","чередовать","рассказчиков,","чтобы","читатель","заметил","противоречия","между","их","версиями","одних","и","тех","же","событий."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Main character"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0006-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0006-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: Poem","correct_answer":"Стихотворение","accepted_answers":[],"metadata":{"tiles":["Стихотворение"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “This poem conveys a sense of loss through fragmented images, leaving the reader the opportunity to reconstruct the link between memories independently.” For this task, use neutral prose order. Outside questions and relative clauses, put explicit subjects before finite verbs and direct objects after their verbs. Keep each preposition with its following phrase. Start with “Это стихотворение” and end with “между воспоминаниями.”.","correct_answer":"Это стихотворение передаёт чувство утраты через обрывочные образы, оставляя читателю возможность самостоятельно восстановить связь между воспоминаниями.","accepted_answers":["Это стихотворение передаёт чувство утраты через обрывочные образы, оставляя читателю возможность восстановить самостоятельно связь между воспоминаниями.","Это стихотворение передаёт чувство утраты через обрывочные образы, оставляя возможность читателю самостоятельно восстановить связь между воспоминаниями.","Это стихотворение передаёт чувство утраты через обрывочные образы, оставляя возможность читателю восстановить самостоятельно связь между воспоминаниями."],"metadata":{"tiles":["Это","стихотворение","передаёт","чувство","утраты","через","обрывочные","образы,","оставляя","читателю","возможность","самостоятельно","восстановить","связь","между","воспоминаниями."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0001-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Попасть в самую точку"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0001-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0001-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Easy as pie"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0001-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0001-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Очень редко"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0001-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0001-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","prompt":"Arrange the words to translate: To let the cat out of the bag","correct_answer":"Проболтаться","metadata":{"tiles":["Проболтаться"],"distractors":[]}},"after":{"prompt":"Arrange every word to translate: “I was afraid of letting the cat out of the bag about the surprise, so I kept my mouth shut until the end of the evening.” For this task, use neutral prose order. Outside questions and relative clauses, put explicit subjects before finite verbs and direct objects after their verbs. Keep each preposition with its following phrase. Start with “Я боялся” and end with “конца вечера.”.","correct_answer":"Я боялся проболтаться о сюрпризе, поэтому держал язык за зубами до конца вечера.","metadata":{"tiles":["Я","боялся","проболтаться","о","сюрпризе,","поэтому","держал","язык","за","зубами","до","конца","вечера."],"distractors":[]}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0002-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Легче лёгкого","Раз плюнуть","Пара пустяков"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0002-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["To cost a fortune"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0002-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0002-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Разболтать секрет","Выдать секрет"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0002-e00000000009","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0002-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Одним ударом убить двух зайцев"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0003-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0003-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Влететь в копеечку"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0003-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0003-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Одним выстрелом убить двух зайцев","Убить двух зайцев одним выстрелом","Одним ударом убить двух зайцев"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0004-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["To be in seventh heaven"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0004-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0004-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Теперь ваша очередь","Теперь ход за вами","Теперь ваш ход"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0005-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Быть на седьмом небе от счастья"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0005-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["To play a prank on someone","To prank someone"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0006-e00000000002","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Подшучивать над кем-то"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0006-e00000000003","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_native","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Very rarely"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0006-e00000000008","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0006-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Растопить лёд в отношениях"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"abeaa6a4-71a5-46d0-af6d-937e1d94abf1","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4004-0003-b20000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"絵画","correct_answer":"Painting","options":["Painting","Metaphor","Inspiration","Symbolism"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4004-c003-b20000000000","distractors":["Inspiration","Metaphor","Symbolism"]},"after":{"prompt":"観客","correct_answer":"Audience","options":["Audience","Metaphor","Inspiration","Symbolism"],"card_id":null,"distractors":["Metaphor","Inspiration","Symbolism"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"ae270784-2de7-481a-a755-9158f928fa56","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"error_correction","metadata":{},"hint_text":"«Каждое утро» means repeated trips — check the motion verb type.","explanation":"Unidirectional «иду» describes one trip in progress right now, which contradicts «каждое утро». Habitual repeated trips require the multidirectional verb: «хожу в бассейн»."},"after":{"metadata":{"correction_instruction":"Describe a regular habit of visiting the pool and returning, using the multidirectional verb ходить. Keep Каждое утро, я and в бассейн; change only the motion verb."},"hint_text":"For the selected general visit/return habit, use the first-person present хожу.","explanation":"«Каждое утро я иду в бассейн» can describe each outbound journey from a directional viewpoint. This task instead requests the general recurring visit-and-return habit, expressed by «Каждое утро я хожу в бассейн»."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"af630975-97b3-4947-9be8-37b976296c32","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":["Si fuera tú, compraría la casa","Si yo fuera tú compraría la casa","Si fuera tú compraría la casa","Si yo fuese tú, compraría la casa","Si fuese tú, compraría la casa","Si yo fuese tú compraría la casa","Si fuese tú compraría la casa"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Si fuera tú, compraría la casa","Si yo fuera tú compraría la casa","Si fuera tú compraría la casa","Si yo fuese tú, compraría la casa","Si fuese tú, compraría la casa","Si yo fuese tú compraría la casa","Si fuese tú compraría la casa","Si yo fuera usted, compraría la casa","Si fuera usted, compraría la casa","Si yo fuese usted, compraría la casa","Si fuese usted, compraría la casa"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"b0222cd7-644b-4d91-af84-c89ee01c6648","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-0004-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"읽다","correct_answer":"읽다","hint_text":"To read","card_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-c004-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"비","correct_answer":"비","hint_text":"Rain","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"b08ae05c-8994-498b-9a91-aec9654dc610","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1005-0001-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"Caliente","correct_answer":"Hot","options":["To read","Friend","Hot","Office"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1005-c007-000000000000","distractors":["Office","To read","Friend"]},"after":{"prompt":"Ingeniero","correct_answer":"Engineer","options":["Doctor","Nurse","Engineer","Teacher"],"card_id":null,"distractors":["Doctor","Nurse","Teacher"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"b306093e-5b46-41e4-9c84-443fca62bf1e","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0002-b20000000000","type":"word_form","explanation":"降られる is the classic suffering passive of an intransitive verb: the rain fell and I was affected. English cannot mirror this — it literally reads \"I was fallen on by the rain.\""},"after":{"explanation":"降られた is the plain-past adversity passive of 降る: the speaker was affected by the rain. English can say “I was rained on”; Japanese explicitly presents the event from the affected person’s viewpoint."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"b31ff4d5-4c3a-446c-856b-bde4d4bd8e9f","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-4006-0002-b20000000000","type":"error_correction","metadata":{"error_sentence":"Quando podes, vem cá jantar."},"hint_text":"«Quando» pointing to the future cannot take the present indicative.","explanation":"The sentence is an invitation for the future, so «quando» must be followed by the futuro do conjuntivo: «puderes» (from «puderam»). The present indicative «podes» would only fit a habitual statement, not this invitation."},"after":{"metadata":{"error_sentence":"Quando podes, vem cá jantar.","correction_instruction":"Make this an invitation for one future occasion, not a habitual invitation. Keep tu and the rest of the sentence; put poder in the futuro do conjuntivo."},"hint_text":"For the selected future occasion, use puderes, the tu form of the futuro do conjuntivo of poder.","explanation":"The requested future invitation uses «Quando puderes, vem cá jantar». The present «Quando podes» can describe a habitual situation; this task explicitly selects a future occasion rather than declaring every present-tense invitation ungrammatical."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"b4402c87-a947-4c4a-a670-f79b40d7106d","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-2001-0004-a20000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["Cousin","Nephew","Niece","Wife"],"distractors":["Wife","Cousin","Niece"]},"after":{"options":["Cousin","Nephew","Grandfather","Wife"],"distractors":["Wife","Cousin","Grandfather"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"b6fb5e42-e9f6-46be-bf30-8554f2e352bc","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-1005-0001-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"Quente","correct_answer":"Hot","options":["Teacher","Friend","Hot","Winter"],"distractors":["Teacher","Winter","Friend"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-5555-1005-c007-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Cozinheiro","correct_answer":"Cook","options":["Doctor","Cook","Teacher","Driver"],"distractors":["Doctor","Teacher","Driver"],"card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"b7169471-b0e3-4c21-a12c-7b4338d199dd","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4006-0001-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","explanation":"A resultative complement after the verb states the outcome: 洗干净 = wash clean. 把 requires the verb to carry a result like this — a bare verb cannot end a 把-sentence."},"after":{"explanation":"洗干净 states the washing result: clean. A 把 predicate normally needs more than a bare verb, but that extra material is not necessarily a result complement; aspect or an action measure can also complete it."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"b89c0db9-fb92-462f-9e54-f002c2b47281","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4006-0001-b20000000000","type":"word_form","explanation":"Present-tense verb statements are reported with -ㄴ/는다고: vowel-final stems take -ㄴ다고 (가다 → 간다고), consonant-final stems take -는다고 (먹다 → 먹는다고). Plain 가다고 is incorrect."},"after":{"explanation":"Present action-verb statements use -ㄴ/는다고: vowel-final stems take -ㄴ다고 (가다 → 간다고), and most consonant-final stems take -는다고 (먹다 → 먹는다고). A final ㄹ drops before -ㄴ다고 (살다 → 산다고). Plain 가다고 is incorrect."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"b94bd554-8089-444a-9b9a-b2e2a9dbe1aa","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0001-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["かていほう"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"b9c3f670-0e25-46c9-88c0-b5ca3bdcd911","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-3008-0004-b10000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["Whatever","Sincerely","Kind of","Regards"],"distractors":["Kind of","Whatever","Sincerely"]},"after":{"options":["Whatever","Awesome","Kind of","Regards"],"distractors":["Kind of","Whatever","Awesome"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"ba70a1dd-8b3a-4c29-ab2d-fbaa12337f44","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"error_correction","metadata":{"error_sentence":"先生、昨日の映画はもう拝見しましたか。"},"hint_text":"拝見する is humble — you cannot use it for the teacher's action.","explanation":"拝見する lowers the person who watches, so it can only describe your own viewing. For the teacher's action use respectful ご覧になる (or the honorific passive 見られる).","accepted_answers":["先生、昨日の映画はもうご覧になりましたか","せんせい、きのうのえいがはもうごらんになりましたか。","先生、昨日の映画はもう見られましたか。","先生、昨日の映画はもう見られましたか"]},"after":{"metadata":{"error_sentence":"先生、昨日の映画はもう拝見しましたか。","correction_instruction":"You are asking your teacher whether the teacher has seen the film. Rewrite with respectful language that honors the teacher’s viewing action."},"hint_text":"Honor the teacher’s viewing with ご覧になる or respectful 見られる.","explanation":"Here the teacher is the person being honored, so use ご覧になりましたか or respectful 見られましたか. 拝見する is humble: it can describe the speaker or someone on the speaker’s side in an appropriate relationship, not only first-person actions.","accepted_answers":["先生、昨日の映画はもうご覧になりましたか","せんせい、きのうのえいがはもうごらんになりましたか。","先生、昨日の映画はもう見られましたか。","先生、昨日の映画はもう見られましたか","先生昨日の映画はもうご覧になりましたか","先生昨日の映画はもう見られましたか"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"bab4780d-a010-4142-8c87-645c2f25b715","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0005-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"ニュースによると、九州で大きな地震があった___です。— Choose the correct form.","explanation":"Hearsay そうだ follows the plain form — including past あった — and pairs naturally with 〜によると. はず (deduction), つもり (intention), and べき (obligation) do not report information from a source, so the によると frame rules them out."},"after":{"prompt":"ニュースによると、九州で大きな地震があった___です。— Report the news using the hearsay form.","explanation":"For the requested hearsay report, use plain past あった + そうです. によると names the source. はず expresses an expectation or deduction, not this direct hearsay report; citing a source does not make はず universally ungrammatical."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"bad44abe-26d0-44dd-bbb6-bc5225aa78b7","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"word_form","explanation":"The result clause 않았을 거예요 (\"wouldn't have made a mistake\") requires a past counterfactual condition: 알았더라면 = \"if I had known.\" Plain 알면 would state a real, open condition instead."},"after":{"explanation":"The prompt explicitly requests a past counterfactual: 알았더라면 or 알았다면 means “if I had known.” Here it combines with 실수하지 않았을 거예요, “I would not have made a mistake.” Similar past-result wording can express inference in other contexts; the requested meaning determines this answer."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"baeae6c0-ab1f-415b-bab8-83a5afb8549f","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0002-b10000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["Then","Suddenly","Plot","Next"],"distractors":["Next","Plot","Suddenly"]},"after":{"options":["Then","Suddenly","Plot","Before"],"distractors":["Before","Plot","Suddenly"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"bb9c0990-8966-4861-a37f-8820442eec5b","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4006-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":["C'est exactement ce qu'il me faut"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["C'est exactement ce qu'il me faut","Voilà exactement ce dont j'ai besoin.","Voilà exactement ce qu'il me faut."]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"bc251eb2-7422-4768-ae7e-00db3dda8f07","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4005-0001-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","hint_text":"To pull someones leg"},"after":{"hint_text":"To pull someone's leg"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"bc54e8bb-d3de-4e8c-a733-3483f2ab0918","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1005-0001-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"热","correct_answer":"Hot","options":["Soccer","To read","Summer","Hot"],"distractors":["To read","Soccer","Summer"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1005-c007-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"厨师","correct_answer":"Cook","options":["Teacher","Cook","Doctor","Driver"],"distractors":["Teacher","Doctor","Driver"],"card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"be0b0006-bcf8-487e-823b-e54267c0da6d","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"error_correction","metadata":{},"hint_text":"Il giorno dopo shows this future was reported from the past.","explanation":"The shifted time phrase il giorno dopo proves the future is viewed from the past, so it must be condizionale passato: sarebbe venuto (or venuta), never the simple future verrà."},"after":{"metadata":{"correction_instruction":"Rewrite this report from a past viewpoint, using the past conditional for the event that was still future then. Keep il giorno dopo."},"hint_text":"Use the condizionale passato: sarebbe venuto or sarebbe venuta.","explanation":"The requested past reporting viewpoint uses sarebbe venuto or sarebbe venuta for the subsequent event. A simple future can occur when the event remains future from the current viewpoint; il giorno dopo alone does not prove that viewpoint impossible."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"be3ea445-bb29-4828-83de-fd5f1bc74d82","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-4006-0005-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","prompt":"___-se muitos livros nesta feira. (vender)"},"after":{"prompt":"Use the present indicative of vender in the standard passive-se construction: ___-se muitos livros nesta feira."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"bf3dafde-bfc1-478d-96c5-2b7d808c205f","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_transformation","metadata":{"instruction":"Rewrite in reported speech: O Pedro disse que…","originalSentence":"«Não posso ir à festa», disse o Pedro."},"hint_text":"«Posso» (present) → imperfeito of «poder».","explanation":"The present «posso» backshifts to the imperfeito «podia»: «disse que não podia ir». The rest of the sentence is unchanged because place and time expressions do not shift here."},"after":{"metadata":{"instruction":"Report from a later, past viewpoint using tense backshift: begin «O Pedro disse que…», change posso to the imperfeito, and keep the rest of the message.","originalSentence":"«Não posso ir à festa», disse o Pedro."},"hint_text":"For this requested past viewpoint, use podia.","explanation":"The requested backshift gives «O Pedro disse que não podia ir à festa». A current report can retain «pode» in a suitable context; this task explicitly asks for the later past viewpoint."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"bf78bc1b-ee8f-43de-a32b-d7c774fb473c","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4006-0001-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","hint_text":"Benché (although) always takes the subjunctive.","explanation":"Concessive conjunctions like benché, sebbene and nonostante always require the subjunctive: sia. With a present-tense main clause, use the present subjunctive, never the indicative è.","prompt":"Benché ___ stanco, Marco continua a lavorare."},"after":{"hint_text":"Use the present subjunctive of essere for Marco being tired now.","explanation":"Sia expresses the present concession here: although Marco is tired, he continues working. Benché commonly introduces subjunctive clauses; a conditional is possible in other concessive meanings, so this is not a universal ban on other moods.","prompt":"Complete with the present subjunctive of essere (Marco is tired now): Benché ___ stanco, Marco continua a lavorare."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"c183027d-597c-4ab9-ae20-e1c09c8b2d01","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1005-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"Oficina","correct_answer":"Office","options":["Cold","Office","Soccer","Winter"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1005-c003-000000000000","distractors":["Winter","Soccer","Cold"]},"after":{"prompt":"Nadar","correct_answer":"To swim","options":["To cook","To run","To read","To swim"],"card_id":null,"distractors":["To cook","To run","To read"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"c1d80410-e098-439e-81a2-2d0ad619c8b9","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4006-0005-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","hint_text":"You work IN a company — the relative needs that preposition plus an article.","explanation":"When the relative expresses place or means, the preposition must appear before it: en la que (also donde or en la cual). Plain «que» cannot absorb the preposition, and «quien» only refers to people."},"after":{"hint_text":"Trabajar en una empresa uses «en». Choose the relative expression that preserves that relationship.","explanation":"Among these choices, en la que expresses the place where he works. En que, en la cual and donde can also form grammatical versions of this sentence, but are not offered here. Plain que does not express the required relationship in this sentence, and quien refers to people."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"c2b39de6-b723-4b9a-8f73-7a9bef776c49","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-2007-0005-a20000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["The best","Better","The worst","Worse"],"distractors":["Worse","Better","The worst"]},"after":{"options":["The best","Cheaper","The worst","Worse"],"distractors":["Worse","Cheaper","The worst"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"c3bfdc45-4a78-45f5-aa23-f76721151cf9","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-1004-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"Время","correct_answer":"Time","options":["Time","Shoes","To pay","Money"],"distractors":["Money","Shoes","To pay"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-9999-1004-c009-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Юбка","correct_answer":"Skirt","options":["Shoes","Shirt","Dress","Skirt"],"distractors":["Shoes","Shirt","Dress"],"card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"c419bdae-8056-4f47-b02d-55c19ad7066c","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"sentence_transformation","accepted_answers":["Dijo que llegaría tarde a la cena"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Paula dijo que ella llegaría tarde a la cena"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"c4aa5145-2767-404b-ad1d-c40a4c5f62c7","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"雕塑","correct_answer":"雕塑","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":"Sculpture","card_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-c004-b20000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"音乐的速度加快了。","correct_answer":"音乐的速度加快了。","accepted_answers":["音樂的速度加快了。"],"hint_text":"The music gets faster.","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"c4d2e013-0cba-486a-aa5d-e10bfb93f192","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3008-0003-b10000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"걱정마","correct_answer":"걱정마"},"after":{"prompt":"걱정 마","correct_answer":"걱정 마"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"c4fe3c2d-8d52-4ebd-80cb-23eb220d6053","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-1005-0004-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"読む","correct_answer":"To read","options":["To read","Teacher","Friend","Soccer"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-6666-1005-c004-000000000000","distractors":["Teacher","Soccer","Friend"]},"after":{"prompt":"雨","correct_answer":"Rain","options":["Snow","Cloud","Rain","Wind"],"card_id":null,"distractors":["Snow","Cloud","Wind"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"c5a79a5e-202d-440c-9370-f42685ae19ee","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4004-0003-b20000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"Pintura","correct_answer":"Painting","options":["Genre","Poem","Painting","Inspiration"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4004-c003-b20000000000","distractors":["Poem","Inspiration","Genre"]},"after":{"prompt":"Público","correct_answer":"Audience","options":["Genre","Audience","Poem","Inspiration"],"card_id":null,"distractors":["Genre","Poem","Inspiration"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"c5d5398e-7b7c-46e4-8868-f2fa1d54ea14","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-3007-0003-b10000000000","type":"listening_type","hint_text":"Instead"},"after":{"hint_text":"Instead of"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"c73009da-eecf-47c3-8216-2cea125655b5","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4006-0005-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","explanation":"This condition is real and possible («если … будет»), so the plain future «останемся» is correct. «Бы» is only for unreal hypotheses, and it can never attach to a present-tense form like «остаёмся бы»."},"after":{"explanation":"The English sentence presents a real future possibility, so the matching result is future «останемся». «Остались бы» would express a hypothetical result instead. In the standard finite conditional construction, бы combines with a past-form verb, not «остаёмся»."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"c871a849-828a-4bb7-a7e6-574e36b35669","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-1004-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Heure","correct_answer":"Heure","hint_text":"Time","card_id":"aabbccdd-2222-1004-c009-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Robe","correct_answer":"Robe","hint_text":"Dress","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"c8dc5915-a343-4adb-8d13-19607ac7eed1","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-1005-0001-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Chaud","correct_answer":"Chaud","hint_text":"Hot","card_id":"aabbccdd-2222-1005-c007-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Cuisinier","correct_answer":"Cuisinier","hint_text":"Cook","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"c8deb24a-91ae-4d69-8312-1dd3cf733ccc","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"sentence_transformation","accepted_answers":["私は泥棒に自転車を盗まれた","わたしはどろぼうにじてんしゃをぬすまれた。","わたしはどろぼうにじてんしゃをぬすまれた","私は泥棒に自転車をぬすまれた。","私は泥棒に自転車をぬすまれた"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["私は泥棒に自転車を盗まれた","わたしはどろぼうにじてんしゃをぬすまれた。","わたしはどろぼうにじてんしゃをぬすまれた","私は泥棒に自転車をぬすまれた。","私は泥棒に自転車をぬすまれた","私は自転車を泥棒に盗まれた"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"c98104aa-5e43-4610-b530-d5ba9255b51e","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-2008-0001-a20000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["Festival","To celebrate","Holiday","Gift"],"distractors":["Festival","To celebrate","Gift"]},"after":{"options":["Winter","To celebrate","Holiday","Gift"],"distractors":["Winter","To celebrate","Gift"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"cc64852f-1a83-42ae-82a1-63cad18f7d99","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-3007-0003-b10000000000","type":"listening_type","hint_text":"Instead"},"after":{"hint_text":"Instead of"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"cc884780-cf79-4151-8413-2bf0fd97fb9a","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"Which sentence correctly honors the subject?","hint_text":"께서 + -(으)시- honor a respected subject; never honor yourself or a friend.","explanation":"선생님 deserves honorifics: the subject particle 께서 plus -(으)시- in the verb (오셨어요). Using them for yourself (제가 오셨어요) or a friend is incorrect, and dropping them for a teacher is impolite."},"after":{"prompt":"Which sentence uses both the honorific subject particle and an honorific verb to say that the teacher came to school?","hint_text":"For this teacher-focused sentence, combine 께서 with the honorific verb ending -(으)시-.","explanation":"선생님께서 학교에 오셨어요 uses both 께서 and subject-honorific 시 to honor the teacher. The friend sentence has a different subject, so it does not answer this question. Honoring a friend can be appropriate in a respectful or formal context; it is not universally forbidden."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"cd943f20-c111-479c-9564-3a8e452d85ea","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3008-0002-b10000000000","type":"listening_choice","correct_answer":"Dear Sir","options":["Cool","Informal","Dear Sir","Dude"]},"after":{"correct_answer":"Respected ... (before a name or title)","options":["Cool","Informal","Respected ... (before a name or title)","Dude"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"cf1f3e3c-a485-428c-bd84-f5f2ebb9bf0d","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"error_correction","accepted_answers":["Ela me perguntou que horas eram.","Ela perguntou-me que horas eram naquele momento."],"metadata":{"error_sentence":"Ela perguntou-me que horas são agora."},"hint_text":"A reported past question cannot keep the present tense together with «agora».","explanation":"With the past reporting verb «perguntou», the embedded question backshifts: «são» → «eram», and «agora» disappears (or becomes «naquele momento»). Keeping «são agora» mixes the original speaker's time with the reporter's."},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Ela me perguntou que horas eram.","Ela perguntou-me que horas eram naquele momento.","Ela perguntou-me que horas eram então.","Ela perguntou-me que horas eram naquele instante.","Ela me perguntou que horas eram naquele momento."],"metadata":{"error_sentence":"Ela perguntou-me que horas são agora.","correction_instruction":"Report the question later, referring to the time of the original question. Keep Ela and me; change são to the imperfeito. Omit agora or replace it with a past-time expression such as naquele momento or então."},"hint_text":"For the selected later report, use eram and refer to the original question time.","explanation":"For this later report, «são» becomes «eram» and «agora» is omitted or replaced by a past-time expression. The original present-tense wording can be valid in an immediate report sharing the same present; it is not universally ungrammatical."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"d00339df-a4a8-4c1c-bbaf-d4d1cd40f665","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4006-0005-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["愈来愈"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"d0853860-a731-4358-b36a-b2d420d90e9d","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4006-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":["Estoy buscando a alguien que tenga experiencia en ventas"],"hint_text":"Indefinite person → personal «a» + subjunctive in the relative clause. Sales = ventas.","explanation":"«Alguien» is indefinite, so the relative verb is subjunctive: tenga. Note the personal «a» before alguien: busco a alguien. Both the mood and the «a» trip up English speakers."},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Estoy buscando a alguien que tenga experiencia en ventas","Busco alguien que tenga experiencia en ventas","Estoy buscando alguien que tenga experiencia en ventas","Yo busco a alguien que tenga experiencia en ventas","Busco una persona que tenga experiencia en ventas"],"hint_text":"For the intended non-specific person, use the subjunctive in the relative clause. With buscar, personal «a» before alguien is optional. Sales = ventas.","explanation":"For someone not yet identified, use tenga: busco (a) alguien que tenga experiencia en ventas. With buscar, both alguien and a alguien are standard here. The subjunctive follows the intended non-specific reading, not the word alguien alone."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"d1691e2f-ef99-4cab-abcd-f4e4958f23ba","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-0004-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"읽다","correct_answer":"To read","options":["Cold","Winter","To read","To cook"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-c004-000000000000","distractors":["Cold","Winter","To cook"]},"after":{"prompt":"비","correct_answer":"Rain","options":["Snow","Cloud","Wind","Rain"],"card_id":null,"distractors":["Snow","Cloud","Wind"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"d1961527-6d0b-4888-b1a4-dd6f0c856964","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-3007-0002-b10000000000","type":"listening_choice","correct_answer":"Would","options":["Perhaps","Would","If","Instead"]},"after":{"correct_answer":"Would do / would make","options":["Perhaps","Would do / would make","If","Instead"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"d2362fff-91c8-4ecb-b002-be57fadb3b10","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":["교수님, 지금 시간이 있으세요","교수님 지금 시간 있으세요","교수님, 지금 시간 있으세요","교수님 지금 시간이 있으십니까","교수님 지금 시간 있으십니까"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["교수님, 지금 시간이 있으세요","교수님 지금 시간 있으세요","교수님, 지금 시간 있으세요","교수님 지금 시간이 있으십니까","교수님 지금 시간 있으십니까","교수님, 지금 시간이 있으십니까","교수님, 지금 시간 있으십니까"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"d32c009e-3a5c-4466-98c1-d7ec838b7f73","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1005-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"办公室","correct_answer":"Office","options":["Office","Soccer","Cold","To cook"],"distractors":["To cook","Cold","Soccer"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-8888-1005-c003-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"我喜欢画画。","correct_answer":"I like drawing.","options":["I like reading.","I like cooking.","I like drawing.","I like swimming."],"distractors":["I like reading.","I like cooking.","I like swimming."],"card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"d36fea7f-4548-4e53-8691-a981d932af82","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","accepted_answers":[],"explanation":"The verbal adverb «вернувшись» frames the completed prior action. The distractor «Вернулся» is a finite verb — using it would produce two main verbs with no conjunction, which Russian does not allow here."},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Вернувшись домой, выпил он чаю"],"explanation":"«Вернувшись домой» is a verbal-adverb phrase marking completion before drinking tea. The distractor «Вернулся» is finite and does not perform the requested verbal-adverb transformation; Russian can otherwise connect finite clauses without a conjunction."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"d42aa73d-1239-4933-8a9b-695fb6ab54d2","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0001-b10000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["If","Suppose","Imagine","Could"],"distractors":["If","Suppose","Could"]},"after":{"options":["If","Must","Imagine","Could"],"distractors":["If","Must","Could"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"d439c25b-7d93-423d-918c-a8696eed265a","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4006-0002-b20000000000","type":"word_form","explanation":"Polite requests use the conditionnel présent: pourrais (stem pourr- + ending -ais). The present « peux » sounds abrupt, and the future « pourras » makes a prediction, not a polite request."},"after":{"explanation":"The requested conditionnel présent is pourrais: pourr- + -ais. The conditional softens a request. Present peux and future pourras can also make requests in suitable contexts, but this exercise explicitly asks for the conditional."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"d4659ae9-5a03-40d3-a579-d2eb2cf43eaf","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-1005-0004-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"Ler","correct_answer":"To read","options":["Cold","Teacher","To read","Soccer"],"distractors":["Soccer","Teacher","Cold"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-5555-1005-c004-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Está chovendo.","correct_answer":"It is raining.","options":["It is cold.","It is hot.","It is snowing.","It is raining."],"distractors":["It is cold.","It is hot.","It is snowing."],"card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"d57e9f23-9386-43a4-97a2-14bda118001a","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0001-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["せつ"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"d5f905af-543c-4046-8d49-f2b2652650a4","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["열리어서"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"d7add334-b68c-476b-9858-ef361e19c0e5","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-1005-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Офис","correct_answer":"Офис","hint_text":"Office","card_id":"aabbccdd-9999-1005-c003-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Я люблю рисовать.","correct_answer":"Я люблю рисовать.","hint_text":"I like drawing.","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"d7d5dce5-5343-4553-b299-c24cf8d28d50","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["ぜんちし"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"d85c16c5-93cd-416c-91fc-122dffe646e5","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-2004-0003-a20000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"慰概"},"after":{"prompt":"慷慨"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"d911a024-284e-4ea6-8cc8-c6c9fe8d4485","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"error_correction","hint_text":"Remove 很; add 多了 (or 得多) after 大 for 'much bigger'.","explanation":"很 is not allowed before the adjective in a 比-sentence. To say \"much bigger\", put 多了 or 得多 after 大: 比那个大多了.","metadata":{"error_sentence":"这个房间比那个很大。"},"accepted_answers":["这个房间比那个大多了。","这个房间比那个大得多","这个房间比那个大得多。"]},"after":{"hint_text":"Remove 很 before 大; use 多了, 得多 or 很多 after 大 for much bigger.","explanation":"For much bigger, use 比那个大多了, 大得多 or 大很多. Bare 很 before 大 does not express the intended degree of difference in this construction.","metadata":{"error_sentence":"这个房间比那个很大。","correction_instruction":"Rewrite to say: This room is much bigger than that one. Keep the comparison with 比 and express much bigger after 大."},"accepted_answers":["这个房间比那个大多了。","这个房间比那个大得多","这个房间比那个大得多。","这个房间比那个大很多"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"dab0e8b2-5a6a-44b4-be25-38a83e4358ea","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0003-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","accepted_answers":[]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["だいめいし"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"db4e8ba3-0415-4dbc-9aeb-597ee38171e4","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Скульптура","correct_answer":"Скульптура","hint_text":"Sculpture","card_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-c004-b20000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Музыка звучит всё быстрее.","correct_answer":"Музыка звучит всё быстрее.","hint_text":"The music gets faster.","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"dbc346d0-caa9-4e75-8b6a-2174adcda40b","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-3007-0002-b10000000000","type":"listening_choice","correct_answer":"Would","options":["Perhaps","Would","Regret","Suppose"]},"after":{"correct_answer":"Would do / would make","options":["Perhaps","Would do / would make","Regret","Suppose"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"dbf9fd46-5303-4977-9d8b-9a43de361712","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Ufficio","correct_answer":"Ufficio","hint_text":"Office","card_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1005-c003-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Mi piace disegnare.","correct_answer":"Mi piace disegnare.","hint_text":"I like drawing.","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"dd3abd3b-85e6-481c-ac42-e522ac730ac5","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-2008-0001-a20000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["Costume","Christmas","Party","Festival"],"distractors":["Christmas","Costume","Festival"]},"after":{"options":["Costume","Christmas","Party","Calendar"],"distractors":["Christmas","Costume","Calendar"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"ddf30b18-56ad-4fe7-a2fa-9086bdd8d94b","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"error_correction","hint_text":"Check the mood after credere che.","explanation":"Credere che requires the subjunctive: venga, not the indicative viene. Venire has an irregular subjunctive stem: venga, veniamo, vengano.","metadata":{}},"after":{"hint_text":"Rewrite in formal Italian using the present subjunctive after credo che.","explanation":"In the formal subjunctive pattern practised here, viene becomes venga. Venire has an irregular subjunctive stem: venga, veniamo, vengano. Colloquial indicative usage is not the target of this exercise.","metadata":{"correction_instruction":"Rewrite the opinion clause in formal Italian using the present subjunctive. Keep the subject and meaning unchanged."}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"deac5044-0d19-4991-b4c2-034f6317d4e6","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-3007-0002-b10000000000","type":"listening_type","hint_text":"Would"},"after":{"hint_text":"Would do / would make (il/elle/on form)"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"deebfc53-d075-4bda-9957-251ff52f3430","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-3007-0003-b10000000000","type":"listening_type","hint_text":"Instead"},"after":{"hint_text":"Instead of"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"dfdbe532-d58f-4084-a116-fb6b3de24dc7","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"sentence_transformation","explanation":"Two changes: the person shifts (abito → third person) and the tense backshifts (present → imperfect): abitava. The connector che is obligatory in Italian reported speech."},"after":{"explanation":"The finite backshifted version is Anna ha detto che abitava a Roma. Because Anna is also the subject of abitare, Anna ha detto di abitare a Roma is a valid infinitival version. Che introduces the finite clause, not every possible reported-speech construction."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"e0990161-82cc-430a-b6e0-7129cb27c11f","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4006-0002-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","accepted_answers":["엄마가 야채를 아이에게 먹였어요"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["엄마가 야채를 아이에게 먹였어요","아이에게 엄마가 야채를 먹였어요","야채를 엄마가 아이에게 먹였어요","아이에게 야채를 엄마가 먹였어요","야채를 아이에게 엄마가 먹였어요"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"e107bcd2-e72b-44c2-8933-00c51ec8cdcc","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"word_form","hint_text":"A conditional main verb calls for the imperfect subjunctive.","explanation":"After a conditional main clause (sarebbe meglio che), the subordinate takes the imperfect subjunctive: rimanessi. This mood sequence is fixed: never the present subjunctive rimanga here."},"after":{"hint_text":"With the advisability expression sarebbe meglio che, use the imperfect subjunctive.","explanation":"Sarebbe meglio che expresses advisability in the present conditional and takes rimanessi in this standard sequence. This particular construction does not establish a rule for every conditional main verb."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"e16e7b1e-bcb2-4db9-a330-7594096f8b0b","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0003-b20000000000","type":"error_correction","metadata":{"error_sentence":"私は先週、部長に二時間も残業しました。"},"accepted_answers":["私は先週、部長に二時間も残業させられました","私は先週部長に二時間も残業させられました。","私は先週部長に二時間も残業させられました","わたしはせんしゅう、ぶちょうににじかんもざんぎょうさせられました。"]},"after":{"metadata":{"error_sentence":"私は先週、部長に二時間も残業しました。","correction_instruction":"Use the causative-passive to say that your manager made you do two hours of overtime last week."},"accepted_answers":["私は先週、部長に二時間も残業させられました","私は先週部長に二時間も残業させられました。","私は先週部長に二時間も残業させられました","わたしはせんしゅう、ぶちょうににじかんもざんぎょうさせられました。","先週、私は部長に二時間も残業させられました","先週私は部長に二時間も残業させられました"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"e261eab7-d9ba-4777-9225-9e1929930b62","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-1005-0004-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Читать","correct_answer":"Читать","hint_text":"To read","card_id":"aabbccdd-9999-1005-c004-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Идёт дождь.","correct_answer":"Идёт дождь.","hint_text":"It is raining.","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"e34a0643-78b8-4df5-8a61-f1c296d2cc0a","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"彫刻","correct_answer":"Sculpture","options":["Metaphor","Sculpture","Inspiration","Masterpiece"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4004-c004-b20000000000","distractors":["Masterpiece","Inspiration","Metaphor"]},"after":{"prompt":"旋律","correct_answer":"Melody","options":["Rhythm","Harmony","Silence","Melody"],"card_id":null,"distractors":["Rhythm","Harmony","Silence"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"e488af3c-be1b-49fb-887c-35438fede3d6","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4006-0001-b20000000000","type":"error_correction","hint_text":"Check the mood of the verb after penso che.","explanation":"The indicative è cannot follow penso che: opinion verbs require the subjunctive sia. Using the indicative after verbs of opinion is the most frequent B2 subjunctive error.","metadata":{}},"after":{"hint_text":"Rewrite the opinion clause in formal Italian using the present subjunctive.","explanation":"For the formal subjunctive construction practised here, change è to sia. Penso che with indicative also occurs in colloquial Italian; this is a register-and-mood transformation.","metadata":{"correction_instruction":"Rewrite the opinion clause in formal Italian using the present subjunctive. Keep the subject and meaning unchanged."}}},{"table":"exercises","id":"e56121c5-168e-4507-8c42-19c6a25456a8","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4006-0005-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":["汉语越来越有意思了。","汉语越来越有意思","汉语越来越有意思。","中文越来越有意思了","中文越来越有意思了。","中文越来越有意思","中文越来越有意思。","汉语越来越有趣了","中文越来越有趣了"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["汉语越来越有意思了。","汉语越来越有意思","汉语越来越有意思。","中文越来越有意思了","中文越来越有意思了。","中文越来越有意思","中文越来越有意思。","汉语越来越有趣了","中文越来越有趣了","汉语越来越有趣","中文越来越有趣"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"e7dc2497-3a9a-4c9b-a975-edfd559eb7c6","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-2003-0006-a20000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"씨다","correct_answer":"씨다"},"after":{"prompt":"씻다","correct_answer":"씻다"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"e962c277-c7f3-4c1c-a0f5-50f0aa566354","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4006-0002-b20000000000","type":"error_correction","hint_text":"One verb is in an impossible form — remember: the conditional never follows «si».","explanation":"«Si tendría» is ungrammatical: after «si» in hypothetical conditions Spanish requires the imperfect subjunctive (tuviera/tuviese). The conditional belongs only in the main clause (aprendería)."},"after":{"hint_text":"In this hypothetical condition, use the imperfect subjunctive after «si»; the main clause keeps the conditional.","explanation":"For this hypothetical present/future condition, standard Spanish uses si tuviera/tuviese, followed by aprendería in the main clause. This rule concerns conditional «si» meaning if; indirect-question «si» meaning whether can be followed by a conditional."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"ea417ca4-a687-4a4d-8eff-e4939ae7c2fc","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4006-0001-b20000000000","type":"word_form","explanation":"Konjunktiv II of strong and mixed verbs is built from the Präteritum plus umlaut: hatte wird hätte. Ich hätte gern ... is the standard way to say what you would like to have."},"after":{"explanation":"The Konjunktiv II of haben is hätte, formed from hatte with an umlaut. Other verbs have their own patterns; not every strong or mixed verb adds an umlaut. Ich hätte gern expresses what the speaker would like to have."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"ea64ee76-fb56-4670-9ea7-8d748508aecf","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-1001-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["Good morning","Hello","Good evening","Yes"],"distractors":["Hello","Good evening","Yes"]},"after":{"options":["Good morning","Good night","Good evening","Yes"],"distractors":["Good night","Good evening","Yes"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"ea9f6da6-9463-491a-9169-886b1fb6adbe","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-3007-0002-b10000000000","type":"listening_type","hint_text":"Would"},"after":{"hint_text":"Would do / would make"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"eb9d95c4-be50-46d2-835d-a8f71fa8ade2","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4005-0001-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","hint_text":"To pull someones leg"},"after":{"hint_text":"To pull someone's leg"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"ebde80bf-8320-4b6d-be8b-9044a535c089","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0005-b20000000000","type":"error_correction","metadata":{"error_sentence":"私は明日、会社を休むらしいです。"},"hint_text":"らしい reports information about others, not your own intentions.","explanation":"らしい marks inference from outside information, so it cannot describe your own plan. State intentions directly: 休むつもりです, 休む予定です, or simply 休みます.","accepted_answers":["私は明日、会社を休むつもりです","私は明日、会社を休む予定です。","私は明日、会社を休む予定です","私は明日、会社を休みます。","私は明日、会社を休みます","わたしはあした、かいしゃをやすむつもりです。"]},"after":{"metadata":{"error_sentence":"私は明日、会社を休むらしいです。","correction_instruction":"State your own deliberate plan directly, rather than reporting information you heard about your schedule. Use つもりです, 予定です, or a direct polite statement."},"hint_text":"Use a direct expression of your intention or plan, such as 休むつもりです.","explanation":"For your directly stated plan, use 休むつもりです, 休む予定です or 休みます. らしい would instead suggest information or inference, possibly even about your own schedule; it is not the direct-intention meaning requested here.","accepted_answers":["私は明日、会社を休むつもりです","私は明日、会社を休む予定です。","私は明日、会社を休む予定です","私は明日、会社を休みます。","私は明日、会社を休みます","わたしはあした、かいしゃをやすむつもりです。","私は明日会社を休むつもりです","私は明日会社を休む予定です","私は明日会社を休みます"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"ec64a513-0706-4857-a328-c177f0f1318d","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4006-0002-b20000000000","type":"sentence_construction","explanation":"Reaching a specific endpoint uses до- with the preposition до: «доехали до центра». The distractor «приехали» (arrived) does not combine with «до центра» — при- takes в or на with the destination."},"after":{"explanation":"Reaching a specific endpoint uses до- with the preposition до: «доехали до центра». The distractor «приехали» (arrived) does not combine with «до центра» — the corresponding arrival phrase here would be «приехали в центр»."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"ecf9d412-435e-45d3-bab9-546e93a219b0","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-3007-0003-b10000000000","type":"listening_choice","correct_answer":"Instead","options":["Instead","Imagine","Should","I wish"]},"after":{"correct_answer":"Instead of","options":["Instead of","Imagine","Should","I wish"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"eda26dfc-0f79-4688-8216-6b4c9cddcacb","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"사무실","correct_answer":"사무실","hint_text":"Office","card_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-c003-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"수영하다","correct_answer":"수영하다","hint_text":"To swim","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"ee46e7ba-5da0-4ab4-a458-af9b1797ef11","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-2004-0003-a20000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["Proud","Angry","Brave","Kind"],"distractors":["Proud","Kind","Brave"]},"after":{"options":["Proud","Angry","Lazy","Kind"],"distractors":["Proud","Kind","Lazy"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"eeb44889-bbf9-466c-8194-5c14a4fe3027","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4006-0002-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","explanation":"An unreal present condition uses se + imperfect subjunctive (fossi) with the conditional in the main clause (comprerei). Se sarei is the classic error: the conditional never follows se."},"after":{"explanation":"This unreal present condition uses se + imperfect subjunctive (fossi), with the conditional comprerei in the main clause. The restriction applies to hypothetical se meaning if, not interrogative se meaning whether."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"ef2a64fa-5f45-4ebc-9769-e8e261200278","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4004-0003-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Pintura","correct_answer":"Pintura","hint_text":"Painting","card_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4004-c003-b20000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Público","correct_answer":"Público","hint_text":"Audience","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"ef838062-e1b6-4209-a36b-2427d851c5ca","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4006-0001-b20000000000","type":"fill_blank","explanation":"«Каждое утро» marks a repeated habit, and habits always take the imperfective. The present-tense form of пить for он is «пьёт» (also typed «пьет»). A perfective verb cannot express a present habitual meaning."},"after":{"explanation":"Here «каждое утро» describes a regular present habit, so use the imperfective present «пьёт» (also typed «пьет»). This is the ordinary present-habit construction; it is not a rule that every description of repeated events must use an imperfective verb."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"f05f45df-f49f-47ea-97e8-29ad3ce7e25f","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4006-0004-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":["Se vendieron las entradas en una hora"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Se vendieron las entradas en una hora","En una hora se vendieron las entradas","Los boletos se vendieron en una hora","Los billetes se vendieron en una hora","Se vendieron los boletos en una hora"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"f07b3c95-8a1d-4ce3-bcbf-c0dcd004b1c0","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-4006-0002-b20000000000","type":"translate_to_target","accepted_answers":["Se tu vires a Maria, diz-lhe a verdade.","Se vires a Maria, conta-lhe a verdade.","Se tu vires a Maria, conta-lhe a verdade.","Se vires Maria, diz-lhe a verdade."]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Se tu vires a Maria, diz-lhe a verdade.","Se vires a Maria, conta-lhe a verdade.","Se tu vires a Maria, conta-lhe a verdade.","Se vires Maria, diz-lhe a verdade.","Diz-lhe a verdade se vires a Maria.","Se vires Maria, conta-lhe a verdade."]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"f094953d-b727-43e7-8f51-2ad1937a6c2a","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-0001-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"더운","correct_answer":"Hot","options":["Hot","To cook","Office","Doctor"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-7777-1005-c007-000000000000","distractors":["Office","To cook","Doctor"]},"after":{"prompt":"엔지니어","correct_answer":"Engineer","options":["Nurse","Teacher","Doctor","Engineer"],"card_id":null,"distractors":["Nurse","Teacher","Doctor"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"f0f149d9-6a47-46a3-922b-d4abf3e38933","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-1001-0002-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["Good morning","Hello","Excuse me","Sorry"],"distractors":["Good morning","Excuse me","Hello"]},"after":{"options":["Good morning","Hello","Good night","Sorry"],"distractors":["Good morning","Good night","Hello"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"f27bfe0a-a415-4ee2-821f-fe19d0c681bb","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-3007-0002-b10000000000","type":"listening_choice","options":["Regret","Could","If","Suppose"],"distractors":["If","Regret","Could"]},"after":{"options":["Regret","Could","Because","Suppose"],"distractors":["Because","Regret","Could"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"f29d2057-2242-4ad5-ad77-3a91908ef964","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4006-0001-b20000000000","type":"cloze_deletion","prompt":"Je ne pense pas qu'elle ___ la vérité. (savoir)","hint_text":"« Ne pas penser que » expresses doubt — which mood follows?","explanation":"Negated opinion verbs like « ne pas penser que » take the subjunctive because the truth is in doubt. « Savoir » is irregular: sache. Affirmative « je pense que » would take the indicative « sait »."},"after":{"prompt":"Express doubt using the present subjunctive of savoir: Je ne pense pas qu'elle ___ la vérité.","hint_text":"Use the present subjunctive of savoir for elle.","explanation":"This exercise selects the subjunctive to present the statement as doubtful: sache. After a negative opinion verb, mood depends on the speaker's stance; indicative or conditional forms can occur in other contexts."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"f471b8e8-ef18-4b83-96b1-f387ab5ae077","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-5555-1005-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Escritório","correct_answer":"Escritório","hint_text":"Office","card_id":"aabbccdd-5555-1005-c003-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"Gosto de desenhar.","correct_answer":"Gosto de desenhar.","hint_text":"I like drawing.","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"f6f97196-7ee0-42eb-bc0d-173ee86a89d4","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","hint_text":"A time-span phrase signals process, not result.","explanation":"«Целый месяц» measures the duration of the activity, so the imperfective «читал» is required. Perfective «прочитал» presents the action as one completed point and cannot combine with a duration phrase."},"after":{"hint_text":"The English was reading selects the ongoing reading activity measured by целый месяц.","explanation":"Here «читал» matches the ongoing reading activity in “was reading … for a whole month”. A completed reading within a month could be expressed as «прочитал за месяц». This does not mean that perfective verbs are instantaneous or that no perfective verb can occur with a duration phrase."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"f777afaf-bd79-480f-a13c-c5e54f859217","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4004-0004-b20000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"彫刻","correct_answer":"彫刻","accepted_answers":[],"hint_text":"Sculpture","card_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4004-c004-b20000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"旋律","correct_answer":"旋律","accepted_answers":["せんりつ"],"hint_text":"Melody","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"f7e10f7c-4934-4511-8f7e-ec874d11d676","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4006-0002-b20000000000","type":"sentence_transformation","accepted_answers":["Si tuviera tiempo iría al gimnasio","Si tuviese tiempo, iría al gimnasio","Si tuviese tiempo iría al gimnasio","Si yo tuviera tiempo, iría al gimnasio","Si yo tuviera tiempo iría al gimnasio","Si yo tuviese tiempo, iría al gimnasio","Si yo tuviese tiempo iría al gimnasio"]},"after":{"accepted_answers":["Si tuviera tiempo iría al gimnasio","Si tuviese tiempo, iría al gimnasio","Si tuviese tiempo iría al gimnasio","Si yo tuviera tiempo, iría al gimnasio","Si yo tuviera tiempo iría al gimnasio","Si yo tuviese tiempo, iría al gimnasio","Si yo tuviese tiempo iría al gimnasio","Si tuviera tiempo, yo iría al gimnasio","Si tuviese tiempo, yo iría al gimnasio"]}},{"table":"exercises","id":"f8c2a4f0-e7fb-4ba7-a89f-87e6ba2e4521","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"error_correction","hint_text":"One verb form is impossible after «si» — swap it for the imperfect subjunctive.","explanation":"The conditional never follows «si»: «si sabría» must become si supiera/supiese. The main clause keeps the conditional: te la diría."},"after":{"hint_text":"In this hypothetical condition, change the si-clause verb to the imperfect subjunctive.","explanation":"This hypothetical condition requires si supiera/supiese in standard Spanish. Keep te la diría in the main clause. The restriction is not a ban on the conditional after indirect-question «si» meaning whether."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"fc51d8ce-36aa-4a39-94cd-548defdbcab5","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4006-0006-b20000000000","type":"multiple_choice","explanation":"Only a participle can modify a noun: «стоящий» agrees with «мальчик». «Стоя» is a verbal adverb and would describe the manner of another verb; «стоит» and «стоять» are finite and infinitive forms that cannot serve as a modifier here."},"after":{"explanation":"Of these options, only the participle supplies the required modifier: «стоящий» agrees with «мальчик». «Стоя» is a verbal adverb and would describe the manner of another verb; «стоит» and «стоять» are finite and infinitive forms that cannot serve as a modifier here."}},{"table":"exercises","id":"fc64267c-86d8-4616-80b3-5fa1b9cb11ed","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-2222-1005-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_type","prompt":"Bureau","correct_answer":"Bureau","hint_text":"Office","card_id":"aabbccdd-2222-1005-c003-000000000000"},"after":{"prompt":"J’aime dessiner.","correct_answer":"J’aime dessiner.","hint_text":"I like drawing.","card_id":null}},{"table":"exercises","id":"fedb1db8-6c38-4140-a81c-c2ae22673f85","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3008-0003-b10000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"걱정마"},"after":{"prompt":"걱정 마"}},{"table":"exercises","id":"feed74fe-c16a-4bf8-9946-80072913d0a0","before":{"lesson_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1005-0003-000000000000","type":"listening_choice","prompt":"Verano","correct_answer":"Summer","options":["Doctor","To cook","Summer","Soccer"],"card_id":"aabbccdd-1111-1005-c009-000000000000","distractors":["Doctor","To cook","Soccer"]},"after":{"prompt":"Guitarra","correct_answer":"Guitar","options":["To cook","Guitar","Soccer","To read"],"card_id":null,"distractors":["To cook","Soccer","To read"]}},{"table":"grammar_rules","id":"01c5536c-6f2d-413f-90d7-29d5176dfaec","before":{"language":"es","cefr_level":"B2","explanation":"Real: si + present indicative, future in the main clause (Si llueve, nos quedaremos). Unreal present: si + imperfect subjunctive + conditional (Si tuviera dinero, viajaría). Unreal past: si + pluperfect subjunctive + conditional perfect (Si hubiera sabido, habría venido). Never put the conditional or future directly after si.","common_errors":[{"note":"The conditional never follows si; use the imperfect subjunctive.","error":"Si tendría tiempo, iría.","correction":"Si tuviera tiempo, iría."}]},"after":{"explanation":"Common patterns: real condition, si + present indicative, with a future, present or imperative result; hypothetical present/future, si + imperfect subjunctive with a conditional result; unreal past, si + pluperfect subjunctive with a conditional perfect or pluperfect subjunctive result. These restrictions apply to conditional si (if), not indirect-question si (whether).","common_errors":[{"note":"In this hypothetical condition, standard Spanish uses the imperfect subjunctive in the si-clause.","error":"Si tendría tiempo, iría.","correction":"Si tuviera tiempo, iría."}]}},{"table":"grammar_rules","id":"0e4a2d10-8de9-4a68-92fc-0cb5e0128cc3","before":{"language":"de","cefr_level":"B2","explanation":"The Vorgangspassiv is werden + Partizip II: wird gebaut, wurde gebaut, ist gebaut worden. With modals: modal + Partizip II + werden. The agent takes von + dative; man-sentences drop man entirely."},"after":{"explanation":"The Vorgangspassiv is werden + Partizip II: wird gebaut, wurde gebaut, ist gebaut worden. With modals: modal + Partizip II + werden. The agent is commonly introduced with von + dative (durch + accusative is also possible in suitable contexts); man-sentences drop man entirely."}},{"table":"grammar_rules","id":"0fad4453-fa0f-4e97-b4d8-172da04a2f77","before":{"language":"ko","cefr_level":"B2","common_errors":[{"note":"A passive verb cannot take a direct object; the agent takes 에게/한테.","error":"도둑이 경찰을 잡혔어요","correction":"도둑이 경찰에게 잡혔어요"}]},"after":{"common_errors":[{"note":"For 잡히다 meaning “be caught” here, mark the police as the agent with 에게 or 한테. This is not a rule that all Korean passive constructions prohibit an object.","error":"도둑이 경찰을 잡혔어요","correction":"도둑이 경찰에게 잡혔어요"}]}},{"table":"grammar_rules","id":"201bf57a-115f-4933-b62a-12800ca9142a","before":{"language":"it","cefr_level":"B2","explanation":"Used after verbs of opinion, emotion, doubt and impersonal expressions: penso che sia, temo che abbia perso, benché fosse. Present/past subjunctive follow a present main verb; the imperfect follows a past or conditional one: volevo che venissi.","common_errors":[{"note":"Opinion verbs + che require the subjunctive, not the indicative.","error":"Penso che Luca ha ragione.","correction":"Penso che Luca abbia ragione."}]},"after":{"explanation":"The subjunctive occurs in constructions expressing opinion, emotion or doubt, and after certain conjunctions: penso che sia, temo che abbia perso, benché fosse. The tense depends on the main verb, the construction and the time relation. Formal opinion clauses generally use the subjunctive; colloquial indicative also occurs. With desire or advisability in the present conditional, the imperfect subjunctive is usual: sarebbe meglio che venissi.","common_errors":[{"note":"Use the subjunctive in the formal opinion-clause pattern practised here.","error":"Penso che Luca ha ragione.","correction":"Penso che Luca abbia ragione."}]}},{"table":"grammar_rules","id":"26384232-4fa9-4124-9576-018540085e4d","before":{"language":"pt","cefr_level":"B2","explanation":"A uniquely Portuguese form: an infinitive with subject endings — tu -es, nós -mos, eles/vocês -em. Use it after prepositions («antes de saíres», «para acabarmos») and impersonal expressions («é melhor irmos»). Never use it after «que», which requires the conjuntivo instead.","tags":["infinitive","unique-to-portuguese","b2"]},"after":{"explanation":"An infinitive with subject endings — tu -es, nós -mos, eles/vocês -em. Use it after prepositions («antes de saíres», «para acabarmos») and impersonal expressions («é melhor irmos»). Distinguish these constructions from finite subjunctive clauses such as «É melhor que saiamos».","tags":["infinitive","b2"]}},{"table":"grammar_rules","id":"2fcf2205-9c89-4448-8b64-c15bae98dd7c","before":{"language":"ko","cefr_level":"B2","explanation":"-(으)면 states a general or open condition. -거든 marks a condition whose main clause must be a command, suggestion, or promise. -았/었더라면 marks a past counterfactual and pairs with -았/었을 거예요 or -았/었을 텐데.","common_errors":[{"note":"An unreal past result needs a counterfactual condition.","error":"돈이 많으면 작년에 샀을 거예요","correction":"돈이 많았더라면 작년에 샀을 거예요"},{"note":"-거든 must be followed by a command, suggestion, or promise.","error":"집에 도착하거든 잤어요","correction":"집에 도착하거든 주무세요"}]},"after":{"explanation":"-(으)면 states a general or open condition and can also precede requests. Conditional -거든 commonly introduces a condition for a subsequent request, suggestion or plan. -았/었더라면 presents a counterfactual past condition. For an unreal past result, it can pair with -았/었을 거예요 or -았/었을 텐데; a different context can instead have a present result.","common_errors":[{"note":"For this future-conditional use, follow 집에 도착하거든 with an appropriate subsequent instruction or plan. 잤어요 instead presents sleeping as already completed.","error":"집에 도착하거든 잤어요","correction":"집에 도착하거든 주무세요"}]}},{"table":"grammar_rules","id":"529a821c-d5f9-4a5a-b048-56aeaec72238","before":{"language":"fr","cefr_level":"B2","explanation":"After a past reporting verb, tenses backshift: présent → imparfait, passé composé → plus-que-parfait, futur → conditionnel. Yes/no questions are reported with si; pronouns, possessives and time words shift too (demain → le lendemain).","common_errors":[{"note":"The backshift is obligatory in French, unlike casual English.","error":"Elle a dit qu'elle est fatiguée.","correction":"Elle a dit qu'elle était fatiguée."},{"note":"Est-ce que disappears in reported questions; use si.","error":"Il a demandé est-ce que je viendrais.","correction":"Il a demandé si je viendrais."}]},"after":{"explanation":"When reporting from a past-time viewpoint, common backshifts are présent → imparfait, passé composé → plus-que-parfait, and futur → conditionnel. With a passé composé reporting verb, the original tense can sometimes remain when still relevant. Report yes/no questions with si. Adjust pronouns, possessives and time words only as the reporting situation requires; for example, demain can become le lendemain.","common_errors":[{"note":"Est-ce que disappears in reported questions; use si.","error":"Il a demandé est-ce que je viendrais.","correction":"Il a demandé si je viendrais."}]}},{"table":"grammar_rules","id":"58fb98aa-bf0f-4c78-ab28-dd683f502e67","before":{"language":"ja","cefr_level":"A2","explanation":"\"B is more X than A\" is AよりBのほうがX: the losing item takes より, the preferred item takes のほうが. The order of the two phrases can flip, but the particles must stay with their items.","common_errors":[{"note":"Use のほうが to mark the preferred item in a comparison.","error":"夏より冬が好きです。","correction":"夏より冬のほうが好きです。"}]},"after":{"explanation":"To compare two things, attach より to the comparison standard: 電車はバスより速いです means “The train is faster than the bus.” The pattern AよりBのほうがX explicitly contrasts B with A. のほうが is useful, but not required in every comparison: 夏より冬が好きです and 夏より冬のほうが好きです both express a preference for winter over summer.","common_errors":[]}},{"table":"grammar_rules","id":"590c8ec1-0551-4b50-997f-a1763a6c89d5","before":{"language":"ru","cefr_level":"B2","explanation":"Prefixes give motion verbs precise meanings: при- arrival (пришёл), у- departure (ушёл), вы- out of (вышел из), в- into, за- a short stop on the way (зашёл в аптеку), до- reaching a point (доехал до центра), пере- across or relocation (переехал). Each prefix pairs with its own preposition: при- with в/на, вы- with из, до- with до.","common_errors":[{"native":"movement out of a room takes вы-, not при-","target":"студенты пришли из класса → студенты вышли из класса"}]},"after":{"explanation":"Prefixes distinguish motion meanings: при- arrival (пришёл), у- departure (ушёл), вы- movement out (вышел из), в- movement into, за- a stop on the way (зашёл в аптеку), до- reaching an endpoint (доехал до центра), пере- crossing or relocation (переехал). Common place phrases include «пришёл в школу», «вышел из класса» and «доехал до центра», but there is no one-preposition-per-prefix rule: arrival can name a person or a source, as in «пришёл к другу из школы».","common_errors":[]}},{"table":"grammar_rules","id":"5e04f672-e66b-4d3c-ac95-95eae46e37f5","before":{"language":"zh","cefr_level":"B2","explanation":"A result follows the verb: 听懂, 找到, 写错. Insert 得/不 between them for possibility: 听得懂 = can understand, 听不懂 = cannot. Use this potential form, not 能/不能, for ability tied to a result.","common_errors":[{"note":"Use the potential form V不C, not 不能 + VC.","error":"我不能听懂。","correction":"我听不懂。"},{"note":"The potential form does not take 了.","error":"我找不到了我的手机。","correction":"我找不到我的手机。"}]},"after":{"explanation":"A result follows the verb: 听懂, 找到, 写错. Inserting 得/不 forms a potential complement: 听得懂, 听不懂. This pattern expresses whether a result can be achieved; modal 能/不能 can also combine with resultative predicates in appropriate contexts.","common_errors":[{"note":"For the negative potential pattern, insert 不 directly between the verb and result.","error":"我听不得懂。","correction":"我听不懂。"},{"note":"Do not place 了 between 找不到 and its object. Sentence-final changed-state 了 is a different use and can occur after the object.","error":"我找不到了我的手机。","correction":"我找不到我的手机。"}]}},{"table":"grammar_rules","id":"6bf12c54-f0de-43a4-9c95-0d7dbc793b6c","before":{"language":"ja","cefr_level":"B2","common_errors":[{"note":"申す is humble — never use it for a superior's speech.","error":"先生が申しました。","correction":"先生がおっしゃいました。"}]},"after":{"common_errors":[{"note":"When the teacher is the person being honored in this context, use おっしゃる. Humble 申す is not limited to first-person speech; an in-group representative can use it when addressing outsiders.","error":"先生が申しました。","correction":"先生がおっしゃいました。"}]}},{"table":"grammar_rules","id":"6dd54293-139a-46ed-9129-65b6e417b37b","before":{"language":"it","cefr_level":"B2","explanation":"After a past reporting verb, tenses backshift: present → imperfect (sono → era), passato prossimo → trapassato (ho perso → aveva perso), future → past conditional (verrò → sarebbe venuto). Time and place words shift too: domani → il giorno dopo, qui → lì."},"after":{"explanation":"When reporting from a past viewpoint, common backshifts are present to imperfect, passato prossimo to trapassato and future to past conditional. Time and place expressions change when the reporting viewpoint changes: domani may become il giorno dopo and qui may become lì. Their choice depends on the actual time and place of the report, not the reporting verb alone."}},{"table":"grammar_rules","id":"777b8c1a-e871-4e5f-bfac-ef88006b4d6f","before":{"language":"ja","cefr_level":"A1","explanation":"が marks the grammatical subject — especially new information, things that exist, and answers to question words. Question words themselves (誰, 何, どこ) always take が, never は.","common_errors":[{"note":"Question words take が, never は.","error":"誰は来ましたか。","correction":"誰が来ましたか。"}]},"after":{"explanation":"が marks the grammatical subject, often introducing new information or identifying who or what performs an action. In an ordinary question asking for the subject, use が with the question word: 誰が来ましたか asks “Who came?” This is not a rule that every question word must take が. Other roles use the appropriate particle, as in 何を食べますか (“What will you eat?”) or どこに行きますか (“Where will you go?”).","common_errors":[{"note":"For the ordinary subject-identification question “Who came?”, use 誰が, not 誰は. Question words in other grammatical roles do not automatically take が.","error":"誰は来ましたか。","correction":"誰が来ましたか。"}]}},{"table":"grammar_rules","id":"9e9e14c0-59b0-4e3d-bd16-5b222947cba6","before":{"language":"fr","cefr_level":"B1","explanation":"The futur simple attaches -ai, -as, -a, -ons, -ez, -ont to the infinitive (parlerai) or an irregular stem (ser-, aur-, ir-, fer-, viendr-). Use it for predictions and promises. After quand referring to the future, French also uses the future: quand tu arriveras.","common_errors":[{"note":"Unlike English, French uses the future after quand for future events.","error":"Quand tu arrives demain, on mangera.","correction":"Quand tu arriveras demain, on mangera."},{"note":"Aller has the irregular future stem ir-.","error":"je serai aller","correction":"j'irai"}]},"after":{"explanation":"The futur simple uses endings -ai, -as, -a, -ons, -ez, -ont with the future stem (parler-, ser-, aur-, ir-, fer-, viendr-). It expresses predictions and promises. French can use the future after quand for a future event: quand tu arriveras. The present can also refer to a scheduled or confidently envisaged future event, so it is not universally wrong in that context.","common_errors":[{"note":"Aller has the irregular future stem ir-.","error":"je serai aller","correction":"j'irai"}]}},{"table":"grammar_rules","id":"9eb20e28-279b-4cae-97c3-26a7f7f8478d","before":{"language":"ja","cefr_level":"B1","explanation":"Godan: -a + せる (書く→書かせる); ichidan: させる (食べる→食べさせる). It means \"make\" or \"let\" someone act. The causee takes に with transitive verbs and を with intransitive ones."},"after":{"explanation":"Godan verbs use the -a stem plus せる (書く→書かせる); ichidan verbs add させる to the stem (食べる→食べさせる). Causatives can mean make or let someone act. With an expressed transitive object marked を, the causee normally takes に. Intransitive causees commonly take を, but に is also possible depending on the verb and context."}},{"table":"grammar_rules","id":"a1d73f33-289d-4dd9-9c75-a2ba5cf08c71","before":{"language":"pt","cefr_level":"B2","explanation":"After a past reporting verb, tenses shift back: presente → imperfeito («falo» → «falava»), pretérito perfeito → mais-que-perfeito («comprei» → «tinha comprado»), futuro → condicional («ajudarei» → «ajudaria»). Time and place words shift too: «hoje» → «naquele dia», «amanhã» → «no dia seguinte».","common_errors":[{"note":"Shift both the tense and the time expression when reporting past speech.","right":"Ela disse que ia no dia seguinte.","wrong":"Ela disse que vai amanhã."}]},"after":{"explanation":"When a report adopts a past viewpoint, common backshifts include presente → imperfeito («falo» → «falava»), pretérito perfeito → mais-que-perfeito («comprei» → «tinha comprado»), and futuro → condicional («ajudarei» → «ajudaria»). Choose tense and reference expressions according to the reporting context. For a later report, «hoje» may become «naquele dia» and «amanhã» may become «no dia seguinte»; a still-current report can keep a present tense or the original time expression.","common_errors":[]}},{"table":"grammar_rules","id":"ae55c745-21b1-405e-b1d2-7a490518f814","before":{"language":"zh","cefr_level":"B2","explanation":"A 比 B + adj (+ 得多/多了/一点儿): 他比我大三岁 — the measure follows the adjective. Negatives: A 没有 B (那么) adj, or A 不如 B (+adj). 越来越 + adj = more and more. Never use 很 before the adjective.","common_errors":[{"note":"No 很 in 比-sentences; use 多了/得多 after the adjective.","error":"今天比昨天很冷。","correction":"今天比昨天冷多了。"},{"note":"Use either an exact measure or 多了, not both.","error":"他比我大三岁多了。","correction":"他比我大三岁。"}]},"after":{"explanation":"A 比 B + adjective compares two things. Put a measure or degree of difference after the adjective: 大三岁, 高得多, 高多了, 高很多. Negatives include A 没有 B (那么) adjective and A 不如 B. 越来越 + adjective expresses an increasing degree. Avoid bare 很 before the adjective in the basic 比 pattern.","common_errors":[{"note":"Put the degree of difference after 冷: 冷多了, 冷得多 or 冷很多.","error":"今天比昨天很冷。","correction":"今天比昨天冷多了。"},{"note":"Use either an exact measure or 多了, not both.","error":"他比我大三岁多了。","correction":"他比我大三岁。"}]}},{"table":"grammar_rules","id":"c49d0078-a69a-4d58-a8c8-31d119e0915c","before":{"language":"ru","cefr_level":"B2","explanation":"Unreal situations use бы + past in BOTH clauses: Если бы я знал, я бы сказал. Real conditions take если + future, without бы. The same бы hides inside чтобы, so чтобы is always followed by the past: Я хочу, чтобы ты пришёл. Polite wishes: хотел бы + infinitive."},"after":{"explanation":"Finite unreal conditionals commonly use a past-form verb with бы in both clauses: «Если бы я знал, я бы сказал». Real future possibilities can use «если» with future forms, without бы. A wish about another person uses a finite чтобы clause with a past-form verb: «Я хочу, чтобы ты пришёл». Чтобы can also introduce an infinitive, as in «чтобы учиться». Polite wishes include «хотел бы» plus an infinitive; бы also occurs in other constructions such as «мне бы отдохнуть»."}},{"table":"grammar_rules","id":"c742ef90-fb40-42e9-845b-bc866665638f","before":{"language":"zh","cefr_level":"B2","common_errors":[{"note":"让/叫 require the agent to be stated.","error":"蛋糕叫吃完了。","correction":"蛋糕叫弟弟吃完了。"},{"note":"The receiver starts the sentence.","error":"被小偷偷走了我的钱包。","correction":"我的钱包被小偷偷走了。"}]},"after":{"common_errors":[{"note":"让/叫 require the agent to be stated.","error":"蛋糕叫吃完了。","correction":"蛋糕叫弟弟吃完了。"},{"note":"In this neutral passive, put the affected subject 我的钱包 before 被.","error":"被小偷偷走了我的钱包。","correction":"我的钱包被小偷偷走了。"}]}},{"table":"grammar_rules","id":"dea133cc-4764-4728-8353-240a18841f8c","before":{"language":"ru","cefr_level":"B2","explanation":"Use the imperfective past for process, duration, and repetition — especially with phrases like весь день, каждый день, всегда, долго: Я весь вечер читал. Use the perfective past for a single completed action with a result, often signalled by наконец, уже, сразу: Я наконец прочитал книгу.","common_errors":[{"native":"a duration phrase cannot combine with a perfective verb","target":"Я весь день прочитал статьи → Я весь день читал статьи"}]},"after":{"explanation":"Use the imperfective past to present an activity, duration or repetition: «Я весь вечер читал книгу». Use perfective «прочитал» to foreground the achieved completion: «Я наконец прочитал книгу». Context matters: imperfective can also state a general fact of a completed action, and perfective verbs can express bounded duration, as in «проспал весь день».","common_errors":[{"native":"To describe reading as an activity throughout the day, use читал; for completing the reading within a day, use прочитал за день.","target":"Я весь день прочитал статьи → Я весь день читал статьи"}]}},{"table":"grammar_rules","id":"ef310328-8f4c-4899-93ce-bd43840bb33c","before":{"language":"zh","cefr_level":"B1","explanation":"Verb + 着 (zhe) marks a continuing state or background action: 门开着 = the door is open; 他笑着说 = he said, smiling. It describes states, not events."},"after":{"explanation":"Verb + 着 marks a continuing state or background action: 门开着 describes an open door; 他笑着说 describes speaking while smiling. With activity verbs, 着 can also participate in a progressive description."}},{"table":"grammar_rules","id":"f89d2427-b249-44d2-b0e5-ce9322b014d5","before":{"language":"it","cefr_level":"B2","explanation":"Real: se piove, resto (indicative). Unreal present: se + imperfect subjunctive + conditional — se fossi ricco, viaggerei. Unreal past: se + trapassato subjunctive + past conditional — se avessi studiato, avrei superato l'esame. Never use the conditional after se.","common_errors":[{"note":"The conditional never follows se; use the imperfect subjunctive.","error":"Se sarei ricco, viaggerei.","correction":"Se fossi ricco, viaggerei."}]},"after":{"explanation":"Real condition: se piove, resto. Unreal present: se + imperfect subjunctive with a conditional result, se fossi ricco, viaggerei. Unreal past: se + trapassato subjunctive with a past conditional result, se avessi studiato, avrei superato l’esame. These patterns concern conditional se meaning if, not se meaning whether in indirect questions.","common_errors":[{"note":"In this unreal present condition, use the imperfect subjunctive in the se-clause.","error":"Se sarei ricco, viaggerei.","correction":"Se fossi ricco, viaggerei."}]}},{"table":"lessons","id":"aabbccdd-5555-4006-0002-b20000000000","before":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-5555-4006-0000-b20000000000","description":"Talk about future conditions with se, quando and assim que — a tense unique to Portuguese"},"after":{"description":"Talk about future conditions with se, quando and assim que using the future subjunctive."}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-1111-3001-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-1111-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-1111-3001-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","content":"El cambio climatico es uno de los problemas mas importantes de nuestro tiempo. Las temperaturas globales estan subiendo, los glaciares se derriten y el nivel del mar aumenta. Los cientificos dicen que debemos reducir las emisiones de carbono para proteger nuestro planeta. Muchos paises estan adoptando energias renovables como la solar y la eolica. Cada persona puede contribuir reciclando, usando transporte publico y ahorrando energia en casa.","title":"El cambio climatico","word_count":150},"after":{"content":"El cambio climático es uno de los problemas más importantes de nuestro tiempo. Las temperaturas globales están subiendo, los glaciares se derriten y el nivel del mar aumenta. Los científicos dicen que debemos reducir las emisiones de carbono para proteger nuestro planeta. Muchos países están adoptando energías renovables como la solar y la eólica. Cada persona puede contribuir reciclando, usando transporte público y ahorrando energía en casa.","title":"El cambio climático","word_count":67}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-1111-3002-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-1111-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-1111-3002-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","content":"Maria tiene una entrevista de trabajo manana. Ella ha preparado su curriculum y ha investigado sobre la empresa. Se siente nerviosa pero emocionada. Su amiga le aconseja que llegue temprano, vista de manera profesional y sea honesta con sus respuestas. Maria practica respondiendo preguntas comunes como: Cuales son sus fortalezas? y Por que quiere trabajar aqui? Ella espera conseguir el puesto.","word_count":120},"after":{"content":"María tiene una entrevista de trabajo mañana. Ella ha preparado su currículum y ha investigado sobre la empresa. Se siente nerviosa pero emocionada. Su amiga le aconseja que llegue temprano, vista de manera profesional y sea honesta con sus respuestas. María practica respondiendo preguntas comunes como: ¿Cuáles son sus fortalezas? y ¿Por qué quiere trabajar aquí? Ella espera conseguir el puesto.","word_count":61}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-1111-3003-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-1111-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-1111-3003-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","content":"El verano pasado, mi familia y yo viajamos a Barcelona. Reservamos un hotel cerca de la playa y visitamos la Sagrada Familia, el Parque Guell y Las Ramblas. La comida fue increible, especialmente la paella y las tapas. Tambien aprendimos algunas palabras en catalan. El viaje duro una semana y fue una experiencia inolvidable. Espero volver el proximo ano.","word_count":100},"after":{"content":"El verano pasado, mi familia y yo viajamos a Barcelona. Reservamos un hotel cerca de la playa y visitamos la Sagrada Familia, el Parque Güell y Las Ramblas. La comida fue increíble, especialmente la paella y las tapas. También aprendimos algunas palabras en catalán. El viaje duró una semana y fue una experiencia inolvidable. Espero volver el próximo año.","word_count":59}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-1111-3004-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-1111-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-1111-3004-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","content":"Hoy en dia, la tecnologia juega un papel importante en la educacion. Los estudiantes usan tablets y computadoras en clase. Las aplicaciones de aprendizaje hacen que estudiar sea mas interactivo y divertido. Sin embargo, algunos expertos se preocupan por el tiempo excesivo frente a las pantallas. Es importante encontrar un equilibrio entre la tecnologia y los metodos tradicionales de ensenanza.","title":"La tecnologia en la educacion","word_count":110},"after":{"content":"Hoy en día, la tecnología juega un papel importante en la educación. Los estudiantes usan tablets y computadoras en clase. Las aplicaciones de aprendizaje hacen que estudiar sea más interactivo y divertido. Sin embargo, algunos expertos se preocupan por el tiempo excesivo frente a las pantallas. Es importante encontrar un equilibrio entre la tecnología y los métodos tradicionales de enseñanza.","title":"La tecnología en la educación","unit_id":"aabbccdd-1111-3005-0000-b10000000000","word_count":60}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-1111-3005-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-1111-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-1111-3005-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","content":"La contaminacion es un problema serio en muchas ciudades. El aire sucio causa problemas de salud, especialmente para los ninos y las personas mayores. Para combatir la contaminacion, algunas ciudades han implementado zonas sin coches y promueven el uso de bicicletas. Tambien es importante plantar mas arboles y reducir el uso de plastico. Todos debemos hacer nuestra parte para proteger el medio ambiente.","word_count":110},"after":{"content":"La contaminación es un problema serio en muchas ciudades. El aire sucio causa problemas de salud, especialmente para los niños y las personas mayores. Para combatir la contaminación, algunas ciudades han implementado zonas sin coches y promueven el uso de bicicletas. También es importante plantar más árboles y reducir el uso de plástico. Todos debemos hacer nuestra parte para proteger el medio ambiente.","unit_id":"aabbccdd-1111-3004-0000-b10000000000","word_count":63}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-1111-3006-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-1111-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-1111-3006-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","content":"Las redes sociales han cambiado la forma en que nos comunicamos. Podemos conectar con personas de todo el mundo, compartir fotos y noticias al instante. Sin embargo, tambien hay desventajas como la desinformacion, el ciberacoso y la adiccion. Es importante usar las redes sociales de manera responsable y verificar la informacion antes de compartirla.","word_count":100},"after":{"content":"Las redes sociales han cambiado la forma en que nos comunicamos. Podemos conectar con personas de todo el mundo, compartir fotos y noticias al instante. Sin embargo, también hay desventajas como la desinformación, el ciberacoso y la adicción. Es importante usar las redes sociales de manera responsable y verificar la información antes de compartirla.","unit_id":"aabbccdd-1111-3005-0000-b10000000000","word_count":54}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-1111-3007-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-1111-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-1111-3007-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","content":"La comida es una parte importante de la cultura. Cada pais tiene sus platos tipicos. En Espana, la paella es famosa. En Italia, la pasta y la pizza. En Japon, el sushi y el ramen. Probar comida de otros paises es una manera deliciosa de aprender sobre diferentes culturas. Hoy en dia, es facil encontrar restaurantes internacionales en casi cualquier ciudad.","word_count":100},"after":{"content":"La comida es una parte importante de la cultura. Cada país tiene sus platos típicos. En España, la paella es famosa. En Italia, la pasta y la pizza. En Japón, el sushi y el ramen. Probar comida de otros países es una manera deliciosa de aprender sobre diferentes culturas. Hoy en día, es fácil encontrar restaurantes internacionales en casi cualquier ciudad.","unit_id":"aabbccdd-1111-3003-0000-b10000000000","word_count":61}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-1111-3008-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-1111-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-1111-3008-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","content":"Hacer ejercicio regularmente es esencial para mantener una buena salud. Los expertos recomiendan al menos treinta minutos de actividad fisica al dia. Caminar, nadar, correr o andar en bicicleta son opciones excelentes. El ejercicio no solo mejora la salud fisica, sino tambien la salud mental. Reduce el estres, mejora el sueno y aumenta la energia.","word_count":100},"after":{"content":"Hacer ejercicio regularmente es esencial para mantener una buena salud. Los expertos recomiendan al menos treinta minutos de actividad física al día. Caminar, nadar, correr o andar en bicicleta son opciones excelentes. El ejercicio no solo mejora la salud física, sino también la salud mental. Reduce el estrés, mejora el sueño y aumenta la energía.","word_count":55}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-1111-4001-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-1111-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4001-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","content":"La inteligencia artificial esta transformando rapidamente el mercado laboral. Muchos trabajos rutinarios estan siendo automatizados, lo que genera preocupacion sobre el desempleo tecnologico. Sin embargo, tambien se estan creando nuevas profesiones que requieren habilidades en programacion, analisis de datos y gestion de sistemas de IA. Los expertos sugieren que la educacion debe adaptarse para preparar a las futuras generaciones. La clave sera la capacidad de trabajar junto a las maquinas, combinando la creatividad humana con la eficiencia de la tecnologia. Las empresas que adopten esta perspectiva hibrida tendran una ventaja competitiva significativa.","word_count":200},"after":{"content":"La inteligencia artificial está transformando rápidamente el mercado laboral. Muchos trabajos rutinarios están siendo automatizados, lo que genera preocupación sobre el desempleo tecnológico. Sin embargo, también se están creando nuevas profesiones que requieren habilidades en programación, análisis de datos y gestión de sistemas de IA. Los expertos sugieren que la educación debe adaptarse para preparar a las futuras generaciones. La clave será la capacidad de trabajar junto a las máquinas, combinando la creatividad humana con la eficiencia de la tecnología. Las empresas que adopten esta perspectiva híbrida tendrán una ventaja competitiva significativa.","word_count":92}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-1111-4002-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-1111-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4002-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","content":"A lo largo de la historia, el arte ha sido una herramienta poderosa de protesta social. Desde los murales de Diego Rivera en Mexico hasta el arte callejero de Banksy en el Reino Unido, los artistas han utilizado su creatividad para denunciar injusticias. La literatura, la musica y el cine tambien han servido como vehiculos de cambio social. En la era digital, las redes sociales han amplificado el alcance del arte protestante, permitiendo que mensajes lleguen a audiencias globales en cuestion de segundos.","word_count":180},"after":{"content":"A lo largo de la historia, el arte ha sido una herramienta poderosa de protesta social. Desde los murales de Diego Rivera en México hasta el arte callejero de Banksy en el Reino Unido, los artistas han utilizado su creatividad para denunciar injusticias. La literatura, la música y el cine también han servido como vehículos de cambio social. En la era digital, las redes sociales han amplificado el alcance del arte protestante, permitiendo que mensajes lleguen a audiencias globales en cuestión de segundos.","word_count":83}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-1111-4003-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-1111-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4003-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","content":"La globalizacion ha conectado al mundo de maneras sin precedentes. Podemos comunicarnos instantaneamente con personas en cualquier continente y acceder a productos de todo el mundo. Sin embargo, esta interconexion ha generado un debate sobre la preservacion de las identidades culturales locales. Algunos argumentan que la globalizacion homogeniza las culturas, mientras que otros creen que facilita un intercambio enriquecedor. La realidad probablemente se encuentra en un punto intermedio: las culturas se influyen mutuamente sin perder necesariamente su esencia unica.","title":"La globalizacion y la identidad cultural","word_count":200},"after":{"content":"La globalización ha conectado al mundo de maneras sin precedentes. Podemos comunicarnos instantáneamente con personas en cualquier continente y acceder a productos de todo el mundo. Sin embargo, esta interconexión ha generado un debate sobre la preservación de las identidades culturales locales. Algunos argumentan que la globalización homogeniza las culturas, mientras que otros creen que facilita un intercambio enriquecedor. La realidad probablemente se encuentra en un punto intermedio: las culturas se influyen mutuamente sin perder necesariamente su esencia única.","title":"La globalización y la identidad cultural","unit_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4002-0000-b20000000000","word_count":79}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-1111-4004-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-1111-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4004-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","content":"El desarrollo de la inteligencia artificial plantea cuestiones eticas fundamentales. Quien es responsable cuando un coche autonomo causa un accidente? Como garantizamos que los algoritmos no perpetuen sesgos raciales o de genero? Estas preguntas no tienen respuestas sencillas, pero es crucial que la sociedad las aborde antes de que la tecnologia avance mas alla de nuestra capacidad de regularla. Necesitamos marcos eticos solidos que equilibren la innovacion con la proteccion de los derechos humanos.","title":"Etica de la inteligencia artificial","word_count":180},"after":{"content":"El desarrollo de la inteligencia artificial plantea cuestiones éticas fundamentales. ¿Quién es responsable cuando un coche autónomo causa un accidente? ¿Cómo garantizamos que los algoritmos no perpetúen sesgos raciales o de género? Estas preguntas no tienen respuestas sencillas, pero es crucial que la sociedad las aborde antes de que la tecnología avance más allá de nuestra capacidad de regularla. Necesitamos marcos éticos sólidos que equilibren la innovación con la protección de los derechos humanos.","title":"Ética de la inteligencia artificial","unit_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4001-0000-b20000000000","word_count":74}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-1111-4005-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-1111-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4005-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","content":"Las historias son fundamentales para la experiencia humana. Desde las pinturas rupestres hasta las series de streaming, los seres humanos siempre han necesitado contar y escuchar historias. Las narrativas nos ayudan a dar sentido al mundo, a desarrollar empatia y a transmitir valores entre generaciones. En el ambito empresarial, el storytelling se ha convertido en una herramienta esencial para conectar con los consumidores a un nivel emocional.","word_count":170},"after":{"content":"Las historias son fundamentales para la experiencia humana. Desde las pinturas rupestres hasta las series de streaming, los seres humanos siempre han necesitado contar y escuchar historias. Las narrativas nos ayudan a dar sentido al mundo, a desarrollar empatía y a transmitir valores entre generaciones. En el ámbito empresarial, el storytelling se ha convertido en una herramienta esencial para conectar con los consumidores a un nivel emocional.","word_count":67}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-1111-4006-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-1111-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-1111-4006-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","content":"Aprender un segundo idioma tiene beneficios cognitivos significativos. Las investigaciones muestran que las personas bilingues tienen mejor memoria, mayor capacidad de concentracion y son mas hábiles en la resolucion de problemas. Ademas, el bilingualismo puede retrasar la aparicion de enfermedades neurodegenerativas como el Alzheimer. El cerebro bilingue esta constantemente ejercitandose al alternar entre dos sistemas linguisticos, lo que fortalece las conexiones neuronales.","word_count":160},"after":{"content":"Aprender un segundo idioma tiene beneficios cognitivos significativos. Las investigaciones muestran que las personas bilingües tienen mejor memoria, mayor capacidad de concentración y son más hábiles en la resolución de problemas. Además, el bilingüismo puede retrasar la aparición de enfermedades neurodegenerativas como el Alzheimer. El cerebro bilingüe está constantemente ejercitándose al alternar entre dos sistemas lingüísticos, lo que fortalece las conexiones neuronales.","word_count":62}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-2222-3004-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-2222-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-2222-3004-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1"},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-2222-3005-0000-b10000000000"}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-2222-3005-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-2222-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-2222-3005-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1"},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-2222-3004-0000-b10000000000"}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-2222-3006-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-2222-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-2222-3006-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1"},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-2222-3005-0000-b10000000000"}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-2222-3007-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-2222-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-2222-3007-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1"},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-2222-3003-0000-b10000000000"}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4003-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-2222-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4003-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","content":"La mondialisation pose des défis importants à l'identité française. D'un côté, elle offre des opportunités : les entreprises françaises exportent leurs produits dans le monde entier, et les jeunes Français travaillent à l'international. De l'autre côté, beaucoup craignent la perte de nos traditions. La gastronomie française, par exemple, doit rivaliser avec la cuisine internationale et les fast-foods. La langue française elle-même est menacée par l'usage croissant de l'anglais dans les affaires et la technologie.\n\nCependant, les Français restent attachés à leur patrimoine. L'UNESCO protège nos sites historiques comme Versailles et Mont-Saint-Michel. Le gouvernement soutient les producteurs locaux et les petits commerces. Les festivals culturels, de Cannes à Avignon, attirent des visiteurs du monde entier et rayonnent la culture française. La mondialisation n'efface pas notre identité ; elle la transforme.","word_count":129},"after":{"content":"La mondialisation pose des défis importants à l'identité française. D'un côté, elle offre des opportunités : les entreprises françaises exportent leurs produits dans le monde entier, et les jeunes Français travaillent à l'international. De l'autre côté, beaucoup craignent la perte de nos traditions. La gastronomie française, par exemple, doit rivaliser avec la cuisine internationale et les fast-foods. La langue française elle-même est menacée par l'usage croissant de l'anglais dans les affaires et la technologie.\n\nCependant, les Français restent attachés à leur patrimoine. L'UNESCO protège nos sites historiques comme Versailles et Mont-Saint-Michel. Le gouvernement soutient les producteurs locaux et les petits commerces. Les festivals culturels, de Cannes à Avignon, attirent des visiteurs du monde entier et font rayonner la culture française. La mondialisation n'efface pas notre identité ; elle la transforme.","word_count":130}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-2222-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4004-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2"},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4001-0000-b20000000000"}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4005-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-2222-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4005-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","content":"Les histoires façonnent notre compréhension du monde depuis la nuit des temps. Qu'il s'agisse d'un film de Luc Besson, d'un roman de Joël Dicker ou d'un reportage sur France Télévisions, les récits nous permettent de donner du sens à nos expériences. En France, les contes de fées de Charles Perrault ont marqué des générations d'enfants, tandis que les films de Claude Régy continuent à inspirer les cinéastes modernes.\n\nAujourd'hui, à l'ère des réseaux sociaux, les récits prennent de nouvelles formes. Les podcasts français comme « Les Pieds sur Terre » captent l'attention de millions d'auditeurs chaque semaine. Les influenceurs racontent leurs histoires personnelles, créant une connexion authentique avec leur public. Ces narrateurs numériques deviennent des figures centrales de notre culture.\n\nMais pourquoi les histoires sont-elles si puissantes ? Simplement parce qu'elles nous permettent de nous identifier à autrui, de vivre d'autres vies, et finalement, de mieux nous comprendre nous-mêmes.","word_count":149},"after":{"content":"Les histoires façonnent notre compréhension du monde depuis la nuit des temps. Qu'il s'agisse d'un film de Luc Besson, d'un roman de Joël Dicker ou d'un reportage sur France Télévisions, les récits nous permettent de donner du sens à nos expériences. En France, les contes de fées de Charles Perrault ont marqué des générations d'enfants, tandis que les mises en scène de Claude Régy continuent à inspirer le théâtre contemporain.\n\nAujourd'hui, à l'ère des réseaux sociaux, les récits prennent de nouvelles formes. Les podcasts français comme « Les Pieds sur Terre » captent l'attention de millions d'auditeurs chaque semaine. Les influenceurs racontent leurs histoires personnelles, créant une connexion authentique avec leur public. Ces narrateurs numériques deviennent des figures centrales de notre culture.\n\nMais pourquoi les histoires sont-elles si puissantes ? Simplement parce qu'elles nous permettent de nous identifier à autrui, de vivre d'autres vies, et finalement, de mieux nous comprendre nous-mêmes.","word_count":151}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-2222-4006-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-2222-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-2222-4006-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","content":"Des neuroscientifiques ont découvert que l'apprentissage d'une langue transforme physiquement notre cerveau. Lorsqu'on apprend le mandarin ou l'allemand, certaines régions du cerveau s'agrandissent et se renforcent, particulièrement l'hippocampe, crucial pour la mémoire.\n\nLes chercheurs de l'Université de Genève ont observé que les bilingues possèdent une matière grise plus dense que les monolingues. Cette différence augmente avec la durée d'apprentissage et le niveau de maîtrise. Étonnamment, même les adultes qui apprennent une langue tardive connaissent ces modifications cérébrales.\n\nCes changements offrent des avantages remarquables : les bilingues développent une meilleure flexibilité cognitive et des capacités de concentration supérieures. Ils résistent mieux au déclin cognitif en vieillissant. L'apprentissage linguistique crée littéralement un cerveau plus puissant et plus résilient."},"after":{"content":"Des neuroscientifiques ont découvert que l'apprentissage d'une langue transforme physiquement notre cerveau. Lorsqu'on apprend le mandarin ou l'allemand, certaines régions du cerveau s'agrandissent et se renforcent, particulièrement l'hippocampe, crucial pour la mémoire.\n\nLes chercheurs de l'Université de Genève ont observé que les bilingues possèdent une matière grise plus dense que les monolingues. Cette différence augmente avec la durée d'apprentissage et le niveau de maîtrise. Étonnamment, même les adultes qui apprennent une langue tardivement connaissent ces modifications cérébrales.\n\nCes changements offrent des avantages remarquables : les bilingues développent une meilleure flexibilité cognitive et des capacités de concentration supérieures. Ils résistent mieux au déclin cognitif en vieillissant. L'apprentissage linguistique crée littéralement un cerveau plus puissant et plus résilient."}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3004-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-3333-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3004-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1"},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3005-0000-b10000000000"}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3005-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-3333-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3005-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","content":"Deutschland hat sich zum Ziel gesetzt, bis 2045 klimaneutral zu sein. Das bedeutet, dass das Land nicht mehr CO₂ in die Atmosphäre ausstoßen darf. Um das zu erreichen, investiert die Regierung viel Geld in erneuerbare Energien wie Windkraftanlagen und Solaranlagen. Auch die Bürger können helfen: Sie können mit dem Fahrrad fahren, weniger Fleisch essen und Energie sparen. In vielen deutschen Städten gibt es bereits Umweltzonen, in denen alte Autos nicht fahren dürfen. Die Unternehmen müssen auch nachhaltiger werden. Zusammen können wir unseren Planeten schützen.","word_count":84},"after":{"content":"Deutschland hat sich zum Ziel gesetzt, bis 2045 klimaneutral zu sein. Das bedeutet, dass nicht mehr Treibhausgase ausgestoßen werden, als wieder aus der Atmosphäre entfernt werden. Um das zu erreichen, investiert die Regierung viel Geld in erneuerbare Energien wie Windkraftanlagen und Solaranlagen. Auch die Bürger können helfen: Sie können mit dem Fahrrad fahren, weniger Fleisch essen und Energie sparen. In einigen deutschen Städten gibt es Umweltzonen mit besonderen Abgasvorschriften für Fahrzeuge. Die Unternehmen müssen auch nachhaltiger werden. Zusammen können wir unseren Planeten schützen.","unit_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3004-0000-b10000000000","word_count":83}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-3333-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3006-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1"},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3005-0000-b10000000000"}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-3333-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3007-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1"},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3003-0000-b10000000000"}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-3333-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-3333-3008-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","content":"Sport ist wichtig für unsere Gesundheit. Wenn wir regelmäßig trainieren, werden wir stärker und fitter. Viele Deutsche gehen gerne joggen oder fahren Fahrrad. Das ist gut für das Herz und die Lungen. Auch Fußball spielen oder Schwimmen sind populäre Aktivitäten. Experten empfehlen mindestens 150 Minuten moderate Bewegung pro Woche. Sport hilft auch gegen Stress und macht bessere Laune. Ein gesundes Leben mit Sport und guter Ernährung ist der beste Weg zu mehr Energie und Wohlbefinden.","word_count":75},"after":{"content":"Sport ist wichtig für unsere Gesundheit. Wenn wir regelmäßig trainieren, werden wir stärker und fitter. Viele Deutsche gehen gerne joggen oder fahren Fahrrad. Das ist gut für das Herz und die Lungen. Auch Fußball spielen oder Schwimmen sind populäre Aktivitäten. Experten empfehlen mindestens 150 Minuten moderate Bewegung pro Woche. Sport hilft auch gegen Stress und macht bessere Laune. Ein gesundes Leben mit Sport und guter Ernährung ist der beste Weg zu mehr Energie und Wohlbefinden. Wenn Sie mit dem Sport beginnen möchten, sprechen Sie bitte zuerst mit Ihrem Arzt oder Ihrer Ärztin.","word_count":92}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-3333-4004-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-3333-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4004-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2"},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-3333-4001-0000-b20000000000"}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3003-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-4444-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3003-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","content":"Marco ha deciso di visitare Barcellona per la prima volta. Ha prenotato un volo da Milano e un hotel nel quartiere di Gràcia. Durante la sua settimana catalana, ha ammirato la Sagrada Familia, l'opera più famosa di Gaudí, e ha passeggiato lungo le Ramblas, la strada principale della città. Ha assaggiato le tapas in un bar tradizionale e ha visitato il Parco Güell con le sue splendide viste sulla città. Nel weekend, ha preso il treno per visitare la spiaggia di Montserrat. Marco è tornato a casa con molte foto e il desiderio di tornare presto a Barcellona."},"after":{"content":"Marco ha deciso di visitare Barcellona per la prima volta. Ha prenotato un volo da Milano e un hotel nel quartiere di Gràcia. Durante la sua settimana catalana, ha ammirato la Sagrada Familia, l'opera più famosa di Gaudí, e ha passeggiato lungo le Ramblas, la strada principale della città. Ha assaggiato le tapas in un bar tradizionale e ha visitato il Parco Güell con le sue splendide viste sulla città. Nel weekend, ha preso il treno per visitare il monastero di Montserrat. Marco è tornato a casa con molte foto e il desiderio di tornare presto a Barcellona."}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3004-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-4444-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3004-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1"},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3005-0000-b10000000000"}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3005-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-4444-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3005-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","content":"L'Italia affronta una grave crisi ambientale. Le temperature aumentano ogni anno, causando siccità nel Sud e alluvioni nel Nord. Nel 2023, la Sicilia ha raggiunto 48 gradi Celsius, record negativo europeo. I ghiacciai delle Alpi si stanno sciogliendo rapidamente, minacciando le riserve d'acqua. Le città italiane come Milano e Roma devono ridurre l'inquinamento atmosferico. Molti cittadini cambiano abitudini: usano biciclette, mangiano meno carne e supportano l'energia rinnovabile. Il governo italiano investe in pannelli solari e turbine eoliche. Proteggere l'ambiente è responsabilità di tutti, dal Trentino alla Sardegna.","word_count":87},"after":{"content":"L'Italia affronta una grave crisi ambientale. Le temperature aumentano ogni anno, causando siccità nel Sud e alluvioni nel Nord. L’11 agosto 2021, in Sicilia è stata misurata una temperatura di 48,8 gradi Celsius, il record europeo confermato dall’Organizzazione meteorologica mondiale. I ghiacciai delle Alpi si stanno sciogliendo rapidamente, minacciando le riserve d'acqua. Le città italiane come Milano e Roma devono ridurre l'inquinamento atmosferico. Molti cittadini cambiano abitudini: usano biciclette, mangiano meno carne e supportano l'energia rinnovabile. Il governo italiano investe in pannelli solari e turbine eoliche. Proteggere l'ambiente è responsabilità di tutti, dal Trentino alla Sardegna.","unit_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3004-0000-b10000000000","word_count":96}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-4444-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3006-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1"},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3005-0000-b10000000000"}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-4444-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1"},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3003-0000-b10000000000"}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-4444-3008-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-4444-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3008-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","content":"Lo sport è importante per mantener la salute. In Italia, molte persone praticano attività fisica regolarmente. La corsa è uno sport popolare nei parchi delle città come Milano e Roma. Anche il ciclismo è molto diffuso, specialmente sulle colline della Toscana. Fare esercizio fisico almeno tre volte alla settimana aiuta il cuore e i muscoli. Il nuoto è eccellente per tutto il corpo. Non è necessario essere atleti professionisti per stare bene: camminare tutti i giorni è sufficiente. La salute migliora quando kombiniamo lo sport con una buona alimentazione, come la dieta mediterranea."},"after":{"content":"Lo sport è importante per mantener la salute. In Italia, molte persone praticano attività fisica regolarmente. La corsa è uno sport popolare nei parchi delle città come Milano e Roma. Anche il ciclismo è molto diffuso, specialmente sulle colline della Toscana. Fare esercizio fisico almeno tre volte alla settimana aiuta il cuore e i muscoli. Il nuoto è eccellente per tutto il corpo. Non è necessario essere atleti professionisti per stare bene: camminare tutti i giorni è sufficiente. La salute migliora quando combiniamo lo sport con una buona alimentazione, come la dieta mediterranea."}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-4444-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","content":"L'intelligenza artificiale sta trasformando rapidamente il mercato del lavoro italiano ed europeo. Secondo uno studio del Politecnico di Milano, entro il 2030 almeno il 40% dei lavori subirà cambiamenti significativi dovuti all'automazione e all'IA.\n\nMolte aziende italiane, dalle fabbriche della Lombardia ai call center di Roma, stanno già implementando sistemi di intelligenza artificiale per aumentare l'efficienza. Tuttavia, questo non significa necessariamente disoccupazione di massa. Storicamente, ogni rivoluzione tecnologica ha creato nuove professioni mentre ne ha eliminate altre.\n\nIl vero sfida è la formazione e l'adattamento. I lavoratori devono sviluppare competenze digitali e creatività, capacità che le macchine non possono facilmente replicare. Il governo italiano ha lanciato diversi programmi di riqualificazione professionale, ma gli esperti sostengono che non sono ancora sufficienti.\n\nLe professioni più colpite saranno quelle ripetitive, come l'inserimento dati e il confezionamento. Invece, settori come il design, la consulenza strategica e le professioni sanitarie avranno maggiore domanda. La chiave del successo sarà l'apprendimento continuo e l'adattabilità."},"after":{"content":"L'intelligenza artificiale sta trasformando rapidamente il mercato del lavoro italiano ed europeo. Secondo uno studio del Politecnico di Milano, entro il 2030 almeno il 40% dei lavori subirà cambiamenti significativi dovuti all'automazione e all'IA.\n\nMolte aziende italiane, dalle fabbriche della Lombardia ai call center di Roma, stanno già implementando sistemi di intelligenza artificiale per aumentare l'efficienza. Tuttavia, questo non significa necessariamente disoccupazione di massa. Storicamente, ogni rivoluzione tecnologica ha creato nuove professioni mentre ne ha eliminate altre.\n\nLa vera sfida è la formazione e l'adattamento. I lavoratori devono sviluppare competenze digitali e creatività, capacità che le macchine non possono facilmente replicare. Il governo italiano ha lanciato diversi programmi di riqualificazione professionale, ma gli esperti sostengono che non sono ancora sufficienti.\n\nLe professioni più colpite saranno quelle ripetitive, come l'inserimento dati e il confezionamento. Invece, settori come il design, la consulenza strategica e le professioni sanitarie avranno maggiore domanda. La chiave del successo sarà l'apprendimento continuo e l'adattabilità."}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-4444-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4002-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","content":"L'arte ha sempre giocato un ruolo importante nella storia della protesta politica e sociale. In Italia, durante il Novecento, molti artisti hanno utilizzato le loro opere per criticare il potere e denunciare le ingiustizie. Un esempio famoso è quello di Lucio Fontana, il quale con i suoi tagli sulla tela rappresentava una rottura con il passato e la ricerca di libertà creativa.\n\nAnche la street art moderna continua questa tradizione. A Roma e Milano, i writer creano murales che affrontano temi come l'inquinamento, la disuguaglianza sociale e i diritti umani. Questi artisti trasformano le muri grigie delle città in gallerie all'aperto, raggiungendo un pubblico molto più ampio rispetto alle mostre tradizionali.\n\nLa musica è un altro mezzo potente di protesta. Cantanti come Ennio Morricone hanno composto brani critici verso la guerra e la violenza. L'arte, in tutte le sue forme, rimane uno strumento fondamentale per dare voce a chi non ha voce e per spingere la società verso il cambiamento."},"after":{"content":"L'arte ha sempre giocato un ruolo importante nella storia della protesta politica e sociale. In Italia, durante il Novecento, molti artisti hanno utilizzato le loro opere per criticare il potere e denunciare le ingiustizie. Un esempio famoso è quello di Lucio Fontana, il quale con i suoi tagli sulla tela rappresentava una rottura con il passato e la ricerca di libertà creativa.\n\nAnche la street art moderna continua questa tradizione. A Roma e Milano, i writer creano murales che affrontano temi come l'inquinamento, la disuguaglianza sociale e i diritti umani. Questi artisti trasformano i muri grigi delle città in gallerie all'aperto, raggiungendo un pubblico molto più ampio rispetto alle mostre tradizionali.\n\nLa musica è un altro mezzo potente di protesta. Compositori come Ennio Morricone hanno composto brani critici verso la guerra e la violenza. L'arte, in tutte le sue forme, rimane uno strumento fondamentale per dare voce a chi non ha voce e per spingere la società verso il cambiamento."}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4004-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-4444-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4004-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2"},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4001-0000-b20000000000"}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-4444-4005-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-4444-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-4444-4005-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","content":"La narrativa è uno strumento potente che plasma il modo in cui comprendiamo il mondo. Sin dall'epoca di Omero, le storie hanno trasmesso valori, insegnamenti e identità culturali. Pensiamo a come i romanzi di Alessandro Manzoni hanno influenzato la percezione dell'Italia unita, o come le novelle di Giovanni Boccaccio riflettevano la società medievale.\n\nOggi, la narrativa rimane essenziale. I film italiani di Pasolini e Fellini non raccontavano semplici trame, ma offrivano visioni critiche della realtà. Analogamente, i podcast e i libri contemporanei continuano a costruire significato nella nostra vita quotidiana.\n\nQuando ascoltiamo una storia, il nostro cervello non rimane passivo. Elaboriamo emozioni, identificazioni e insegnamenti che trasformano il nostro pensiero. Una narrazione ben costruita può cambiare prospettive, creare empatia e motivare azioni concrete.\n\nPer questo motivo, comprendre come funziona una narrativa—la struttura, i personaggi, i temi—è cruciale nel nostro mondo moderno, dove le storie ci circondano costantemente."},"after":{"content":"La narrativa è uno strumento potente che plasma il modo in cui comprendiamo il mondo. Sin dall'epoca di Omero, le storie hanno trasmesso valori, insegnamenti e identità culturali. Pensiamo a come i romanzi di Alessandro Manzoni hanno influenzato la percezione dell'Italia unita, o come le novelle di Giovanni Boccaccio riflettevano la società medievale.\n\nOggi, la narrativa rimane essenziale. I film italiani di Pasolini e Fellini non raccontavano semplici trame, ma offrivano visioni critiche della realtà. Analogamente, i podcast e i libri contemporanei continuano a costruire significato nella nostra vita quotidiana.\n\nQuando ascoltiamo una storia, il nostro cervello non rimane passivo. Elaboriamo emozioni, identificazioni e insegnamenti che trasformano il nostro pensiero. Una narrazione ben costruita può cambiare prospettive, creare empatia e motivare azioni concrete.\n\nPer questo motivo, comprendere come funziona una narrativa—la struttura, i personaggi, i temi—è cruciale nel nostro mondo moderno, dove le storie ci circondano costantemente."}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-5555-3004-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-5555-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-5555-3004-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1"},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-5555-3005-0000-b10000000000"}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-5555-3005-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-5555-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-5555-3005-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1"},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-5555-3004-0000-b10000000000"}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-5555-3006-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-5555-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-5555-3006-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1"},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-5555-3005-0000-b10000000000"}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-5555-3007-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-5555-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-5555-3007-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1"},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-5555-3003-0000-b10000000000"}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-5555-4002-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-5555-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-5555-4002-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","content":"A arte tem sido uma ferramenta poderosa de protesto ao longo da história portuguesa. Durante o regime do Estado Novo, artistas como Júlio Pomar usavam as suas obras para criticar a opressão política, mesmo correndo grandes riscos. As pinturas e esculturas tornavam-se mensagens silenciosas contra a censura.\n\nHoje em dia, a arte de rua continua a ser uma voz importante nas cidades portuguesas. Muros em Lisboa e Porto exibem murais coloridos que questionam temas sociais como a desigualdade, a crise habitacional e o ambiente. Artistas urbanos anónimos transformam espaços públicos em galerias de reflexão política.\n\nA arte de protesto não se limita apenas às artes visuais. A música, particularmente o hip-hop e o punk português, também desafia o status quo. Bandas como Deolinda combinam melodias tradicionais com letras críticas sobre problemas contemporâneos.\n\nO que torna esta expressão artística especial é a sua capacidade de comunicar emoções profundas sem necessidade de palavras explicitas, atingindo diretamente o coração do espectador."},"after":{"content":"A arte tem sido uma ferramenta poderosa de protesto ao longo da história portuguesa. Durante o regime do Estado Novo, artistas como Júlio Pomar usavam as suas obras para criticar a opressão política, mesmo correndo grandes riscos. As pinturas e esculturas tornavam-se mensagens silenciosas contra a censura.\n\nHoje em dia, a arte de rua continua a ser uma voz importante nas cidades portuguesas. Muros em Lisboa e Porto exibem murais coloridos que questionam temas sociais como a desigualdade, a crise habitacional e o ambiente. Artistas urbanos anónimos transformam espaços públicos em galerias de reflexão política.\n\nA arte de protesto não se limita apenas às artes visuais. A música, particularmente o hip-hop e o punk português, também desafia o status quo. Bandas como Deolinda combinam melodias tradicionais com letras críticas sobre problemas contemporâneos.\n\nO que torna esta expressão artística especial é a sua capacidade de comunicar emoções profundas sem necessidade de palavras explícitas, atingindo diretamente o coração do espectador."}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-5555-4004-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-5555-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-5555-4004-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2"},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-5555-4001-0000-b20000000000"}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-6666-3001-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-6666-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-6666-3001-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","word_count":560},"after":{"word_count":286}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-6666-3002-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-6666-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-6666-3002-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","word_count":413},"after":{"word_count":222}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-6666-3003-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-6666-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-6666-3003-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","word_count":376},"after":{"word_count":190}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-6666-3004-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-6666-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-6666-3004-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","word_count":383},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-6666-3005-0000-b10000000000","word_count":200}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-6666-3005-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-6666-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-6666-3005-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","word_count":359},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-6666-3004-0000-b10000000000","word_count":182}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-6666-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-6666-3006-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","word_count":379},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-6666-3005-0000-b10000000000","word_count":186}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-6666-3007-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-6666-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-6666-3007-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","word_count":351},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-6666-3003-0000-b10000000000","word_count":184}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-6666-3008-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-6666-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-6666-3008-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","word_count":320},"after":{"word_count":174}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-6666-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","content":"近年、日本の企業でも人工知能（AI）の導入が急速に進んでいます。トヨタやソニーなどの大手企業だけでなく、中小企業でもAIを活用する動きが広がっています。\n\nAIが得意とするのは、大量のデータを素早く分析することです。例えば、銀行の融資審査では、従来は人間が何日もかけて顧客の信用情報を調べていました。しかし今では、AIがわずか数分で分析を完了します。同様に、医療現場でもAIは医師の診断を支援し、画像診断の精度を高めています。\n\nしかし、AIの普及に伴い、多くの人が職を失うのではないかという不安も生まれています。実際、事務作業や単純な製造業の仕事は、AIやロボットに置き換わる可能性が高いと指摘されています。日本銀行の調査によれば、今後20年で、自動化される可能性がある職業は全体の約49％に上るとされています。\n\nただし、新しい技術は同時に新しい仕事も生み出します。AIを開発・管理する人材、AIを使いこなすコンサルタント、データ分析の専門家など、これまで存在しなかった職種が増えています。さらに、人間にしかできない創造的な仕事、例えばデザインやカウンセリング、教育などの価値は高まるでしょう。\n\n重要なのは、社会がこの変化にどう対応するかということです。日本政府も「人生100年時代」に向けて、生涯学習の推進やスキルアップ支援に力を入れています。企業側も従業員の研修制度を充実させ、新しい技術に対応できる人材育成に取り組む必要があります。\n\nAIの発展は避けられません。大切なのは、AIとどう共存するかを考え、準備することです。変化を恐れるのではなく、学習し適応することで、誰もが新しい時代で活躍できるようになるはずです。","word_count":704},"after":{"content":"近年、日本の企業でも人工知能（AI）の導入が急速に進んでいます。トヨタやソニーなどの大手企業だけでなく、中小企業でもAIを活用する動きが広がっています。\n\nAIが得意とするのは、大量のデータを素早く分析することです。例えば、銀行の融資審査では、従来は人間が何日もかけて顧客の信用情報を調べていました。しかし今では、AIがわずか数分で分析を完了します。同様に、医療現場でもAIは医師の診断を支援し、画像診断の精度を高めています。\n\nしかし、AIの普及に伴い、多くの人が職を失うのではないかという不安も生まれています。実際、事務作業や単純な製造業の仕事は、AIやロボットに置き換わる可能性が高いと指摘されています。野村総合研究所が2015年に発表した推計では、日本の労働人口の約49％が就く職業は、その後10～20年で技術的にはAIやロボットに代替される可能性があるとされました。これは、実際にそれだけの仕事が失われるという予測ではありません。\n\nただし、新しい技術は同時に新しい仕事も生み出します。AIを開発・管理する人材、AIを使いこなすコンサルタント、データ分析の専門家など、これまで存在しなかった職種が増えています。さらに、人間にしかできない創造的な仕事、例えばデザインやカウンセリング、教育などの価値は高まるでしょう。\n\n重要なのは、社会がこの変化にどう対応するかということです。日本政府も「人生100年時代」に向けて、生涯学習の推進やスキルアップ支援に力を入れています。企業側も従業員の研修制度を充実させ、新しい技術に対応できる人材育成に取り組む必要があります。\n\nAIの発展は避けられません。大切なのは、AIとどう共存するかを考え、準備することです。変化を恐れるのではなく、学習し適応することで、誰もが新しい時代で活躍できるようになるはずです。","word_count":400}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-6666-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4002-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","word_count":650},"after":{"word_count":347}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-6666-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4003-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","content":"近年、グローバル化の進展により、世界中の文化が急速に融合しています。日本もこの波に大きく影響を受けており、若い世代を中心に西洋文化への関心が高まっています。一方で、日本の伝統文化を守ろうとする動きも活発化しています。\n\n東京や大阪などの大都市では、ハンバーガーショップやコーヒーチェーン店が増え、欧米のライフスタイルが浸透しています。また、SNSの普及により、外国の音楽やファッション、映画などのコンテンツが容易にアクセスできるようになりました。多くの若者がこれらの文化を積極的に受け入れ、自分たちのアイデンティティの一部としています。\n\nしかし同時に、茶道や書道、歌舞伎などの伝統文化への関心も再評価されています。特に京都や奈良では、観光客の増加に伴い、寺院や神社などの伝統的な建造物の保存が重視されるようになりました。また、和食がユネスコの無形文化遺産に登録されたことで、日本の食文化への誇りが高まっています。\n\n重要なのは、グローバル化が必ずしも文化の喪失を意味しないということです。むしろ、世界との交流を通じて、自分たちの文化の価値をより深く理解する機会が生まれています。日本の若い世代は、洋風のファッションを着ながらも、成人式では振袖を選びます。これは、異なる文化を柔軟に受け入れつつ、自分たちのルーツを大切にする姿勢を示しています。\n\nグローバル化の時代において、日本の課題は、西洋文化の影響を避けることではなく、自分たちの伝統と新しい価値観のバランスを見つけることです。このプロセスを通じて、日本は独自の文化的アイデンティティをさらに強化していく可能性があります。","word_count":681},"after":{"content":"近年、グローバル化の進展により、世界中の文化が急速に融合しています。日本もこの波に大きく影響を受けており、若い世代を中心に西洋文化への関心が高まっています。一方で、日本の伝統文化を守ろうとする動きも活発化しています。\n\n東京や大阪などの大都市では、ハンバーガーショップやコーヒーチェーン店が増え、欧米のライフスタイルが浸透しています。また、SNSの普及により、外国の音楽やファッション、映画などのコンテンツに容易にアクセスできるようになりました。多くの若者がこれらの文化を積極的に受け入れ、自分たちのアイデンティティの一部としています。\n\nしかし同時に、茶道や書道、歌舞伎などの伝統文化への関心も再評価されています。特に京都や奈良では、観光客の増加に伴い、寺院や神社などの伝統的な建造物の保存が重視されるようになりました。また、和食がユネスコの無形文化遺産に登録されたことで、日本の食文化への誇りが高まっています。\n\n重要なのは、グローバル化が必ずしも文化の喪失を意味しないということです。むしろ、世界との交流を通じて、自分たちの文化の価値をより深く理解する機会が生まれています。日本の若い世代は、洋風のファッションを着ながらも、成人式では振袖を選びます。これは、異なる文化を柔軟に受け入れつつ、自分たちのルーツを大切にする姿勢を示しています。\n\nグローバル化の時代において、日本の課題は、西洋文化の影響を避けることではなく、自分たちの伝統と新しい価値観のバランスを見つけることです。このプロセスを通じて、日本は独自の文化的アイデンティティをさらに強化していく可能性があります。","word_count":338}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4004-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-6666-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4004-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","word_count":662},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4001-0000-b20000000000","word_count":344}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4005-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-6666-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4005-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","word_count":540},"after":{"word_count":293}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-6666-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-6666-4006-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","word_count":574},"after":{"word_count":306}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3001-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-7777-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3001-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","word_count":230},"after":{"word_count":70}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3002-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-7777-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3002-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","word_count":185},"after":{"word_count":56}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3003-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-7777-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3003-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","word_count":157},"after":{"word_count":40}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3004-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-7777-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3004-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","word_count":191},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3005-0000-b10000000000","word_count":59}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3005-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-7777-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3005-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","word_count":177},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3004-0000-b10000000000","word_count":53}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-7777-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3006-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","word_count":197},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3005-0000-b10000000000","word_count":57}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3007-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-7777-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3007-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","word_count":182},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3003-0000-b10000000000","word_count":60}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-7777-3008-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-7777-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-7777-3008-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","word_count":185},"after":{"word_count":57}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4001-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-7777-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4001-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","word_count":292},"after":{"word_count":88}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-7777-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4002-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","content":"역사 속에서 예술은 단순한 아름다움을 넘어 사회 변화의 도구로 기능해왔다. 1980년대 한국의 민주화 운동 시기, 많은 미술가들은 캔버스와 조각으로 억압에 맞섰다. 광주 비엔날레와 같은 전시회들은 정치적 메시지를 담은 작품들의 무대가 되었다.\n\n세계적으로도 이러한 경향은 두드러진다. 영국의 스트릿 아트 아티스트 뱅크시는 벽화를 통해 전쟁과 소비주의를 비판한다. 그의 작품들은 갤러리가 아닌 거리에서 일반인들과 만난다. 이렇게 예술이 저항의 형태가 될 때, 그것은 더 이상 엘리트만의 문화가 아니라 대중의 목소리가 된다.\n\n예술은 말로 표현하기 어려운 감정과 생각을 시각화하며, 사회에 질문을 던진다. 이것이 예술이 가진 진정한 힘이다.","word_count":273},"after":{"content":"역사 속에서 예술은 단순한 아름다움을 넘어 사회 변화의 도구로 기능해왔다. 1980년대 한국의 민주화 운동 시기, 많은 미술가들은 캔버스와 조각으로 억압에 맞섰다. 그 후 1995년에 처음 열린 광주 비엔날레와 같은 전시회들은 정치적 메시지를 담은 작품들의 무대가 되었다.\n\n세계적으로도 이러한 경향은 두드러진다. 영국의 스트릿 아트 아티스트 뱅크시는 벽화를 통해 전쟁과 소비주의를 비판한다. 그의 작품들은 갤러리가 아닌 거리에서 일반인들과 만난다. 이렇게 예술이 저항의 형태가 될 때, 그것은 더 이상 엘리트만의 문화가 아니라 대중의 목소리가 된다.\n\n예술은 말로 표현하기 어려운 감정과 생각을 시각화하며, 사회에 질문을 던진다. 이것이 예술이 가진 진정한 힘이다.","word_count":87}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-7777-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4003-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","word_count":322},"after":{"word_count":96}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4004-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-7777-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4004-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","content":"최근 몇 년 동안 인공지능 기술이 빠르게 발전하면서 우리 사회에도 많은 변화가 일어나고 있습니다. 네이버의 클로바, 카카오의 카카오 브레인 같은 AI 서비스들이 일상생활 속에 깊숙이 들어와 있습니다. 하지만 이러한 편리함 뒤에는 중요한 윤리적 문제들이 숨어 있습니다.\n\n먼저 개인정보 보호 문제가 있습니다. AI 시스템이 사용자의 데이터를 수집할 때 얼마나 투명하게 그 과정을 공개해야 할까요? 또한 AI가 내린 결정이 차별로 이어질 수 있다는 점도 중요합니다. 예를 들어, 채용 과정에서 AI가 특정 집단을 불공정하게 평가할 수도 있습니다.\n\n전문가들은 AI 개발 과정에서부터 윤리 기준을 세워야 한다고 강조합니다. 정부와 기업이 함께 협력하여 책임감 있는 AI 사회를 만들어야 합니다.","word_count":291},"after":{"content":"최근 몇 년 동안 인공지능 기술이 빠르게 발전하면서 우리 사회에도 많은 변화가 일어나고 있습니다. 네이버의 클로바는 AI 기술 브랜드입니다. 카카오의 AI 연구·개발 자회사였던 카카오브레인은 언어 모델과 이미지 생성 모델을 개발했습니다. 하지만 이러한 편리함 뒤에는 중요한 윤리적 문제들이 숨어 있습니다.\n\n먼저 개인정보 보호 문제가 있습니다. AI 시스템이 사용자의 데이터를 수집할 때 얼마나 투명하게 그 과정을 공개해야 할까요? 또한 AI가 내린 결정이 차별로 이어질 수 있다는 점도 중요합니다. 예를 들어, 채용 과정에서 AI가 특정 집단을 불공정하게 평가할 수도 있습니다.\n\n전문가들은 AI 개발 과정에서부터 윤리 기준을 세워야 한다고 강조합니다. 정부와 기업이 함께 협력하여 책임감 있는 AI 사회를 만들어야 합니다.","unit_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4001-0000-b20000000000","word_count":96}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-7777-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4005-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","word_count":266},"after":{"word_count":86}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-7777-4006-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-7777-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-7777-4006-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","word_count":265},"after":{"word_count":81}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-8888-3001-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-8888-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-8888-3001-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","word_count":233},"after":{"word_count":116}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-8888-3002-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-8888-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-8888-3002-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","word_count":193},"after":{"word_count":112}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-8888-3003-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-8888-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-8888-3003-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","word_count":161},"after":{"word_count":92}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-8888-3004-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-8888-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-8888-3004-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","word_count":167},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-8888-3005-0000-b10000000000","word_count":89}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-8888-3005-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-8888-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-8888-3005-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","word_count":176},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-8888-3004-0000-b10000000000","word_count":95}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-8888-3006-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-8888-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-8888-3006-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","word_count":157},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-8888-3005-0000-b10000000000","word_count":89}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-8888-3007-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-8888-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-8888-3007-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","word_count":162},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-8888-3003-0000-b10000000000","word_count":85}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-8888-3008-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-8888-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-8888-3008-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","word_count":155},"after":{"word_count":83}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-8888-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","word_count":301},"after":{"word_count":158}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-8888-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4002-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","word_count":281},"after":{"word_count":149}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-8888-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4003-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","word_count":321},"after":{"word_count":165}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-8888-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4004-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","word_count":293},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4001-0000-b20000000000","word_count":156}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-8888-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4005-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","word_count":295},"after":{"word_count":153}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-8888-4006-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-8888-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-8888-4006-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","content":"你知道吗？学习新语言可以改变你的大脑。科学家发现，当我们学习一门外语时，大脑中负责语言处理的区域会变得更加活跃。这个过程叫做神经可塑性。\n\n研究表明，说两种或多种语言的人往往有更强的记忆力和注意力。他们的大脑在处理信息时更加高效。在中国，很多学生都在学习英语或其他外语，这实际上是在锻炼他们的大脑。\n\n有趣的是，学习语言的最佳时期是童年。孩子的大脑更容易接受新信息。但是，成年人也可以学习新语言，只是需要花更多时间和精力。专家建议每天至少花30分钟学习新语言，这样可以帮助大脑保持年轻和活跃。","word_count":242},"after":{"content":"你知道吗？学习新语言可以改变你的大脑。科学家发现，当我们学习一门外语时，大脑中负责语言处理的区域会变得更加活跃。大脑还能随着学习和经验改变结构、功能以及神经连接，这种能力叫做神经可塑性。\n\n研究表明，说两种或多种语言的人往往有更强的记忆力和注意力。他们的大脑在处理信息时更加高效。在中国，很多学生都在学习英语或其他外语，这实际上是在锻炼他们的大脑。\n\n有趣的是，学习语言的最佳时期是童年。孩子的大脑更容易接受新信息。但是，成年人也可以学习新语言，只是需要花更多时间和精力。专家建议每天至少花30分钟学习新语言，这样可以帮助大脑保持年轻和活跃。","word_count":143}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-9999-3003-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-9999-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-9999-3003-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","content":"Мария решила провести неделю в Барселоне. Она купила билет на самолёт и забронировала небольшой отель в центре города. В первый день она посетила парк Гюэль, где видела необычные мозаики и красивые виды на город. Во второй день она гуляла по готическому кварталу и посетила собор Святого Семейства. Вечером она сидела в кафе и пила испанское вино. Барселона ей очень понравилась. Она ела паэлью, слушала музыку и чувствовала себя счастливой. На последний день она купила сувениры и поехала в аэропорт.","title":"Выходные в Барселоне"},"after":{"content":"Мария решила провести неделю в Барселоне. Она купила билет на самолёт и забронировала небольшой отель в центре города. В первый день она посетила парк Гюэль, где видела необычные мозаики и красивые виды на город. Во второй день она гуляла по готическому кварталу и посетила собор Святого Семейства. Вечером она сидела в кафе и пила испанское вино. Барселона ей очень понравилась. Она ела паэлью, слушала музыку и чувствовала себя счастливой. В последний день она купила сувениры и поехала в аэропорт.","title":"Неделя в Барселоне"}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-9999-3004-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-9999-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-9999-3004-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1"},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-9999-3005-0000-b10000000000"}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-9999-3005-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-9999-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-9999-3005-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","content":"Россия сталкивается со многими экологическими проблемами. Одна из самых серьёзных – загрязнение воздуха в больших городах, особенно в Москве и Санкт-Петербурге. Заводы и автомобили выбрасывают вредные вещества в атмосферу.\n\nДругая важная проблема – загрязнение озера Байкал. Это самое глубокое озеро в мире, но оно становится грязнее из-за промышленных отходов. Также люди вырубают леса в Сибири, что влияет на климат и животных.\n\nМного россиян беспокоят эти проблемы и участвуют в движениях защиты окружающей среды. Правительство пытается улучшить ситуацию через новые законы и проекты."},"after":{"content":"Россия сталкивается со многими экологическими проблемами. Одна из самых серьёзных – загрязнение воздуха в больших городах, особенно в Москве и Санкт-Петербурге. Заводы и автомобили выбрасывают вредные вещества в атмосферу.\n\nДругая важная проблема – загрязнение озера Байкал. Это самое глубокое озеро в мире, но оно становится грязнее из-за промышленных отходов. Также люди вырубают леса в Сибири, что влияет на климат и животных.\n\nМногие россияне обеспокоены этими проблемами и участвуют в движениях защиты окружающей среды. Правительство пытается улучшить ситуацию через новые законы и проекты.","unit_id":"aabbccdd-9999-3004-0000-b10000000000"}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-9999-3006-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-9999-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-9999-3006-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1"},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-9999-3005-0000-b10000000000"}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-9999-3007-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-9999-0000-0000-b10000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-9999-3007-0000-b10000000000","cefr_level":"B1","content":"Современная Москва предлагает огромный выбор международной кухни. В центре города вы найдёте итальянские рестораны с настоящей пастой, японские суши-бары и французские бистро. Особенно популярна азиатская кухня — тайская, корейская и китайская. Многие москвичи любят пробовать блюда из разных стран. Международные шефы готовят традиционные рецепты с современным стилем. Цены варьируются от дешёвых кафе до дорогих ресторанов. Попробовать мировую кухню в Москве — это интересный способ путешествовать без границ!"},"after":{"content":"Современная Москва предлагает огромный выбор международной кухни. В центре города вы найдёте итальянские рестораны с настоящей пастой, японские суши-бары и французские бистро. Особенно популярна азиатская кухня — тайская, корейская и китайская. Многие москвичи любят пробовать блюда из разных стран. Международные шефы готовят традиционные рецепты с современным стилем. Здесь есть и недорогие кафе, и дорогие рестораны. Попробовать мировую кухню в Москве — это интересный способ путешествовать без границ!","unit_id":"aabbccdd-9999-3003-0000-b10000000000"}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4001-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-9999-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4001-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","content":"Искусственный интеллект (ИИ) быстро меняет рынок труда в России и во всём мире. Уже сейчас компании в Москве и Санкт-Петербурге используют ИИ для анализа данных, обслуживания клиентов и автоматизации производства. Это создаёт как новые возможности, так и вызовы для работников.\n\nС одной стороны, ИИ может выполнять рутинную работу быстрее и дешевле, чем люди. Банковские служащие, операторы колл-центров и некоторые специалисты в области бухгалтерии могут столкнуться с сокращением рабочих мест. Однако, с другой стороны, появляются новые профессии: разработчики ИИ, аналитики данных и специалисты по кибербезопасности очень востребованы и получают высокие зарплаты.\n\nЭксперты советуют молодым людям учиться навыкам, которые пока не может освоить машина: творчество, критическое мышление и общение с людьми. Компании начинают вкладывать в переподготовку своих сотрудников, чтобы они могли работать рядом с ИИ, а не вместо них.","word_count":127},"after":{"content":"Искусственный интеллект (ИИ) быстро меняет рынок труда в России и во всём мире. Уже сейчас компании в Москве и Санкт-Петербурге используют ИИ для анализа данных, обслуживания клиентов и автоматизации производства. Это создаёт как новые возможности, так и вызовы для работников.\n\nС одной стороны, ИИ может выполнять рутинную работу быстрее и дешевле, чем люди. Банковские служащие, операторы колл-центров и некоторые специалисты в области бухгалтерии могут столкнуться с сокращением рабочих мест. Однако, с другой стороны, появляются новые профессии: разработчики ИИ, аналитики данных и специалисты по кибербезопасности очень востребованы и получают высокие зарплаты.\n\nЭксперты советуют молодым людям учиться навыкам, которые пока не может освоить машина: творчество, критическое мышление и общение с людьми. Компании начинают вкладывать в переподготовку своих сотрудников, чтобы они могли работать вместе с ИИ, а не быть заменёнными им.","word_count":128}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4002-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-9999-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4002-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2","content":"Искусство всегда было мощным инструментом социального изменения. На протяжении истории художники, музыканты и писатели использовали своё творчество, чтобы выражать недовольство и бороться за справедливость.\n\nВ России примером служит творчество художника Владимира Маяковского, который своими революционными стихами вдохновлял людей на перемены. Его произведения были не просто красивыми словами — они были призывом к действию.\n\nСегодня протестное искусство по-прежнему актуально. Граффити на городских стенах, уличная музыка и перформансы помогают людям поднимать важные вопросы об окружающей среде, правах человека и политических проблемах. Художники используют символы и образы, которые понимает каждый.\n\nТакое искусство опасно для властей, потому что оно говорит с народом на его языке. Оно не требует цензуры или разрешения — оно просто существует и существует долго, вдохновляя следующие поколения к переменам."},"after":{"content":"Искусство всегда было мощным инструментом социального изменения. На протяжении истории художники, музыканты и писатели использовали своё творчество, чтобы выражать недовольство и бороться за справедливость.\n\nВ России примером служит творчество художника Владимира Маяковского, который своими революционными стихами вдохновлял людей на перемены. Его произведения были не просто красивыми словами — они были призывом к действию.\n\nСегодня протестное искусство по-прежнему актуально. Граффити на городских стенах, уличная музыка и перформансы помогают людям поднимать важные вопросы об окружающей среде, правах человека и политических проблемах. Художники используют символы и образы, которые понимает каждый.\n\nТакое искусство опасно для властей, потому что оно говорит с народом на его языке. Оно не требует цензуры или разрешения — оно просто существует и существует долго, вдохновляя следующие поколения на перемены."}},{"table":"reading_passages","id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-a001-000000000000","before":{"course_id":"aabbccdd-9999-0000-0000-b20000000000","unit_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4004-0000-b20000000000","cefr_level":"B2"},"after":{"unit_id":"aabbccdd-9999-4001-0000-b20000000000"}},{"table":"reading_questions","id":"003ae4eb-92f2-444b-86f3-89e2362d70bc","before":{"passage_id":"aabbccdd-4444-3007-a001-000000000000","question_type":"short_answer","acce